WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:06.240
The year was 1983, and seven year old Andrea
Bradbury was wandering the streets of Nashville,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.240
Tennessee.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.980
One of her favourite activities was to head
down to the local movie theater and fantasize

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.679
about the movies she’d one day be old enough
to see.

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:20.800
This fateful weekend, Andrea’s local theater
was playing a brand new release: Jaws 3D.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.390
What she didn’t know is that this simple,
innocent activity would bring little Andrea

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:30.890
into dangerous contact with SCP - 178 and
change her life forever.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:36.199
Jaws 3D isn’t exactly a classic - it was
one of the many forgettable sequels pumped

00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:40.149
out to cash in on the 3D craze of the early
1980s.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:44.300
People paid extra for the privilege of sitting
in the dark with an uncomfortable pair of

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.190
cardboard glasses while cheesy effects leapt
out of the screen towards them.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.730
Many of the moviegoers simply threw away the
cheap, disposable glasses as soon as they

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.889
left the theater, leaving them scattered on
the sidewalk outside.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:01:01.719
Seeing a pair of 3D glasses on the ground,
right there for the taking, was the highlight

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:03.449
of little Andrea’s week.

00:01:03.449 --> 00:01:07.750
She may not have been old enough to see any
of the movies, but she knew that a local shop

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:13.430
sold books with images that popped off the
page with a simple pair of 3D glasses.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:18.160
Excited by the prospect of getting to experience
3D, Andrea grabbed a pair of glasses and ran

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.190
straight for the bookstore.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:25.130
Later that night, she was in her bedroom,
with a stereoscopic image of a Ferris wheel..

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:30.540
Andrea adjusted the glasses - and the Ferris
wheel really did pop right off the page.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.200
She marveled at the image coming out of the
book and felt like she could almost touch

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.200
it.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.500
But suddenly a strange feeling came over her.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.420
She had the feeling that she wasn’t… alone.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.840
Still wearing the glasses, Andrea looked up
from her book and saw it, standing in the

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.170
corner of her room.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.420
Something huge.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.960
Something monstrous.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.590
Andrea’s parents heard her scream and came
rushing into her room.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.950
There was their little girl, dead.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:03.300
It looked like she’d been mauled to death
by a wild animal, but there was no sign of

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.710
her killer.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:08.850
The windows were shut tight, unable to be
opened from outside.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:13.450
It was like whatever horrible creature had
done this had vanished into thin air.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:17.720
The coroner's report didn’t give any other
clues as to who could have done this, except

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:23.200
that whoever, or whatever had murdered her,
it appeared to have three long and incredibly

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.280
sharp claws.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.440
The terrible tragedy of Andrea’s death rocked
Nashville, but it never made the national

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.440
papers.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.440
Why?

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.560
Because the SCP Foundation was immediately
on the case.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:40.120
Undercover agents in the US Fish and Wildlife
Service flagged the strange death as anomalous,

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:44.880
and SCP field personnel arrived to do their
own investigation of the crime scene.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.390
There they quickly discovered Andrea’s 3D
glasses - which would eventually be classified

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.650
as SCP - 178.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.959
An Agent looked over the glasses.

00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:58.090
There didn’t seem to be anything out of
the ordinary about them, just your regular

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.820
cardboard frames with blue and red tinted
film over the eyes.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.480
Everything about them seemed normal, so he
tried the glasses on himself.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.740
He picked up the open book up off the ground
where Andrea had likely dropped it, and saw

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.440
the Ferris wheel pop up off the page.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.030
Nothing abnormal.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:18.870
Until he turned his head slightly...

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:25.130
He saw the head of some kind of… thing,
only an inch away from his own, looking over

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.140
his shoulder at the book.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:32.300
Being a trained SCP agent, he maintained his
composure, and looked around the room.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:36.820
As he did he saw that several other creatures
were standing and watching.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:41.080
None of the rest of the recovery team seemed
to notice the creatures, and when the agent

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.630
removed SCP - 178, they vanished.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:48.850
It appeared that they had found whatever had
caused Andrea Bradbury’s death.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:53.050
The glasses were immediately taken to the
nearest Foundation containment site for further

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:54.050
testing.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:58.550
Seeing these mysterious entities through SCP
- 178 may have answered one question, but

00:03:58.550 --> 00:03:59.930
it raised many others.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.050
What are these creatures?

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:07.550
Were they real, or merely illusions created
by SCP - 178?

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:13.150
If they are real, are they somehow summoned
by SCP - 178, or simply revealed by them?

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.840
There was already one death that could be
tied to the glasses with some certainty, but

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.220
just how dangerous were they?

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.630
The SCP Foundation was about to find out.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.600
Foundation scientists devised a series of
experiments, with a test chamber separated

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.310
from an adjoining observation chamber by a
panel of reinforced bulletproof glass.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:38.240
A member of D-Class personnel was placed into
the test chamber, along with SCP - 178.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.270
He was instructed to put on the glasses and
report what he saw back to the researchers.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:47.960
The D-Class followed the orders, however when
he did so, he quickly entered a state of extreme

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.150
distress.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.740
He threw away the glasses and covered his
eyes, screaming wildly.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:57.620
When ordered to compose himself and explain
what he saw under threat of termination, the

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:02.139
D-Class described a “hideous” creature
standing close to his face, watching.

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:06.720
When asked to elaborate, he described it as
having “too many eyes.”

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.240
After that, the D-Class refused to put the
glasses back on again, despite direct orders

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.550
and threats from Foundation staff.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.300
He was then removed from the test chamber
and observed.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.860
Although he experienced two days of mild paranoia,
after thirty total days of observation the

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:24.960
D-Class was found to have no long lasting
psychological effects.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.050
Disappointed by the meager results of the
first test, the researchers had at least confirmed

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:35.320
that they did indeed have an anomalous object
in their possession, and pressed on with the

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.320
experiments.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.550
They used the same methodology again on another
D-Class.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:43.570
She was placed into the chamber and instructed
to put on SCP - 178, then describe the entity

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.630
she saw in great detail.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:50.810
When she put on the glasses she recoiled in
horror at the monster she saw staring back

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.810
at her.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:56.460
She said that the creature was tall and bipedal,
with two additional upper appendages ending

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.840
in large conical protrusions.

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:03.170
She also described the creature’s head as
being “smooth.”

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:07.820
When asked if the creature exhibited any kind
of aggression or hostility, she said that

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.270
it was completely still.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.660
It was just standing there.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:16.070
After a few minutes though, the creature seemed
to lose interest, and began staring at the

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.070
wall.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:20.880
The researchers were happy to learn more about
the creature’s physicality, but they still

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:24.370
weren’t confident that it wasn’t just
an illusion created by the glasses.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:27.949
They needed to engineer an interaction.

00:06:27.949 --> 00:06:31.160
For the next experiment, they decided to alter
the particulars.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:35.900
A fractal blue and red image, in a similar
style to the stereoscopic Ferris wheel from

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.440
the book Andrea had purchased was fixed to
one wall.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:43.910
Against the opposite wall, they placed a bucket
containing ten standard tennis balls.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:48.490
This time, the D-Class - a convicted murderer
and arsonist - was told that he was helping

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.790
to test a new 3D augmented reality project.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:57.380
The entities he would see, as far as he knew,
were little more than digital projections.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:02.600
Though when he actually wore SCP - 178 and
saw them, he commented that whoever designed

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.389
them must be crazy.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:07.830
The researchers instructed the D-Class to
pick up a tennis ball and throw it at one

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:08.960
of the entities.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:13.509
The second he did so, deep lacerations began
appearing all over his body.

00:07:13.509 --> 00:07:18.820
The onslaught was brutal and quick, and the
D-Class was dead soon after that.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:22.730
This confirmed to the researchers that the
creatures did seem to have some level of tangible

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:26.960
presence, and they could be extremely violent
if provoked.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.229
Next, they wished to see if it was possible
to have any kind of interaction with the creatures

00:07:31.229 --> 00:07:35.280
without it immediately descending into violence.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:39.560
To test this theory, the researchers brought
a nineteen year old D-Class into the testing

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:44.229
chamber under the same pretence of testing
new 3D technology.

00:07:44.229 --> 00:07:48.580
Much like the others, she was still horrified
by the appearance of the creatures, but was

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:50.340
calmed down by the researchers.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:55.340
They asked her to speak to the creatures directly,
without exhibiting any kind of aggression.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:08:00.220
She said, “Hello, weird thing, how are you
today?” in a somewhat bored voice.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:05.310
And this was all it took to sign her death
warrant - she was immediately slashed to death

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.979
by invisible creatures.

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:11.289
The results seemed clear: Any interaction
whatsoever with the creatures while wearing

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:16.410
SCP - 178 was a death sentence, like a slightly
more outgoing Shy Guy.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:22.389
But the researchers would soon find that this
anomaly had even more surprises.

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:28.340
For their next test, they brought in two subjects:
One would wear SCP - 178, and dictate to the

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:31.410
other how they should interact with a creature
they could not see.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.659
The results of this experiment were bloody,
yet informative.

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:39.990
Both subjects were slashed to death when the
unseeing D-Class interacted with one of the

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.450
creatures on her companion’s instructions.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:46.040
It appeared that anyone with sufficient knowledge
of the creatures who attempts to interact

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:50.370
with them is doomed, even if they can’t
directly see one of them.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:56.740
It was an upsetting realization for the researchers:
SCP - 178 may be much more dangerous than

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:57.740
they initially imagined.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:01.750
And what they’d learn in the next experiment
was even worse.

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:07.320
They adopted the same methodology as the last
for the following experiment - two subjects,

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.320
one seeing and the other interacting.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.630
However, this time, as soon as Subject number
one put on the glasses, they knew that something

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:15.970
was terribly wrong.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:21.410
He began panicking, stating that the entire
chamber was full of the creatures, all standing

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:22.550
and watching.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:26.170
The researchers undertook these experiments
knowing that they didn’t often turn out

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:30.649
well for the D-Class, so they didn’t seem
too worried about this new development…

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:35.060
that is until the subject stated that they
could see three more of the creatures, and

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:37.270
they weren’t in the test chamber.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.600
They were in the observation room.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.720
In fact, one of them was looking right over
one of the three researchers’ shoulders.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:47.680
Immediately, the researchers lost composure
and began to panic.

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:52.180
They were used to putting D-Class in danger,
that was part of the job, but they weren’t

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.520
prepared for this!

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:58.529
In just moments, the observation room became
a bloodbath as the three researchers who’d

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:03.330
been designing and performing all the experiments
were torn to pieces by creatures they couldn’t

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.330
see

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:09.540
SCP - 178 had gone from being one of the more
innocent looking anomalies to one of the most

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.760
mysterious and deadly.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:16.170
The creatures seemed to be powerful, violent,
and incredibly numerous.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:20.670
The fact that they can only be observed through
178’s stereoscopic lenses and kill anyone

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:24.980
who even attempts to interact with them makes
them almost impossible to understand.

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:31.330
It was always a tragedy when the Foundation
lost good researchers, but the work must continue,

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:34.980
and the experiments were soon restarted with
increased safety measures.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:39.339
Of course those didn’t do much good, and
after another disastrous experiment that resulted

00:10:39.339 --> 00:10:45.420
in the whole sector getting locked down, all
research into SCP - 178 was placed under increased

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.420
scrutiny.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:50.210
They needed to find some way of observing
the creatures, without the risk of having

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.350
to share space with them.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:56.870
The proposed solution was seeing if the SCP
- 178 glasses were compatible with camera

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:58.720
technology for remote viewing.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.780
Much like all stereoscopic glasses, they found
that looking through only one lens at a time

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.420
was ineffective.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:10.690
The solution was relatively simple: A dual-lens
camera in a roughly similar configuration

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:11.710
to human eyes.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:16.380
This, however, didn’t give them the comfort,
or the answers they hoped for.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:20.860
Researchers commented, upon finally seeing
the creatures, that they were even more hideous

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.700
than they’d ever imagined.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:27.080
As they observed a victim interacting with
the creatures via their new camera, they found

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:31.250
that as soon as the creatures were interacted
with in any way, they would grow three long

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.230
claws and attack.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:36.930
And they were as fast as they were ferocious.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:40.850
From the observations, there were only a few
things that the Foundation now knew about

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:46.160
them for sure: Their physical appearance,
their violent nature, their enhanced physical

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.280
abilities, and the fact they appear to be
pretty much everywhere.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:54.839
And who knows how long they’d been here,
observing us humans while we glided by them,

00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:56.700
ignorant to their presence?

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:00.980
It’s enough to make you think twice before
putting on a pair of 3D glasses again.

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:05.320
But of course, never putting on the glasses
doesn’t mean you’re safe.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.230
Just knowing about them puts you in danger.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:13.310
They could be standing next to you right now,
looking over your shoulder as you watch this

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:14.310
video.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:20.570
Just remember: If you want to be safe, you
can’t ever let them know you’re aware.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:28.000
After all, just because you can’t see something,
doesn’t mean it can’t hurt you.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:33.279
SCP Foundation agents stationed at Area 37
had intercepted chatter from a normally closed

00:12:33.279 --> 00:12:35.680
communication system in a nearby city.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:40.459
To anyone else, the calls that the Foundation
were eavesdropping would seem innocent - even

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:45.600
boring, but the Foundation immediately recognized
the coded language being used.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.771
They were listening to communications between
underground cells of The Serpent’s Hand

00:12:49.771 --> 00:12:55.600
- a dangerous paramilitary organization that
stands in opposition to everything the Foundation

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.320
is trying to do.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:02.630
Once deciphered, the Serpent’s Hand messages
revealed plans for killing Foundation personnel,

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:07.621
breaking into containment sites, and releasing
anomalous creatures and objects into the world

00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:12.870
- pretty standard stuff for the Foundation’s
least-favorite, anomaly-loving insurgents.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:17.580
But they kept using one code that even the
Foundation didn’t have any intel on - they

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:21.019
kept asking about the condition of The Sisters.

00:13:21.019 --> 00:13:26.410
Fate has a funny way of sneaking up on you
though, and in time, they would know more

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.650
about the powerful, sadistic, reality-warping
beings known as The Sisters than they could

00:13:31.650 --> 00:13:33.240
have possibly imagined.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:38.070
But what they would eventually learn was not
the kind of data that anyone would ever want

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:39.450
to have.

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:44.300
After intercepting clear lines of communication
from a local Serpent’s Hand cell, triangulating

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:49.029
the location of their compound was child’s
play, and Mobile Task Forces were dispatched

00:13:49.029 --> 00:13:54.010
from Area 37 with orders to neutralize the
potential threat before they could mount an

00:13:54.010 --> 00:13:56.070
attack on a facility.

00:13:56.070 --> 00:14:00.540
Just when the Serpent’s Hands least expected
it, they had heavily-armed Foundation soldiers

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:05.830
kicking down their doors, crashing through
windows, and rappelling down from the ceiling.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:10.420
As expected, the Serpent’s Hand put up a
fight, but thanks to their superior training

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:15.220
and the element of surprise, the Foundation’s
Mobile Task Forces came out on top.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:19.610
They were able to capture fifteen surviving
members of the group for interrogation, as

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:23.380
well as a collection of anomalous objects
being stored by the group.

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:27.820
Among them were a small wooden loom, an enamel
needle, and a glass eye.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:32.829
When the task force obtained these seemingly
mundane items, a haunted-looking Serpent’s

00:14:32.829 --> 00:14:35.080
Hand began laughing wildly.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:40.190
He kept repeating, “You have no idea what
you’re getting yourselves into...”

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.930
Nobody knew just how right this man was.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.020
Not yet, anyway.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:49.840
Congratulating themselves on a job well done,
the Mobile Task Forces hauled their captives

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:55.100
and the new anomalous items back to Area 37
- a heavily isolated Foundation site that

00:14:55.100 --> 00:15:00.600
specializes in the early containment of anomalous
objects for initial observation and study.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:04.830
The objects hadn’t displayed any anomalous
properties in transit - maybe the Serpent’s

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:09.839
Hand was lying and these weren’t dangerous
items at all, or it was actually just a pile

00:15:09.839 --> 00:15:10.839
of junk.

00:15:10.839 --> 00:15:15.950
Either way, they were sent to a Foundation
researcher on site to conduct preliminary

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:16.950
tests.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:21.329
The loom, the needle, and the glass eye were
laid out across the table for observation,

00:15:21.329 --> 00:15:26.350
when suddenly, the attending researcher felt
a dark presence looming behind him.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:31.830
He turned, with sweat beading on his brow,
and saw three humanoid, translucent figures

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.089
floating in the air behind him.

00:15:34.089 --> 00:15:40.520
They would soon become known as SCP - 1765
One, Two, and Three.

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.910
The researcher could feel the power emanating
from these silhouettes - reality seemed to

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:50.200
bend and shimmer around them, the way heat
distorts the air into a mirage.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.970
He could tell right away that they were powerful
reality-warpers.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.540
Even in their brief time communicating with
the researcher, One, Two, and Three displayed

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.790
both intelligence and unique personalities.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:06.010
One was clearly the ringleader - displaying
an articulate command of language.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:12.100
Two displayed a more mischievous side, speaking
with a cockney accent and had a tendency towards

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:13.570
creepy giggling.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:18.240
Three was the least communicative of them
all - preferring to speak in short, simple

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.880
sentences, often consisting of just single
words.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:26.990
Though of course, actions speak far louder
than words - and it didn’t take long for

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:30.470
the Sisters to define themselves with their
actions.

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:35.160
One told the scared and confused researcher
that they’d been observing the SCP Foundation

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:39.480
for quite some time, and that they deeply
admired the Foundation’s adherence to the

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:40.980
scientific method.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:44.850
Of course, the researcher wasn’t so much
“flattered” by the Sister’s statement

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:47.519
as they were “afraid for their life.”

00:16:47.519 --> 00:16:51.810
They tried to call security for backup, but
found that their tongue was withering and

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:55.360
turning into a shrivelled, blackened husk
in their mouth.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.230
The Sisters didn’t like to be interrupted.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:02.500
As the tongueless researcher slowly collapsed
in front of them, the Sisters explained the

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:07.129
purpose of their visit - They wished to assist
the Foundation in their quest for knowledge,

00:17:07.129 --> 00:17:11.649
and, as such, they would conduct a number
of experiments on their behalf.

00:17:11.649 --> 00:17:16.419
They would then happily share the resulting
data with the Foundation to compare notes.

00:17:16.419 --> 00:17:21.959
One expressed optimism, saying that she believed
they were about to embark on a beautiful scientific

00:17:21.959 --> 00:17:22.959
relationship.

00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:26.220
The reality couldn’t be further from the
truth.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:30.879
The Sisters began their work, moving rapidly
around the facility, bending and twisting

00:17:30.879 --> 00:17:32.830
reality wherever they went.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:37.739
They circled Area 37, marking it as separate
from the rest of the world it inhabited.

00:17:37.739 --> 00:17:43.250
Area 37 no longer belonged to planet earth
- it belonged to the Sisters.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:48.649
It was their private experimentation lab,
filled with live and unwilling guinea pigs.

00:17:48.649 --> 00:17:54.379
The Foundation attempted to retake the facility
by force, sending Mobile Task Force Iota-6,

00:17:54.379 --> 00:17:58.989
also known as the Canvas Cats, into the belly
of the beast, but they never returned.

00:17:58.989 --> 00:18:03.559
In addition to changing the fabric of reality
itself, they also altered the physical structure

00:18:03.559 --> 00:18:07.499
of Area 37 to better serve their experimental
designs.

00:18:07.499 --> 00:18:15.480
It was divided into four sections, marked
A, B, C, and D, each with its own unique purpose.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:21.179
Section A - which had formerly been Area 37’s
storekeeping, mess hall, and dormitories - had

00:18:21.179 --> 00:18:24.440
been the least affected by the Sisters’
attacks on reality.

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:29.330
The biggest alterations were the appearance
of two large, metal vats situated in the east

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:34.129
corner of the mess hall, a monitoring station
connected to other sections of Area 37 that

00:18:34.129 --> 00:18:39.389
replaced the storekeeping zones, and an imposing
marble sign hanging above the dormitories

00:18:39.389 --> 00:18:41.869
that reads “CONTROL GROUP.”

00:18:41.869 --> 00:18:46.210
A quick refresher from science class, the
control group in an experiment is the group

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:50.720
that isn’t subjected to the experimental
effect the others are, so they can be used

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.789
as a benchmark to measure against.

00:18:52.789 --> 00:18:57.470
The same was true here - the prisoners in
the control group were the safest of all,

00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:02.600
but they were forced to do something almost
as bad, they had to watch the horrors playing

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.870
out across the rest of the facility.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.729
One of the Sisters would occasionally return
to this section to oversee the feeding of

00:19:08.729 --> 00:19:13.950
the control subjects, and to encourage them
to take part in the observation of their unlucky

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:15.039
peers.

00:19:15.039 --> 00:19:19.989
Section B - which had formerly been Area 37’s
outer grounds and sports facilities - had

00:19:19.989 --> 00:19:24.220
been transformed into the center of a localized
spatial-temporal abnormality.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:29.940
In layman’s terms, this meant that its size,
climate, atmospheric composition, pressure,

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:34.490
and temporal flow were all subject to constant
changes based on the whims of Sister Number

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:38.860
One - who oversaw all the experiments performed
in Section B.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:46.399
For those unfortunate enough to be trapped
in Section B, SCP-1765-1 was their god.

00:19:46.399 --> 00:19:49.059
But she didn’t subject them to her whims
randomly.

00:19:49.059 --> 00:19:54.450
No, in her own words, the purpose of Section
B was to delve into the effects of repetitive

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:58.710
action performed under unusual conditions
on the human psyche.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:03.039
For example, one experiment was set up to
test the physical and mental fortitude of

00:20:03.039 --> 00:20:07.059
a Researcher, a Field Agent, and a sanitation
worker.

00:20:07.059 --> 00:20:11.159
The trio were confined in a sports center
and ordered to measure the length of every

00:20:11.159 --> 00:20:16.249
single pipe and the angle at which each connected
to others with nothing more than a wrench,

00:20:16.249 --> 00:20:19.899
a ruler, a brown paper pad and a ballpoint
pen.

00:20:19.899 --> 00:20:23.320
The task was an arduous one taking over ten
hours.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:27.349
And as soon as the subjects were done, One
restructured the sports center and ordered

00:20:27.349 --> 00:20:29.360
them to perform the task again.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:35.720
The same happened another 459 times before
One finally concluded the experiment, leaving

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:39.649
the subjects with broken bodies and minds
in the aftermath.

00:20:39.649 --> 00:20:43.759
Section C - which had previously been the
facility’s main office block - exhibited

00:20:43.759 --> 00:20:48.740
a similar level of anomalous activity to Section
B, except that it was the domain of the more

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:51.929
sadistic and mischievous Sister Number Two.

00:20:51.929 --> 00:20:56.740
Her main area of scientific interest was studying
group dynamics and interpersonal relationships

00:20:56.740 --> 00:21:01.840
during extreme conditions - very extreme conditions.

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:06.409
For one experiment, the office block had been
transformed into a kind of football stadium,

00:21:06.409 --> 00:21:09.989
with the goal posts removed and replaced by
concrete bunkers.

00:21:09.989 --> 00:21:15.320
The two teams were the captured Serpent Hand
members, and the members of MTF Iota-6, fresh

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:17.730
off their attempt to retake the site.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:22.679
The two groups were forced into a deadly game
with incomprehensible rules - including rising

00:21:22.679 --> 00:21:28.400
platforms and hooded figures throwing fiery
projectiles into the crowd, trying to incinerate

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:29.400
the players.

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:33.940
But victory didn’t lead to safety, as the
winners of the game were crushed to death

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:37.070
with giant metal hammers, just for the fun
of it.

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:42.929
Two didn’t even try to pretend that this
act had a valid scientific justification.

00:21:42.929 --> 00:21:48.239
Section D - which had once been the facility’s
high-risk containment area - was now the strangest

00:21:48.239 --> 00:21:50.559
and most mysterious section of all.

00:21:50.559 --> 00:21:55.879
Under the charge of the equally peculiar and
enigmatic Sister Number Three, this area appeared

00:21:55.879 --> 00:22:00.259
physically unchanged from its state prior
to the arrival of the Sisters.

00:22:00.259 --> 00:22:04.529
Temporally, however, Section D was the most
warped of them all.

00:22:04.529 --> 00:22:09.849
It existed in a kind of temporal bubble, outside
of the rest of our reality’s timeline, giving

00:22:09.849 --> 00:22:14.989
Three a frightening amount of control over
all that went on in her domain outside of

00:22:14.989 --> 00:22:15.989
time.

00:22:15.989 --> 00:22:19.850
There she was performing the most strange
and incomprehensible experiment of all.

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:23.130
The subject was the former Site Director of
Area 37.

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:27.529
He was brought to a table, and asked to choose
between two different flavors of ice cream

00:22:27.529 --> 00:22:29.010
that were presented to him.

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:32.570
Sounds simple enough, so then why is this
the worst of them all?

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:35.190
Because the Site Director is caught in a time
loop.

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:40.529
He’s been choosing between various flavors
of ice cream for over ten thousand hours,

00:22:40.529 --> 00:22:42.429
and he doesn’t even seem to know.

00:22:42.429 --> 00:22:44.979
Three’s only comment on the matter?

00:22:44.979 --> 00:22:46.190
“Delicious.”

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.500
All attempts to liberate the unfortunate inhabitants
of Area 37 have failed miserably.

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:57.090
The Sisters don’t appear to operate on any
form of logic or empathy, and thus, cannot

00:22:57.090 --> 00:22:58.090
be reasoned with.

00:22:58.090 --> 00:23:02.919
With talks having failed and Mobile Task Force
Iota-6’s attempt to retake the site ending

00:23:02.919 --> 00:23:08.110
in disaster, the only solution left was to
create a guarded perimeter around the area,

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:12.500
using technology like the Scranton Reality
Anchor to fight back against any potential

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:14.309
escape by the Sisters.

00:23:14.309 --> 00:23:19.179
The Sisters are potentially so dangerous that
if they ever truly set their minds to leaving,

00:23:19.179 --> 00:23:23.820
it’s considered acceptable to detonate the
facility’s on-site nuclear warhead in hopes

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:25.980
of finally putting a stop to them.

00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:30.309
In the meantime, the Foundation has built
giant external servers for processing the

00:23:30.309 --> 00:23:35.740
vast quantities of research data the Sisters
are constantly sending from their horrifying

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:36.740
experiments.

00:23:36.740 --> 00:23:41.779
Sadly for the inhabitants of Area 37, their
grim fate continues to this day.

00:23:41.779 --> 00:23:46.830
The experiments never stop, and the subjects
of said experiments seem to be condemned to

00:23:46.830 --> 00:23:51.070
the eternal torment of SCP - 1765.

00:23:51.070 --> 00:23:55.960
In a way, their unwilling sacrifice protects
us all - because if ever the Sisters were

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:59.830
interested in performing experiments on a
larger sample size…

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:06.210
Well, all we can do is hope we end up in the
control group.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:12.289
One of the primary aims of the SCP foundation
is to contain the anomalies that they discover.

00:24:12.289 --> 00:24:16.359
Secure, Contain, Protect is their mission
statement, after all.

00:24:16.359 --> 00:24:22.419
However, there are some forces so unknowable
and malevolent that there is no way to truly

00:24:22.419 --> 00:24:24.509
contain them.

00:24:24.509 --> 00:24:28.299
SCP-4205 is one such force.

00:24:28.299 --> 00:24:34.940
Very little is known about SCP-4205, even
compared to other SCPs, many of which are

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:36.919
mysterious by their very nature.

00:24:36.919 --> 00:24:42.570
We do not know what it is, we do not know
what it wants, and we do not have any meaningful

00:24:42.570 --> 00:24:44.239
way to stop it.

00:24:44.239 --> 00:24:49.219
The best that can be done to protect yourself
from it is to implement the few known preventative

00:24:49.219 --> 00:24:54.700
measures available, and pray that it doesn’t
set its sights on you.

00:24:54.700 --> 00:25:00.859
The little information that exists on SCP-4205
was recorded by Wade Dalitz, a former junior

00:25:00.859 --> 00:25:02.679
researcher at the Foundation.

00:25:02.679 --> 00:25:08.501
He wrote the initial report on SCP-4205 on
a computer, Terminal 4, which was linked to

00:25:08.501 --> 00:25:09.501
his brain and consciousness as he wrote.

00:25:09.501 --> 00:25:12.360
Though his work was highly valuable, and provided
many previously unknown insights about the

00:25:12.360 --> 00:25:16.539
nature of the SCP, sadly his knowledge could
not save him.

00:25:16.539 --> 00:25:25.179
The official entry on SCP-4205 was his final
act before his death on December 11, 1992.

00:25:25.179 --> 00:25:29.440
Before we get deeper into that entry, and
Wade’s final day on earth, it’s important

00:25:29.440 --> 00:25:32.399
to understand what SCP-4205 is.

00:25:32.399 --> 00:25:36.419
Or, at least, understand the little we know
about what it is.

00:25:36.419 --> 00:25:43.499
4205 is a Keter class SCP, meaning that it’s
incredibly difficult or complicated to contain.

00:25:43.499 --> 00:25:46.610
It also shows extreme hostility toward all
life.

00:25:46.610 --> 00:25:51.309
It is described as an amber-colored pair of
human-like eyes, with the ability to appear

00:25:51.309 --> 00:25:56.950
spontaneously in windows, mirrors, or any
other glass or glass-like surface.

00:25:56.950 --> 00:26:01.539
One of the reasons so little is known about
these eyes, is that anyone who sees them dies

00:26:01.539 --> 00:26:02.700
within seconds.

00:26:02.700 --> 00:26:03.700
The effect is nearly instantaneous.

00:26:03.700 --> 00:26:10.509
Much like the mythical basilisk, the gaze
of SCP-4205 is deadly and inescapable.

00:26:10.509 --> 00:26:16.379
The eyes only seem to appear to people who
are alone in a room, and never in places where

00:26:16.379 --> 00:26:18.950
there’s more than one person.

00:26:18.950 --> 00:26:24.049
But aside from that, there is no way to predict
where the eyes will appear.

00:26:24.049 --> 00:26:28.389
Since it is unknown if the eyes are part of
a corporeal body, or even present on this

00:26:28.389 --> 00:26:33.630
plane of reality, there is no way to contain
them or stop them from killing.

00:26:33.630 --> 00:26:38.299
This brings us back to that fateful day, December
11, 1992.

00:26:38.299 --> 00:26:43.450
The day that the SCP Foundation would finally
be given some tangible information on the

00:26:43.450 --> 00:26:48.889
mysterious amber eyes, at the cost of one
of their researcher’s lives.

00:26:48.889 --> 00:26:53.389
Wade Dalitz, a young man fresh out of his
university studies, was brought onboard as

00:26:53.389 --> 00:26:57.719
a Junior Researcher by Dr. Mark Forsyth, a
Senior Researcher.

00:26:57.719 --> 00:27:02.320
Dr. Forsyth recruited Wade after giving a
guest lecture at his university and being

00:27:02.320 --> 00:27:07.580
impressed by Wade’s keen observational skills,
thirst for knowledge of the unexplained, and

00:27:07.580 --> 00:27:11.990
determination to understand that which seemed
to defy explanation.

00:27:11.990 --> 00:27:16.299
After Wade graduated, he was recruited by
Dr. Forsyth, and given the position of Junior

00:27:16.299 --> 00:27:18.200
Researcher at the SCP Foundation.

00:27:18.200 --> 00:27:23.740
where he assisted Dr. Forsyth, now a site
supervisor, in his research.

00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:28.320
After several months of working under Dr.
Forsyth with minimal responsibilities, Wade

00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:36.049
was finally given the opportunity to write
his first SCP report... on SCP-4205.

00:27:36.049 --> 00:27:41.349
Following some initial documented appearances
of 4205, Dr. Forsyth approved further research

00:27:41.349 --> 00:27:45.839
into the anomaly, with Wade appointed as the
lead researcher on the subject.

00:27:45.839 --> 00:27:51.549
According to Wade’s entry, he was responsible
for the discovery of SCP-4205 when he spotted

00:27:51.549 --> 00:27:52.860
the anomaly in a window.

00:27:52.860 --> 00:27:57.599
Though later reviews of security footage determined
that he was not the first person to observe

00:27:57.599 --> 00:28:03.130
the eyes, he did claim to be the first to
observe them and live to tell the tale.

00:28:03.130 --> 00:28:07.200
In his writing on the subject, Wade is puzzled
by the fact that he survived his encounter

00:28:07.200 --> 00:28:12.539
with SCP-4205, and wonders what could have
set him apart from the others that fell victim

00:28:12.539 --> 00:28:13.989
to its gaze.

00:28:13.989 --> 00:28:20.570
He found himself frustrated as he documented
SCP-4205, his rough drafts of reports dissolving

00:28:20.570 --> 00:28:23.339
into angry rants about his own incompetence.

00:28:23.339 --> 00:28:29.130
Wade had difficulty adjusting to his new responsibilities,
especially with the added element of his assigned

00:28:29.130 --> 00:28:31.739
subject’s mysterious and volatile nature.

00:28:31.739 --> 00:28:37.889
In between his reports on SCP-4205, its previous
appearances, and its effects on its victims,

00:28:37.889 --> 00:28:42.269
he wrote letters to his father, desperate
for reassurance that he was not messing everything

00:28:42.269 --> 00:28:43.269
up.

00:28:43.269 --> 00:28:45.700
Letters that would sadly go unsent.

00:28:45.700 --> 00:28:51.700
In his coverage of SCP-4205, Wade made note
of a troubling recurring element in each victim’s

00:28:51.700 --> 00:28:52.700
death.

00:28:52.700 --> 00:28:56.049
When medical professionals attempted to revive
the victims, it was always noted that their

00:28:56.049 --> 00:29:00.860
brain activity stopped much more quickly than
in cases of death by natural causes.

00:29:00.860 --> 00:29:05.269
When examined, all aspects of the body aside
from the brain were completely unharmed.

00:29:05.269 --> 00:29:10.710
The brain, however, showed massive nerve damage
in the amygdala, hippocampus, medial temporal

00:29:10.710 --> 00:29:12.039
lobe, and occipital lobe.

00:29:12.039 --> 00:29:16.229
The appearance of this brain trauma has been
compared to the effects of electrical shock

00:29:16.229 --> 00:29:18.210
or a severe head injury.

00:29:18.210 --> 00:29:24.149
In addition to Wade, six other people on record
encountered SCP-4205.

00:29:24.149 --> 00:29:29.059
Every encounter ended the same way, with sudden
brain death and severe nerve damage immediately

00:29:29.059 --> 00:29:32.099
after viewing the eyes in a reflective surface.

00:29:32.099 --> 00:29:36.929
The first encounter occurred on January 5,
1990, when Deputy Liaison Gena viewed the

00:29:36.929 --> 00:29:39.929
eyes in a reflective glass one-way window.

00:29:39.929 --> 00:29:43.460
Security tape reveals that the eyes appeared
in the window eight minutes before the Deputy

00:29:43.460 --> 00:29:45.690
Liaison spotted them.

00:29:45.690 --> 00:29:49.399
As soon as he did, he fell from his chair
and immediately died.

00:29:49.399 --> 00:29:54.039
Though the specifics varied from case to case,
the end result of every encounter was the

00:29:54.039 --> 00:29:58.039
same, with none surviving long enough to relate
what they experienced.

00:29:58.039 --> 00:30:00.450
Every encounter except Wade’s.

00:30:00.450 --> 00:30:08.159
As he continued his documentation of SCP-4205,
Wade’s mental state quickly began to deteriorate.

00:30:08.159 --> 00:30:13.179
The process of his mind coming apart, and
his thoughts giving way to confusion, fear,

00:30:13.179 --> 00:30:17.320
and anger at his own survival, is documented
in his reports on the SCP.

00:30:17.320 --> 00:30:24.349
He agonized over the question of why he was
able to survive gazing into the eyes of SCP-4205

00:30:24.349 --> 00:30:27.039
when so many others had not?

00:30:27.039 --> 00:30:31.999
The question consumed him until he was unable
to eat, sleep, or do anything but obsess over

00:30:31.999 --> 00:30:34.509
the SCP he was tasked with researching.

00:30:34.509 --> 00:30:39.799
As he became more agitated, he began to write
about the eyes appearing to him again.

00:30:39.799 --> 00:30:43.980
On one occurrence, he attempted to touch them,
and described the sensation like touching

00:30:43.980 --> 00:30:48.320
a balloon to your arm after it has been charged
with static electricity.

00:30:48.320 --> 00:30:50.639
He continued to report seeing the eyes.

00:30:50.639 --> 00:30:55.839
The worst was when trying to sleep, during
which he was overtaken by violent sleep paralysis

00:30:55.839 --> 00:30:58.869
and plagued with visions of the amber eyes.

00:30:58.869 --> 00:31:02.409
The only comfort Wade seemed to find was in
memories of his loved ones.

00:31:02.409 --> 00:31:07.269
He wrote about his mother and his father,
even as their memories grew foggier to him.

00:31:07.269 --> 00:31:11.869
He also mentioned a man by the name of Theodore
Quale, who he claimed was a researcher at

00:31:11.869 --> 00:31:13.039
the Foundation.

00:31:13.039 --> 00:31:16.679
Later fact checking determined that this was
not the case, and that Quale must have been

00:31:16.679 --> 00:31:18.149
someone from Wade’s past.

00:31:18.149 --> 00:31:23.549
He wrote about Quale wistfully, mournfully,
with words of love and loss, tormented by

00:31:23.549 --> 00:31:28.759
the sense that he was losing his grip on reality
and everything he once held dear.

00:31:28.759 --> 00:31:33.769
As Wade descended deeper into a hell inside
his own mind, he continued to mull over the

00:31:33.769 --> 00:31:36.850
questions of SCP-4205.

00:31:36.850 --> 00:31:38.580
Was there more to it than what was visible?

00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:40.570
Did it have a body?

00:31:40.570 --> 00:31:42.559
Why had he survived his encounter with it?

00:31:42.559 --> 00:31:44.250
And what did it want from him?

00:31:44.250 --> 00:31:48.119
He decided that those who had perished immediately
were the lucky ones.

00:31:48.119 --> 00:31:51.700
They had escaped the torture that had overtaken
his life.

00:31:51.700 --> 00:31:56.029
The eyes were everywhere now, watching him
even as he attempted to unlock their secrets

00:31:56.029 --> 00:31:57.469
on a Foundation computer.

00:31:57.469 --> 00:32:02.029
He spoke to the eyes at one point, but refused
to write down what they had said to him.

00:32:02.029 --> 00:32:07.840
His last entry, his last thought, was a plea
for Theodore Quale’s embrace.

00:32:07.840 --> 00:32:13.050
There is no more written about the research,
or about the eyes, only a simple, desperate

00:32:13.050 --> 00:32:16.179
need for a comfort that is long lost.

00:32:16.179 --> 00:32:19.809
Now is the part of our story where terror
meets tragedy.

00:32:19.809 --> 00:32:24.639
Contrary to what Wade thought, and what was
recorded in his final computer entries, he

00:32:24.639 --> 00:32:28.209
did not survive his brief brush with SCP-4205.

00:32:28.209 --> 00:32:32.909
The truth is that he spotted the amber eyes
in the glass above his terminal monitor while

00:32:32.909 --> 00:32:35.919
recording the entry, and died seconds later.

00:32:35.919 --> 00:32:41.759
Though his death was swift, it felt agonizingly
slow, as revealed by his descent into panic

00:32:41.759 --> 00:32:44.389
and paranoia recorded in his writings.

00:32:44.389 --> 00:32:49.129
The entries recorded as a result of the connection
Wade and the computer, his physical contact

00:32:49.129 --> 00:32:55.429
with it at the moment of exposure to SCP-4205’s
anomalous effects allowing the terminal to

00:32:55.429 --> 00:33:00.970
archive his final thoughts before he succumbed
to the deadly nature of the eyes.

00:33:00.970 --> 00:33:06.039
The entries were never physically typed, but
rather jumped from his dying mind into the

00:33:06.039 --> 00:33:07.039
mainframe.

00:33:07.039 --> 00:33:13.379
His entries, the echoes of a dying mind, offer
a glimpse into the way that SCP-4205 kills

00:33:13.379 --> 00:33:14.740
its victims.

00:33:14.740 --> 00:33:19.450
In the seconds leading up to death, the amber
eyes fast-forward a person’s mind, feeding

00:33:19.450 --> 00:33:24.009
on the electrical impulses that it gives off
as it speeds through what seem to be days

00:33:24.009 --> 00:33:26.850
of fear and of a loosening grip on reality.

00:33:26.850 --> 00:33:31.690
The death may be swift, but the suffering
is long.

00:33:31.690 --> 00:33:36.869
Wade left the foundation with a digital fingerprint,
an echo of the person he was at his core in

00:33:36.869 --> 00:33:41.959
addition to his experiences with SCP-4205
itself.

00:33:41.959 --> 00:33:46.769
Wade spent his final moments terrified for
his life, dreaming of a father that he missed

00:33:46.769 --> 00:33:50.029
and a long-lost love from his college days.

00:33:50.029 --> 00:33:53.009
His sacrifice must not be forgotten.

00:33:53.009 --> 00:33:59.269
Because no one ever survives an encounter
with SCP-4205, his documented final moments

00:33:59.269 --> 00:34:02.409
are the only first-hand account in existence.

00:34:02.409 --> 00:34:06.539
Junior Researcher Wade Dalitz gave us a gift
in death.

00:34:06.539 --> 00:34:12.609
He allowed the SCP Foundation a glimpse into
the true horror of the amber eyes, and a reminder

00:34:12.609 --> 00:34:15.419
of what they are capable of stealing from
us.

00:34:15.419 --> 00:34:22.260
So be careful of windows, mirrors, screens,
and all reflective surfaces.

00:34:22.260 --> 00:34:29.369
When you look into them, you never know what
you might see looking back.

00:34:29.369 --> 00:34:35.389
It goes without saying that the SCP Foundation
archives are filled with some terrifying monsters.

00:34:35.389 --> 00:34:40.639
Even the deadliest creatures can, in theory,
be defeated, or at least soundly avoided.

00:34:40.639 --> 00:34:45.629
After all, they’re just flesh and blood
- or in some cases, metal or concrete.

00:34:45.629 --> 00:34:48.710
But what if reality as you know it one day
just…broke.

00:34:48.710 --> 00:34:54.240
Or worse, you were transported to a reality
so frightening and alien to our own that death

00:34:54.240 --> 00:34:58.829
seemed like the only escape – but you couldn’t
even give yourself that.

00:34:58.829 --> 00:35:05.550
This brings us to today’s topic – the
terrifying alternate reality of SCP – 3001.

00:35:05.550 --> 00:35:10.769
The Foundation is no stranger to freaky alternate
dimensions, but what was experienced by joint-lead

00:35:10.769 --> 00:35:16.390
researcher Dr. Robert Scranton at Site 120
is a truly unique nightmare.

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:22.160
Co-managed by his wife, Dr. Anna Lang, Site
120 is a facility largely designed for research

00:35:22.160 --> 00:35:29.200
into SCPs with dangerous reality-warping capabilities
in order to mitigate future containment breaches.

00:35:29.200 --> 00:35:34.019
Reality warpers are among some of the more
perplexing and dangerous SCPs, from the pocket

00:35:34.019 --> 00:35:40.710
dimension-creating SCP – 106 to the SCP-creating
Doctor Wondertainment, and everything in between.

00:35:40.710 --> 00:35:45.279
Scranton and Lang’s goal to further study
such entities was an admirable one, if a little

00:35:45.279 --> 00:35:50.710
over-ambitious, and on January 2nd, 2000,
during the testing of a new technology created

00:35:50.710 --> 00:35:55.819
by the Foundation’s leading power couple,
disaster finally struck.

00:35:55.819 --> 00:35:59.630
Scranton and Lang had already been the brains
behind one of the Foundation’s most valuable

00:35:59.630 --> 00:36:05.400
tools in the fight against reality-bending
SCPs: The Scranton Reality Anchors.

00:36:05.400 --> 00:36:10.230
Their follow up, the Lang-Scranton Stabilizer
– or LSS – likely would have been an even

00:36:10.230 --> 00:36:14.779
more advanced variant of their earlier invention
and should have been a huge success for the

00:36:14.779 --> 00:36:15.779
team.

00:36:15.779 --> 00:36:17.619
But things didn’t turn out that way…

00:36:17.619 --> 00:36:22.069
Dr. Scranton and several other researchers
were gathered in Reality Lab A performing

00:36:22.069 --> 00:36:24.630
routine tests on the LSS prototypes.

00:36:24.630 --> 00:36:29.859
While other technicians ran diagnostics tests,
Scranton stood at the control panel, the blinking

00:36:29.859 --> 00:36:34.019
red light above the console confirming that
everything was going according to plan.

00:36:34.019 --> 00:36:37.599
But as anyone who’s fallen victim to one
of the Foundation’s many anomalies will

00:36:37.599 --> 00:36:42.289
tell you, just because you’ve done everything
correctly doesn’t mean you’re safe.

00:36:42.289 --> 00:36:46.170
Scranton began operating the machine, not
knowing that something was rumbling up towards

00:36:46.170 --> 00:36:47.490
him from below.

00:36:47.490 --> 00:36:53.619
Without warning, a sudden, unexpected burst
of seismic activity rocked the entire base.

00:36:53.619 --> 00:36:57.750
Researchers grabbed onto whatever was closest
as the world shook around them.

00:36:57.750 --> 00:37:02.380
In his panic, Dr. Scranton clung to the LSS
control panel as the seismic blast fried the

00:37:02.380 --> 00:37:05.870
circuits and kicked it into overdrive.

00:37:05.870 --> 00:37:10.150
There was a blast of magnificent, blinding
light, and when the rumbling stopped not only

00:37:10.150 --> 00:37:14.280
was the doctor gone, he had been erased from
reality as we know it.

00:37:14.280 --> 00:37:18.619
The earthquake had caused a deadly malfunction
in the machine meant to stabilize reality,

00:37:18.619 --> 00:37:23.940
and instead tore a rift in it, dragging the
unfortunate doctor and the control panel into

00:37:23.940 --> 00:37:25.490
oblivion.

00:37:25.490 --> 00:37:30.910
His wife, Dr. Lang, and the many researchers
who idolized him were devastated by his unexpected

00:37:30.910 --> 00:37:34.369
demise at the hand of what should have been
his crowning achievement.

00:37:34.369 --> 00:37:38.860
The one silver lining was that this reality-ripping
event had almost definitely eliminated the

00:37:38.860 --> 00:37:41.130
doctor quickly and painlessly.

00:37:41.130 --> 00:37:44.840
As far as The Foundation and his loved ones
were concerned, Scranton’s death had been

00:37:44.840 --> 00:37:50.160
immediate and complete – a luxury afforded
to few Foundation employees who die anomalous

00:37:50.160 --> 00:37:51.160
deaths.

00:37:51.160 --> 00:37:57.410
But sadly that isn’t how Dr. Scranton’s
story – or the story of SCP – 3001 – ends.

00:37:57.410 --> 00:37:59.760
No, this is where it all begins.

00:37:59.760 --> 00:38:02.410
How do we know all this?

00:38:02.410 --> 00:38:06.320
In the hellish new place where Scranton had
been transported, the control panel from the

00:38:06.320 --> 00:38:11.270
LSS that he’d been clinging to for dear
life had been transported with him, and continued

00:38:11.270 --> 00:38:14.750
to record audio data from this anomalous location.

00:38:14.750 --> 00:38:18.340
Not that Dr. Scranton realized it, not at
first, anyway.

00:38:18.340 --> 00:38:22.799
As far as he knew, he’d suddenly been transported
into a pitch-black location.

00:38:22.799 --> 00:38:26.240
No sights, no sounds, no scents.

00:38:26.240 --> 00:38:27.240
True nothingness.

00:38:27.240 --> 00:38:30.220
At first, the doctor was confused.

00:38:30.220 --> 00:38:35.579
One second, he was testing out his new technology,
and the next he was quite literally nowhere.

00:38:35.579 --> 00:38:39.970
In spite of his current situation, the doctor
was still an intelligent and rational man.

00:38:39.970 --> 00:38:44.049
He took a moment to compose himself, hoping
that in time his eyes would adjust to the

00:38:44.049 --> 00:38:45.680
new darkness around him.

00:38:45.680 --> 00:38:50.700
But that moment never came: The darkness remained
perfectly absolute.

00:38:50.700 --> 00:38:55.670
Much like the darkness in another reality-defying
SCP, the deadly endless staircase known as

00:38:55.670 --> 00:39:00.620
SCP – 087, the dark seemed thick, almost
like you could touch it.

00:39:00.620 --> 00:39:04.890
The doctor, not wanting to give himself to
despair and die in this impossible place,

00:39:04.890 --> 00:39:08.369
and with no other options seemingly available,
began walking.

00:39:08.369 --> 00:39:11.740
Either he’d find his way out, or the Foundation
would find him.

00:39:11.740 --> 00:39:13.559
No need to panic.

00:39:13.559 --> 00:39:17.410
It may have altered the doctor’s temperament
if he knew that the Foundation already assumed

00:39:17.410 --> 00:39:21.250
he was dead, and that no search party was
going to come looking for him.

00:39:21.250 --> 00:39:25.930
Still, logic dictates that if a person walks
for long enough, they’re bound to find something.

00:39:25.930 --> 00:39:31.290
The problem Scranton was about to face was
that SCP – 3001 doesn’t run by any kind

00:39:31.290 --> 00:39:33.309
of conventional logic.

00:39:33.309 --> 00:39:38.539
He walked and walked and walked, but he didn’t
seem to get any nearer to or farther from

00:39:38.539 --> 00:39:41.010
anything but how could even know?

00:39:41.010 --> 00:39:46.329
After all, in total darkness, there aren’t
any landmarks to assist in navigation.

00:39:46.329 --> 00:39:51.680
The doctor walked and paced and screamed for
days on end, but he made no progress.

00:39:51.680 --> 00:39:54.100
He was alone in an empty world.

00:39:54.100 --> 00:40:00.030
He had no choice though, so he kept walking,
and walking, and walking.

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:01.930
For eleven days.

00:40:01.930 --> 00:40:05.440
During that time, he felt his hunger and thirst
grow.

00:40:05.440 --> 00:40:10.590
He was in terrible pain from a mix of starvation
and dehydration, but the release of death

00:40:10.590 --> 00:40:12.369
didn’t seem to come for him.

00:40:12.369 --> 00:40:16.390
He was going to have to learn the rules of
this new place the hard way, and it grimly

00:40:16.390 --> 00:40:21.079
dawned on Dr. Scranton that dying in this
place might not even be the worst possible

00:40:21.079 --> 00:40:22.079
outcome.

00:40:22.079 --> 00:40:26.470
He paced and repeated facts to himself, hoping
to ground himself in the moment and avoid

00:40:26.470 --> 00:40:28.369
the panic that could so easily set in.

00:40:28.369 --> 00:40:30.579
“Name, Robert Scranton.

00:40:30.579 --> 00:40:32.039
Age, 39.

00:40:32.039 --> 00:40:34.329
Birthday, September 19, 1961.

00:40:34.329 --> 00:40:35.940
Favorite color, blue.

00:40:35.940 --> 00:40:38.809
Favorite song, "Living on a Prayer."

00:40:38.809 --> 00:40:39.940
Wife…

00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:41.079
Anna…”

00:40:41.079 --> 00:40:46.049
Little by little, the words seemed to turn
to nonsense in his mouth as the terror grew.

00:40:46.049 --> 00:40:50.829
Just as he felt like he was about to lose
his mind, he noticed something - a small oasis

00:40:50.829 --> 00:40:58.049
in the endless darkness of SCP – 3001: The
glowing red light of the LSS control panel.

00:40:58.049 --> 00:40:59.420
Where had it come from?

00:40:59.420 --> 00:41:01.230
And how was it still recording?

00:41:01.230 --> 00:41:05.920
The doctor had no idea, but he was grateful
for any kind of familiarity in the strange

00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:07.579
darkness around him.

00:41:07.579 --> 00:41:11.250
Perhaps the LSS could be the key to saving
him, or at least figuring out what on earth

00:41:11.250 --> 00:41:12.980
was going on here?

00:41:12.980 --> 00:41:17.760
Whatever the case, there was no denying that
having the panel here was better than nothing.

00:41:17.760 --> 00:41:22.849
At least, when it was found… if it was ever
found, then people would know what had happened

00:41:22.849 --> 00:41:23.849
to him.

00:41:23.849 --> 00:41:29.339
As the days passed and he continued to mysteriously
survive, Dr Scranton deduced that one didn’t

00:41:29.339 --> 00:41:33.809
need food or water to survive continually
in SCP – 3001.

00:41:33.809 --> 00:41:37.619
The location had an anomalous effect on its
inhabitants.

00:41:37.619 --> 00:41:41.940
As the days passed and turned to weeks of
wandering in the darkness, Dr. Scranton further

00:41:41.940 --> 00:41:46.420
deduced that he was no longer in his home
dimension – this was an entirely separate

00:41:46.420 --> 00:41:52.330
pocket dimension, much like the one possessed
by SCP – 106, but featureless.

00:41:52.330 --> 00:41:55.690
A perfect, self-contained void.

00:41:55.690 --> 00:42:00.170
Now dimly illuminated by the red light of
the panel, Dr. Scranton explored further into

00:42:00.170 --> 00:42:01.470
the void around him.

00:42:01.470 --> 00:42:06.660
He travelled for months on end, the pain of
his deficiencies growing by the day, but found

00:42:06.660 --> 00:42:08.760
he was getting nowhere.

00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:13.131
All things considered, he wasn’t even sure
he was moving, or whether reality and the

00:42:13.131 --> 00:42:16.250
darkness was swirling around him like a thick
liquid.

00:42:16.250 --> 00:42:21.670
Rather than walking on a single flat surface,
he was moving in all directions across a three-dimensional

00:42:21.670 --> 00:42:22.670
plane.

00:42:22.670 --> 00:42:26.349
The space-time continuum appeared to be entirely
broken here, where movement is more defined

00:42:26.349 --> 00:42:30.480
by the conscious intention to move than any
real geographical repositioning.

00:42:30.480 --> 00:42:36.309
Dr. Scranton knew that this place broke every
single one of Kejel's Laws of Reality Parameters,

00:42:36.309 --> 00:42:40.990
and from his years working with a plethora
of reality warpers in Site 120, he had a theory

00:42:40.990 --> 00:42:47.160
for why this pocket dimension was so strange:
It had an extraordinarily weak Hume field.

00:42:47.160 --> 00:42:51.000
Before we get back to Dr. Scranton’s semi-living
nightmare, we need a quick primer on Hume

00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:53.960
theory, and why having a weak Hume field is
such a problem.

00:42:53.960 --> 00:42:58.220
A Hume is a unit of measurement for the strength
and amount of reality in a given location

00:42:58.220 --> 00:42:59.220
or being.

00:42:59.220 --> 00:43:04.980
In an area with an incredibly low Hume field
relative to our world, such as SCP – 3001,

00:43:04.980 --> 00:43:08.200
universe breaches and anomalous incidences
rise significantly.

00:43:08.200 --> 00:43:12.759
At the time of his being trapped there, SCP
– 3001 had the lowest number of Humes in

00:43:12.759 --> 00:43:17.069
any recorded environment, making it a phenomenally
anomalous zone.

00:43:17.069 --> 00:43:21.329
It was for this reason that starvation and
dehydration never took hold of him despite

00:43:21.329 --> 00:43:25.619
causing him great pain, and the worst by far
was yet to come.

00:43:25.619 --> 00:43:29.450
Dr. Scranton wasn’t trapped in this dimension
for weeks or even months.

00:43:29.450 --> 00:43:31.839
He was trapped in the darkness for years.

00:43:31.839 --> 00:43:35.000
And it took a nightmarish toll on his body
and mind.

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:39.970
The small flashing red light on his LSS control
panel became his only friend and as the years

00:43:39.970 --> 00:43:44.900
drew on, he would hold entire conversations
with his only source of illumination.

00:43:44.900 --> 00:43:48.690
He knew that his days were numbered – if
he didn’t escape dimension within around

00:43:48.690 --> 00:43:53.970
three years, the Hume field would diffuse
further, and he would be left in a truly horrific

00:43:53.970 --> 00:43:54.970
state.

00:43:54.970 --> 00:43:58.470
But based on how little headway he’d made
in the time he’d been there, he didn’t

00:43:58.470 --> 00:43:59.570
feel optimistic.

00:43:59.570 --> 00:44:03.509
He kept speaking into the recorder, if only
to break the silence and prevent him from

00:44:03.509 --> 00:44:05.730
going completely insane.

00:44:05.730 --> 00:44:08.950
But even that would only hold it off for so
long.

00:44:08.950 --> 00:44:13.200
Alone and talking to himself endlessly in
the darkness, Dr. Scranton could feel his

00:44:13.200 --> 00:44:18.400
mind slipping as the confines of the pocket
dimension constricted and his body began to

00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:19.400
change.

00:44:19.400 --> 00:44:23.730
The low Hume field slowly diffused his physical
matter, destroying the physical integrity

00:44:23.730 --> 00:44:27.920
of his body but never being merciful enough
to actually let him die.

00:44:27.920 --> 00:44:32.250
In his haunting audio logs, the doctor described
his hands as diffusing and thinning out like

00:44:32.250 --> 00:44:33.750
spider webs.

00:44:33.750 --> 00:44:39.380
Over time, there was less and less of him,
and what was left wasn’t entirely human.

00:44:39.380 --> 00:44:44.660
As Scranton’s Hume level lowered to equalize
with that of SCP – 3001, the lines between

00:44:44.660 --> 00:44:49.800
his body and the LSS control console began
to blur in a twisted marriage of warped flesh

00:44:49.800 --> 00:44:51.029
and machine.

00:44:51.029 --> 00:44:54.240
The Lang-Scranton Stabilizer was anything
but stable.

00:44:54.240 --> 00:44:58.809
Before his mind and body became something
else entirely, the doctor still had the presence

00:44:58.809 --> 00:45:03.510
of mind to finally realize how he’d come
to be in this terrible place.

00:45:03.510 --> 00:45:09.549
The LSS had opened a wormhole known as a Class-C
“Broken Entry” into a paradoxical pocket

00:45:09.549 --> 00:45:12.759
dimension between layers of reality, and taken
him through it.

00:45:12.759 --> 00:45:17.380
He’d slipped through a crack in reality
into absolute darkness, and now he was stuck

00:45:17.380 --> 00:45:19.930
with a fate far worse than death.

00:45:19.930 --> 00:45:21.500
How do we know any of this?

00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:25.349
Much like the event in the first place, it’s
a total accident.

00:45:25.349 --> 00:45:29.610
Testing superior reality-bending technology
almost six years after the disappearance caused

00:45:29.610 --> 00:45:34.549
the sudden return of the missing LSS to Site
120’s Reality Labs.

00:45:34.549 --> 00:45:38.330
The only trace of Dr. Scranton that it brought
back with it was the blood and viscera that

00:45:38.330 --> 00:45:43.369
coated the console, much to the abject horror
of his still grieving wife, Dr. Anna Lang.

00:45:43.369 --> 00:45:47.809
To this day, Dr. Scranton, formerly one of
the Foundation’s brightest minds, remains

00:45:47.809 --> 00:45:51.319
trapped in the nightmare of SCP – 3001.

00:45:51.319 --> 00:45:55.319
His current condition whether the doctor is
still alive after twenty years of being warped

00:45:55.319 --> 00:46:00.049
by the low Hume field of 3001’s darkened
confines is still unknown.

00:46:00.049 --> 00:46:04.881
But, for the doctor’s own sake, we hope
he’s been dead for quite some time, because

00:46:04.881 --> 00:46:09.089
few things on earth are as horrifying as the
alternative…

00:46:09.089 --> 00:46:14.769
It’s 3:00 AM, and the facility is quiet.

00:46:14.769 --> 00:46:17.299
Office workers and administrators roam the
halls.

00:46:17.299 --> 00:46:22.119
Security Officers stand at their posts, clad
in advanced tactical armour and carrying standard-issue

00:46:22.119 --> 00:46:23.270
M4 Carbines.

00:46:23.270 --> 00:46:27.089
Three Foundation employees sit at flickering
monitors, watching a live feed of footage

00:46:27.089 --> 00:46:32.670
from the containment cell of the infamous
SCP-106, or as it’s referred to by staff,

00:46:32.670 --> 00:46:33.700
The Old Man.

00:46:33.700 --> 00:46:38.270
No Foundation personnel are permitted to travel
within sixty feet of the cell for security

00:46:38.270 --> 00:46:42.210
reasons, and nobody is permitted to physically
interact with the anomaly without the approval

00:46:42.210 --> 00:46:44.440
of two-thirds of O5-Command.

00:46:44.440 --> 00:46:49.090
The observer’s eyes itch and sting from
the hours of unending blue-light exposure,

00:46:49.090 --> 00:46:50.359
but they can’t look away.

00:46:50.359 --> 00:46:54.740
The Old Man is crafty – he may have the
insatiable bloodlust of a hungry great white

00:46:54.740 --> 00:46:56.060
shark, but he’s not mindless.

00:46:56.060 --> 00:47:00.880
He’s a calculating predator, more sadistic
than the worst human serial killer, and he’s

00:47:00.880 --> 00:47:03.000
always searching for the next opportunity.

00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:06.799
According to Foundation records, he’s been
active since at least World War II, and it

00:47:06.799 --> 00:47:10.480
is estimated that he has hundreds if not thousands
of victims to his name.

00:47:10.480 --> 00:47:15.319
And many of those made the simple, but extremely
foolish mistake of underestimating him.

00:47:15.319 --> 00:47:20.049
After all, it only takes a few seconds of
inattentiveness, the briefest moment of distraction,

00:47:20.049 --> 00:47:21.700
to give him the window he needs.

00:47:21.700 --> 00:47:23.109
To do what, you ask?

00:47:23.109 --> 00:47:26.440
Oh, don’t worry, you’ll find out – just
like they did.

00:47:26.440 --> 00:47:31.400
The Old Man has his nickname for a reason
– most of the time, he really does look

00:47:31.400 --> 00:47:32.970
like exactly that - an old man.

00:47:32.970 --> 00:47:38.160
Or more specifically, an Old Man’s decaying
corpse, his body covered in rotten, dark greyish-black

00:47:38.160 --> 00:47:40.509
flesh that looks like putrid meat.

00:47:40.509 --> 00:47:44.509
Though the creature has been observed being
able to change shape, the rot seems to run

00:47:44.509 --> 00:47:47.200
too deep for the Old Man to ever hide it.

00:47:47.200 --> 00:47:51.740
Foundation employees that have observed SCP-106
for extended periods of time have reported

00:47:51.740 --> 00:47:56.589
seeing it assume the form of grinning, decayed
children, and women whose rotted flesh barely

00:47:56.589 --> 00:47:58.569
hangs on to their creaking bones.

00:47:58.569 --> 00:48:02.859
Just seeing the images through a video feed
is enough to cause a lifetime of insomnia

00:48:02.859 --> 00:48:04.359
and other sleeping issues.

00:48:04.359 --> 00:48:07.880
Still, they have a job to do, and the cameras
remain fixed on the Old Man.

00:48:07.880 --> 00:48:11.990
He’s been completely motionless for three
months, just sitting there, like a Buddhist

00:48:11.990 --> 00:48:13.420
monk in deep meditation.

00:48:13.420 --> 00:48:17.460
A novice might see this period of inactivity
as a cause for celebration, but those with

00:48:17.460 --> 00:48:21.349
experience know that this is merely the calm
before the storm.

00:48:21.349 --> 00:48:25.140
SCP–106 can remain in a dormant state for
months at a time.

00:48:25.140 --> 00:48:29.020
Described by Foundation scientists as a “lulling
state,” it is believed that The Old Man

00:48:29.020 --> 00:48:33.509
is simply waiting for its captors to get soft,
make a mistake, or simply have a momentary

00:48:33.509 --> 00:48:36.930
lapse in concentration, which is all it needs
to make its move.

00:48:36.930 --> 00:48:40.809
It had happened so many times before, and
it was about to happen again.

00:48:40.809 --> 00:48:45.410
One of the observers must have felt an overwhelming
wave of anxiety when he saw the creature ever

00:48:45.410 --> 00:48:47.579
so slightly twitch.

00:48:47.579 --> 00:48:49.769
Just a tiny quiver in the shoulder muscles.

00:48:49.769 --> 00:48:53.859
But that was enough to tell the observer that
their day had just taken a terrifying turn.

00:48:53.859 --> 00:48:58.079
He grabbed the emergency phone fixed to his
desk and practically screamed into the receiver

00:48:58.079 --> 00:49:01.760
that 106 is moving, that they needed a tactical
team stat.

00:49:01.760 --> 00:49:02.760
But it was already too late.

00:49:02.760 --> 00:49:07.130
He and the two other observers stared into
the monitors with their mouths agape, as a

00:49:07.130 --> 00:49:11.210
gooey, rust-like substance began to pool around
the creature on the floor of its cell.

00:49:11.210 --> 00:49:13.799
Slowly, the creature craned its withered neck
around.

00:49:13.799 --> 00:49:17.559
Its face was fixed into a broad, yellow-toothed,
lipless grin.

00:49:17.559 --> 00:49:21.119
Its eyes had the kind of dull, flat malice
of an underwater predator.

00:49:21.119 --> 00:49:23.480
It looked directly into the camera.

00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:24.480
Directly at them.

00:49:24.480 --> 00:49:25.480
And smiled.

00:49:25.480 --> 00:49:27.319
The observers know this was bad.

00:49:27.319 --> 00:49:28.950
Really, really bad.

00:49:28.950 --> 00:49:33.780
With what they could have sworn was a little
nod, the Old Man began sinking into the rusty

00:49:33.780 --> 00:49:37.910
puddle it’d made on the ground beneath it,
until it had disappeared entirely.

00:49:37.910 --> 00:49:42.450
SCP–106 is capable of phasing through any
solid surface with ease, making it one of

00:49:42.450 --> 00:49:47.130
the hardest entities to reliably contain,
and earning it a spot on the dreaded “Keter”

00:49:47.130 --> 00:49:51.440
class – reserved for the anomalies that
are a complete nightmare to keep locked up.

00:49:51.440 --> 00:49:54.950
Through years of costly research and deadly
trial and error, the Foundation would later

00:49:54.950 --> 00:49:57.509
devise ways of at least slowing the creature
down.

00:49:57.509 --> 00:50:02.009
It’s shown to have an aversion to lead,
highly complex or random physical structures,

00:50:02.009 --> 00:50:03.769
and intense bright light.

00:50:03.769 --> 00:50:07.930
None of these cause harm to the creature – as
far as we know, literally nothing can – but

00:50:07.930 --> 00:50:13.470
they’ll at least buy you some precious extra
seconds with which to at least try and escape,

00:50:13.470 --> 00:50:15.730
seconds the three observers didn’t have.

00:50:15.730 --> 00:50:19.450
One of them grabbed the emergency line again
and barked into it that they had lost visual

00:50:19.450 --> 00:50:20.640
on the anomaly.

00:50:20.640 --> 00:50:25.390
Just then the observers heard a faint crackling
sound behind them, and the hissing of a chemical

00:50:25.390 --> 00:50:26.390
burn.

00:50:26.390 --> 00:50:30.300
They turned in horror to see a huge, rusty
burnmark expanding across the wall, right

00:50:30.300 --> 00:50:33.079
next to the door – which was their only
escape route.

00:50:33.079 --> 00:50:37.819
They backed as far away from the door as they
could as a rotten hand began reaching out

00:50:37.819 --> 00:50:43.650
of the mass of corrosive, black sludge, followed
by the grinning face of SCP–106, ready to

00:50:43.650 --> 00:50:44.920
have some fun.

00:50:44.920 --> 00:50:48.999
Meanwhile, two heavily-armed Security Officers
– Agents Goodwin and Resnick – came charging

00:50:48.999 --> 00:50:51.069
down the corridor towards the observation
rooms.

00:50:51.069 --> 00:50:55.819
It’d become a bleak slogan during SCP–106
escape attempts that all you need to do is

00:50:55.819 --> 00:50:56.819
“follow the screams.”

00:50:56.819 --> 00:51:00.549
And that motto was proven true that night,
because awful things were happening to the

00:51:00.549 --> 00:51:03.609
observation personnel, they were certainly
screaming about it.

00:51:03.609 --> 00:51:07.650
Of course, even with top-of-the-line firearms,
there was little they could do to harm the

00:51:07.650 --> 00:51:09.150
rampaging Old Man.

00:51:09.150 --> 00:51:11.690
He seemed immune to all forms of physical
damage.

00:51:11.690 --> 00:51:15.549
All they could hope to do was keep the thing
distracted until the scientists and containment

00:51:15.549 --> 00:51:20.089
specialists finished the preparations to lure
him back into his containment cell.

00:51:20.089 --> 00:51:22.920
Goodwin surged forward while Resnick covered
his six.

00:51:22.920 --> 00:51:27.920
Vigilance was key, as – unlike a standard
human combatant – SCP–106 could attack

00:51:27.920 --> 00:51:31.150
from literally any angle including above or
below.

00:51:31.150 --> 00:51:34.730
Physical obstacles were irrelevant to him
and no cover was safe.

00:51:34.730 --> 00:51:38.630
The hardened security officers could see the
burnmark on the wall of the observation room

00:51:38.630 --> 00:51:39.970
as they approached.

00:51:39.970 --> 00:51:45.059
SCP–106 was perpetually coated in a thick,
black mucus with powerful corrosive properties

00:51:45.059 --> 00:51:48.319
that left any surfaces it touched permanently
marred.

00:51:48.319 --> 00:51:52.490
Foundation Scientists speculated that this
mucus served as a kind of pre-digestive substance

00:51:52.490 --> 00:51:57.271
that tenderizes meat and bone alike, but to
what purpose this serves is a mystery as the

00:51:57.271 --> 00:51:59.279
Old Man has never been observed eating.

00:51:59.279 --> 00:52:02.609
It’s postulated that the only purpose is
causing additional pain.

00:52:02.609 --> 00:52:07.339
Goodwin and Resnick knew to treat this hissing
sludge as a potential threat, as the corrosive

00:52:07.339 --> 00:52:11.559
properties would remain active for as much
as six hours before finally fizzling out.

00:52:11.559 --> 00:52:16.200
The two officers shared a quiet nod, before
Goodwin breached the observation room door

00:52:16.200 --> 00:52:17.380
with a hard kick.

00:52:17.380 --> 00:52:20.150
The two of them surged inside, guns at the
ready.

00:52:20.150 --> 00:52:24.240
In their time working at the Foundation, they’d
seen some truly horrific sights.

00:52:24.240 --> 00:52:29.130
From the mutilation of D-Class Personnel – typically
death row prison inmates brought in for use

00:52:29.130 --> 00:52:33.369
as SCP guinea pigs – to the violence and
mayhem of a containment breach.

00:52:33.369 --> 00:52:36.940
But there was nothing in their past that would
ever make the horrifying sight they saw in

00:52:36.940 --> 00:52:39.809
the observation room that night feel “normal.”

00:52:39.809 --> 00:52:41.740
All three observers were dead.

00:52:41.740 --> 00:52:46.230
Almost nothing remained of two of them, and
the third, while still intact, no longer looked

00:52:46.230 --> 00:52:47.230
human.

00:52:47.230 --> 00:52:50.460
He looked like he’d somehow been dead a
hundred years in the brief period that the

00:52:50.460 --> 00:52:51.490
Old Man had been free.

00:52:51.490 --> 00:52:56.660
His skin was grey and completely dried out,
and his mouth was locked into a perpetual

00:52:56.660 --> 00:52:57.660
scream.

00:52:57.660 --> 00:52:59.819
It was a massacre, but there was no sign of
the Old Man.

00:52:59.819 --> 00:53:03.960
Goodwin grabbed his radio, and whispered “This
is Goodwin in observation room six.

00:53:03.960 --> 00:53:04.960
Requesting immediate back up.

00:53:04.960 --> 00:53:08.890
We have no idea where this thing—”
But his sentence was cut off by a sudden scream

00:53:08.890 --> 00:53:10.190
from Agent Resnick.

00:53:10.190 --> 00:53:14.240
SCP Foundation security officers are as tough
as nails – the best of the best, you might

00:53:14.240 --> 00:53:19.130
say, recruited from the top military organizations
in the world – so hearing one of them scream

00:53:19.130 --> 00:53:22.220
in fright is a rare if not impossible occurrence.

00:53:22.220 --> 00:53:26.589
But even they were forced to yell out in fear
when they looked up to see the Old Man standing

00:53:26.589 --> 00:53:28.750
on the ceiling, grinning down at them.

00:53:28.750 --> 00:53:32.770
Resnick raised his M4 and shot a three-round
burst at center mass.

00:53:32.770 --> 00:53:34.660
SCP–106 didn’t care.

00:53:34.660 --> 00:53:38.510
Even under sustained gunfire from the two
security officers, it didn’t even flinch.

00:53:38.510 --> 00:53:42.589
The Old Man simply reached down and snatched
Agent Resnick from the ground, like it was

00:53:42.589 --> 00:53:44.349
picking an apple from a tree.

00:53:44.349 --> 00:53:49.150
The Old Man held Resnick in one hand and pounded
its other rotten fist into the Agent’s body,

00:53:49.150 --> 00:53:50.700
breaking all of his bones.

00:53:50.700 --> 00:53:53.890
Resnick screamed for his partner to help him
but there was no time.

00:53:53.890 --> 00:53:58.920
Before Goodwin could do anything, SCP–106
began receding back into another slimy burnmark

00:53:58.920 --> 00:53:59.980
on the wall.

00:53:59.980 --> 00:54:03.109
Only this time, he was taking his screaming
victim with him.

00:54:03.109 --> 00:54:07.589
Agent Resnick gave one more horrified scream
before he was pulled backwards into the inky

00:54:07.589 --> 00:54:12.090
darkness leaving the room silent except for
the burning hiss of the corrosive goo left

00:54:12.090 --> 00:54:13.090
behind.

00:54:13.090 --> 00:54:15.480
You might think this would be the end of it,
but no.

00:54:15.480 --> 00:54:18.569
For poor Agent Resnick, the worst was yet
to come.

00:54:18.569 --> 00:54:23.540
He was being dragged into what SCP Foundation
scientists refer to as the Old Man’s “Pocket

00:54:23.540 --> 00:54:28.089
Dimension”, a miniature layer of reality
within our own where the malicious SCP is

00:54:28.089 --> 00:54:31.460
essentially a cruel, all-powerful God.

00:54:31.460 --> 00:54:35.789
According to witness reports extracted from
victims who were taken to this little nightmare

00:54:35.789 --> 00:54:40.119
realm, the dimension resembles a series of
twisting, endless corridors where the Old

00:54:40.119 --> 00:54:44.570
Man stalks and tortures his captured victims
to the breaking point, manipulating space

00:54:44.570 --> 00:54:47.009
and time to its own sadistic ends.

00:54:47.009 --> 00:54:51.740
On rare occasions, the SCP will even release
its victims, just for the joy of hunting,

00:54:51.740 --> 00:54:54.650
capturing, and torturing them all over again.

00:54:54.650 --> 00:54:58.770
While Agent Resnick was learning the true
meaning of terror, containment specialists

00:54:58.770 --> 00:55:03.559
were mobilizing in its cell, preparing the
one known tried-and-true method of luring

00:55:03.559 --> 00:55:08.020
the Old Man back: Tempting it with the prospect
of causing even more suffering.

00:55:08.020 --> 00:55:12.440
In order to do this, Foundation personnel
take one of the aforementioned Class D personnel

00:55:12.440 --> 00:55:17.960
and begin inducing extreme pain by breaking
a major bone or slicing a tendon every twenty

00:55:17.960 --> 00:55:18.960
minutes.

00:55:18.960 --> 00:55:23.359
The victim’s agonized screams are then played
over the facility’s intercom, acting as

00:55:23.359 --> 00:55:25.559
bait for the pain-loving Old Man.

00:55:25.559 --> 00:55:30.009
The screams echo through the facility’s
otherwise silent halls, as the mutilated corpse

00:55:30.009 --> 00:55:33.230
of Agent Resnick falls from a new scorch mark
on the ceiling.

00:55:33.230 --> 00:55:36.972
The Old Man can hear the sounds of suffering
ringing out through the air around him, and

00:55:36.972 --> 00:55:41.130
he can barely contain his excitement over
the prospect of a new plaything.

00:55:41.130 --> 00:55:45.579
The snapped femurs, the torn Achilles tendons,
it was all too good to miss.

00:55:45.579 --> 00:55:50.279
Having had its twisted fun with the security
officers and observers, SCP-106 wandered back

00:55:50.279 --> 00:55:53.740
to its containment cell, where a new screaming
victim awaited.

00:55:53.740 --> 00:55:58.569
The other security officers, containment specialists,
and scientists evacuated the area, leaving

00:55:58.569 --> 00:56:00.559
the Old Man alone with his prey.

00:56:00.559 --> 00:56:04.339
While the unfortunate Class D was left to
his fate, the rest of the staff commenced

00:56:04.339 --> 00:56:08.750
clean up procedures, which mainly involved
wiping the brown and black mucus from the

00:56:08.750 --> 00:56:09.750
walls.

00:56:09.750 --> 00:56:13.119
It would probably be at least another month
before anything like this happened again,

00:56:13.119 --> 00:56:17.050
and new personnel would be transferred over
to the facility to replace the fallen.

00:56:17.050 --> 00:56:21.349
All in all, just another night at The SCP
Foundation.

00:56:21.349 --> 00:56:27.569
The year is 1941, and the world is gripped
by the most violent and widespread war in

00:56:27.569 --> 00:56:29.069
history.

00:56:29.069 --> 00:56:33.680
Millions march to war as bloody battles are
fought across the globe, horrendous atrocities

00:56:33.680 --> 00:56:38.779
are carried out on groups of people, and parts
of London are bombed to rubble on a weekly

00:56:38.779 --> 00:56:40.029
basis.

00:56:40.029 --> 00:56:44.050
Considering it’s only been twenty years
since the last world war, it must seem to

00:56:44.050 --> 00:56:49.420
the residents of the early 20th century that
the world is coming apart at the seams.

00:56:49.420 --> 00:56:53.859
And amongst all this chaos, it’d be easy
not to notice a secluded manor house in the

00:56:53.859 --> 00:56:59.559
English countryside disappearing without a
trace for eleven days, before suddenly returning

00:56:59.559 --> 00:57:01.160
to our reality.

00:57:01.160 --> 00:57:06.920
But thankfully, one organization makes it
its sole duty to notice the unnoticeable and

00:57:06.920 --> 00:57:10.869
understand the impossible - The SCP Foundation.

00:57:10.869 --> 00:57:16.530
And within that anomalous manor house, Foundation
agents and researchers were about to find

00:57:16.530 --> 00:57:20.579
horrors beyond even their darkest imaginations.

00:57:20.579 --> 00:57:26.489
This is the grim tale of SCP - 1461, better
known as…

00:57:26.489 --> 00:57:28.640
The House of the Worm.

00:57:28.640 --> 00:57:33.180
When the manor house reappeared after its
eleven day absence, the Foundation zeroed

00:57:33.180 --> 00:57:36.320
in, sending agents inside to investigate.

00:57:36.320 --> 00:57:41.309
It was a two-level dwelling complete with
twelve bedrooms, four baths, three studies,

00:57:41.309 --> 00:57:46.739
a main foyer slash ballroom, a library, a
kitchen, and a pantry-basement.

00:57:46.739 --> 00:57:51.529
The Foundation observed that a number of these
rooms had been fitted with rows of bunk beds,

00:57:51.529 --> 00:57:54.089
similar to a boarding house or barracks.

00:57:54.089 --> 00:57:56.670
Only later would they understand why.

00:57:56.670 --> 00:58:01.509
They found that the upper portion of the home
exhibited no abnormal qualities whatsoever,

00:58:01.509 --> 00:58:06.579
but as the agents investigated further, they
found an entrance to the truly anomalous portion

00:58:06.579 --> 00:58:10.180
of the manor - The extensive sub-level system.

00:58:10.180 --> 00:58:14.089
No previous records of the building kept by
the local council indicated that there would

00:58:14.089 --> 00:58:19.130
be anything below the manor’s basement - so
either the mysterious previous occupants,

00:58:19.130 --> 00:58:24.089
who were nowhere to be found, had built this
sub-level, or it’d just appeared here on

00:58:24.089 --> 00:58:25.359
its own.

00:58:25.359 --> 00:58:29.829
Regardless of which was the case, agents and
researchers knew that whatever had happened

00:58:29.829 --> 00:58:34.829
down here had everything to do with the manor’s
mysterious disappearance.

00:58:34.829 --> 00:58:40.339
They descended into the depths of what seemed
like a man-made cave system, constructed primarily

00:58:40.339 --> 00:58:43.309
from a mix of concrete, iron, and brass.

00:58:43.309 --> 00:58:49.579
It was a behemoth of 20th century technology
- intricate, snaking systems of pipes, gears,

00:58:49.579 --> 00:58:51.040
and pumping pistons.

00:58:51.040 --> 00:58:55.359
It was like someone had built an entire factory
down here - but for what?

00:58:55.359 --> 00:59:00.109
The agents began to spread out through the
labyrinthine bowels of the manor, hoping to

00:59:00.109 --> 00:59:05.249
find some answers, but all they seemed to
discover was more questions.

00:59:05.249 --> 00:59:08.650
This place hadn’t been built with any form
of comprehensible logic.

00:59:08.650 --> 00:59:14.480
It was full of dead ends, stairways that ascended
and descended to nowhere, doors that would

00:59:14.480 --> 00:59:18.109
open to reveal just walls behind them or not
open at all.

00:59:18.109 --> 00:59:20.589
It was like a maze built by a maniac.

00:59:20.589 --> 00:59:24.799
It didn’t help that it looked like the place
was recently hit by an earthquake with some

00:59:24.799 --> 00:59:28.550
passages caved in and mangled machinery strewn
about.

00:59:28.550 --> 00:59:33.410
It seemed that no human workers had interfered
with the impossibly complex and bizarre machinery

00:59:33.410 --> 00:59:34.880
in quite some time.

00:59:34.880 --> 00:59:39.380
A number of the materials used to construct
said machinery, as well as the gray sandstone

00:59:39.380 --> 00:59:43.999
filling in the collapsed passageways, remain
unidentified to this day.

00:59:43.999 --> 00:59:48.799
Already, the sub-level was proving to be a
complex puzzle box with only an estimated

00:59:48.799 --> 00:59:53.230
75% of its layout ultimately being mapped
by Foundation researchers.

00:59:53.230 --> 00:59:58.530
However, they would soon realize that this
place wasn’t just confusing - it was deadly.

00:59:58.530 --> 01:00:02.650
The only method of self-maintenance detected
by the exploring agents were pipes that would

01:00:02.650 --> 01:00:06.670
fire a thick, black lubricant onto the surrounding
machinery.

01:00:06.670 --> 01:00:10.400
One of the Foundation agents had the misfortune
of getting covered in it while exploring a

01:00:10.400 --> 01:00:15.049
darkened passageway, and eighty percent of
his body was melted as a result.

01:00:15.049 --> 01:00:20.950
It appeared that the viscous, black goo was
incredibly corrosive to all organic matter.

01:00:20.950 --> 01:00:26.410
A number of the machines also emitted dangerously
high quantities of gamma and X-ray radiation,

01:00:26.410 --> 01:00:30.760
making it difficult to explore many of the
caverns without heavy hazmat protection.

01:00:30.760 --> 01:00:35.890
And worst of all, were the extremely hostile
creatures living in the caves who would regularly

01:00:35.890 --> 01:00:38.220
attack Foundation personnel.

01:00:38.220 --> 01:00:45.069
These abominations came to be known as SCP
- 1461 - 1, vicious, steampunk Frankenstein

01:00:45.069 --> 01:00:50.470
monsters - once human, but with large parts
of their bodies replaced by crude, mechanical

01:00:50.470 --> 01:00:54.750
implants - including metal teeth and claws.

01:00:54.750 --> 01:00:59.890
1461-1’s have displayed a taste for human
flesh, and they have dragged multiple Foundation

01:00:59.890 --> 01:01:04.260
agents down into their lair to be “converted”
into monsters like them.

01:01:04.260 --> 01:01:09.339
It’s believed that SCP-1461 is capable of
controlling these beasts through the strategic

01:01:09.339 --> 01:01:14.640
use of sound from its brass speaking pipes,
leading them into areas where Foundation personnel

01:01:14.640 --> 01:01:17.540
are present to instigate conflict.

01:01:17.540 --> 01:01:21.619
Many of these pitiful creatures have had their
throats replaced by phonographs, endlessly

01:01:21.619 --> 01:01:25.690
repeating the same nonsense phrases over and
over again:

01:01:25.690 --> 01:01:27.680
“I am what you have made me.

01:01:27.680 --> 01:01:29.700
I am choice and I am tyranny.

01:01:29.700 --> 01:01:30.700
Forgive me.

01:01:30.700 --> 01:01:32.819
I am then and I am now.

01:01:32.819 --> 01:01:34.650
What gods they will be, then.

01:01:34.650 --> 01:01:36.789
I am evil and I am flesh.

01:01:36.789 --> 01:01:37.859
I am the trap.

01:01:37.859 --> 01:01:39.309
I am the trapped.

01:01:39.309 --> 01:01:41.420
I am beauty and I am chaos.

01:01:41.420 --> 01:01:42.420
Children are selfish.

01:01:42.420 --> 01:01:43.930
I am the worm.

01:01:43.930 --> 01:01:46.130
I have broken God.”

01:01:46.130 --> 01:01:52.210
Still, in spite of mazes, monsters, and deadly
chemicals, the agents persisted, and managed

01:01:52.210 --> 01:01:54.980
to discover several important locations.

01:01:54.980 --> 01:02:00.380
The Gel Production chamber on Sub-Level 3
creates glass jars from the unidentified sandstone,

01:02:00.380 --> 01:02:04.319
and fills them with a slime that looks to
contain living eyes and teeth.

01:02:04.319 --> 01:02:09.170
The Factory Deliveries room is filled with
a huge number of crates and boxes, which seem

01:02:09.170 --> 01:02:12.809
to shift and change in number between Foundation
patrols.

01:02:12.809 --> 01:02:17.630
The Speaking Tube Room on Sub-Level Eleven
contains a grand pulpit that acts as the connecting

01:02:17.630 --> 01:02:23.049
point for the complex array of speaking tubes
running through the entire cave system.

01:02:23.049 --> 01:02:28.950
The body parts of a deceased female also appear
to be wired into the machinery, like spare

01:02:28.950 --> 01:02:29.950
parts.

01:02:29.950 --> 01:02:34.009
And on Sub-Level Twelve, they found the so-called
Catalyst Room.

01:02:34.009 --> 01:02:39.259
Here, they discovered a huge, complicated,
clockwork and steam-powered machine that appeared

01:02:39.259 --> 01:02:42.420
to be broken and missing some parts.

01:02:42.420 --> 01:02:47.569
Most horrifying of all though, is the raised
platform in the center of the Catalyst Room

01:02:47.569 --> 01:02:50.529
on top of which is a metal hospital bed.

01:02:50.529 --> 01:02:56.029
A desiccated male corpse rests upon this bed,
its chest punctured by large syringes connected

01:02:56.029 --> 01:02:58.890
by tubes to some kind of pumping machine.

01:02:58.890 --> 01:03:02.680
The parts connecting this pumping machine
to the overall apparatus of the room were

01:03:02.680 --> 01:03:06.339
missing though, leaving its purpose a mystery.

01:03:06.339 --> 01:03:11.599
The Foundation assumed that fluids used to
be drawn out of this corpse to somehow power

01:03:11.599 --> 01:03:12.680
the machine.

01:03:12.680 --> 01:03:16.839
You may be starting to worry that there don’t
seem to be any answers here, that this house

01:03:16.839 --> 01:03:21.839
is one big mystery - but lucky for you, you’re
wrong.

01:03:21.839 --> 01:03:26.119
An old journal was also discovered in the
Catalyst Room, and if what is written inside

01:03:26.119 --> 01:03:31.180
is to be believed, then we may finally have
some truth about who created the House of

01:03:31.180 --> 01:03:36.589
the Worm, why it was created, and what horrible
events triggered its mysterious disappearance

01:03:36.589 --> 01:03:37.729
and reappearance.

01:03:37.729 --> 01:03:42.479
His true name has been redacted by the Foundation
and special efforts have been made to maintain

01:03:42.479 --> 01:03:47.260
secrecy around the House, seeing as it’s
an anomaly of great interest to a cult known

01:03:47.260 --> 01:03:52.549
as the Church of the Broken God, so we’ll
just call the one who made this place “The

01:03:52.549 --> 01:03:53.549
Inventor.”

01:03:53.549 --> 01:03:58.339
Before any of this, the Inventor was one of
the many Englishmen traumatized and almost

01:03:58.339 --> 01:04:02.039
killed in the horrific trench battles of World
War One.

01:04:02.039 --> 01:04:07.039
After a near death experience, the Inventor,
like many geniuses and madmen, was plagued

01:04:07.039 --> 01:04:09.809
by surreal and nightmarish visions.

01:04:09.809 --> 01:04:15.579
He saw a huge creature that he referred to
as “The Worm” - a gigantic, metal monstrosity

01:04:15.579 --> 01:04:20.920
with dragon-like jaws full of gnashing gears
that rampaged through Europe, destroying and

01:04:20.920 --> 01:04:23.829
devouring everything in its path.

01:04:23.829 --> 01:04:28.779
These apocalyptic visions also presented him
with a solution, vague blueprints for a machine

01:04:28.779 --> 01:04:34.310
that might be the salvation of him and any
others willing to take his new gospel to heart.

01:04:34.310 --> 01:04:38.869
An escape from a world that the Inventor knew
in his heart was about to end.

01:04:38.869 --> 01:04:43.289
He hired work-starved labourers from across
the country to help him make his visions a

01:04:43.289 --> 01:04:49.369
reality and began a massive, secret construction
project beneath his isolated country manor

01:04:49.369 --> 01:04:50.390
house.

01:04:50.390 --> 01:04:53.079
For The Inventor, it was all a labour of love.

01:04:53.079 --> 01:04:58.910
He wanted to protect his wife, son, and daughter
from the terrible jaws of the Worm.

01:04:58.910 --> 01:05:04.059
But as the project stretched on, his wife
began to suspect that he’d lost his mind.

01:05:04.059 --> 01:05:07.029
Many of his workers, however, felt just the
opposite.

01:05:07.029 --> 01:05:11.119
They became infatuated by the Inventor’s
sermons on the nature of the Worm and the

01:05:11.119 --> 01:05:13.710
coming apocalypse they hoped to escape.

01:05:13.710 --> 01:05:18.720
Soon enough, they had become a bonafide cult,
constructing the elaborate sublevels underneath

01:05:18.720 --> 01:05:22.749
the house in preparation for the fast approaching
day of reckoning.

01:05:22.749 --> 01:05:25.029
Then came World War Two.

01:05:25.029 --> 01:05:29.970
The Inventor saw Hitler, hungry for war, as
one of the avatars of the Worm.

01:05:29.970 --> 01:05:35.140
Finally, knowing the time was right, he activated
the machine, and successfully trapped the

01:05:35.140 --> 01:05:37.630
Worm in the bowels of his mechanized home.

01:05:37.630 --> 01:05:41.970
However, as the Blitz raged and London’s
bombing began, the Inventor felt as though

01:05:41.970 --> 01:05:44.180
he hadn’t stopped anything.

01:05:44.180 --> 01:05:49.410
He realized once and for all that he was never
meant to stop the apocalypse, only escape

01:05:49.410 --> 01:05:50.410
it.

01:05:50.410 --> 01:05:54.259
And by throwing the final switch and setting
the machine he and his followers had built

01:05:54.259 --> 01:05:58.309
into overdrive, he did just that.

01:05:58.309 --> 01:06:03.200
This was the moment the House of the Worm
disappeared, transporting the Inventor, his

01:06:03.200 --> 01:06:06.299
family, and his devoted staff to a different
world.

01:06:06.299 --> 01:06:12.529
An empty grey world, devoid of war, but also
lacking all the comforts of regular life,

01:06:12.529 --> 01:06:13.749
including food.

01:06:13.749 --> 01:06:18.309
Things went downhill from there, as their
supplies quickly began to run out, and the

01:06:18.309 --> 01:06:21.749
cult descended into cannibalism in order to
survive.

01:06:21.749 --> 01:06:24.799
Things weren’t going much better in the
Inventor’s personal life.

01:06:24.799 --> 01:06:29.400
His wife, fearing what would happen to the
family, took her own life and the life of

01:06:29.400 --> 01:06:30.410
his daughter.

01:06:30.410 --> 01:06:35.049
Though by this point, the Inventor’s mind
was so fractured that it’s possible he may

01:06:35.049 --> 01:06:36.499
have killed them himself.

01:06:36.499 --> 01:06:42.249
Either way, it was only the Inventor and his
son left, and more trouble was brewing.

01:06:42.249 --> 01:06:47.599
Eudora, one of the staff trapped in the building
with the Inventor and his cult, started a

01:06:47.599 --> 01:06:48.599
mutiny.

01:06:48.599 --> 01:06:52.509
She claimed the Worm spoke to her from below,
and that their only path to salvation was

01:06:52.509 --> 01:06:53.979
pleasing the Worm.

01:06:53.979 --> 01:06:55.319
How would they please it?

01:06:55.319 --> 01:06:57.489
A sacrifice, of course.

01:06:57.489 --> 01:07:00.270
They would give it the son of the man who
had trapped it.

01:07:00.270 --> 01:07:06.200
The mutineers took the Inventor’s only remaining
child, and descended into the lowest sub levels.

01:07:06.200 --> 01:07:11.509
The Inventor followed, hoping to track them
down, save his son, and salvage something

01:07:11.509 --> 01:07:12.809
from this nightmare.

01:07:12.809 --> 01:07:17.049
As he ventured deeper, battling the members
of Eudora’s new cult, he found that they

01:07:17.049 --> 01:07:21.960
were changing themselves, becoming the half-human
cyborg creatures that the Foundation would

01:07:21.960 --> 01:07:23.180
later discover.

01:07:23.180 --> 01:07:26.890
The Inventor would find Eudora herself in
the Speaking Tube Room.

01:07:26.890 --> 01:07:31.979
Her body, still living, was wired into the
machinery, and she had sacrificed his son

01:07:31.979 --> 01:07:33.079
to the Worm.

01:07:33.079 --> 01:07:38.509
In a rage, the Inventor murdered Eudora, or
whatever was left of her, then heard a familiar

01:07:38.509 --> 01:07:41.450
voice speaking out of a nearby speaking tube.

01:07:41.450 --> 01:07:42.450
It said:

01:07:42.450 --> 01:07:44.549
“I am what you have made me.

01:07:44.549 --> 01:07:47.120
I am then and I am now.

01:07:47.120 --> 01:07:49.400
I am choice and I am tyranny.

01:07:49.400 --> 01:07:52.249
I am evil and I am flesh.

01:07:52.249 --> 01:07:54.789
I am beauty and I am chaos.

01:07:54.789 --> 01:07:57.329
I am the worm."

01:07:57.329 --> 01:07:59.369
The voice was his own.

01:07:59.369 --> 01:08:04.729
In that terrible moment, the Inventor realised
that the Worm wasn’t a giant, all-devouring

01:08:04.729 --> 01:08:07.020
monster, it was him.

01:08:07.020 --> 01:08:11.069
In trying to protect his loved ones from a
perceived apocalypse, he’d brought them

01:08:11.069 --> 01:08:12.950
all to their horrible demise.

01:08:12.950 --> 01:08:17.110
He’d trapped them with the monster he’d
hoped for them all to escape from, because

01:08:17.110 --> 01:08:21.259
no matter what you build, you can’t escape
who you are.

01:08:21.259 --> 01:08:25.819
Grief stricken and broken, the Inventor descended
into the Catalyst Room.

01:08:25.819 --> 01:08:32.449
There was his son, stuck with the syringes,
drained of all life to fuel the mighty machine

01:08:32.449 --> 01:08:34.420
his father created.

01:08:34.420 --> 01:08:39.960
In his last moments, the Inventor decided
to do the only noble thing: He threw himself

01:08:39.960 --> 01:08:45.130
into the machine, destroying both it and himself
in the process.

01:08:45.130 --> 01:08:51.960
The house was transported back to our reality,
but the Worm, in a sense, was no more.

01:08:51.960 --> 01:08:54.670
But who knows if the Worm is really dead.

01:08:54.670 --> 01:09:00.069
Its thoughts and poisonous intent still lingers
in the caverns, and rattles through the speaking

01:09:00.069 --> 01:09:01.069
pipes.

01:09:01.069 --> 01:09:05.299
Whatever really happened, the Foundation is
still picking up the pieces today - and who

01:09:05.299 --> 01:09:11.630
knows what lurks in the parts still hidden
from our knowledge.

01:09:11.630 --> 01:09:17.279
It all started in 1983 with reports of human
trafficking in the heart of Sin City.

01:09:17.279 --> 01:09:22.069
The FBI had gotten word of a potential trafficking
ring operating out of an abandoned department

01:09:22.069 --> 01:09:27.420
store in Las Vegas, Nevada, and immediately
began organizing a secret raid on the building.

01:09:27.420 --> 01:09:31.900
While they would indeed encounter something
horrifying within that abandoned department

01:09:31.900 --> 01:09:35.569
store, it wasn’t criminals or human trafficking.

01:09:35.569 --> 01:09:38.630
In fact, it wasn’t human at all.

01:09:38.630 --> 01:09:43.069
This is the horrifying story of SCP - 847.

01:09:43.069 --> 01:09:48.009
After weeks of planning, the raid on the department
store was conducted in the dead of night.

01:09:48.009 --> 01:09:52.719
Agents covered all the exits and entrances
and a helicopter was stationed nearby in case

01:09:52.719 --> 01:09:54.380
anyone attempted to run.

01:09:54.380 --> 01:09:56.630
It should have been a perfect trap.

01:09:56.630 --> 01:10:00.679
But things never go as planned when you don’t
know what you’re dealing with.

01:10:00.679 --> 01:10:04.030
The agents breached the door, and began searching
the darkened building.

01:10:04.030 --> 01:10:08.699
It didn’t appear that there was any power,
so the traffickers must have had great night

01:10:08.699 --> 01:10:11.900
vision and a high tolerance for creepy locales.

01:10:11.900 --> 01:10:15.840
Agents soon heard a faint humming sound coming
from below - a generator.

01:10:15.840 --> 01:10:20.780
It must be located in the basement and be
the hub of this criminal enterprise.

01:10:20.780 --> 01:10:25.260
Readying themselves for whatever they were
about to find, the agents descended into the

01:10:25.260 --> 01:10:26.260
basement.

01:10:26.260 --> 01:10:30.590
As they moved deeper into the building, they
found that lighting rigs had been set up - they

01:10:30.590 --> 01:10:35.530
must be getting closer to something, but that
“something” was still a mystery.

01:10:35.530 --> 01:10:40.480
A senior FBI Special Agent was leading the
charge, his pistol drawn and ready.

01:10:40.480 --> 01:10:41.560
It was quiet.

01:10:41.560 --> 01:10:42.560
Too quiet.

01:10:42.560 --> 01:10:45.880
Did the traffickers already realize they were
coming and clear out?

01:10:45.880 --> 01:10:51.230
He was ready to consider this bust a bust
when he heard a quiet mewling in the distance.

01:10:51.230 --> 01:10:55.880
A persistent, whining whimper that was undeniably
human.

01:10:55.880 --> 01:10:59.060
He gave the signal to his fellow agents to
follow the noise.

01:10:59.060 --> 01:11:03.920
They proceeded forward towards the pained
sounds and found themselves in a wide, well-lit

01:11:03.920 --> 01:11:06.840
room filled with department store mannequins.

01:11:06.840 --> 01:11:12.010
All were broken to some degree - some were
totally smashed to pieces, some were chained

01:11:12.010 --> 01:11:16.469
to walls and locked in cages, others were
wrapped in plastic.

01:11:16.469 --> 01:11:21.130
The agent wondered whether this was some kind
of twisted joke, or a messed up avant garde

01:11:21.130 --> 01:11:22.179
art piece.

01:11:22.179 --> 01:11:28.300
That’s when he noticed Her: A single, crouched
figure in the distance, hunched over and whimpering

01:11:28.300 --> 01:11:31.840
in a darkened corner of the room near a full-length
mirror.

01:11:31.840 --> 01:11:36.510
He couldn’t fully make her out, but he got
the sense that something was wrong - she was

01:11:36.510 --> 01:11:37.880
injured, bent over.

01:11:37.880 --> 01:11:39.620
Was she even missing an arm?

01:11:39.620 --> 01:11:42.300
Just what had these monsters done to this
woman?

01:11:42.300 --> 01:11:45.739
He whispered a request for back up into his
radio, and pushed on.

01:11:45.739 --> 01:11:50.940
When they got within 50 meters of the strange
woman, her demeanor changed entirely.

01:11:50.940 --> 01:11:55.480
She jerked around - her movements forced,
erratic, and painful-looking.

01:11:55.480 --> 01:12:00.610
The woman stared directly into the agent’s
eyes and began hobbling towards him., occasionally

01:12:00.610 --> 01:12:04.489
stopping to strike a pose as if modelling
during a photo shoot.

01:12:04.489 --> 01:12:09.540
Just then the agent made a horrifying realization
- this thing moving towards them wasn’t

01:12:09.540 --> 01:12:13.000
a woman at all, it was a living mannequin.

01:12:13.000 --> 01:12:17.280
As she got closer though, he also realized
that the mannequin’s broken left forearm

01:12:17.280 --> 01:12:20.130
had been carved into a large shiv.

01:12:20.130 --> 01:12:24.449
A female junior FBI agent had been one of
the many to pour into the room when the raid

01:12:24.449 --> 01:12:26.280
leader had radioed for backup.

01:12:26.280 --> 01:12:31.690
The second she entered the fifty meter range
of this strange mannequin, everything changed.

01:12:31.690 --> 01:12:37.030
In an instant, its eyes and mouth began dripping
with a thick, viscous resin.

01:12:37.030 --> 01:12:42.600
Its whimpering gasps suddenly became vicious,
earsplitting screeches, and it turned its

01:12:42.600 --> 01:12:44.550
gaze from the senior FBI agent.

01:12:44.550 --> 01:12:49.469
It was now focused on the junior agent who
had just entered the room and broke into a

01:12:49.469 --> 01:12:51.449
terrifying run straight towards her.

01:12:51.449 --> 01:12:55.099
The mannequin moved with a violent, single-minded
purpose.

01:12:55.099 --> 01:13:00.130
Other agents began firing but it was running
freakishly fast and easily dodged most of

01:13:00.130 --> 01:13:01.130
the bullets.

01:13:01.130 --> 01:13:04.940
The few that actually hit seemed to do nothing
to slow the creature down.

01:13:04.940 --> 01:13:08.550
It shrugged off the damage and kept running.

01:13:08.550 --> 01:13:12.849
With a great leap, it landed on the terrified
junior agent, and began jabbing at her with

01:13:12.849 --> 01:13:14.010
its bladed arm.

01:13:14.010 --> 01:13:18.280
The other agents stopped firing, fearing they
might accidentally hit their colleague during

01:13:18.280 --> 01:13:19.280
the panic.

01:13:19.280 --> 01:13:24.590
The mannequin was ruthless, clawing and stabbing,
with the strange resin leaking out of its

01:13:24.590 --> 01:13:26.460
every orifice.

01:13:26.460 --> 01:13:30.550
Terrified and unable to reach her gun, the
agent remembered her training - she reached

01:13:30.550 --> 01:13:34.989
into her belt and grabbed her stun gun, jamming
the two probes up against the creature’s

01:13:34.989 --> 01:13:37.590
chest and giving it 30,000 volts.

01:13:37.590 --> 01:13:43.429
The creature spasmed, fell backwards, and
collapsed in a heap on the ground - frozen.

01:13:43.429 --> 01:13:48.980
This was the first recorded encounter with
SCP - 847 - a violent living mannequin with

01:13:48.980 --> 01:13:51.780
a serious problem with women.

01:13:51.780 --> 01:13:55.800
This terrifying report was passed up the chain
of command until it landed on the desk of

01:13:55.800 --> 01:13:58.489
a Foundation Agent working in the FBI.

01:13:58.489 --> 01:14:02.900
The Foundation quickly swooped in and claimed
the mannequin, delivered necessary amnestic

01:14:02.900 --> 01:14:07.860
treatment to all who’d witnessed it, and
closely observed the female junior FBI agent’s

01:14:07.860 --> 01:14:11.340
recovery in a private hospital with Foundation
ties.

01:14:11.340 --> 01:14:16.320
As it turns out, they were right to do so,
as the junior agent was in for a gruesome

01:14:16.320 --> 01:14:17.320
fate.

01:14:17.320 --> 01:14:22.400
While the wounds she’d suffered at the hands
of SCP - 847 didn’t appear fatal, the fact

01:14:22.400 --> 01:14:28.170
that the mannequin’s anomalous resin excretions
entered the open wound changed everything.

01:14:28.170 --> 01:14:32.670
Several hours after being committed, the junior
agent began complaining of limb stiffness

01:14:32.670 --> 01:14:34.489
and difficulty moving.

01:14:34.489 --> 01:14:37.380
This quickly developed into full paralysis.

01:14:37.380 --> 01:14:43.300
Over time, her skin and internal organs began
to harden, until the process - dubbed plastination

01:14:43.300 --> 01:14:45.400
- came to a gruesome end.

01:14:45.400 --> 01:14:51.150
The junior agent wasn’t just dead, she had
been transformed into a mannequin.

01:14:51.150 --> 01:14:55.969
Foundation researchers were met with a truly
horrifying realization - This meant that all

01:14:55.969 --> 01:15:02.550
the other broken mannequins found with SCP
- 847 were likely once living humans, attacked

01:15:02.550 --> 01:15:08.480
and transformed by the anomaly, now a source
for new harvested body parts.

01:15:08.480 --> 01:15:15.000
Now safely interred at a Foundation containment
facility though, the real tests on SCP - 847

01:15:15.000 --> 01:15:18.810
to determine its behavior and physical attributes
could begin.

01:15:18.810 --> 01:15:24.760
The most important detail about SCP - 847
is that its aggression is exclusively directed

01:15:24.760 --> 01:15:31.480
towards women, as opposed to when it encounters
men and its instincts are more self-destructive.

01:15:31.480 --> 01:15:36.300
Through a series of tests and observations,
researchers have been able to pin down three

01:15:36.300 --> 01:15:41.400
different distinct patterns of behavior for
SCP - 847.

01:15:41.400 --> 01:15:46.429
Pattern Z behaviors occur when there are no
humans standing within fifty meters of SCP

01:15:46.429 --> 01:15:47.469
- 847.

01:15:47.469 --> 01:15:51.719
The mannequin will seek out a full length
mirror, and pose in front of it, much like

01:15:51.719 --> 01:15:55.230
a department store mannequin attempting to
show off its clothes.

01:15:55.230 --> 01:15:59.880
It remains largely inanimate during these
periods, and will very occasionally use a

01:15:59.880 --> 01:16:05.429
finger - or whatever appendage is available,
given its habit for self-mutilation - to scratch

01:16:05.429 --> 01:16:08.280
messages on nearby surfaces.

01:16:08.280 --> 01:16:13.460
Pattern Y behaviors occur when male humans
with XY chromosomes enter a fifty meter radius

01:16:13.460 --> 01:16:16.460
around SCP - 847.

01:16:16.460 --> 01:16:22.389
Just like its reaction to the male FBI agents
who found it, 847 will initially emit vocalizations

01:16:22.389 --> 01:16:28.080
that seem like whimpering gasps, before making
eye contact and striking provocative poses

01:16:28.080 --> 01:16:29.550
while approaching the subject.

01:16:29.550 --> 01:16:34.310
It will then remain static, and allow the
male subject to pose its body.

01:16:34.310 --> 01:16:39.500
However, after the male subject leaves the
area, 847 will enter a state of considerable

01:16:39.500 --> 01:16:43.429
distress, and begin removing or shattering
parts of its body.

01:16:43.429 --> 01:16:47.610
The Foundation has found that the parts removed
or shattered are often consistent with parts

01:16:47.610 --> 01:16:52.739
that the male subjects found displeasing during
interactions, showing a masochistic desire

01:16:52.739 --> 01:16:54.239
to impress.

01:16:54.239 --> 01:16:58.000
These parts are then harvested back from plastinated
victims.

01:16:58.000 --> 01:17:02.560
Which brings us to the most dangerous of its
behavior patterns.

01:17:02.560 --> 01:17:07.840
Pattern X behaviors occur when female humans
enter a 50 meter radius around the creature.

01:17:07.840 --> 01:17:13.150
847 will immediately become brutally aggressive,
switching its noises from whimpers to violent

01:17:13.150 --> 01:17:14.750
screeches and growls.

01:17:14.750 --> 01:17:20.840
847 also experiences enhanced physical capabilities
during Pattern X states - its speed has been

01:17:20.840 --> 01:17:27.290
measured at 45 kilometers per hour, making
it as fast as the legendary SCP - 096.

01:17:27.290 --> 01:17:31.460
It’s also been shown to exhibit extreme
physical strength.

01:17:31.460 --> 01:17:36.320
It’s during this pattern of behavior that
it begins excreting its deadly resin, which

01:17:36.320 --> 01:17:39.360
has been proven to only be dangerous to women.

01:17:39.360 --> 01:17:44.460
In these states, the only thing capable of
reliably pacifying the being is a powerful

01:17:44.460 --> 01:17:45.800
electric shock.

01:17:45.800 --> 01:17:50.400
The shock causes the creature’s resin to
harden, temporarily incapacitating it for

01:17:50.400 --> 01:17:52.360
roughly five minutes.

01:17:52.360 --> 01:17:58.860
Other conventional weapons and damage has
no meaningful effect on SCP - 847.

01:17:58.860 --> 01:18:03.420
After a number of incidents that had sad and
violent endings, the Foundation Ethics Committee

01:18:03.420 --> 01:18:09.050
forbade the use of female D-Class personnel
in SCP - 847 testing.

01:18:09.050 --> 01:18:14.590
When it came to female subjects, 847 always
slipped into a state of extreme aggression,

01:18:14.590 --> 01:18:19.480
so instead the Foundation began testing with
male subjects in hopes of better understanding

01:18:19.480 --> 01:18:24.900
the dynamics between human males and SCP-847.

01:18:24.900 --> 01:18:29.699
Various misogynistic D-Class males were introduced
into the containment chamber, which was modelled

01:18:29.699 --> 01:18:33.260
to look like a bedroom for the purposes of
behavioral study.

01:18:33.260 --> 01:18:39.349
Each one, either during or after their interaction
with SCP - 847, was told to comment on some

01:18:39.349 --> 01:18:41.599
aspect they felt dissatisfied with.

01:18:41.599 --> 01:18:46.800
The mannequin shattered its own chest after
hearing it described as being out of proportion.

01:18:46.800 --> 01:18:51.050
After another D-Class called its nose ugly,
the mannequin broke it off.

01:18:51.050 --> 01:18:55.050
After another said that its hair was out of
fashion and commented on its inability to

01:18:55.050 --> 01:18:58.570
drink, it tore out its hair and liver.

01:18:58.570 --> 01:19:01.760
All parts were replaced after the experiments.

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:07.590
Things took their most violent and upsetting
turn yet with the introduction of D-7294.

01:19:07.590 --> 01:19:12.889
A lot of the time, D-Class personnel are considered
to be as anonymous as they are expendable.

01:19:12.889 --> 01:19:16.679
But D-7294 is an exception.

01:19:16.679 --> 01:19:20.949
Before becoming D-Class, he was a successful
cello teacher who brutally murdered one of

01:19:20.949 --> 01:19:23.040
his teenage students and her mother.

01:19:23.040 --> 01:19:27.469
He’s typically employed in tests when the
Foundation wishes to see interactions between

01:19:27.469 --> 01:19:32.260
anomalies and humans with confirmed psychopathic
personalities.

01:19:32.260 --> 01:19:37.489
During his interaction with SCP - 847, he
belittled and humiliated the mannequin.

01:19:37.489 --> 01:19:41.800
He forced it into uncomfortable poses, and
even snapped off one of its fingers before

01:19:41.800 --> 01:19:44.900
being dragged from the room by Foundation
guards.

01:19:44.900 --> 01:19:48.719
In the following debrief, he further berated
the mannequin as “useless” and “lousy”

01:19:48.719 --> 01:19:52.080
at its job of being controlled by him.

01:19:52.080 --> 01:19:59.070
In response, 847 extracted its own brains,
eyes, and clavicle before shattering its own

01:19:59.070 --> 01:20:01.099
hands in dismay.

01:20:01.099 --> 01:20:03.510
So why does SCP - 847 behave this way?

01:20:03.510 --> 01:20:08.969
While it may appear monstrous, it seems that
the reason SCP - 847 does what it does is

01:20:08.969 --> 01:20:15.260
all too human: It hurts women because it itself
is hurting, and it’s willing to hurt itself

01:20:15.260 --> 01:20:18.929
even more for the approval of the objects
of its desire.

01:20:18.929 --> 01:20:24.929
As a result, it’s an anomaly trapped in
an endless cycle of pain and violence.

01:20:24.929 --> 01:20:29.800
Perhaps one day it’ll be able to free itself
from the loop, but that day is unlikely to

01:20:29.800 --> 01:20:34.560
come for this murderous mannequin anytime
soon.

01:20:34.560 --> 01:20:37.949
It’s the holiday season.

01:20:37.949 --> 01:20:41.719
Outside, it’s cold and there's snow blanketing
the ground.

01:20:41.719 --> 01:20:46.480
But inside, you’re warm, and gathered around
the light of a roaring fireplace and a glowing

01:20:46.480 --> 01:20:47.900
Christmas tree.

01:20:47.900 --> 01:20:53.470
This is what Christmas is all about – warmth,
joy, and togetherness.

01:20:53.470 --> 01:20:56.989
But just because you’re comfortable doesn’t
mean you’re safe.

01:20:56.989 --> 01:21:02.510
You were so busy opening presents and stuffing
yourself at dinner that you didn’t notice

01:21:02.510 --> 01:21:05.170
the face pressed up against the window.

01:21:05.170 --> 01:21:12.860
That long, gaunt face, with the staring eyes,
the wide mouth full of yellow teeth, and the

01:21:12.860 --> 01:21:14.210
scraggly, white beard.

01:21:14.210 --> 01:21:19.739
You don’t know it yet, but within a few
days, you’ll be dead.

01:21:19.739 --> 01:21:24.330
You might be able to avert this horrible fate,
if only you knew what exactly you were dealing

01:21:24.330 --> 01:21:29.860
with: SCP – 4666, also known as The Yule
Man.

01:21:29.860 --> 01:21:35.599
A Keter-Class Christmas monster so violent,
sadistic, and terrifying, he makes Krampus

01:21:35.599 --> 01:21:37.880
look like jolly Saint Nick.

01:21:37.880 --> 01:21:44.400
And this year, just like every other, he’s
planning on being very, very naughty.

01:21:44.400 --> 01:21:50.290
The SCP Foundation began cataloguing the Yule
Man in 1974 after a string of violent and

01:21:50.290 --> 01:21:55.540
eerily similar home invasions during the holiday
season, but they have reason to believe that

01:21:55.540 --> 01:21:59.260
this entity has been around for a whole lot
longer.

01:21:59.260 --> 01:22:02.020
Over 2000 years in fact.

01:22:02.020 --> 01:22:06.300
Stories that describe what look to be Yule
Man massacres date as far back as the First

01:22:06.300 --> 01:22:11.420
Century BC in Scandinavia, and there have
been reports of similar clusters of events

01:22:11.420 --> 01:22:15.070
happening around the same time every year
since.

01:22:15.070 --> 01:22:19.620
This monster is prolific, and may have one
of the highest body counts of any creature

01:22:19.620 --> 01:22:22.370
under observation by the Foundation.

01:22:22.370 --> 01:22:26.840
The Yule Man’s trail of destruction became
clearer in the eighteenth century, as accounts

01:22:26.840 --> 01:22:30.040
of the carnage it leaves became more detailed.

01:22:30.040 --> 01:22:35.040
Later still, authorities even managed to find
physical evidence like the Yule Man’s fingerprints

01:22:35.040 --> 01:22:39.640
– which are similar to human fingerprints,
but display a distinct double-whorl pattern

01:22:39.640 --> 01:22:42.290
not seen in human fingerprints.

01:22:42.290 --> 01:22:47.050
Much about the anomalous nature of the Yule
Man is still unknown though, and the Foundation

01:22:47.050 --> 01:22:50.150
has yet to discover an effective way to contain
it.

01:22:50.150 --> 01:22:55.310
Their only hope is intercepting it before
it can get its long, gnarled fingers on its

01:22:55.310 --> 01:22:56.850
intended prey.

01:22:56.850 --> 01:23:00.090
Maybe you’re feeling worried, or that you’re
being watched.

01:23:00.090 --> 01:23:05.170
You have a good reason to be afraid, because
during his yearly active period – the twelve

01:23:05.170 --> 01:23:11.230
days between December 21st and January 2nd
– he’s always searching for prey.

01:23:11.230 --> 01:23:15.370
Nowhere is safe, because while it was initially
believed that he only appeared to those who

01:23:15.370 --> 01:23:20.790
lived north of 40 degrees latitude, it’s
now believed that much like Santa Claus, the

01:23:20.790 --> 01:23:23.570
Yule Man operates worldwide.

01:23:23.570 --> 01:23:29.000
Anyone could be in his sights right now, blissfully
unaware of the nightmare coming down the tracks

01:23:29.000 --> 01:23:30.199
towards them.

01:23:30.199 --> 01:23:35.270
Thankfully, the SCP Foundation, through analysis
of these attacks which are known as Weissnacht

01:23:35.270 --> 01:23:38.349
Events, they’ve been able to find certain
patterns.

01:23:38.349 --> 01:23:42.910
But first, what does the creature known as
The Yule Man even look like?

01:23:42.910 --> 01:23:49.290
Much like SCP – 096, the Yule Man is a long
and lanky humanoid standing about two meters

01:23:49.290 --> 01:23:54.739
tall, who resembles an emaciated human of
European descent, and never wears any clothes

01:23:54.739 --> 01:23:58.790
or other coverings despite the frigid temperatures
he operates in.

01:23:58.790 --> 01:24:03.219
You might be sad if you’re spending Christmas
alone, but it at least guarantees you safety

01:24:03.219 --> 01:24:07.960
from the Yule Man, as he only appears at the
homes of families with a child under the age

01:24:07.960 --> 01:24:09.190
of eight present.

01:24:09.190 --> 01:24:14.410
He also seems to favor isolated and rural
locations, and Weissnacht Events only occur

01:24:14.410 --> 01:24:18.780
when there’s a healthy covering of snow
on the ground during the event – hence the

01:24:18.780 --> 01:24:22.190
name which means “White Night” in English.

01:24:22.190 --> 01:24:26.810
It’s also vital that you recognize the three
distinct stages of a Weissnacht Event, too,

01:24:26.810 --> 01:24:30.050
or you won’t be seeing much of the New Year.

01:24:30.050 --> 01:24:32.830
The first stage occurs during the space of
a week.

01:24:32.830 --> 01:24:35.780
Children in the home might start to seem worried
or afraid.

01:24:35.780 --> 01:24:39.050
They might tell you that they see something
strange in the distance.

01:24:39.050 --> 01:24:44.100
The figure of a man they don’t recognize,
standing just far enough away that you can’t

01:24:44.100 --> 01:24:47.030
fully make him out, except that he’s really
tall.

01:24:47.030 --> 01:24:51.000
Of course, you probably won’t see anything,
and your instinct will be to tell them there’s

01:24:51.000 --> 01:24:52.870
nothing to be afraid of.

01:24:52.870 --> 01:24:57.389
Even when they tell you, through tears, that
there’s a man pressing his face up against

01:24:57.389 --> 01:24:59.500
their bedroom window at night.

01:24:59.500 --> 01:25:03.390
But they are right to be afraid, and you should
be, too.

01:25:03.390 --> 01:25:08.090
Already at this point, your only hope is to
try and spread the word as soon as possible:

01:25:08.090 --> 01:25:12.630
Report the incident to the local police, write
about it on Facebook, tweet about it.

01:25:12.630 --> 01:25:14.260
Whatever it takes.

01:25:14.260 --> 01:25:18.000
The SCP Foundation has operatives trawling
the internet and monitoring police reports

01:25:18.000 --> 01:25:22.800
constantly during this period, especially
for reports of mysterious men in the snow

01:25:22.800 --> 01:25:25.460
watching homes from a distance.

01:25:25.460 --> 01:25:29.210
Getting the Foundation’s attention is your
best hope of stopping this thing.

01:25:29.210 --> 01:25:30.760
And if you don’t?

01:25:30.760 --> 01:25:36.110
Next comes stage two, taking place between
nights eight and eleven of the active period.

01:25:36.110 --> 01:25:39.070
No longer will the Yule Man just be lurking
on the periphery.

01:25:39.070 --> 01:25:41.190
Now he’s getting closer.

01:25:41.190 --> 01:25:46.170
You’ll start to hear strange noises in your
attic or on the roof, noises that sound almost

01:25:46.170 --> 01:25:47.170
like footsteps.

01:25:47.170 --> 01:25:50.870
That’s crazy, you think, it’s probably
just an animal.

01:25:50.870 --> 01:25:53.360
But then, the smell starts.

01:25:53.360 --> 01:25:59.490
An awful, rotten stench that fills the house,
but no matter how hard you look, you can’t

01:25:59.490 --> 01:26:00.820
find the source.

01:26:00.820 --> 01:26:04.650
Finally, on the last night of December, you
tell yourself that you’ll take this matter

01:26:04.650 --> 01:26:05.650
to the police.

01:26:05.650 --> 01:26:08.909
But of course, it’s already too late.

01:26:08.909 --> 01:26:11.520
The Yule Man is here for the twelfth night.

01:26:11.520 --> 01:26:15.239
The Weissnacht is finally upon you.

01:26:15.239 --> 01:26:17.790
At this point, one of two scenarios will happen.

01:26:17.790 --> 01:26:22.880
In the first, you and your entire family will
be tortured and murdered, except the youngest

01:26:22.880 --> 01:26:25.599
child, who the Yule Man will kidnap.

01:26:25.599 --> 01:26:30.770
The SCP Foundation keeps files on a number
of notable instances of this kind of Weissnacht,

01:26:30.770 --> 01:26:33.580
and the details are truly gruesome.

01:26:33.580 --> 01:26:38.600
Reports of incidents have involved crucifixion,
the removal of tongues, burning, dismemberment,

01:26:38.600 --> 01:26:41.960
post mortem bitemarks, and decapitation.

01:26:41.960 --> 01:26:47.330
In all instances though, the entire family
was killed except the youngest child, who

01:26:47.330 --> 01:26:48.719
simply disappeared.

01:26:48.719 --> 01:26:51.230
The Yule Man is a merciless and sadistic beast.

01:26:51.230 --> 01:26:55.489
You’re now probably wondering: If that’s
the first of two Weissnacht possibilities,

01:26:55.489 --> 01:26:57.000
what’s the second?

01:26:57.000 --> 01:27:02.230
In the second, if you’re tremendously lucky,
you and your family will survive – but that

01:27:02.230 --> 01:27:05.530
doesn’t mean you won’t face a grisly experience.

01:27:05.530 --> 01:27:10.000
In this scenario, which occurs during about
fifteen percent of Weissnacht Events, you’ll

01:27:10.000 --> 01:27:14.219
hear footsteps throughout the night, but thankfully,
you wake up alive.

01:27:14.219 --> 01:27:17.710
And when you do so, there are gifts waiting
for you.

01:27:17.710 --> 01:27:21.870
The problem is, all these gifts are made out
of human body parts.

01:27:21.870 --> 01:27:28.270
For example, in 1976 in Canada, one family
received the gift of a ball made from a severed

01:27:28.270 --> 01:27:30.090
human head wrapped in skin.

01:27:30.090 --> 01:27:36.420
In Kazakhstan in 1903, a family received a
flute made from a hollowed out human femur.

01:27:36.420 --> 01:27:42.230
And in the Netherlands in 2003, a family received
a wooden hairbrush, covered in human teeth

01:27:42.230 --> 01:27:46.900
ranging from 400 years old to a mere few days.

01:27:46.900 --> 01:27:53.040
These gruesome gifts are referred to as SCP
– 4666 – A, and it was one of these gifts

01:27:53.040 --> 01:27:58.650
that gave us the best insight yet available
into the true nature of the Yule Man.

01:27:58.650 --> 01:28:03.960
Several gifts were dropped off at a family's
residence in Hoonah, Alaska, in 2018, but

01:28:03.960 --> 01:28:14.520
most notable among them was the horrific SCP-4666-A-0960
– a life-sized doll made from a human body,

01:28:14.520 --> 01:28:17.750
with its eyes removed and mouth sewn shut.

01:28:17.750 --> 01:28:21.570
Worst of all though, was that the girl was
still alive.

01:28:21.570 --> 01:28:25.590
The family who received this twisted gift
was given amnestics by the Foundation, and

01:28:25.590 --> 01:28:28.550
the living doll was taken for medical treatment.

01:28:28.550 --> 01:28:33.360
Before succumbing to her extensive injuries,
the girl was able to deliver some insights

01:28:33.360 --> 01:28:38.460
into what exactly happened to the children
who were abducted during Weissnacht Events.

01:28:38.460 --> 01:28:43.050
The children taken by the Yule Man are forced
into a large sack that seems much bigger on

01:28:43.050 --> 01:28:49.110
the inside than it appears as he makes his
rounds, travelling from house to house, murdering

01:28:49.110 --> 01:28:50.290
and kidnapping.

01:28:50.290 --> 01:28:55.701
His victims are taken to a kind of underground
grotto and workshop filled with bones, like

01:28:55.701 --> 01:29:00.300
a twisted Santa’s workshop, where they’re
forced to make toys out of the bodies of their

01:29:00.300 --> 01:29:02.090
fellow victims.

01:29:02.090 --> 01:29:07.060
During this time, the Yule Man will continue
to torture and torment his victims.

01:29:07.060 --> 01:29:11.949
He’ll even take some of them away to cook
and eat whenever he feels like it.

01:29:11.949 --> 01:29:16.670
When asked how she was turned into this human
doll, the girl told Foundation personnel that

01:29:16.670 --> 01:29:21.369
her fellow victims were forced to turn her
into this by the Yule Man when she became

01:29:21.369 --> 01:29:23.990
too weak to continue making toys herself.

01:29:23.990 --> 01:29:31.730
Her chilling last words were, “When you
can’t make the toys, you become the toys.”

01:29:31.730 --> 01:29:36.530
So if strange things happen to you and your
family between the 21st of December and the

01:29:36.530 --> 01:29:38.719
1st of January, don’t ignore it.

01:29:38.719 --> 01:29:41.829
After all, you never know who’s watching.

01:29:41.829 --> 01:29:47.360
But if it is the Yule Man’s grinning face
pressed up against your window, it may already

01:29:47.360 --> 01:29:49.480
be too late.

01:29:49.480 --> 01:29:53.070
Happy Holidays…

01:29:53.070 --> 01:29:57.730
In a remote part of Russia, a mysterious disease
outbreak was tearing through a tiny farming

01:29:57.730 --> 01:30:00.430
village with terrifying side effects.

01:30:00.430 --> 01:30:05.909
There was no cure, no clue to where it came
from, and worst of all, the disease’s terrifying

01:30:05.909 --> 01:30:08.250
impact didn’t end with death.

01:30:08.250 --> 01:30:14.320
No, it was after those carrying the disease
died, that the real horror started.

01:30:14.320 --> 01:30:18.730
After an agonizing fever that leaves the victims
writhing in pain, they quickly succumb to

01:30:18.730 --> 01:30:23.340
the disease, only to rise from their graves
to wreak havoc on the living.

01:30:23.340 --> 01:30:28.150
The virus continues to spread, until the corpses
outnumber those trying to hide from them,

01:30:28.150 --> 01:30:30.949
as the world spirals into almost certain ruin.

01:30:30.949 --> 01:30:35.730
It sounds like the plot of a zombie movie,
but for the SCP Foundation this is anything

01:30:35.730 --> 01:30:40.550
but fiction, and the terror that unfolded
in that little Siberian town is the first

01:30:40.550 --> 01:30:47.090
recorded encounter with SCP - 610, also known
as, The Flesh That Hates.

01:30:47.090 --> 01:30:49.880
First, livestock began to vanish from farms.

01:30:49.880 --> 01:30:55.080
Theft or wild animals were suspected, but
no suspects could be found, and no mutilated

01:30:55.080 --> 01:30:56.510
remains turned up.

01:30:56.510 --> 01:31:00.880
The animals weren’t being stolen, and they
weren’t being eaten, so…what happened

01:31:00.880 --> 01:31:01.880
to them?

01:31:01.880 --> 01:31:06.361
With no more animals left to lose, the farmers
themselves then began to disappear, but the

01:31:06.361 --> 01:31:10.020
authorities refused to take the missing persons
cases seriously.

01:31:10.020 --> 01:31:14.340
The missing farmers’ families would contact
the police, make a report, and then the whole

01:31:14.340 --> 01:31:15.830
thing was forgotten.

01:31:15.830 --> 01:31:20.330
It was written off just as another unsolved
disappearance, which wasn’t uncommon in

01:31:20.330 --> 01:31:22.389
the wild and unforgiving region.

01:31:22.389 --> 01:31:26.230
Then the police themselves began to disappear.

01:31:26.230 --> 01:31:30.200
The families of the missing farmers would
sometimes report strange sounds from the surrounding

01:31:30.200 --> 01:31:34.970
woods, describing moans and inhuman screeches
of pain.

01:31:34.970 --> 01:31:39.190
One young boy reported seeing a cow with what
he described as “tentacles” lurking around

01:31:39.190 --> 01:31:41.060
the edge of the trees.

01:31:41.060 --> 01:31:45.260
Regional police were dispatched to the location,
and ordered to investigate and report back

01:31:45.260 --> 01:31:47.329
on their findings within 24 hours.

01:31:47.329 --> 01:31:53.239
But the units sent to the area didn’t report
back, and were never heard from again.

01:31:53.239 --> 01:31:57.830
Upon learning of the reports, the Russian
government grew increasingly concerned, fearing

01:31:57.830 --> 01:32:01.449
domestic insurgency or foreign espionage of
some kind could be at play.

01:32:01.449 --> 01:32:07.960
They sent a small team of special agents to
the area, and, one by one, those agents disappeared,

01:32:07.960 --> 01:32:09.740
just like the others before them.

01:32:09.740 --> 01:32:13.920
It seemed no one who went into the village
after the disappearances started ever came

01:32:13.920 --> 01:32:15.230
out again.

01:32:15.230 --> 01:32:17.790
They had all simply vanished.

01:32:17.790 --> 01:32:21.270
Desperate for answers, the Russian government
contacted the only people in the world who

01:32:21.270 --> 01:32:23.630
could help - The SCP Foundation.

01:32:23.630 --> 01:32:28.159
What the Foundation found over the course
of their investigation would shock and unnerve

01:32:28.159 --> 01:32:32.450
them, going beyond anything they had previously
discovered.

01:32:32.450 --> 01:32:36.679
Before the investigation officially began,
the affected area was sealed off by the Russian

01:32:36.679 --> 01:32:37.690
government.

01:32:37.690 --> 01:32:42.239
Not knowing if it would be safe to send researchers
into the containment perimeter, the Foundation

01:32:42.239 --> 01:32:47.290
set up a small camera mounted unit, nicknamed
Herbie, to capture footage of whatever remained

01:32:47.290 --> 01:32:48.369
of the village.

01:32:48.369 --> 01:32:53.170
The images captured by Herbie revealed what
exactly had become of the people in this doomed

01:32:53.170 --> 01:32:57.639
village, and the true, nightmarish nature
of SCP-610.

01:32:57.639 --> 01:33:04.270
SCP-610 is a Keter-class entity, meaning it’s
an anomaly that’s exceedingly difficult

01:33:04.270 --> 01:33:09.070
to contain consistently or reliably, with
containment procedures often being extensive

01:33:09.070 --> 01:33:10.199
and complex.

01:33:10.199 --> 01:33:15.580
610 is a highly contagious skin disease that
initially manifests like an ordinary allergic

01:33:15.580 --> 01:33:20.040
reaction, with symptoms including increased
sensitivity, itching, and a rash.

01:33:20.040 --> 01:33:24.530
But within just three hours of those initial
symptoms appearing, the rash starts to turn

01:33:24.530 --> 01:33:28.079
into masses of scar tissue on the chest and
arms.

01:33:28.079 --> 01:33:32.520
These masses spread over the legs and back
of the victim, and completely consume them

01:33:32.520 --> 01:33:36.280
in thick, rubbery flesh within five hours.

01:33:36.280 --> 01:33:39.640
Once they’re covered, the victim will cease
all vital functions.

01:33:39.640 --> 01:33:44.360
Unfortunately for them, and doubly so for
those around them, they do not stay dead.

01:33:44.360 --> 01:33:48.530
About three minutes after expiring, the victim’s
vitals will restart at a heightened rate,

01:33:48.530 --> 01:33:53.410
and the masses of flesh encasing their body
will begin to move and multiply, mutating

01:33:53.410 --> 01:33:57.250
them into a form beyond anything resembling
the human they once were.

01:33:57.250 --> 01:34:01.800
The specific type of mutation varies from
case to case, but has included the head becoming

01:34:01.800 --> 01:34:08.210
massive and bulbous, the growth of extra limbs,
and, in especially gruesome cases, the victim’s

01:34:08.210 --> 01:34:13.349
body splitting apart to allow extra tendrils
of flesh to sprout from the open wound.

01:34:13.349 --> 01:34:17.489
Occasionally, an infected person will stop
moving and become rooted to the ground in

01:34:17.489 --> 01:34:19.180
a set location.

01:34:19.180 --> 01:34:23.780
Once it is settled, their flesh will spread
itself across the ground, encasing all nearby

01:34:23.780 --> 01:34:26.190
objects in flaps of scar tissue.

01:34:26.190 --> 01:34:30.679
The infected that maintain their mobility
are highly aggressive, even violent, and will

01:34:30.679 --> 01:34:34.730
attempt to infect any living thing that comes
into their line of sight.

01:34:34.730 --> 01:34:38.961
The disease does not only infect humans, and
can take over any living organism within a

01:34:38.961 --> 01:34:40.739
matter of hours.

01:34:40.739 --> 01:34:45.010
Due to the highly contagious and dangerous
nature of the disease, safe observation of

01:34:45.010 --> 01:34:50.480
infected specimens and areas is only possible
with drones and mounted cameras.

01:34:50.480 --> 01:34:55.190
This brings us back to Herbie, the first such
mounted camera to record footage of the infected

01:34:55.190 --> 01:34:56.210
area.

01:34:56.210 --> 01:35:00.880
Herbie was deployed into the infection site,
also known as Site A, without any damage.

01:35:00.880 --> 01:35:05.760
It remained at the outside perimeter of the
village for two hours, observing several infected

01:35:05.760 --> 01:35:10.480
humans, and fire damage to many of the homes,
before following an infected into an intact

01:35:10.480 --> 01:35:11.480
house.

01:35:11.480 --> 01:35:15.090
Herbie’s camera feed captured the infected
person entering the house and sitting down

01:35:15.090 --> 01:35:16.260
at the table inside.

01:35:16.260 --> 01:35:21.730
There were several other infected humans in
the house, and one unidentified infected creature

01:35:21.730 --> 01:35:24.400
that remained immobile under the table.

01:35:24.400 --> 01:35:28.409
After viciously assaulting one of the other
infected humans, the infected returned to

01:35:28.409 --> 01:35:31.840
the table and began to lay out plates on top
of it.

01:35:31.840 --> 01:35:37.070
Pieces of its flesh began to wriggle and tear
away from its body, before settling onto each

01:35:37.070 --> 01:35:38.070
plate.

01:35:38.070 --> 01:35:41.619
Once the plates were filled, the infected
sitting at the table began to grab at the

01:35:41.619 --> 01:35:47.690
flesh and crush it into their mouths, in a
perverse imitation of a normal mealtime gathering.

01:35:47.690 --> 01:35:51.909
After capturing this stomach-churning display,
Herbie left the house and continued to explore

01:35:51.909 --> 01:35:52.909
the village.

01:35:52.909 --> 01:35:56.830
It recorded footage of a large stack of bodies
that seemed to be made up of both Russian

01:35:56.830 --> 01:36:00.880
military and civilians, with an infected sitting
on top.

01:36:00.880 --> 01:36:04.840
As Herbie maneuvered toward the remains of
the town hall, an infected grabbed the rover

01:36:04.840 --> 01:36:05.840
off of the ground.

01:36:05.840 --> 01:36:10.000
Herbie’s camera was able to capture the
face of the infected that grabbed the rover.

01:36:10.000 --> 01:36:15.890
The face was that of a young girl around ten
years old, strangely intact atop a large,

01:36:15.890 --> 01:36:17.020
distorted body.

01:36:17.020 --> 01:36:21.449
The final moments of Herbie’s camera feed
captured the infected girl’s face bursting

01:36:21.449 --> 01:36:26.110
open, revealing tendrils of flesh that pulled
Herbie into the gaping maw.

01:36:26.110 --> 01:36:28.900
Then, the feed cut to black.

01:36:28.900 --> 01:36:33.790
Herbie was regarded as lost, but the video
feed briefly resumed five hours later, showing

01:36:33.790 --> 01:36:37.000
the camera covered with an unidentified slime.

01:36:37.000 --> 01:36:42.050
After this, the video feed was cut for good,
and Herbie abandoned in Site A.

01:36:42.050 --> 01:36:46.559
The Foundation has sent several manned expeditions
into Site A, where many expedition forces

01:36:46.559 --> 01:36:49.020
have fallen victim to the infected.

01:36:49.020 --> 01:36:53.550
Several operatives were also lost in an earthquake
that revealed a network of underground tunnels.

01:36:53.550 --> 01:36:57.619
A manned expedition into these tunnels was
attempted, and the video feed that was captured

01:36:57.619 --> 01:37:01.230
by the researchers on the expedition was deeply
disturbing.

01:37:01.230 --> 01:37:06.050
There were images of an abandoned church filled
with infected, and a mass of uninfected or

01:37:06.050 --> 01:37:08.790
partially infected human captives.

01:37:08.790 --> 01:37:12.960
The final moments of the video feed from this
expedition captured several operatives being

01:37:12.960 --> 01:37:18.199
murdered by an infected human wielding a farming
scythe, indicating that the infected are capable

01:37:18.199 --> 01:37:21.989
of using simple weaponry in addition to brute
force.

01:37:21.989 --> 01:37:26.710
The use of this weapon, paired with the presence
of captives in the underground tunnels, paints

01:37:26.710 --> 01:37:31.260
a terrifying picture of the kind of organization
the infected are capable of.

01:37:31.260 --> 01:37:37.110
No more manned expeditions have been attempted,
or, if they have, they have been highly classified.

01:37:37.110 --> 01:37:42.190
Ordinarily, once a new SCP is discovered,
it is placed in containment at the Foundation,

01:37:42.190 --> 01:37:46.230
with special procedures in place, so that
it can be studied or even neutralized in the

01:37:46.230 --> 01:37:48.760
rare occasions where it’s deemed necessary.

01:37:48.760 --> 01:37:53.739
When it comes to SCP-610 though, containment
might just be impossible.

01:37:53.739 --> 01:37:58.969
It simply covers too much area, and is too
dangerous to expose to human researchers.

01:37:58.969 --> 01:38:03.790
Instead, all infected areas have been isolated
with the permission of the Russian government.

01:38:03.790 --> 01:38:07.750
There is an official perimeter established
around these areas, and any civilians that

01:38:07.750 --> 01:38:12.130
approach them are told to leave under the
pretense of ongoing military operations.

01:38:12.130 --> 01:38:16.719
For once, a top secret military project is
the more innocent answer.

01:38:16.719 --> 01:38:20.760
Armed guards are placed at the perimeter of
every infected area, and any living thing

01:38:20.760 --> 01:38:26.350
with symptoms of SCP-610 spotted near the
perimeter is to be immobilized, killed, and

01:38:26.350 --> 01:38:28.830
burned from as far away as possible.

01:38:28.830 --> 01:38:34.760
Any living thing that comes in contact with
SCP-610, whether a soldier, a scientist, or

01:38:34.760 --> 01:38:39.400
a civilian, is immediately terminated, and
their remains destroyed.

01:38:39.400 --> 01:38:43.360
If someone comes within three meters of an
infected organism, they will be quarantined

01:38:43.360 --> 01:38:46.800
and remotely examined to determine if they
have been infected.

01:38:46.800 --> 01:38:51.930
While the spread of SCP-610 can be airborne,
it has been determined to be far less contagious

01:38:51.930 --> 01:38:56.219
when spread through air particles as opposed
to physical contact.

01:38:56.219 --> 01:39:01.190
The infection sites remain active to this
day, like modern day leper colonies.

01:39:01.190 --> 01:39:05.400
Though they are isolated from the general
population, and the military is doing everything

01:39:05.400 --> 01:39:11.389
in their power to contain the infected, SCP-610
is still very much alive.

01:39:11.389 --> 01:39:16.469
It is rare for an entity to exist that the
Foundation cannot truly contain, but can only

01:39:16.469 --> 01:39:21.240
try to guard against, and that makes this
infection all the more terrifying.

01:39:21.240 --> 01:39:26.349
Who knows how much it has mutated over the
years, growing, spreading, hungry for new

01:39:26.349 --> 01:39:27.349
hosts?

01:39:27.349 --> 01:39:32.030
There is still so much that the Foundation
does not know about the Flesh That Hates,

01:39:32.030 --> 01:39:37.290
such as how it works, what it can do, or even
where it came from, since the origin of the

01:39:37.290 --> 01:39:40.790
first infection is still, at this point, entirely
unknown.

01:39:40.790 --> 01:39:46.260
It has shown itself to be capable of learning,
planning, and protecting itself, so who is

01:39:46.260 --> 01:39:50.290
to say that it couldn’t figure out a way
to escape from its isolated area?

01:39:50.290 --> 01:39:56.120
It is so highly contagious, and spreads so
quickly, that just one tiny, infected rabbit,

01:39:56.120 --> 01:40:02.070
and one inattentive soldier, could be enough
for SCP-610 to reach the general population.

01:40:02.070 --> 01:40:09.239
If it did, its violent, destructive nature
and hatred for all life would mean that everything,

01:40:09.239 --> 01:40:15.840
not just the people but animals, plants, and
the world itself, could be at risk.

01:40:15.840 --> 01:40:18.130
And no one is ready for this kind of infection.

01:40:18.130 --> 01:40:23.880
A disease that turns the human body against
itself, turns our skin into a weapon and a

01:40:23.880 --> 01:40:29.489
tomb, stripping away identity, humanity, and
everything that isn’t made of that same

01:40:29.489 --> 01:40:30.580
hateful flesh.

01:40:30.580 --> 01:40:36.630
So, let’s hope that the perimeter holds,
and, the next time you feel a little itchy,

01:40:36.630 --> 01:40:40.239
try not to think about what might happen next.

01:40:40.239 --> 01:40:46.770
It was November 20th, 2019, and the helicopter
circled far above in the freezing wind of

01:40:46.770 --> 01:40:47.929
the Antarctic.

01:40:47.929 --> 01:40:53.469
SCP Foundation Site Director Jason Monroe
looked down at the isolated above-ground facilities

01:40:53.469 --> 01:40:55.480
of Provisional Site-344-1.

01:40:55.480 --> 01:40:58.619
Something about this place made him nervous.

01:40:58.619 --> 01:40:59.619
Edgy.

01:40:59.619 --> 01:41:06.679
And for good reason: Between 2003 and 2019,
twenty-nine Mobile Task Force units and seventy-three

01:41:06.679 --> 01:41:11.180
members of D-Class personnel had gone missing
here and never been found.

01:41:11.180 --> 01:41:17.480
Monroe thought he was here for a routine investigation
into negligence and mismanagement, but little

01:41:17.480 --> 01:41:20.560
did he know, he was in for so much more.

01:41:20.560 --> 01:41:28.050
This is the story of SCP - 5545, and one man’s
journey into his own worst nightmare.

01:41:28.050 --> 01:41:29.050
Literally.

01:41:29.050 --> 01:41:33.130
But this nightmare began a long time ago - 300
years, to be exact.

01:41:33.130 --> 01:41:37.059
And like most nightmares, it started as a
dream.

01:41:37.059 --> 01:41:41.639
That dream was one of expansion - national
powers across Europe wanted to be the first

01:41:41.639 --> 01:41:47.170
to conquer the globe and expand into new territories,
and sent countless exploratory missions off

01:41:47.170 --> 01:41:50.030
into the unknown to achieve this goal.

01:41:50.030 --> 01:41:54.300
Any history book will tell you that the first
outsiders to lay eyes upon the continent of

01:41:54.300 --> 01:41:59.889
Antarctica did so in 1820 - the reality is
that the first ones to get there actually

01:41:59.889 --> 01:42:02.480
landed in the late 1700s.

01:42:02.480 --> 01:42:08.119
The hapless explorers ventured into mainland
Antarctica and made base camps, before searching

01:42:08.119 --> 01:42:11.260
and digging for any useful resources nearby.

01:42:11.260 --> 01:42:16.200
They came upon a strange discovery: A hallway,
hidden beneath the ice.

01:42:16.200 --> 01:42:21.830
Not a passage in the ice, but a true hallway
- complete with light fixtures.

01:42:21.830 --> 01:42:26.829
The confused explorers ventured down into
these impossible hallways, and for many of

01:42:26.829 --> 01:42:30.150
them, it would be the last thing they ever
did.

01:42:30.150 --> 01:42:34.809
No matter how long they walked, it seemed
like the hallways just kept going.

01:42:34.809 --> 01:42:39.480
As they continued to walk for hours, they
hoped they’d find something… anything.

01:42:39.480 --> 01:42:41.119
And eventually, they did.

01:42:41.119 --> 01:42:45.929
They passed from these hallways into somewhere
different altogether, and most of them were

01:42:45.929 --> 01:42:47.889
never heard from again.

01:42:47.889 --> 01:42:52.960
Those who did manage to escape often died
or took their own lives soon after.

01:42:52.960 --> 01:42:57.560
Whatever it was they’d discovered down there,
they didn’t want to live with it on their

01:42:57.560 --> 01:42:58.560
minds.

01:42:58.560 --> 01:43:02.560
It’s believed that over seventy colonial
explorers disappeared or died this way and

01:43:02.560 --> 01:43:07.450
that most who found these endless hallways
beneath the Antarctic ice never returned.

01:43:07.450 --> 01:43:13.949
The multiple anomalous objects and phenomena
that make up SCP-5545 came into the Foundation’s

01:43:13.949 --> 01:43:19.699
hands several centuries later on September
18th, 2003, when during an expedition into

01:43:19.699 --> 01:43:23.280
the Antarctic, they too found the endless
hallways.

01:43:23.280 --> 01:43:28.580
The Foundation built Provisional Site-344-1
around them, hoping to safely seal them off

01:43:28.580 --> 01:43:32.540
from any other unwitting Antarctic explorers
or researchers.

01:43:32.540 --> 01:43:36.440
But there was something else lurking beneath
the ice in Antarctica.

01:43:36.440 --> 01:43:37.570
Something dangerous.

01:43:37.570 --> 01:43:43.829
The hallways were designated as SCP - 5545
- 1 and were thought to be the extent of the

01:43:43.829 --> 01:43:50.699
anomalous activity at the site, but soon SCP
- 5545 - 2 was discovered, which resulted

01:43:50.699 --> 01:43:53.500
in the deaths of sixteen researchers.

01:43:53.500 --> 01:43:56.060
So what exactly is 5545 - 2?

01:43:56.060 --> 01:44:01.329
It’s an entity so volatile that even knowing
about it is considered to be a containment

01:44:01.329 --> 01:44:06.250
breach, and - as a result - it’s kept in
Provisional Site-344-2.

01:44:06.250 --> 01:44:12.639
Unlike Site - 344 - 1, 344 - 2 isn’t a physical
space.

01:44:12.639 --> 01:44:17.420
It’s conceptual, accessible only through
the endless hallways, created with the express

01:44:17.420 --> 01:44:23.070
purpose of keeping 5545 - 1 and 5545 - 2 separate.

01:44:23.070 --> 01:44:24.070
Why?

01:44:24.070 --> 01:44:30.480
Because whenever the two come into contact,
the result is 5545 - 3: The network of endless

01:44:30.480 --> 01:44:32.350
hallways expanding.

01:44:32.350 --> 01:44:36.790
If they remained in contact, the hallways
would continue to expand and the entire planet

01:44:36.790 --> 01:44:40.460
could be filled with endless hallways in just
four to six hours.

01:44:40.460 --> 01:44:47.389
While the two are apart though, 5545 - 3 reverses,
but it always would take just a few hours

01:44:47.389 --> 01:44:52.159
to throw the whole world into a chaos of infinite
hallways.

01:44:52.159 --> 01:44:55.699
SCP-5545 has been given the classification
“Safe”…

01:44:55.699 --> 01:45:00.330
Wait, we’re dealing with a mysterious and
volatile anomaly that’s claimed a huge number

01:45:00.330 --> 01:45:06.210
of lives and still somehow eludes true Foundation
understanding, yet the official SCP Foundation

01:45:06.210 --> 01:45:07.880
classification is “Safe?”

01:45:07.880 --> 01:45:09.510
How could this be?

01:45:09.510 --> 01:45:14.520
Monroe was the Director of Site - 58, and
was the definition of no-nonsense.

01:45:14.520 --> 01:45:18.401
Prior to taking the Site Director position,
he was a decorated member of Mobile Task Force

01:45:18.401 --> 01:45:21.969
Eta-10 and helped contain numerous Keter-Class
anomalies.

01:45:21.969 --> 01:45:26.630
He’d been around the proverbial block when
it came to anomalous activity, and something

01:45:26.630 --> 01:45:34.190
about SCP - 5545, and the management of Provisional
Site 344, seemed awfully suspicious to him.

01:45:34.190 --> 01:45:36.180
And he had questions.

01:45:36.180 --> 01:45:39.950
Like how such an unpredictable anomaly could
be declared “safe”?

01:45:39.950 --> 01:45:44.639
And why had there been such a lapse of communication
between the Foundation and Doctor Gabriel

01:45:44.639 --> 01:45:48.119
Reed, who’d been running the facility for
the past two decades?

01:45:48.119 --> 01:45:54.429
And most of all, just what exactly was the
mysterious SCP - 5545 - 2?

01:45:54.429 --> 01:45:59.340
Monroe started to believe that something terrible
had happened at the site, and Reed was covering

01:45:59.340 --> 01:46:00.340
it all up.

01:46:00.340 --> 01:46:05.710
But to find out for sure, he’d need to go
to Antarctica and investigate it himself.

01:46:05.710 --> 01:46:09.790
Information around this supposedly “Safe”
anomaly was highly classified - those without

01:46:09.790 --> 01:46:12.460
O5 clearance could face termination for snooping.

01:46:12.460 --> 01:46:14.469
But that didn’t scare Jason Monroe.

01:46:14.469 --> 01:46:18.110
He’d dealt with Keters before, he could
deal with this.

01:46:18.110 --> 01:46:19.699
Or so he thought.

01:46:19.699 --> 01:46:24.059
Monroe submitted a request and was granted
unanimous approval by the O5 Council to travel

01:46:24.059 --> 01:46:28.270
to Provisional Site 344 and get to the bottom
of this mystery.

01:46:28.270 --> 01:46:32.960
He took a chopper to the base soon after,
armed with a concealed firearm and a Hostile

01:46:32.960 --> 01:46:38.599
Meme Detector - or HMD - to test whether the
base and its staff had somehow fallen under

01:46:38.599 --> 01:46:42.360
a hazardous memetic effect from SCP - 5545.

01:46:42.360 --> 01:46:46.079
He’d find the answers, or die trying.

01:46:46.079 --> 01:46:50.659
The moment Monroe arrived, he couldn’t help
but notice the strange way the staff behaved.

01:46:50.659 --> 01:46:53.500
They seemed listless; almost depressive.

01:46:53.500 --> 01:46:59.580
When he showed his credentials to a researcher,
they simply said “SCP-5545-2 is contained

01:46:59.580 --> 01:47:01.710
in Site-344-2.”

01:47:01.710 --> 01:47:04.849
His request to see Dr. Reed that night was
denied.

01:47:04.849 --> 01:47:07.239
Dr. Reed was busy, he was told.

01:47:07.239 --> 01:47:08.540
Wait until tomorrow.

01:47:08.540 --> 01:47:13.309
The next day, Monroe met with Dr. Reed, but
the results of the meeting were underwhelming

01:47:13.309 --> 01:47:14.890
to say the least.

01:47:14.890 --> 01:47:19.400
Just like the rest of the staff on the site,
he seemed exhausted, as though he hadn’t

01:47:19.400 --> 01:47:20.590
slept in days.

01:47:20.590 --> 01:47:25.210
His responses were quiet and evasive, and
he refused to tell Monroe anything that wasn’t

01:47:25.210 --> 01:47:27.179
in the official files already.

01:47:27.179 --> 01:47:31.730
Monroe ran the conversation through the HMD
and found nothing out of the ordinary.

01:47:31.730 --> 01:47:32.869
What was going on here?

01:47:32.869 --> 01:47:36.230
Monroe was irritated, but not deterred.

01:47:36.230 --> 01:47:39.370
Nothing would stop him from finding out the
truth.

01:47:39.370 --> 01:47:44.619
The next day, he flexed his O5 credentials
and hacked into the base’s security system.

01:47:44.619 --> 01:47:49.929
This gave him access to cameras around Site
- 344 -1, but more importantly, there was

01:47:49.929 --> 01:47:54.540
a single camera inside the mysterious Site
- 344 - 2.

01:47:54.540 --> 01:47:55.540
Jackpot.

01:47:55.540 --> 01:48:03.349
But when he looked at it, the feed was an
entirely black screen with the words “SCP-5545-2

01:48:03.349 --> 01:48:06.199
is contained in Site-344-2.”

01:48:06.199 --> 01:48:12.250
The footage of the staff in 344 - 1 was equally
strange: The eighteen employees on site all

01:48:12.250 --> 01:48:16.700
sat at computer banks, with nothing but static
playing on their screens.

01:48:16.700 --> 01:48:21.540
Monroe kept digging though, and was able to
hack into the security footage of Dr. Reed’s

01:48:21.540 --> 01:48:22.540
office.

01:48:22.540 --> 01:48:27.090
As he watched, he discovered a fifteen minute
period where Reed left the office each day.

01:48:27.090 --> 01:48:34.580
He could use this brief window to break in
and collect more intel on SCP - 5545 - 2.

01:48:34.580 --> 01:48:38.909
Monroe was so wrapped up in the investigation
that he almost forgot the more immediate danger

01:48:38.909 --> 01:48:45.320
around him, and nearly wandered into one of
the endless hallways of 5545 - 1 by mistake.

01:48:45.320 --> 01:48:48.440
He made a note to be more careful in future...

01:48:48.440 --> 01:48:53.159
His first attempt at breaking into Dr. Reed’s
office didn’t produce many answers - one

01:48:53.159 --> 01:48:57.180
piece of evidence was a blurry picture of
what looked like a Mobile Task Force entering

01:48:57.180 --> 01:49:00.690
a 5545 - 1 hallway in the dark.

01:49:00.690 --> 01:49:04.929
Another was a spreadsheet featuring all the
personnel, living or dead, who’d worked

01:49:04.929 --> 01:49:10.429
at the site - but one name, and the details
of whether this person was alive or dead,

01:49:10.429 --> 01:49:12.400
was completely redacted.

01:49:12.400 --> 01:49:15.570
Anything particularly juicy was hidden behind
O5 clearance.

01:49:15.570 --> 01:49:20.159
If Monroe wanted the answers, he’d need
to break through.

01:49:20.159 --> 01:49:25.429
That night, he had a horrific recurring nightmare,
one that had plagued him since he joined MTF

01:49:25.429 --> 01:49:26.429
Eta-10.

01:49:26.429 --> 01:49:29.760
He dreamed he was in a fancy dining room with
a grand fireplace.

01:49:29.760 --> 01:49:32.599
The room was full of statues of men and women.

01:49:32.599 --> 01:49:35.749
The men looked angry, and the women looked
afraid.

01:49:35.749 --> 01:49:40.900
As he approached the fireplace, the ceiling
extended infinitely up into the darkness.

01:49:40.900 --> 01:49:45.550
Suddenly, the zombie-like body of a teenage
girl appears in the fireplace, hanging from

01:49:45.550 --> 01:49:46.550
a long thread.

01:49:46.550 --> 01:49:51.981
Her eyes look furious and full of rage, and
Monroe somehow knows that he’s the reason

01:49:51.981 --> 01:49:53.200
for her hate.

01:49:53.200 --> 01:49:58.190
When he steps into the fireplace in this dream,
she attacks him, the two intertwine, and they

01:49:58.190 --> 01:49:59.190
burn forever.

01:49:59.190 --> 01:50:04.179
The one difference was that in this new iteration
of the dream, he blinked upon entering the

01:50:04.179 --> 01:50:07.389
fireplace, and suddenly, he was in a hallway.

01:50:07.389 --> 01:50:12.080
He awoke sure that something was terribly
wrong here, but he couldn’t give up now.

01:50:12.080 --> 01:50:16.449
The next day, Monroe broke into Dr. Reed’s
office and made a horrifying discovery.

01:50:16.449 --> 01:50:22.540
He found files indicating that Dr. Reed was
knowingly sending Mobile Task Forces and D-Class

01:50:22.540 --> 01:50:27.320
personnel into the infinite hallways of 5545
- 1 to their doom.

01:50:27.320 --> 01:50:32.540
He also found evidence that Reed and the researchers
had been spying on him, somehow intercepting

01:50:32.540 --> 01:50:34.619
copies of the notes he had been taking.

01:50:34.619 --> 01:50:37.780
That’s when Dr. Reed entered the office
and interrupted him.

01:50:37.780 --> 01:50:41.290
Monroe panicked and drew his weapon, holding
the doctor at gunpoint.

01:50:41.290 --> 01:50:46.449
He was breaking so many Foundation rules,
but right now, he feared for his life.

01:50:46.449 --> 01:50:49.239
The doctor seemed unbothered by Monroe’s
threats though.

01:50:49.239 --> 01:50:54.460
He told Monroe that everything was going to
plan, and that he should go back to his room.

01:50:54.460 --> 01:50:59.070
Monroe was becoming increasingly paranoid
- he felt that, at any moment, guards might

01:50:59.070 --> 01:51:01.119
burst in and execute him.

01:51:01.119 --> 01:51:02.650
Nothing about this place made sense.

01:51:02.650 --> 01:51:05.689
He worried he was going insane.

01:51:05.689 --> 01:51:10.711
Perhaps the only way to find answers was to
go even deeper: To risk it all, and venture

01:51:10.711 --> 01:51:18.579
through the endless hallways to find SCP - 5545
- 2 himself, and finally discover what this

01:51:18.579 --> 01:51:20.760
thing actually was.

01:51:20.760 --> 01:51:25.691
Monroe left his room and stepped into one
of the endless hallways of 5545 - 1 that was

01:51:25.691 --> 01:51:28.130
located just across from his dorm.

01:51:28.130 --> 01:51:33.100
He found that it was a hallway like all the
others on site - Plain concrete, worn with

01:51:33.100 --> 01:51:35.820
age, with simple light fixtures on the walls.

01:51:35.820 --> 01:51:38.920
He walked for hours, recording with a concealed
device.

01:51:38.920 --> 01:51:43.080
The lights suddenly went out, leaving him
in complete darkness.

01:51:43.080 --> 01:51:48.070
When they flicked back on, he was in a very
different environment: A grand, old carpeted

01:51:48.070 --> 01:51:50.869
hallway, the kind you’d see in an old mansion.

01:51:50.869 --> 01:51:52.960
He broke into a cold sweat.

01:51:52.960 --> 01:51:58.260
What was so familiar about this place?He kept
walking, wracked with terror, until this new

01:51:58.260 --> 01:52:05.260
hallway finally led him to the place he’d
been seeking: Site 344 - 2, the domain of

01:52:05.260 --> 01:52:07.070
5545 - 2.

01:52:07.070 --> 01:52:13.140
It was a large, poorly-lit room, filled with
grimacing statues and a large fireplace at

01:52:13.140 --> 01:52:14.320
the far end.

01:52:14.320 --> 01:52:20.210
It was the exact same room from Monroe’s
dream - with one horrifying difference.

01:52:20.210 --> 01:52:25.020
Monroe noticed a single white thread hanging
down from the infinite ceiling, and when he

01:52:25.020 --> 01:52:27.699
looked up to find its source, he screamed.

01:52:27.699 --> 01:52:32.340
There were hundreds of bodies hanging and
swinging from the ceiling above him - everyone

01:52:32.340 --> 01:52:39.400
who SCP - 5545 - 2 had ever killed, including
MTF members, D-Class Personnel, and even the

01:52:39.400 --> 01:52:42.889
colonial explorers from hundreds of years
before.

01:52:42.889 --> 01:52:44.710
And all of them were him.

01:52:44.710 --> 01:52:46.230
Every single one.

01:52:46.230 --> 01:52:47.800
They had his face.

01:52:47.800 --> 01:52:52.660
And there, hanging in the middle of the room
at ground level, was the body of a teenage

01:52:52.660 --> 01:52:55.310
girl, the one from his dream.

01:52:55.310 --> 01:53:00.699
In that moment, he finally recognized her:
She was the girl he killed.

01:53:00.699 --> 01:53:02.080
The first him.

01:53:02.080 --> 01:53:04.010
Hundreds of years ago.

01:53:04.010 --> 01:53:07.270
Much like Monroe, you’re probably wondering:
What is going on here?

01:53:07.270 --> 01:53:12.710
Thanks to declassified communications between
Dr. Reed and the O5 Council, we can tell you.

01:53:12.710 --> 01:53:18.119
Jason Monroe is a man who’s been reincarnated
hundreds of times over the last three hundred

01:53:18.119 --> 01:53:21.500
years, ever since he murdered a teenage girl…

01:53:21.500 --> 01:53:24.849
A girl named Emily… his daughter.

01:53:24.849 --> 01:53:31.370
This murder sparked the existence of SCP - 5545
as an eternally recurring punishment for his

01:53:31.370 --> 01:53:32.370
crimes.

01:53:32.370 --> 01:53:36.750
Since figuring this out, the Foundation has
kept tabs on Monroe’s reincarnations - whether

01:53:36.750 --> 01:53:40.949
they’re MTF members, D-Class personnel,
or even Site Directors.

01:53:40.949 --> 01:53:47.480
They see to it that these reincarnations always
find their way back to 5545 - 2 to take his

01:53:47.480 --> 01:53:52.199
punishment, and prevent the infinite hallway
expansion that threatens to destroy the world.

01:53:52.199 --> 01:53:55.990
It’s a plan everyone is in on - everyone
except him.

01:53:55.990 --> 01:54:00.389
But every time he enters that nightmare-haunting
room, it all comes rushing back.

01:54:00.389 --> 01:54:06.050
In that moment though, he knew his crime,
and he somehow knew how many times this punishment

01:54:06.050 --> 01:54:07.310
had unfolded for him.

01:54:07.310 --> 01:54:13.289
He now had two choices: Repent and accept
the punishment again, or leave and activate

01:54:13.289 --> 01:54:19.550
5545 - 3, potentially allowing the endless
tunnels to expand across the world.

01:54:19.550 --> 01:54:23.349
Like his many predecessors, Monroe made the
decent choice.

01:54:23.349 --> 01:54:28.020
He accepted his punishment and allowed his
own string to coil around him as the lights

01:54:28.020 --> 01:54:32.150
in the room went off, one by one, leaving
only darkness.

01:54:32.150 --> 01:54:37.400
Jason Monroe - that version of him, at least
- was never seen again.

01:54:37.400 --> 01:54:42.900
But The SCP Foundation is already eyeing up
his next reincarnation, and preparing to let

01:54:42.900 --> 01:54:49.000
this twisted cycle play out all over again.

01:54:49.000 --> 01:54:50.639
Stop me if you've heard this one before.

01:54:50.639 --> 01:54:55.680
A young man was driving home from work late
one rainy night when he spotted a woman in

01:54:55.680 --> 01:55:00.250
a white dress and a red sweater walking along
the shoulder of the road.

01:55:00.250 --> 01:55:04.590
Concerned for her safety, he slowed down and
rolled down the window so he could talk to

01:55:04.590 --> 01:55:05.590
her.

01:55:05.590 --> 01:55:08.980
When he asked where she was going, she said
she was walking to her parents' house.

01:55:08.980 --> 01:55:12.080
The man pulled over and offered her a ride
that she accepted.

01:55:12.080 --> 01:55:16.809
The woman gave him the address of her home,
hopped in the backseat, and the man drove

01:55:16.809 --> 01:55:17.809
off.

01:55:17.809 --> 01:55:20.989
He sensed that she must've been cold from
walking in the rain, so he cranked up the

01:55:20.989 --> 01:55:23.480
car's heater to help her dry off.

01:55:23.480 --> 01:55:27.409
Soon she removed her heavy red sweater and
placed it on the seat next to her.

01:55:27.409 --> 01:55:31.930
The man tried to make friendly conversation
- asking if the woman had a job, what she

01:55:31.930 --> 01:55:37.039
was studying at school, where she'd been that
day - but she remained quiet, staring out

01:55:37.039 --> 01:55:38.230
the window.

01:55:38.230 --> 01:55:41.110
Until they drove past an old graveyard.

01:55:41.110 --> 01:55:46.020
The woman began pounding on the glass of the
car as if she desperately wanted something.

01:55:46.020 --> 01:55:50.710
Unsure of what to do, the man pulled over,
but before he could ask her what was happening

01:55:50.710 --> 01:55:52.440
she had gotten out of the car.

01:55:52.440 --> 01:55:57.619
He exited the car to try and find her but
the woman was nowhere to be seen.

01:55:57.619 --> 01:55:59.480
She must have somehow ran off.

01:55:59.480 --> 01:56:03.000
Confused, the man got back in his car and
drove away.

01:56:03.000 --> 01:56:07.510
He went on his way and didn’t think of it
again until the next day, when he noticed

01:56:07.510 --> 01:56:10.520
her sweater was still in the back of his car.

01:56:10.520 --> 01:56:15.139
He decided to go to the house she had originally
given him the address for and give it back

01:56:15.139 --> 01:56:16.139
to her.

01:56:16.139 --> 01:56:19.909
He found the home without any trouble, but
when he knocked on the door the old woman

01:56:19.909 --> 01:56:22.469
who answered it was confused by his story.

01:56:22.469 --> 01:56:27.040
She told him that her daughter couldn't have
possibly left her sweater in his car, because

01:56:27.040 --> 01:56:30.620
she'd died in a car accident 30 years ago.

01:56:30.620 --> 01:56:34.989
The vanishing hitchhiker is a classic ghost
story, with the details varying from place

01:56:34.989 --> 01:56:38.119
to place and storyteller to storyteller.

01:56:38.119 --> 01:56:43.250
In Chicago, she goes by Resurrection Mary,
named after the graveyard she asks for rides

01:56:43.250 --> 01:56:44.250
to.

01:56:44.250 --> 01:56:50.500
In Okinawa, Japan, she's known as the Nightwalker
of Nago, and she only appears to taxi drivers.

01:56:50.500 --> 01:56:55.590
In Kent, England, she's Suzanne, a bride killed
in a car wreck on the way to her bachelorette

01:56:55.590 --> 01:56:56.590
party.

01:56:56.590 --> 01:57:00.449
In North Carolina, her name is Lydia, and
in Hawaii she's believed to be the goddess

01:57:00.449 --> 01:57:02.750
Pele in human form.

01:57:02.750 --> 01:57:07.400
But as far as our friends at the SCP Foundation
are concerned, the vanishing hitchhiker's

01:57:07.400 --> 01:57:13.090
name is Mary Talish, also known as SCP-1337.

01:57:13.090 --> 01:57:18.840
On the 19th of May, 1952, college sophomore
Mary Talish was abducted on her way to class

01:57:18.840 --> 01:57:21.310
in her hometown of Muncie, Indiana.

01:57:21.310 --> 01:57:25.429
When police found her body 2 weeks later,
her eyes and heart had been torn from her

01:57:25.429 --> 01:57:30.360
body in a ritualistic fashion, and she had
scrapes and bruises that suggested she'd been

01:57:30.360 --> 01:57:31.900
beaten before her murder.

01:57:31.900 --> 01:57:37.409
Her killers were never caught, and her body
was returned to her family for burial in Tomlinson

01:57:37.409 --> 01:57:38.650
Cemetery.

01:57:38.650 --> 01:57:44.239
Starting on the 19th of June that same year,
someone matching Mary's description - a caucasian

01:57:44.239 --> 01:57:50.409
woman with blonde hair, standing 150 cm tall
and wearing a red sweater - was spotted trying

01:57:50.409 --> 01:57:54.510
to flag down passing vehicles along Mayflower
Road.

01:57:54.510 --> 01:58:00.000
Since then, every month, on the 19th, Mary
has been sighted along that stretch of road,

01:58:00.000 --> 01:58:03.520
and every month, the same scenario plays out.

01:58:03.520 --> 01:58:08.010
Mary gives anyone who picks her up directions
to her parents' house, then on the way, she

01:58:08.010 --> 01:58:11.640
instructs the driver to stop at the graveyard
where she was buried.

01:58:11.640 --> 01:58:14.610
She vanishes from the car, leaving her sweater.

01:58:14.610 --> 01:58:18.590
The driver of the car tries to return the
sweater to her parents' house, only to be

01:58:18.590 --> 01:58:20.639
told that Mary Talish was dead.

01:58:20.639 --> 01:58:25.130
When the SCP foundation was made aware of
Mary Talish's pattern of haunting in the late

01:58:25.130 --> 01:58:30.210
50's, they set up a system where agents would
patrol Mayflower Road at hourly intervals

01:58:30.210 --> 01:58:33.039
with the intention of picking Mary up.

01:58:33.039 --> 01:58:38.059
Agents were sent on their own in non-Foundation
cars and instructed to stick to the accepted

01:58:38.059 --> 01:58:43.639
script of the vanishing hitchhiker legend,
without attempting to engage Mary in further

01:58:43.639 --> 01:58:44.639
conversation.

01:58:44.639 --> 01:58:48.250
Mary's parents were also given E-class Agent
status to keep them from speaking out about

01:58:48.250 --> 01:58:52.840
the haunting, and told that the Foundation
was working on a way to set the spirit to

01:58:52.840 --> 01:58:53.840
rest.

01:58:53.840 --> 01:58:58.770
Early attempts to study the apparition were
inconclusive - it proved impossible for the

01:58:58.770 --> 01:59:03.650
Foundation to relocate her or trigger her
manifestation outside of the 19th of every

01:59:03.650 --> 01:59:07.929
month, and attempts to analyze her sweater
were fruitless, since if the sweater wasn't

01:59:07.929 --> 01:59:12.820
returned to the Talish family home it would
simply vanish from containment at or around

01:59:12.820 --> 01:59:15.580
sunset on the next 19th.

01:59:15.580 --> 01:59:21.139
For 20 years, SCP-1337 events continued to
happen as normal.

01:59:21.139 --> 01:59:24.909
D-Class personnel under the instruction of
the Foundation would pick Mary up, drive her

01:59:24.909 --> 01:59:28.610
past the cemetery, and return her sweater
to her parents.

01:59:28.610 --> 01:59:33.789
It was business as usual, and in fact, it
was one of the more sedate recurring apparitions

01:59:33.789 --> 01:59:36.000
the Foundation had to deal with.

01:59:36.000 --> 01:59:40.670
But, as you might have guessed, that peace
wouldn't last forever.

01:59:40.670 --> 01:59:48.409
Enter Dr. Lawson - who, in 1972, was placed
in charge of all resources regarding SCP-1337.

01:59:48.409 --> 01:59:54.179
Dr. Lawson was getting sick of all this phantom
hitchhiker business, and while most of the

01:59:54.179 --> 01:59:58.159
Foundation was happy to keep this routine
going, Lawson thought that the continual picking

01:59:58.159 --> 02:00:03.340
up and dropping off of Mary Talish and her
red sweater was a waste of the Foundation’s

02:00:03.340 --> 02:00:04.520
valuable time.

02:00:04.520 --> 02:00:10.079
After all, it was the early 70's - the price
of oil was at an all-time high, so the expense

02:00:10.079 --> 02:00:15.639
of sending car after car up and down the same
road for a solid day once a month just to

02:00:15.639 --> 02:00:18.869
pick up a ghost was more trouble than it was
worth.

02:00:18.869 --> 02:00:24.090
So, Lawson started developing a plan, one
that he didn't go through the proper Foundation

02:00:24.090 --> 02:00:25.699
channels to approve.

02:00:25.699 --> 02:00:31.010
He reasoned that the reason Mary's ghost kept
coming back was because she wanted something.

02:00:31.010 --> 02:00:34.539
Since always asked for a ride home, then it
must mean that she wanted to return back to

02:00:34.539 --> 02:00:35.679
her parents.

02:00:35.679 --> 02:00:42.210
So, logic followed that if she had nothing,
or no one, to go back to then she'd stop appearing.

02:00:42.210 --> 02:00:48.230
On 18th June, 1973, Lawson went ahead with
his plan without his superiors' knowledge

02:00:48.230 --> 02:00:53.350
and ordered the execution of Mary Talish's
parents, as well as the immediate demolition

02:00:53.350 --> 02:00:55.300
of their family home.

02:00:55.300 --> 02:01:00.059
According to his journals, Lawson had hoped
that his attempt at decommissioning 1337 would

02:01:00.059 --> 02:01:05.190
significantly cut the Foundation's gas bills,
freeing up valuable funds, at which point

02:01:05.190 --> 02:01:08.639
he'd surely be promoted in 'recognition of
his brilliance'.

02:01:08.639 --> 02:01:11.210
But that wasn't what happened.

02:01:11.210 --> 02:01:16.510
Lawson was demoted from team leader to junior
staff, and only kept on 1337 detail out of

02:01:16.510 --> 02:01:21.630
the belief that, without a family to return
to, Lawson would become the new focal point

02:01:21.630 --> 02:01:24.380
of the haunting should Mary Talish ever return.

02:01:24.380 --> 02:01:29.900
Though Lawson's actions weren't at all above
board, even by SCP Foundation standards, they

02:01:29.900 --> 02:01:31.570
did seem to have worked.

02:01:31.570 --> 02:01:35.150
The 19th of June came and went without a single
Mary sighting.

02:01:35.150 --> 02:01:37.010
And she wasn't seen the next month either.

02:01:37.010 --> 02:01:42.310
A full year went by without any sign of the
Mayflower Road apparition.

02:01:42.310 --> 02:01:46.860
Satisfied with this turn of events, the Foundation
made the decision to officially reclassify

02:01:46.860 --> 02:01:52.900
SCP-1337 from “Safe” to “Safe Decommissioned”
and the gas money that was budgeted for the

02:01:52.900 --> 02:01:58.730
Mayflower Road patrol was redirected to the
SCP-682 tank acid fund.

02:01:58.730 --> 02:02:04.230
But even though everything seemed to have
been sorted out, Lawson wasn't entirely satisfied.

02:02:04.230 --> 02:02:06.400
And just because of his demotion.

02:02:06.400 --> 02:02:11.520
Whether it was intuition or merely guilt-induced
paranoia is unclear, but he suspected that

02:02:11.520 --> 02:02:13.869
Mary was still out there somewhere.

02:02:13.869 --> 02:02:17.699
At first he thought that she might show up
on the anniversary of her parents' deaths,

02:02:17.699 --> 02:02:23.170
but then that date came and went, as did eight
more anniversaries after it.

02:02:23.170 --> 02:02:29.300
Finally, on the 19th of June, 1983, Lawson
decided he had to see for himself.

02:02:29.300 --> 02:02:34.250
Fitted with recording equipment, he drove
alone, in a non-Foundation standard car, down

02:02:34.250 --> 02:02:39.530
that lonely stretch of road where so many
before him had stopped to pick up that mysterious

02:02:39.530 --> 02:02:41.739
blonde woman with the red sweater.

02:02:41.739 --> 02:02:46.650
He had to prove to himself that she wouldn't
show up, that he had really and truly gotten

02:02:46.650 --> 02:02:48.250
rid of her for good.

02:02:48.250 --> 02:02:51.690
It was about 5 o'clock in the evening when
he reached Mayflower Road.

02:02:51.690 --> 02:02:54.630
At first, he didn't experience anything strange.

02:02:54.630 --> 02:02:59.940
He scanned the roadside, looking for the phantom
hitchhiker walking along it, but there was

02:02:59.940 --> 02:03:00.940
nobody there.

02:03:00.940 --> 02:03:06.059
Dr. Lawson breathed a sigh of relief - he
may have orchestrated the deaths of two innocent

02:03:06.059 --> 02:03:08.880
people, but at least it hadn't been for nothing.

02:03:08.880 --> 02:03:13.610
He turned on the recorder he'd brought with
him and logged that nothing had happened.

02:03:13.610 --> 02:03:16.940
SCP-1337 had been permanently neutralized.

02:03:16.940 --> 02:03:21.079
As he approached the t-intersection and prepared
to turn onto Marsh Avenue, he looked up to

02:03:21.079 --> 02:03:22.809
adjust his rear view mirror.

02:03:22.809 --> 02:03:27.969
To his horror, he found that he wasn't alone
in the car - someone was in the seat behind

02:03:27.969 --> 02:03:32.110
him, someone with blonde hair and a red sweater.

02:03:32.110 --> 02:03:36.829
His last transmission consisted only of “Wait,
who the hell are yo-“, before the recording

02:03:36.829 --> 02:03:38.110
abruptly stopped.

02:03:38.110 --> 02:03:42.139
Lawson's car was found soon after by Foundation
agents.

02:03:42.139 --> 02:03:46.340
Lawson was dead in the front seat, bruised
and bloody, with his eyes and heart ripped

02:03:46.340 --> 02:03:48.860
out in a ritualistic fashion.

02:03:48.860 --> 02:03:53.930
Just the way Mary Talish had been found all
the way back in 1952.

02:03:53.930 --> 02:03:57.449
It turns out that Mary hadn't been neutralized
after all.

02:03:57.449 --> 02:04:02.820
She'd just been waiting for a chance to get
revenge on the man who killed her family.

02:04:02.820 --> 02:04:05.150
And Mary didn't stop with Dr. Lawson.

02:04:05.150 --> 02:04:09.769
No longer does she appear, walking along the
road waiting for someone to offer her a ride

02:04:09.769 --> 02:04:11.889
before disappearing without incident.

02:04:11.889 --> 02:04:16.679
Now, should someone pass by without offering
a ride, she will appear in their backseat

02:04:16.679 --> 02:04:19.980
before re-enacting the method of her own death
upon the driver.

02:04:19.980 --> 02:04:23.230
And her physical appearance has changed too.

02:04:23.230 --> 02:04:27.309
Whereas before she looked like the image of
the pretty young woman before her tragedy,

02:04:27.309 --> 02:04:31.731
now recordings show that she appears with
the wounds of her death present, her eyes

02:04:31.731 --> 02:04:37.510
gouged out of their sockets and a massive
hole in her chest where her heart should be.

02:04:37.510 --> 02:04:41.039
The same wounds she inflicts on her victims.

02:04:41.039 --> 02:04:45.970
The SCP Foundation has tried closing off and
even destroying the road, but that has only

02:04:45.970 --> 02:04:51.110
resulted in Mary manifesting at other locations
in and around Muncie.

02:04:51.110 --> 02:04:54.780
Foundation documents reveal that any back
road in the city can potentially serve as

02:04:54.780 --> 02:05:00.719
host to a 1337 event, and all attempts to
contain the apparition have failed.

02:05:00.719 --> 02:05:05.530
The only way someone who has seen Mary can
avoid her wrath is by stopping to pick her

02:05:05.530 --> 02:05:10.400
up, at which point she will de-materialize
before reappearing on another road.

02:05:10.400 --> 02:05:15.739
Mobile Task Forces have been unsuccessful,
as Mary only appears to those driving alone,

02:05:15.739 --> 02:05:19.770
and all agents who have been sent on solo
missions to apprehend her have resulted in

02:05:19.770 --> 02:05:22.090
the death of the agent.

02:05:22.090 --> 02:05:26.860
SCP-1337 was reinstated, this time as Euclid
class.

02:05:26.860 --> 02:05:32.820
Currently, the foundation's method of managing
SCP-1337 is to dispatch a security team on

02:05:32.820 --> 02:05:37.540
the 19th of every month to monitor all of
the places where a potential sighting could

02:05:37.540 --> 02:05:38.789
take place.

02:05:38.789 --> 02:05:43.559
As soon as signs of a manifestation are identified,
a remotely controlled vehicle containing a

02:05:43.559 --> 02:05:46.700
single D-class is driven to the location.

02:05:46.700 --> 02:05:52.350
Once Mary appears in the car, the car is piloted
to the empty lot where her home used to stand,

02:05:52.350 --> 02:05:56.090
and the remains of the D-class are then disposed
of.

02:05:56.090 --> 02:06:01.730
Like a lot of stories that get passed down
as urban legends, the story of SCP-1337 has

02:06:01.730 --> 02:06:03.769
a lesson that can be taken away from it.

02:06:03.769 --> 02:06:10.179
This SCP started off as an ordinary local
haunting, no more deadly than Lydia, Suzanne,

02:06:10.179 --> 02:06:15.220
Resurrection Mary, or any of the countless
other local versions of the vanishing hitchhiker

02:06:15.220 --> 02:06:16.220
story.

02:06:16.220 --> 02:06:20.389
But, thanks to one rogue Foundation doctor
and his desire to rush to what he thought

02:06:20.389 --> 02:06:25.650
would be an efficient solution, the spirit
not only became harder to control but also

02:06:25.650 --> 02:06:30.920
much more violent and bloodthirsty than anyone
was prepared to deal with.

02:06:30.920 --> 02:06:36.519
So, if there's anything we can learn here,
it's that no matter if you're a student, an

02:06:36.519 --> 02:06:42.159
office worker, or a researcher with the SCP
Foundation, think twice about cutting corners.

02:06:42.159 --> 02:06:47.570
It might save you a little bit of time and
money in the short term, but in the long term,

02:06:47.570 --> 02:06:50.940
the results could be fatal.

02:06:50.940 --> 02:06:58.239
It was 1965 and the Chicago PD was investigating
a meatpacking plant reported to be the home

02:06:58.239 --> 02:07:02.989
of a devil worshipping cult, complete with
allegations of human sacrifice.

02:07:02.989 --> 02:07:05.200
There the cops were met with heavy resistance.

02:07:05.200 --> 02:07:09.650
A firefight broke out between the police and
the occult worshippers who flooded out of

02:07:09.650 --> 02:07:11.050
the plant’s basement.

02:07:11.050 --> 02:07:16.599
The cops were pinned down, and in trouble,
but they had a secret weapon - heavily armed,

02:07:16.599 --> 02:07:21.770
decked out in sophisticated ballistic armour,
and covered in strange insignia.

02:07:21.770 --> 02:07:26.869
Mobile Task Force Epsilon-9, also known as
the Fire Eaters, here to assist the cops on

02:07:26.869 --> 02:07:29.420
behalf of the SCP Foundation.

02:07:29.420 --> 02:07:34.119
As always with the Foundation, they had no
interest in some mere human cultists.

02:07:34.119 --> 02:07:37.079
Those were a dime a dozen in the world of
anomalous monsters.

02:07:37.079 --> 02:07:43.070
What the Foundation had taken an interest
in was who or what these cultists were worshipping.

02:07:43.070 --> 02:07:48.489
It’d all begun a few weeks back, near Danforth
Meatpacking, an abandoned meat packing plant

02:07:48.489 --> 02:07:50.489
just outside of Chicago.

02:07:50.489 --> 02:07:55.840
No one had given the place a thought in decades,
that is until people started going missing.

02:07:55.840 --> 02:07:59.639
Rumors spread of people being snatched in
the surrounding woods by figures dressed in

02:07:59.639 --> 02:08:00.920
robes.

02:08:00.920 --> 02:08:05.170
Mysterious voices and noises were said to
be coming out from the cavernous belly of

02:08:05.170 --> 02:08:06.429
the plant.

02:08:06.429 --> 02:08:13.119
Some even reported seeing smoke rising out
of the building - thick, black, noxious smoke.

02:08:13.119 --> 02:08:15.920
Something was terribly wrong here.

02:08:15.920 --> 02:08:18.310
Something was...anomalous.

02:08:18.310 --> 02:08:22.960
The Chicago Police Department Strike Force,
in association with the Fire Eaters from the

02:08:22.960 --> 02:08:24.160
Foundation, mobilized at Danforth Meatpacking.

02:08:24.160 --> 02:08:29.130
While the police were initially reluctant
to work with these mysterious figures they

02:08:29.130 --> 02:08:31.570
turned out to be indispensable for the raid.

02:08:31.570 --> 02:08:35.550
There were forty-seven cultists holding out
in the basement of the plant, many of them

02:08:35.550 --> 02:08:41.300
heavily armed and all of them hopped up on
zealous devotion to their unknown master.

02:08:41.300 --> 02:08:45.849
All except one of the cultists fought to the
death during a tense firefight with Chicago

02:08:45.849 --> 02:08:47.840
PD and the Fire Eaters.

02:08:47.840 --> 02:08:52.750
The single survivor was still heavily injured,
and was taken to a secure Foundation facility

02:08:52.750 --> 02:08:55.260
for emergency treatment and debriefing.

02:08:55.260 --> 02:08:59.789
Typically, the Foundation would need to perform
extensive tests on the Danforth Meatpacking

02:08:59.789 --> 02:09:04.820
plant to discover the source of the anomaly’s
activity, however, this time, it was a Chicago

02:09:04.820 --> 02:09:08.170
detective who asked the question that busted
the case wide open:

02:09:08.170 --> 02:09:09.929
“The hell’s with the giant pig?”

02:09:09.929 --> 02:09:15.159
And while it would turn out to be a whole
lot more than that, there was indeed a giant,

02:09:15.159 --> 02:09:19.250
iron furnace shaped like a pig in the center
of the facility.

02:09:19.250 --> 02:09:25.699
Measuring 15m by 25m by 20m at its widest
points, the thing was a behemoth.

02:09:25.699 --> 02:09:30.590
It had an internal furnace despite no apparent
fuel source, and a five centimeter slot of

02:09:30.590 --> 02:09:35.000
unknown purpose on the side of the machine’s
immense, rusted hide.

02:09:35.000 --> 02:09:39.889
Naturally, all the police officers involved
in the raid had their memories wiped and restructured.

02:09:39.889 --> 02:09:44.590
And they were lucky, because they’d remain
forever ignorant of the true horrors about

02:09:44.590 --> 02:09:48.670
to unfold in the confines of that godforsaken
factory.

02:09:48.670 --> 02:09:53.750
As is standard procedure, the plant was isolated,
and a Foundation research team - led by Lead

02:09:53.750 --> 02:09:58.340
Researcher Westrin, under the authority of
Regional Director Caleb - was installed on

02:09:58.340 --> 02:10:00.739
the new provisional site to conduct tests.

02:10:00.739 --> 02:10:07.139
Other than everyone feeling somewhat uneasy
around it, this new anomaly, dubbed SCP - 4511,

02:10:07.139 --> 02:10:12.750
didn’t seem to exhibit any strange activity
save for its perpetually burning fire, but

02:10:12.750 --> 02:10:18.610
during the initial research period, a small,
white card suddenly popped out of the slot

02:10:18.610 --> 02:10:20.599
in SCP - 4511’s side.

02:10:20.599 --> 02:10:24.310
A researcher carefully approached and looked
at the card, there was writing.

02:10:24.310 --> 02:10:29.339
It said, “CURRENT DEMAND: A flock of my
own.

02:10:29.339 --> 02:10:30.360
- SATISFIED.”

02:10:30.360 --> 02:10:34.320
Though nobody on the team had any idea what
this meant.

02:10:34.320 --> 02:10:38.690
After going through a shoot out with a considerable
death toll to get to it, having a giant metal

02:10:38.690 --> 02:10:42.510
pig shaped furnace spit out a cryptic card
was strange.

02:10:42.510 --> 02:10:47.239
But at the secret medical facility where the
surviving cultist was being held, things were

02:10:47.239 --> 02:10:50.050
about to get a whole lot stranger.

02:10:50.050 --> 02:10:54.619
As he lay in a bed suffering from his injuries,
he pulled one of the medical staff close and

02:10:54.619 --> 02:11:00.300
uttered cryptic, dying words: “Give it whatever
it demands, or your suffering will be beyond

02:11:00.300 --> 02:11:01.360
measure.”

02:11:01.360 --> 02:11:06.500
He expired seconds later, less than 72 hours
after the raid.

02:11:06.500 --> 02:11:11.289
Back at the meat packing plant, at the exact
same time, another white card was produced

02:11:11.289 --> 02:11:17.840
by the machine, reading “CURRENT DEMAND:
The metal teeth that endlessly churn.

02:11:17.840 --> 02:11:20.869
PERIOD: One Week.”

02:11:20.869 --> 02:11:24.349
Perhaps this entity was a little more intelligent
than they thought.

02:11:24.349 --> 02:11:29.080
A number of researchers on the team, invigorated
by this new development, were eager to press

02:11:29.080 --> 02:11:31.219
forward with experiments.

02:11:31.219 --> 02:11:35.429
Lead Researcher Westrin, however, did not
share their enthusiasm.

02:11:35.429 --> 02:11:39.310
Something about this entire situation felt
like a grim omen to him.

02:11:39.310 --> 02:11:45.150
This entity had a plan far beyond their understanding
- and on some deep, animal level, he knew

02:11:45.150 --> 02:11:50.960
that helping this thing see its plans through
would lead to disastrous results.

02:11:50.960 --> 02:11:55.030
On this first gut impulse, he denied the request
for further experiments.

02:11:55.030 --> 02:11:58.230
But Regional Director Caleb had other ideas.

02:11:58.230 --> 02:12:02.980
Caleb overruled Westrin’s command, and the
experiments began shortly after.

02:12:02.980 --> 02:12:09.130
The entity, jokingly nicknamed The Swine God
by researchers, had made its demand: The metal

02:12:09.130 --> 02:12:11.039
teeth that endlessly churn.

02:12:11.039 --> 02:12:12.800
But what could that mean?

02:12:12.800 --> 02:12:17.599
It wasn’t long before the entity began to
produce more cards, each with their own strange

02:12:17.599 --> 02:12:19.199
and esoteric demands.

02:12:19.199 --> 02:12:25.639
However, on some instinctual level, the researchers
at the site understood the demands perfectly.

02:12:25.639 --> 02:12:30.050
The next card’s demand was "The metal of
this suffocating prison."

02:12:30.050 --> 02:12:35.559
Upon receiving this demand, researchers collected
scrap metal from around the new site, and

02:12:35.559 --> 02:12:39.369
tossed them into the furnace beyond the Swine
God’s jaws one by one.

02:12:39.369 --> 02:12:42.780
Inside, they heard the sound of metal crunching.

02:12:42.780 --> 02:12:48.139
Hours later, all the other metal in the site
began to rapidly oxidize and rust - though

02:12:48.139 --> 02:12:52.090
SCP-4511 itself remained unaffected.

02:12:52.090 --> 02:12:58.619
The card that came after delivered another
simple request: "Oil to slicken my frozen

02:12:58.619 --> 02:12:59.929
joints."

02:12:59.929 --> 02:13:04.349
The researchers understood and procured three
large barrels of oil and tossed them into

02:13:04.349 --> 02:13:05.480
the furnace.

02:13:05.480 --> 02:13:11.239
The entity let out a deep gurgle, before shaking
violently and expelling excess oil, rusted

02:13:11.239 --> 02:13:14.369
metal, and two domesticated pig femurs.

02:13:14.369 --> 02:13:19.210
It turns out that the Swine God had an appetite
for pigs, as the next card that rumbled out

02:13:19.210 --> 02:13:27.020
of the machine bore the request, “Two of
my children, made in my image, made in flesh."

02:13:27.020 --> 02:13:31.409
In response, the researchers provided the
entity with two adult pigs.

02:13:31.409 --> 02:13:35.770
Just like the previous requests, they too
were tossed into the fiery depths of the giant

02:13:35.770 --> 02:13:42.349
pig’s mouth, from which came the horrible
sounds of pigs squealing, and then a low,

02:13:42.349 --> 02:13:43.469
guttural gurgling.

02:13:43.469 --> 02:13:48.889
Next, the request was, “The hooks used to
hang my children's corpses."

02:13:48.889 --> 02:13:53.099
To satisfy this request the researchers provided
seventeen meat hooks.

02:13:53.099 --> 02:13:59.269
In response, 4511 spat out a metal sphere
at an extremely high velocity, killing observing

02:13:59.269 --> 02:14:00.500
Foundation Agent McHenry.

02:14:00.500 --> 02:14:05.550
For reasons that weren’t apparent at the
time, rather than giving Agent McHenry a proper

02:14:05.550 --> 02:14:09.760
burial, his body was also fed into the hungry
machine.

02:14:09.760 --> 02:14:13.750
Lead Researcher Westrin’s concerns were
mounting, but that didn’t amount to much

02:14:13.750 --> 02:14:14.750
now.

02:14:14.750 --> 02:14:20.810
4511 had developed a taste for flesh, and
the researchers were all too eager to obey

02:14:20.810 --> 02:14:22.099
its command.

02:14:22.099 --> 02:14:24.580
On the Swine God’s order, it was fed a German
shepherd.

02:14:24.580 --> 02:14:27.900
An hour later, the entity spat out some teeth.

02:14:27.900 --> 02:14:31.269
Six of which came from a dog, and one from
a human.

02:14:31.269 --> 02:14:36.289
More than once, it released a card with the
blunt request “A worker for the line.”

02:14:36.289 --> 02:14:41.510
The researchers knew exactly what this meant:
It required a human sacrifice.

02:14:41.510 --> 02:14:45.460
SCP-4511 was given two D-Class personnel.

02:14:45.460 --> 02:14:49.889
One was flung back out seconds later, crunched
and burned to death with several internal

02:14:49.889 --> 02:14:51.210
organs missing.

02:14:51.210 --> 02:14:56.170
The other had a more mysterious and altogether
upsetting fate.

02:14:56.170 --> 02:15:00.409
The second D-class was heard screaming in
the belly of the furnace for roughly two hours.

02:15:00.409 --> 02:15:04.949
Thirty four minutes later, a strange liquid
was excreted by the machine.

02:15:04.949 --> 02:15:09.340
When the liquid was tested, they found trace
amounts of chemicals like pig urine and motor

02:15:09.340 --> 02:15:15.139
oil - but most disturbing of all, human genetic
material that was identical to that of Lead

02:15:15.139 --> 02:15:16.909
Researcher Westrin.

02:15:16.909 --> 02:15:21.219
It seemed that the Swine God had finally taken
an interest in him.

02:15:21.219 --> 02:15:25.889
After some final requests for large quantities
of coal, and even human children, to fuel

02:15:25.889 --> 02:15:30.739
its fires, it made the request that sent the
whole thing crashing down...

02:15:30.739 --> 02:15:36.500
“The false foreman, delivered to my maw
to prove your faith."

02:15:36.500 --> 02:15:40.030
Lead Researcher Westrin knew what this meant.

02:15:40.030 --> 02:15:41.500
They all did.

02:15:41.500 --> 02:15:45.639
The Swine God was demanding him in sacrifice.

02:15:45.639 --> 02:15:49.760
Lead Researcher Westrin tried to shut down
the entire project, but the Swine God was

02:15:49.760 --> 02:15:51.159
faster than him.

02:15:51.159 --> 02:15:55.080
One of his own researchers shot Westrin in
the leg, as the others gathered round and

02:15:55.080 --> 02:15:56.840
forcibly restrained him.

02:15:56.840 --> 02:16:01.300
He tried to reason with his subordinates,
but it didn’t do him any good.

02:16:01.300 --> 02:16:06.710
The Swine God had crawled into all their minds
and corrupted them - they were His servants

02:16:06.710 --> 02:16:09.570
now, and Westrin was doomed.

02:16:09.570 --> 02:16:14.690
Despite his protests, the servants forced
him into the mouth of SCP - 4511, and after

02:16:14.690 --> 02:16:21.630
a little over four minutes of screaming, Westrin
was devoured just like all the other sacrifices.

02:16:21.630 --> 02:16:25.920
Upon receiving news of the horrors unfolding
in the Danforth Meat Packing Plant, Regional

02:16:25.920 --> 02:16:30.880
Director Caleb declared the security of the
site compromised, and sent in Mobile Force

02:16:30.880 --> 02:16:34.320
Epsilon-11, aka the Nine-Tailed Fox.

02:16:34.320 --> 02:16:38.430
The four elite MTF soldiers were given the
simple instruction to figure out exactly what

02:16:38.430 --> 02:16:43.450
had happened, and to eliminate any potentially
compromised Foundation staff members who’d

02:16:43.450 --> 02:16:45.540
fallen under the Swine God’s power.

02:16:45.540 --> 02:16:51.120
When the team arrived, they realized just
how far gone the whole place was.

02:16:51.120 --> 02:16:55.960
Almost everyone was dead, having been sacrificed
to the machine, and the ones that were left

02:16:55.960 --> 02:16:57.830
were completely insane.

02:16:57.830 --> 02:17:02.961
They attacked the task force, shouting in
their madness about how no matter what the

02:17:02.961 --> 02:17:07.010
Foundation does to them, it would be nothing
compared to what it would do.

02:17:07.010 --> 02:17:10.631
It had them all under its rusty, iron foot.

02:17:10.631 --> 02:17:15.270
The team was forced to fend off repeated attacks
from the pig’s devotees, and even found

02:17:15.270 --> 02:17:19.080
the powers of the Swine God starting to affect
their own minds.

02:17:19.080 --> 02:17:22.530
The beast was more powerful and dangerous
than anyone had imagined.

02:17:22.530 --> 02:17:27.540
The trained Foundation researchers and guards
had been transformed into the same cultists

02:17:27.540 --> 02:17:32.801
they’d fought to gain control of the building
by the mind-bending power of the Swine God.

02:17:32.801 --> 02:17:37.710
The MTF were forced to retreat and return
with reinforcements to truly clean the place

02:17:37.710 --> 02:17:38.710
out.

02:17:38.710 --> 02:17:41.660
Once a slaughterhouse, always a slaughterhouse.

02:17:41.660 --> 02:17:47.540
At this point, Regional Director Caleb took
personal responsibility over the casualties

02:17:47.540 --> 02:17:51.770
since he’d been the one who signed off on
the experiments in the first place.

02:17:51.770 --> 02:17:56.551
He gave up his Regional Director rank, and
deemed himself the new Lead Researcher on

02:17:56.551 --> 02:17:58.541
the 4511 case.

02:17:58.541 --> 02:18:03.430
Now that he fully understood the scope and
danger of the entity they were dealing with,

02:18:03.430 --> 02:18:08.350
he wanted to lead the charge in discovering
more about the anomaly, and hopefully someday

02:18:08.350 --> 02:18:11.060
negating its deadly effects.

02:18:11.060 --> 02:18:15.550
This may sound like a happy ending, in spite
of all the violence, bloodshed, and human

02:18:15.550 --> 02:18:17.390
sacrifice that brought us here.

02:18:17.390 --> 02:18:20.800
But beware of the premature celebration.

02:18:20.800 --> 02:18:26.831
Despite investigation, the Swine God retained
no evidence of the objects, animals, and people

02:18:26.831 --> 02:18:29.000
it’d consumed and burned.

02:18:29.000 --> 02:18:34.301
Perhaps it’d burnt them down to their very
atoms, if those even still existed.

02:18:34.301 --> 02:18:39.211
What we do know is that not long after, after
Lead Researcher Caleb and his subordinates

02:18:39.211 --> 02:18:46.390
installed themselves into the facility, SCP
- 4511 produced one more little, white card.

02:18:46.390 --> 02:18:51.370
It read, “CURRENT DEMAND: A flock of my
own.

02:18:51.370 --> 02:18:52.980
- SATISFIED.”

02:18:52.980 --> 02:18:58.051
And if we’ve learned anything today, it’s
that the Swine God gets whatever it demands.

02:18:58.051 --> 02:19:04.290
A brutal truth that Lead Researcher Caleb
is likely to understand much sooner than he

02:19:04.290 --> 02:19:05.330
thought...

02:19:05.330 --> 02:19:06.930
It was just a job.

02:19:06.930 --> 02:19:11.540
You were meant to be mopping floors and cleaning
toilets at the Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals

02:19:11.540 --> 02:19:13.640
Research Center for minimum wage.

02:19:13.640 --> 02:19:19.090
And you were happy about it, grateful for
any kind of employment - you didn’t even

02:19:19.090 --> 02:19:24.640
know that the company signing your checks
was the SCP Foundation, an organization dedicated

02:19:24.640 --> 02:19:30.730
to securing and containing anomalies and protecting
humanity from their negative effects at any

02:19:30.730 --> 02:19:31.730
cost.

02:19:31.730 --> 02:19:36.331
And today, you’re going to find out exactly
how steep that cost can be.

02:19:36.331 --> 02:19:40.620
The Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals Research
Center isn’t actually a research center

02:19:40.620 --> 02:19:46.170
at all: It’s a Foundation front business,
with a building solely dedicated to the containment

02:19:46.170 --> 02:19:50.870
of a single anomaly: SCP-3280.

02:19:50.870 --> 02:19:55.940
But again, you’re just the janitor, it’s
not like they would bother telling you what’s

02:19:55.940 --> 02:19:57.101
being contained here.

02:19:57.101 --> 02:20:01.840
If it breaks out, you won’t even know what’s
killing you until it’s too late.

02:20:01.840 --> 02:20:06.431
It begins, like most classic horror stories,
on a dark and stormy night.

02:20:06.431 --> 02:20:11.771
You’re mopping up a silent hallway, whistling
a little tune to yourself, when rain starts

02:20:11.771 --> 02:20:14.580
hammering down on the window next to you.

02:20:14.580 --> 02:20:19.620
Not long after, you see a bolt of lightning
split the distant sky followed by an immense

02:20:19.620 --> 02:20:21.290
thunder crack.

02:20:21.290 --> 02:20:24.630
Soon after you hear screaming and panicking
from below.

02:20:24.630 --> 02:20:25.630
Frantic footsteps.

02:20:25.630 --> 02:20:28.440
Then, the flashing lights and sirens.

02:20:28.440 --> 02:20:31.301
You think back to your employee orientation.

02:20:31.301 --> 02:20:37.240
These flashing lights and wailing sirens can
only mean one thing: Containment breach.

02:20:37.240 --> 02:20:40.670
You run for it, not even knowing what you’re
running from.

02:20:40.670 --> 02:20:44.580
You bring your mop and bucket with you, perhaps
just out of habit.

02:20:44.580 --> 02:20:49.760
You seek refuge in the only place in the facility
that truly seems to belong to you: The broom

02:20:49.760 --> 02:20:50.780
closet.

02:20:50.780 --> 02:20:53.331
The alarm blares as you lock yourself in the
closet.

02:20:53.331 --> 02:20:57.551
You’re shaking with terror and can hear
the screaming of your colleagues.

02:20:57.551 --> 02:21:04.851
You hear more noises - running, scrambling,
a wet dripping sound, gunshots, and then…

02:21:04.851 --> 02:21:05.851
silence.

02:21:05.851 --> 02:21:12.110
All this time, you can’t help but wonder,
“Why isn’t anybody coming to help us?”

02:21:12.110 --> 02:21:16.750
After a while, the only thing you can hear
is the rain and the distant thunder.

02:21:16.750 --> 02:21:17.950
It’s been hours.

02:21:17.950 --> 02:21:23.150
You’ve only managed to stave off dehydration
by drinking the filthy water from the mop

02:21:23.150 --> 02:21:24.150
sink.

02:21:24.150 --> 02:21:27.660
But at least it seems like the chaos outside
has died down.

02:21:27.660 --> 02:21:31.370
Carefully, you open the door and peek out
of the closet.

02:21:31.370 --> 02:21:34.431
Darkness, but no detectable movement.

02:21:34.431 --> 02:21:38.181
Now’s your chance and you make a break for
it, creeping down the hall.

02:21:38.181 --> 02:21:43.660
The dark hallway is suddenly lit up by lightning
and you can see that there are bodies everywhere.

02:21:43.660 --> 02:21:48.271
You step over the corpse of Dr. Cawthrone,
one of the few scientists working here who

02:21:48.271 --> 02:21:50.250
actually knew your name.

02:21:50.250 --> 02:21:54.811
If you can make it to the security office,
you might be able to radio for help, or maybe

02:21:54.811 --> 02:21:56.530
access a computer terminal.

02:21:56.530 --> 02:22:00.960
On the way to the office you hear another
horrific scream start to echo through the

02:22:00.960 --> 02:22:03.351
complex before it’s cut off by a thunderclap.

02:22:03.351 --> 02:22:06.750
You have to ignore it though and push on.

02:22:06.750 --> 02:22:11.750
When you enter the security room, you see
that the head security officer, Nichols, is

02:22:11.750 --> 02:22:12.940
already dead.

02:22:12.940 --> 02:22:17.351
His body has been cut open from neck to groin;
gutted.

02:22:17.351 --> 02:22:21.400
The anomaly, whatever it is, has already been
here.

02:22:21.400 --> 02:22:24.650
You access the computer terminal and open
the file for SCP-3280.

02:22:24.650 --> 02:22:31.811
You’re warned that, as Janitorial Staff,
you have Level 0 Clearance, and as a result,

02:22:31.811 --> 02:22:34.660
information will be omitted from the files
you access.

02:22:34.660 --> 02:22:35.681
It doesn’t matter.

02:22:35.681 --> 02:22:38.330
You press on and open up the file.

02:22:38.330 --> 02:22:41.510
Both the object class and the description
have been redacted.

02:22:41.510 --> 02:22:44.610
You can only see the Special Containment Procedures.

02:22:44.610 --> 02:22:49.911
They dictate that 3280 is to remain contained
at the Johnston Labs and Pharmaceuticals Research

02:22:49.911 --> 02:22:53.550
Center until long term Containment Procedures
can be drawn up.

02:22:53.550 --> 02:22:59.840
If the entity ever reaches beyond Sub-Level
2, the facility enters full lockdown mode.

02:22:59.840 --> 02:23:04.951
Not even information is allowed in or out
of the facility, as this could result in an

02:23:04.951 --> 02:23:07.580
XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

02:23:07.580 --> 02:23:11.701
In other words, nobody is coming to save you.

02:23:11.701 --> 02:23:16.450
The only other information on the page is
a picture of a lightning storm, much like

02:23:16.450 --> 02:23:19.601
the one you find yourself in right now.

02:23:19.601 --> 02:23:21.131
Lightning flashes in the hall.

02:23:21.131 --> 02:23:25.160
You dart around, paranoid, knowing the anomaly
could be anywhere.

02:23:25.160 --> 02:23:30.670
All you can hear now is a quiet drip, drip,
drip of blood coming from the body of Security

02:23:30.670 --> 02:23:32.400
Officer Nichols.

02:23:32.400 --> 02:23:35.021
Whatever this thing had done to him looked
painful.

02:23:35.021 --> 02:23:39.610
You try to remember him as he was in life,
and then, a revelation hits you.

02:23:39.610 --> 02:23:43.860
A security officer probably has a lot better
clearance than a janitor.

02:23:43.860 --> 02:23:48.240
You feel around Nichols’ mutilated torso
until you find his key card.

02:23:48.240 --> 02:23:52.780
Thankfully, Nichols was the kind of guy who’d
write his password on the underside of the

02:23:52.780 --> 02:23:54.280
card so he wouldn’t forget it.

02:23:54.280 --> 02:23:59.090
You easily gain access to the Foundation servers
with his login credentials.

02:23:59.090 --> 02:24:01.891
You now have Level 2 Security Clearance.

02:24:01.891 --> 02:24:06.221
The terminal gives you the option to view
security footage taken throughout the site.

02:24:06.221 --> 02:24:10.641
You’re given access to every camera still
working after the containment breach and the

02:24:10.641 --> 02:24:12.171
subsequent carnage.

02:24:12.171 --> 02:24:15.090
You select the camera feed for the Second
Floor Barracks.

02:24:15.090 --> 02:24:20.440
There, you see Researcher Jenson hanging from
a makeshift noose attached to his bunk.

02:24:20.440 --> 02:24:22.721
There’s a puddle underneath his corpse.

02:24:22.721 --> 02:24:25.530
You access the feed from the Second Floor
East Wing.

02:24:25.530 --> 02:24:29.450
There, you see Doctor Emmanuel stumbling down
a dark corridor.

02:24:29.450 --> 02:24:32.971
His movements are oddly listless, like he’s
in a trance.

02:24:32.971 --> 02:24:37.420
Suddenly, there’s another flash of lightning
and a crack of thunder.

02:24:37.420 --> 02:24:41.250
Doctor Emmanuel clutches his gut in pain and
crumples to the floor.

02:24:41.250 --> 02:24:44.370
You access the camera feed from the First
Floor Entrance.

02:24:44.370 --> 02:24:48.771
It seems that the whole area is flooded, is
this because of the storm?

02:24:48.771 --> 02:24:53.950
In a panic, many lower-tier staff members
had tried to escape, defying the lockdown

02:24:53.950 --> 02:24:56.620
protocols in the special containment procedures.

02:24:56.620 --> 02:25:01.160
Now, they’re floating face down in the water,
all dead.

02:25:01.160 --> 02:25:06.830
You access the camera feed from Sub Level
2, and see another corpse lying in the corner.

02:25:06.830 --> 02:25:12.210
He’s wearing an orange jumpsuit - D-Class,
no idea why he was down there.

02:25:12.210 --> 02:25:17.780
The only other notable thing in the basement
was a burst pipe, leaking and spraying more

02:25:17.780 --> 02:25:18.780
water everywhere.

02:25:18.780 --> 02:25:23.540
With trembling fingers, you select the camera
feed for the First Floor Cafeteria.

02:25:23.540 --> 02:25:28.461
The whole room is practically underwater - the
only evidence of the massacre that must have

02:25:28.461 --> 02:25:32.710
taken place are the fragments of clothing
floating on the surface of the water.

02:25:32.710 --> 02:25:38.132
That, and the fleshy, pink slurry forming
at the bottom of the windows.

02:25:38.132 --> 02:25:41.790
It reminds you of the gooey meat runoff in
chicken nugget factories.

02:25:41.790 --> 02:25:44.980
You close your eyes and try to center yourself.

02:25:44.980 --> 02:25:46.670
It’s violent chaos.

02:25:46.670 --> 02:25:49.110
Looking at more of it isn’t getting you
anywhere.

02:25:49.110 --> 02:25:54.360
Instead, you decide to put those new Level
2 Security Access credentials to good use,

02:25:54.360 --> 02:25:56.181
and hop back onto the file for SCP-3280.

02:25:56.181 --> 02:26:01.551
You think to yourself, “There has to be
something I can use on here...”

02:26:01.551 --> 02:26:06.000
But even as you wait for the file to load,
some part of you knows that time is running

02:26:06.000 --> 02:26:07.460
out for you.

02:26:07.460 --> 02:26:12.920
Perhaps it’s the stress, or the fear, or
the filthy mop water you drank, but you’re

02:26:12.920 --> 02:26:15.761
feeling the pressure start to mount, physically.

02:26:15.761 --> 02:26:17.891
Your stomach is beginning to ache.

02:26:17.891 --> 02:26:21.141
You can see blurry shapes moving in the corners
of your eyes.

02:26:21.141 --> 02:26:26.480
It’s getting harder to focus your vision,
and harder still to quiet the terrified voices

02:26:26.480 --> 02:26:27.580
in your mind.

02:26:27.580 --> 02:26:31.801
But you can’t get up - not without knowing
what is doing this to you.

02:26:31.801 --> 02:26:35.780
The containment class for SCP-3280 is now
declassified.

02:26:35.780 --> 02:26:36.780
“Euclid.”

02:26:36.780 --> 02:26:41.010
And what’s more, the Special Containment
Procedures have altered, too.

02:26:41.010 --> 02:26:46.251
They now explain that every week, a new member
of D-Class personnel is to be deposited into

02:26:46.251 --> 02:26:51.400
the entity’s lair in Sub Level 2 through
Subterranean Access Point Gamma.

02:26:51.400 --> 02:26:57.110
The D-Class- or more accurately, the sacrifices
- are to be told lies about why exactly they

02:26:57.110 --> 02:27:00.300
need to descend to the lowest point in the
facility.

02:27:00.300 --> 02:27:05.460
They’re even given a working flashlight
and a defensive nightstick to create the illusion

02:27:05.460 --> 02:27:09.420
that the Foundation expects them to ever return
from the depths.

02:27:09.420 --> 02:27:14.250
Little do they know, they also have a tiny
transmitter sewn into their jumpsuit.

02:27:14.250 --> 02:27:21.021
This broadcasts a frequency that will attract
an eager SCP-3280 to the D-Class’ location,

02:27:21.021 --> 02:27:23.370
like a dinner bell only it can hear.

02:27:23.370 --> 02:27:28.291
The file specifies that SCP-3280 always prefers
live prey.

02:27:28.291 --> 02:27:33.591
“Well, at least that explains the dead D-Class
in Sub Level 2,” you think, hoping that

02:27:33.591 --> 02:27:38.940
it’ll somehow overwhelm the dizziness you’re
feeling, or the nagging pain in your gut.

02:27:38.940 --> 02:27:40.080
You read on.

02:27:40.080 --> 02:27:43.391
Somehow, the file’s tone becomes even more
severe.

02:27:43.391 --> 02:27:49.080
It says that failure to maintain the containment
of SCP-3280 will not only trigger a lockdown,

02:27:49.080 --> 02:27:54.891
it will always call in the intervention of
two different Mobile Task Forces: MTF Iota-12,

02:27:54.891 --> 02:28:00.190
“The Silencers”, and Tau-4, also known
as “Water, Water Everywhere.”

02:28:00.190 --> 02:28:04.690
If twelve hours pass from the point of initial
containment breach, and the O5 Council hasn’t

02:28:04.690 --> 02:28:09.090
been given the “all clear” signal by one
of these teams, preparation begins for an

02:28:09.090 --> 02:28:12.721
imminent XK-Class End of the World Scenario.

02:28:12.721 --> 02:28:15.320
Just reading the words sends you into a cold
sweat.

02:28:15.320 --> 02:28:16.351
“End of the World?

02:28:16.351 --> 02:28:18.380
What on Earth is this creature?”

02:28:18.380 --> 02:28:20.811
Finally, you reach the description.

02:28:20.811 --> 02:28:24.740
You get to find out what this horrifying entity
actually is.

02:28:24.740 --> 02:28:30.710
But the last thing you expect is for the first
sentence in the file to read, “SCP-3280

02:28:30.710 --> 02:28:36.690
is a sapient entity composed of a fluid physically
identical to water, capable of traveling roughly

02:28:36.690 --> 02:28:39.381
two and a half kilometers per hour.”

02:28:39.381 --> 02:28:40.440
It’s water.

02:28:40.440 --> 02:28:44.650
It’s literally a living, thinking blob of
water.

02:28:44.650 --> 02:28:50.910
As you read on, the concerning details pile
up: Any water that the anomalous SCP-3280

02:28:50.910 --> 02:28:55.011
water touches, it integrates into its own
mass.

02:28:55.011 --> 02:29:00.910
But any time water is separated from this
mass, it remains anomalous, and continues

02:29:00.910 --> 02:29:02.211
to act independently.

02:29:02.211 --> 02:29:07.551
When the creature was first discovered, it
was a mere 66.4 liters in volume.

02:29:07.551 --> 02:29:10.681
Now, it’s around twenty five hundred.

02:29:10.681 --> 02:29:16.721
The water infected by SCP-3280 is hostile
to all humans, and not just in a defensive

02:29:16.721 --> 02:29:17.721
manner.

02:29:17.721 --> 02:29:20.740
SCP-3280 will actively seek out human prey.

02:29:20.740 --> 02:29:25.521
And when it finds them, it forces its mass
into any available bodily orifice, including

02:29:25.521 --> 02:29:27.400
the victim’s pores.

02:29:27.400 --> 02:29:32.301
This can happen in such a subtle manner that
you may not even notice yourself being infiltrated.

02:29:32.301 --> 02:29:39.210
But below this, the file has a list of symptoms
for those experiencing 3280 infiltration:

02:29:39.210 --> 02:29:45.700
loss of motor control, weakening of the micturition
reflex, visual hallucinations, and abdominal

02:29:45.700 --> 02:29:46.700
pain.

02:29:46.700 --> 02:29:50.530
As you read the words, your stomach gives
another painful churn.

02:29:50.530 --> 02:29:53.370
Almost like something is moving around inside
you.

02:29:53.370 --> 02:29:55.341
It’s all coming together.

02:29:55.341 --> 02:29:56.341
You read on.

02:29:56.341 --> 02:30:02.170
The file states that SCP-3280 is so difficult
to contain because it exhibits claustrophobic

02:30:02.170 --> 02:30:03.170
tendencies.

02:30:03.170 --> 02:30:08.790
Any time it’s placed inside a container,
whether organic or inorganic, it escapes with

02:30:08.790 --> 02:30:13.400
pressurized water jets that travel at over
255 miles per hour.

02:30:13.400 --> 02:30:20.011
If the water is inside a human, it may literally
explode out of them, killing them in the process.

02:30:20.011 --> 02:30:24.000
Your jittering eyes turn to the gutted body
of Security Officer Nichols.

02:30:24.000 --> 02:30:26.021
It all makes sense now.

02:30:26.021 --> 02:30:30.610
Everything is becoming clear as the pain in
your stomach builds in its intensity.

02:30:30.610 --> 02:30:36.490
The file goes on to say that if ever SCP-3280
escapes Sub Level 2, it may be impossible

02:30:36.490 --> 02:30:38.200
to contain again.

02:30:38.200 --> 02:30:43.831
If 3280 ever escaped the site proper, it would
indeed cause an XK-Class End of the World

02:30:43.831 --> 02:30:49.811
Scenario to unfold, as 3280 merged with our
water cycle and destroyed all of humanity

02:30:49.811 --> 02:30:51.420
on a global scale.

02:30:51.420 --> 02:30:55.420
It would become truly impossible for anyone
to escape.

02:30:55.420 --> 02:30:57.050
You can’t read any more.

02:30:57.050 --> 02:30:59.380
The pain in your stomach is unbearable.

02:30:59.380 --> 02:31:04.170
You jerk from your seat and stumble out into
the hall, doubled over in agony.

02:31:04.170 --> 02:31:06.351
You can feel it pulsing in there.

02:31:06.351 --> 02:31:07.351
Fighting its way out.

02:31:07.351 --> 02:31:10.510
It must have gotten in through the filthy
mop water you were drinking.

02:31:10.510 --> 02:31:15.070
You didn’t even know it, but your fate has
been sealed for hours.

02:31:15.070 --> 02:31:17.780
You’ve been a dead man walking.

02:31:17.780 --> 02:31:21.641
The hum of pain builds in your ears and renders
you almost deaf.

02:31:21.641 --> 02:31:24.960
All you can hear is the patter of rain and
the distant thunder.

02:31:24.960 --> 02:31:30.280
You collapse against the glass, feeling the
coolness of it against the skin of your face.

02:31:30.280 --> 02:31:35.671
And in that moment, you see the water droplets
on the window pane reverse direction.

02:31:35.671 --> 02:31:39.760
They’re slithering up the glass towards
your face in defiance of gravity.

02:31:39.760 --> 02:31:45.410
Then, you realize it’s already over, and
not just for you.

02:31:45.410 --> 02:31:47.300
SCP-3280 has escaped.

02:31:47.300 --> 02:31:51.971
It’s out there, and it’s going to drown
the entire world.

02:31:51.971 --> 02:31:56.431
As you collapse to your knees and prepare
to be torn apart from the inside, your final

02:31:56.431 --> 02:32:00.880
thought is that at least you won’t be alive
to see it.

02:32:00.880 --> 02:32:06.250
Have you ever had a nightmare that you’re
running down a long, dark hallway, getting

02:32:06.250 --> 02:32:08.490
chased by something you can’t see?

02:32:08.490 --> 02:32:12.051
The thing behind you isn’t fast, but that
doesn’t matter.

02:32:12.051 --> 02:32:14.681
You can’t run forever, and the thing knows
it.

02:32:14.681 --> 02:32:17.030
It is a patient predator.

02:32:17.030 --> 02:32:19.070
It toys with its food.

02:32:19.070 --> 02:32:22.021
At first, you move with speed and rhythm.

02:32:22.021 --> 02:32:24.961
The metallic scraping noise behind you grows
quieter.

02:32:24.961 --> 02:32:27.090
You run and stumble through the dark.

02:32:27.090 --> 02:32:30.110
Your muscles start to ache and your lungs
burn.

02:32:30.110 --> 02:32:31.290
Your pace slows.

02:32:31.290 --> 02:32:32.460
It’s still coming.

02:32:32.460 --> 02:32:34.960
You can hear the scraping getting louder.

02:32:34.960 --> 02:32:36.370
You start to panic.

02:32:36.370 --> 02:32:37.370
It’s completely dark.

02:32:37.370 --> 02:32:40.500
You don’t know where you’re running or
even what you’re running from.

02:32:40.500 --> 02:32:45.640
All you know - as you bump against the walls
and the sharp corners that rush towards you

02:32:45.640 --> 02:32:48.800
- is that you can’t run forever.

02:32:48.800 --> 02:32:53.940
You trip, fall, and pain explodes through
your leg as your knee shatters on the concrete

02:32:53.940 --> 02:32:54.940
ground.

02:32:54.940 --> 02:32:56.620
That scraping is getting louder.

02:32:56.620 --> 02:32:58.271
You can barely breathe.

02:32:58.271 --> 02:33:00.480
You can’t run anymore with your injury.

02:33:00.480 --> 02:33:03.291
There’s no way to stop what’s coming.

02:33:03.291 --> 02:33:05.670
There is no escape.

02:33:05.670 --> 02:33:06.981
The scraping is right behind you.

02:33:06.981 --> 02:33:07.981
You scream.

02:33:07.981 --> 02:33:10.590
And then… you wake up.

02:33:10.590 --> 02:33:15.171
Your heart is pounding like thunder in your
chest and your sheets are soaked with sweat,

02:33:15.171 --> 02:33:16.290
but you’re safe.

02:33:16.290 --> 02:33:18.561
You’re out of those awful, dark hallways.

02:33:18.561 --> 02:33:21.681
But what if this wasn’t just a nightmare?

02:33:21.681 --> 02:33:26.340
What if this scenario was real, and there
was no escape from the horror chasing you

02:33:26.340 --> 02:33:27.340
in the darkness?

02:33:27.340 --> 02:33:33.300
That’s what it’s like to have a close
encounter with SCP-1918, a sadistic, sentient

02:33:33.300 --> 02:33:37.080
object that loves playing twisted games with
its prey.

02:33:37.080 --> 02:33:43.570
But this monster never plays fair, and even
worse, it’s always just a simple door away.

02:33:43.570 --> 02:33:49.410
It might even be hiding behind a door near
you, right now, waiting to start a game with

02:33:49.410 --> 02:33:51.181
its new playmate.

02:33:51.181 --> 02:33:56.681
But soon you’ll understand why some doors
should never, ever be opened, and why some

02:33:56.681 --> 02:33:59.230
games are better left unplayed.

02:33:59.230 --> 02:34:05.510
x
SCP - 1918 is an anomaly with two parts: SCP-1918

02:34:05.510 --> 02:34:11.551
itself, and SCP-1918-2, the monster’s underground
lair.

02:34:11.551 --> 02:34:18.251
The duo are a match made in hell, as the chambers
and hallways of 1918-2 are perfectly tailored

02:34:18.251 --> 02:34:21.340
to 1918’s violent hobbies.

02:34:21.340 --> 02:34:27.051
Nobody knows how long this anomaly has been
operating, but it’s probably behind countless

02:34:27.051 --> 02:34:28.210
disappearances.

02:34:28.210 --> 02:34:32.870
After all, 1918 has a habit of breaking its
toys...

02:34:32.870 --> 02:34:38.830
The nightmare began in a small town in Maine,
with a population of only 226 people.

02:34:38.830 --> 02:34:42.431
But that population was about to get lower.

02:34:42.431 --> 02:34:47.261
People in the town began to report strange
noises at night, a droning, metal-on-concrete

02:34:47.261 --> 02:34:51.400
scraping noise, like someone dragging a lead
pipe along the ground.

02:34:51.400 --> 02:34:53.581
At first, people just ignored the sound.

02:34:53.581 --> 02:34:58.921
It was all in their heads, or maybe just a
faulty oven or a washing machine on the fritz.

02:34:58.921 --> 02:35:03.070
Anything that would allow them to forget about
the noise and get on with their daily lives.

02:35:03.070 --> 02:35:05.870
But the noises were coming from below.

02:35:05.870 --> 02:35:11.851
They could be heard out on the streets, most
audibly near manholes and sewer grates.

02:35:11.851 --> 02:35:14.421
People started feeling unsafe in their homes.

02:35:14.421 --> 02:35:17.440
The noises were spooking animals and children.

02:35:17.440 --> 02:35:18.931
People were losing sleep.

02:35:18.931 --> 02:35:23.280
That scraping they all tried to ignore was
beginning to get to them all.

02:35:23.280 --> 02:35:28.051
Letters, emails, and angry phone calls to
the town council were piling up.

02:35:28.051 --> 02:35:31.940
Something had to be done before the whole
town went crazy with fear.

02:35:31.940 --> 02:35:36.061
The mayor authorized four utility workers
to investigate the source of the noise at

02:35:36.061 --> 02:35:38.751
a local sewage treatment facility.

02:35:38.751 --> 02:35:42.480
Considering the scraping was loudest near
the sewer grates, everyone just assumed that

02:35:42.480 --> 02:35:46.210
whatever was causing all this must be connected
to the sewers.

02:35:46.210 --> 02:35:50.920
Four utility workers were sent to investigate
the facility, only to find that the machinery

02:35:50.920 --> 02:35:53.320
on site was working just fine.

02:35:53.320 --> 02:35:57.681
The source of the problems must have been
coming directly from the underground sewer-lines

02:35:57.681 --> 02:35:58.851
themselves.

02:35:58.851 --> 02:36:03.101
The four workers, equipped with headlamps,
descended into a long service tunnel that

02:36:03.101 --> 02:36:05.250
fed into the sewer system.

02:36:05.250 --> 02:36:09.240
As they passed deeper into the tunnel, the
darkness around them became thicker.

02:36:09.240 --> 02:36:14.811
It was a tangible presence that drowned out
the light of their headlamps, similar to the

02:36:14.811 --> 02:36:18.501
anomalous phenomenon exhibited by SCP - 087.

02:36:18.501 --> 02:36:24.360
When the utility workers tried to turn back,
they discovered another impossibility: It

02:36:24.360 --> 02:36:28.820
seemed that the tunnel behind them had become
a solid concrete wall.

02:36:28.820 --> 02:36:30.490
They were trapped, but where?

02:36:30.490 --> 02:36:32.141
It was too dark to tell.

02:36:32.141 --> 02:36:36.980
Confused and terrified, the four men stuck
together, attempting to find a way out.

02:36:36.980 --> 02:36:41.931
It was too dark to see their hand in front
of their face, so all they could do was navigate

02:36:41.931 --> 02:36:44.831
slowly by feeling the walls around them.

02:36:44.831 --> 02:36:46.671
These walls felt oddly...crusty.

02:36:46.671 --> 02:36:53.450
There was a kind of faint, metallic stench
hanging in the air, too, like old blood.

02:36:53.450 --> 02:36:58.570
Something horrible had happened here, and
something horrible was about to happen again.

02:36:58.570 --> 02:37:01.851
All they could do was keep moving and try
to stay calm.

02:37:01.851 --> 02:37:07.131
Eventually, after hours of pawing at walls
in the dark, they found an open doorway.

02:37:07.131 --> 02:37:12.410
One by one, they filed inside, only to feel
blinded when bright, white ceiling lights

02:37:12.410 --> 02:37:13.960
suddenly switched on.

02:37:13.960 --> 02:37:20.721
The room was all white, and filled with pipes,
large and small, running from wall to wall.

02:37:20.721 --> 02:37:24.851
Just then one of the utility workers let out
an ear-splitting scream and pointed towards

02:37:24.851 --> 02:37:25.870
the doorway.

02:37:25.870 --> 02:37:28.400
His colleagues turned, and gasped in shock.

02:37:28.400 --> 02:37:32.811
There was something outside the door, and
it was staring at them.

02:37:32.811 --> 02:37:35.561
The object filled up almost the entire doorway.

02:37:35.561 --> 02:37:40.670
It seemed like a demonic hobby horse, made
from a black-and-white, candy-striped metal

02:37:40.670 --> 02:37:43.570
pole with a crude plastic head on top.

02:37:43.570 --> 02:37:49.910
The head looked like a clown’s, with a wide,
toothy grin, but no visible eyes.

02:37:49.910 --> 02:37:53.090
It was SCP-1918.

02:37:53.090 --> 02:37:58.021
The utility workers were frozen as the object
leaned forward slightly, and slithered into

02:37:58.021 --> 02:38:02.030
the room, the bottom of the metal pipe scraping
against the ground.

02:38:02.030 --> 02:38:07.530
It was the exact same scraping noise that’d
been haunting the concerned townsfolk up above.

02:38:07.530 --> 02:38:09.860
This was the thing behind it all.

02:38:09.860 --> 02:38:17.141
And as the object moved, its metal pole started
to scrape words into the ground: Tik Tak Tow

02:38:17.141 --> 02:38:20.620
None of the four utility workers were ever
seen again.

02:38:20.620 --> 02:38:25.641
It didn’t take long for the SCP Foundation
to descend upon this quiet Maine town and

02:38:25.641 --> 02:38:27.150
pick up the pieces.

02:38:27.150 --> 02:38:31.971
All relevant officials were provided amnestics,
and cover stories were created for the disappearances

02:38:31.971 --> 02:38:34.130
of the four utility workers.

02:38:34.130 --> 02:38:38.061
The Foundation also commandeered the sewage
treatment facility that held the entrance

02:38:38.061 --> 02:38:45.440
to SCP-1918-2, replacing all key roles at
the facility with undercover Foundation personnel.

02:38:45.440 --> 02:38:51.490
SCP-1918 was given a Euclid' classification
due to the fixed nature of its hunting grounds,

02:38:51.490 --> 02:38:54.010
and then the real research began.

02:38:54.010 --> 02:38:57.701
The Foundation soon made some disturbing discoveries.

02:38:57.701 --> 02:39:02.910
Entrances into the SCP-1918-2 area didn’t
follow any kind of logic.

02:39:02.910 --> 02:39:09.330
The hunting ground of SCP-1918 can be entered
from almost any location, if you’re unlucky

02:39:09.330 --> 02:39:10.330
enough.

02:39:10.330 --> 02:39:15.250
There are currently 9 known entrances, including
5 sewage grates, 3 utility shafts located

02:39:15.250 --> 02:39:18.230
in a sewage facility, and 1 toilet.

02:39:18.230 --> 02:39:21.590
And these are just the ones the Foundation
knows about.

02:39:21.590 --> 02:39:29.051
There are a huge number of ways to enter SCP-1918-2,
but to this day, nothing has ever been able

02:39:29.051 --> 02:39:30.801
to leave.

02:39:30.801 --> 02:39:36.090
SCP-1918-2 is contained twenty meters below
the streets of this unassuming Maine town.

02:39:36.090 --> 02:39:41.591
Personnel, aside from Foundation-approved
D-class guinea pigs. are refused entrance.

02:39:41.591 --> 02:39:47.150
Researchers have mapped out the layout of
1918-2 through seismic imaging of SCP-1918’s

02:39:47.150 --> 02:39:48.670
movements.

02:39:48.670 --> 02:39:55.391
There are 18 identical room pairs in SCP-1918-2,
or 9 compound rooms.

02:39:55.391 --> 02:40:00.280
Rooms are differentiated between a '1' room
and a '2' room by crude carvings on the floors

02:40:00.280 --> 02:40:03.061
outside of the individual rooms.

02:40:03.061 --> 02:40:09.291
SCP-1918-2 is symmetrical, with half a meter
wide paths circling each compound room.

02:40:09.291 --> 02:40:13.500
The only deviations to this construction are
the location of entrances on the sides of

02:40:13.500 --> 02:40:18.351
each individual room, which vary randomly
while the location is “active.”

02:40:18.351 --> 02:40:22.630
What exactly does SCP-1918 do in this private
little maze?

02:40:22.630 --> 02:40:25.070
It plays games, of course.

02:40:25.070 --> 02:40:30.501
Its two favorites - as indicated by the words
it scrapes onto the ground - are “Tik Tak

02:40:30.501 --> 02:40:32.461
Tow” and “Memoree”

02:40:32.461 --> 02:40:39.290
In Tik Tak Tow, 1918 moves to each “1”
room, leaving behind "X" markings on the floors

02:40:39.290 --> 02:40:44.021
if the room is not already marked with an
"O" in a manner similar to a game of "Tic

02:40:44.021 --> 02:40:45.021
Tac Toe''.

02:40:45.021 --> 02:40:50.090
How a victim is meant to accomplish making
a mark or understand this process is unknown,

02:40:50.090 --> 02:40:52.040
as no aides are given.

02:40:52.040 --> 02:40:56.851
Blood is commonly used by victims to make
their markings, hence the rusty smell in many

02:40:56.851 --> 02:40:57.851
of the rooms.

02:40:57.851 --> 02:41:03.561
In Memoree, the trapped victim is rendered
unconscious by blunt force, presumably from

02:41:03.561 --> 02:41:05.410
SCP-1918.

02:41:05.410 --> 02:41:09.690
The subject regains consciousness in a random
section of the facility.

02:41:09.690 --> 02:41:13.450
Success is marked by finding a “1” room
identical to the central room.

02:41:13.450 --> 02:41:18.971
This event seems to possess a time limit,
as the subject is pursued by SCP-1918 throughout

02:41:18.971 --> 02:41:20.811
the halls of the facility.

02:41:20.811 --> 02:41:25.160
The subject "wins'' by marking the correct
room with an "O".

02:41:25.160 --> 02:41:28.181
What happens if you win or lose these games?

02:41:28.181 --> 02:41:34.551
It’s important to note that SCP-1918 is
very competitive, and doesn’t play fair.

02:41:34.551 --> 02:41:39.230
If you win, the object will merely accuse
you of cheating, and start a new game.

02:41:39.230 --> 02:41:44.590
This will happen again and again, until eventually…
you lose.

02:41:44.590 --> 02:41:45.590
And when you do?

02:41:45.590 --> 02:41:53.061
Well, take the horrifying encounter D-Class
personnel member D-2934 had with SCP-1918.

02:41:53.061 --> 02:42:00.580
Wearing video and audio equipment, D-2934
was led into SCP-1918-2 by Foundation researchers.

02:42:00.580 --> 02:42:05.601
When he eventually found his way to the central
room, 1918 challenged him to a game of Tik

02:42:05.601 --> 02:42:06.601
Tak Tow.

02:42:06.601 --> 02:42:11.040
And, against all odds, D-2934 won the game.

02:42:11.040 --> 02:42:14.160
But 1918 didn’t take kindly to that.

02:42:14.160 --> 02:42:19.570
It accused D-2934 of cheating, carving its
accusations into the ground before challenging

02:42:19.570 --> 02:42:22.400
him to a deadly game of Memoree.

02:42:22.400 --> 02:42:27.670
After hours of chasing, D-2934 eventually
lost his mind and was backed into a corner

02:42:27.670 --> 02:42:29.370
by 1918.

02:42:29.370 --> 02:42:33.960
As the object made its way towards him, he
panicked, ripped a pipe from the wall, and

02:42:33.960 --> 02:42:36.601
began smashing 1918’s head.

02:42:36.601 --> 02:42:40.780
As the plastic cracked under the force of
the blows, Foundation scientists could see

02:42:40.780 --> 02:42:42.811
real brains inside.

02:42:42.811 --> 02:42:46.330
D-2934 screamed, and the video feed cut off.

02:42:46.330 --> 02:42:51.820
When the video turned back on some time later,
1918 stared into the camera with a different

02:42:51.820 --> 02:42:54.340
head mounted atop its metal pole.

02:42:54.340 --> 02:42:58.671
One that, just a few hours earlier, had belonged
to the unfortunate D-2934.

02:42:58.671 --> 02:43:05.200
If there’s one lesson to be learned from
this terrifying anomaly, it’s that there

02:43:05.200 --> 02:43:10.311
truly is no escape from SCP-1918.

02:43:10.311 --> 02:43:16.420
Imagine this - it’s summer vacation and
you're a kid.

02:43:16.420 --> 02:43:20.400
You and your friends are playing in the woods
near your neighborhood, just like you've been

02:43:20.400 --> 02:43:23.471
doing most days during the break from school.

02:43:23.471 --> 02:43:25.440
One day, you spot a treehouse.

02:43:25.440 --> 02:43:30.880
It’s not that high off the ground and it's
very simply built from leaves, grass, and

02:43:30.880 --> 02:43:31.880
scraps of wood.

02:43:31.880 --> 02:43:35.260
You and your friends are curious, so you decide
to check it out.

02:43:35.260 --> 02:43:38.050
Upon investigation, you find a kid in there.

02:43:38.050 --> 02:43:41.490
He says his name is Billy, and this is his
treehouse.

02:43:41.490 --> 02:43:45.660
You don't recognize him from school, but you
figure he must just be new in town.

02:43:45.660 --> 02:43:51.660
He asks if he can join your group, and, wanting
to be nice to the new kid, you tell him “okay.”

02:43:51.660 --> 02:43:56.271
You spend the rest of the day playing with
him - games like hide and seek, tag, and red

02:43:56.271 --> 02:44:00.501
rover, until it's time for everyone to go
home for dinner.

02:44:00.501 --> 02:44:05.450
Strangely, Billy doesn't seem to leave, he
just stays in his treehouse.

02:44:05.450 --> 02:44:09.490
For the rest of the week, playing with Billy
and his treehouse become a regular fixture

02:44:09.490 --> 02:44:15.200
of your daily routine, but oddly enough, he
never comes to hang out at any of your houses,

02:44:15.200 --> 02:44:19.150
and you never seem to see him anywhere else
but in the woods.

02:44:19.150 --> 02:44:23.870
One day, however, he decides to invite one
of your friends, Amy, to hang out with him

02:44:23.870 --> 02:44:25.540
at the treehouse alone.

02:44:25.540 --> 02:44:29.791
You think nothing of it, but after that point,
you never see Billy again.

02:44:29.791 --> 02:44:34.300
It’s a couple of weeks before you and your
friends see Amy again, and when you do, she

02:44:34.300 --> 02:44:36.150
appears off somehow.

02:44:36.150 --> 02:44:39.420
She seems to be spending a lot of time in
that treehouse.

02:44:39.420 --> 02:44:43.820
Billy has disappeared, but you and Amy and
the rest of the kids keep meeting up to play

02:44:43.820 --> 02:44:45.431
together in the woods.

02:44:45.431 --> 02:44:51.070
One day Amy pulls you aside, she wants you
to come meet with her tomorrow at the treehouse…

02:44:51.070 --> 02:44:52.170
alone.

02:44:52.170 --> 02:44:58.470
This is typically how an SCP-974 infestation
begins - with a mysterious new kid inviting

02:44:58.470 --> 02:45:02.421
a group of friends to hang out in his crudely
made treehouse.

02:45:02.421 --> 02:45:10.711
But as you might have guessed, this kid isn't
a kid - he's SCP-974, a carnivorous monster

02:45:10.711 --> 02:45:13.340
that only looks like a human child.

02:45:13.340 --> 02:45:18.440
It can live on small woodland animals, but
its preferred prey… is kids between the

02:45:18.440 --> 02:45:25.110
ages of 6 and 12, taking the phrase 'you are
what you eat' to the next level.

02:45:25.110 --> 02:45:29.931
The entity will install itself in an area
with a sufficient amount of trees, in proximity

02:45:29.931 --> 02:45:31.920
to a decent population of children.

02:45:31.920 --> 02:45:37.450
It will then construct a crude treehouse to
serve as its nest, and begin befriending groups

02:45:37.450 --> 02:45:40.101
of between 2 and 5 children.

02:45:40.101 --> 02:45:44.080
The creature will engage in normal outdoor
games and allow its new 'friends' to come

02:45:44.080 --> 02:45:48.660
and go as they please, building the trust
of its newfound playmates.

02:45:48.660 --> 02:45:52.920
But then, after about a week, it will select
its victim.

02:45:52.920 --> 02:45:58.460
SCP-974 will single out one member of the
group and invite them to the treehouse alone.

02:45:58.460 --> 02:46:04.250
Whether they accept or deny the invitation
is irrelevant, because this is the point where

02:46:04.250 --> 02:46:09.190
SCP-974 will strike, subduing and then devouring
that child.

02:46:09.190 --> 02:46:13.891
After doing so, the creature will disappear
from the area, going into a state of hibernation

02:46:13.891 --> 02:46:15.811
for roughly 12 days.

02:46:15.811 --> 02:46:20.480
During that time, it goes through a period
of metamorphosis, transforming from whoever

02:46:20.480 --> 02:46:26.080
it looked like before into an exact likeness
of the child it just consumed.

02:46:26.080 --> 02:46:31.351
SCP-974 will continue this cycle of selecting
and catching prey until there are no children

02:46:31.351 --> 02:46:32.990
left in the surrounding area.

02:46:32.990 --> 02:46:39.450
While it's initially friendly to children,
SCP-974 has an intense fear of any older human

02:46:39.450 --> 02:46:40.470
beings.

02:46:40.470 --> 02:46:44.421
The mere presence of a person older than 13
is enough to trigger the creature's fight

02:46:44.421 --> 02:46:48.910
or flight response, and it will run away if
it sees any adults coming.

02:46:48.910 --> 02:46:55.070
When running isn't an option, SCP-974 will
resort to violence to defend itself.

02:46:55.070 --> 02:47:01.751
Despite its looks, SCP-974 is much stronger,
faster, and more resistant to damage than

02:47:01.751 --> 02:47:06.830
a child, and it has been known to completely
rip adults apart in situations where it felt

02:47:06.830 --> 02:47:08.780
threatened and cornered.

02:47:08.780 --> 02:47:14.080
SCP-974 does not appear to be affected by
bullets or striking weapons, and the only

02:47:14.080 --> 02:47:18.280
reliable way to put down an instance seems
to be with fire.

02:47:18.280 --> 02:47:23.371
When infestations are discovered in the wild,
the normal SCP foundation protocol is to attempt

02:47:23.371 --> 02:47:28.501
to capture the creature, but if deadly force
is required, agents will set fire to the creature's

02:47:28.501 --> 02:47:33.870
nest and a portion of the surrounding area
until it has been confirmed dead, before covering

02:47:33.870 --> 02:47:37.250
up the destruction as the result of a regular
forest fire.

02:47:37.250 --> 02:47:43.960
The SCP foundation was able to capture one
instance of SCP-974 and place it in containment,

02:47:43.960 --> 02:47:48.120
hoping that having one in captivity would
provide insight into the creature's origins.

02:47:48.120 --> 02:47:54.141
It was placed in a lightly wooded enclosure
at Zoological Reserve Site 16, where it immediately

02:47:54.141 --> 02:47:58.570
started constructing multiple treehouse nests
from the plant life it found.

02:47:58.570 --> 02:48:04.471
Initially, the containment of SCP-974 involved
offering the creature live human prey.

02:48:04.471 --> 02:48:09.671
Once every 3 months, a group of 4 children
would be brought in, in accordance with Protocol

02:48:09.671 --> 02:48:10.671
12.

02:48:10.671 --> 02:48:15.010
The children would be given room and board
in on-site barracks, and encouraged to explore

02:48:15.010 --> 02:48:18.601
the enclosure and play with SCP-974.

02:48:18.601 --> 02:48:23.980
If 974 had not selected a victim within 5
days, the group of children would be sent

02:48:23.980 --> 02:48:27.070
away and a new group would be introduced.

02:48:27.070 --> 02:48:31.811
This system worked for a few years, but as
you might expect, the Ethics Committee had

02:48:31.811 --> 02:48:35.980
a problem with the practice of offering up
live children to a deadly anomaly.

02:48:35.980 --> 02:48:42.530
Now, as of January 1st, 2015, the team at
Zoological Reserve Site 16 are no longer able

02:48:42.530 --> 02:48:46.320
to evoke Protocol 12 in order to acquire children.

02:48:46.320 --> 02:48:52.110
Attempts to use another SCP - SCP-1680, a
collection of clones of a missing 8-year-old

02:48:52.110 --> 02:48:56.650
boy - failed, as SCP-974 refused to eat them.

02:48:56.650 --> 02:49:01.190
The procedures then changed to only allow
small animals to be introduced into the enclosure

02:49:01.190 --> 02:49:02.190
as prey.

02:49:02.190 --> 02:49:08.320
While it might seem like this was a good idea
that would stop SCP-974 from killing any more

02:49:08.320 --> 02:49:13.150
children, like a lot of seemingly good changes
to containment procedures in the Foundation,

02:49:13.150 --> 02:49:17.740
this well intentioned move would ultimately
have deadly consequences.

02:49:17.740 --> 02:49:23.011
SCP-974 at first seemed to behave normally
despite being denied its favorite food.

02:49:23.011 --> 02:49:29.440
But then, on August 16th, 2015, while on their
weekly sweep of the enclosure, patrol teams

02:49:29.440 --> 02:49:35.141
found that 974 had destroyed all of the treehouses
it had built in its time in containment.

02:49:35.141 --> 02:49:38.790
The SCP itself was also nowhere to be found.

02:49:38.790 --> 02:49:43.790
There was something new in the enclosure though,
a small oval of disturbed soil.

02:49:43.790 --> 02:49:48.811
A geological team was called in, and through
ground penetrating radar, it was found that

02:49:48.811 --> 02:49:52.860
there was a humanoid figure buried there,
curled up in a fetal position.

02:49:52.860 --> 02:49:55.480
This couldn't be SCP-974, could it?

02:49:55.480 --> 02:49:59.690
The figure was much too long and thin to be
anything resembling a human child.

02:49:59.690 --> 02:50:05.210
But it had to be SCP-974 - it was the only
living thing in the enclosure.

02:50:05.210 --> 02:50:09.440
The scientists were intrigued, and they theorized
that the SCP might have been entering a new

02:50:09.440 --> 02:50:10.940
life stage.

02:50:10.940 --> 02:50:13.700
Further scans were conducted over the next
10 days.

02:50:13.700 --> 02:50:18.320
During that time, the creature never moved
from its position, though it did continue

02:50:18.320 --> 02:50:19.320
to grow.

02:50:19.320 --> 02:50:22.931
It seemed like it was absorbing nutrients
from the surrounding soil.

02:50:22.931 --> 02:50:25.950
The team decided to exhume the creature to
examine it.

02:50:25.950 --> 02:50:32.570
When they dug it up, they found that SCP-974
had stretched out, now measuring 220 cm in

02:50:32.570 --> 02:50:36.061
length and weighing just 37.4 kilograms.

02:50:36.061 --> 02:50:41.391
It had no features or orifices of any kind
anywhere on its body, and its now pale white

02:50:41.391 --> 02:50:47.211
skin was covered in some kind of sticky mucus
that, when examined, was found to contain

02:50:47.211 --> 02:50:49.910
a previously undiscovered enzyme.

02:50:49.910 --> 02:50:52.561
The creature was alive, but barely.

02:50:52.561 --> 02:50:57.671
It wasn't breathing, and its heartbeat was
extremely slow, almost to the point of being

02:50:57.671 --> 02:50:59.190
undetectable.

02:50:59.190 --> 02:51:05.740
SCP-974 was examined for an additional four
weeks, after which it died, and was sent for

02:51:05.740 --> 02:51:06.860
dissection.

02:51:06.860 --> 02:51:11.171
Some of the scientists and researchers at
Zoological Site 16 were disappointed to hear

02:51:11.171 --> 02:51:13.200
about 974's death.

02:51:13.200 --> 02:51:18.141
As vicious and feral as the creature was,
they'd developed a certain fondness for it,

02:51:18.141 --> 02:51:20.050
and its many little treehouses.

02:51:20.050 --> 02:51:25.120
Luckily, it wouldn't be too much longer until
a new specimen was obtained.

02:51:25.120 --> 02:51:32.580
On October 16th, 2016, a group of no less
than 7 instances of SCP-974 were discovered

02:51:32.580 --> 02:51:34.620
near a major American city.

02:51:34.620 --> 02:51:38.580
The containment team was forced to kill 6
of the anomalies in the attempts to capture

02:51:38.580 --> 02:51:43.820
them, but one instance survived and was taken
to Zoological Site 16.

02:51:43.820 --> 02:51:49.501
As was mandated, the area was burned and Foundation
counterintelligence disseminated a cover story

02:51:49.501 --> 02:51:53.660
about a forest fire caused by an improperly
extinguished campfire.

02:51:53.660 --> 02:52:00.370
The new SCP-974 was, like the original one,
placed in the enclosure and denied human prey.

02:52:00.370 --> 02:52:05.650
Also like the first one, this 974 buried itself
after being denied its preferred meals for

02:52:05.650 --> 02:52:06.931
several months.

02:52:06.931 --> 02:52:11.990
The decision was made to leave the SCP underground
longer than in the first instance, to see

02:52:11.990 --> 02:52:16.211
what it might become if this developmental
stage wasn't interrupted.

02:52:16.211 --> 02:52:22.500
On January 25th, 2017, the creature finally
dug itself free from the earth.

02:52:22.500 --> 02:52:29.920
Now designated SCP-974-A, it was far more
aggressive than any instance of 974 had ever

02:52:29.920 --> 02:52:31.300
been before.

02:52:31.300 --> 02:52:35.370
As soon as it was free from the dirt, it made
a beeline straight for the nearest monitoring

02:52:35.370 --> 02:52:36.370
station.

02:52:36.370 --> 02:52:41.210
It ripped the roof off and tore the 6 team
members stationed there to shreds in just

02:52:41.210 --> 02:52:42.581
90 seconds.

02:52:42.581 --> 02:52:47.730
When the response team arrived 15 minutes
later, only 12% of the human remains were

02:52:47.730 --> 02:52:49.551
able to be recovered.

02:52:49.551 --> 02:52:54.720
But, strangely enough, it at first seemed
that one of the team had been spared.

02:52:54.720 --> 02:52:59.410
Georgia Stone, one of the monitoring team,
was severely injured, but apparently in a

02:52:59.410 --> 02:53:00.820
stable condition.

02:53:00.820 --> 02:53:05.210
Disoriented, she approached the response team,
begging for assistance and urging them to

02:53:05.210 --> 02:53:07.090
take her out of the enclosure.

02:53:07.090 --> 02:53:12.120
But the team was skeptical - they knew that
SCP-974 could become an exact copy of any

02:53:12.120 --> 02:53:18.841
child it consumed, so it followed that the
fully-grown SCP-974-A might be able to copy

02:53:18.841 --> 02:53:19.841
adults.

02:53:19.841 --> 02:53:25.101
They asked Georgia questions in order to confirm
her identity, but she was unable to answer

02:53:25.101 --> 02:53:26.101
them.

02:53:26.101 --> 02:53:31.220
Having been found out, SCP-974, still mimicking
Georgia, attacked the response team.

02:53:31.220 --> 02:53:36.230
They'd been armed with flamethrowers, but
unfortunately, on top of its resistance to

02:53:36.230 --> 02:53:42.750
damage, the adult form of 974 didn't seem
to be afraid of, or harmed by, fire.

02:53:42.750 --> 02:53:47.030
The team was at a loss for how to kill this
thing, or even subdue it long enough to get

02:53:47.030 --> 02:53:49.061
out safely.

02:53:49.061 --> 02:53:54.580
SCP-974-A was tearing through the members
of the team like they were made of paper.

02:53:54.580 --> 02:53:59.141
Thinking quickly, one member of the response
team, a guard named Emilio, pulled out one

02:53:59.141 --> 02:54:01.940
of his standard issue Foundation hand grenades.

02:54:01.940 --> 02:54:08.220
When SCP-974-A came at him, he pulled the
pin and, holding the grenade, shoved his arm

02:54:08.220 --> 02:54:09.931
into the creature's open mouth.

02:54:09.931 --> 02:54:16.290
While the explosion destroyed Emilio's arm,
it didn't even break the skin of SCP-974-A.

02:54:16.290 --> 02:54:22.190
However, it did result in serious damage to
its internal organs, which finally killed

02:54:22.190 --> 02:54:23.190
it.

02:54:23.190 --> 02:54:27.570
Following its death, an autopsy was conducted,
revealing enough about the creature that a

02:54:27.570 --> 02:54:32.460
new file of effective methods of extermination
was able to be created.

02:54:32.460 --> 02:54:38.141
After this event, the protocols for SCP-974
containment were completely overhauled.

02:54:38.141 --> 02:54:44.360
Any instances of SCP-974-A seen in the wild
are to be killed as quickly as possible.

02:54:44.360 --> 02:54:48.900
More disturbingly though, the ethics committee
rescinded their previous decision, and any

02:54:48.900 --> 02:54:55.311
instances of 974 that are brought into containment
are to be provided with human prey again.

02:54:55.311 --> 02:55:01.181
Letting SCP-974 kill children might not be
a very humane way of keeping it contained,

02:55:01.181 --> 02:55:06.641
but given how much more aggressive and hard
to kill this SCP's adult form is, any option

02:55:06.641 --> 02:55:11.400
that stops the creature's metamorphosis from
happening is likely the best option in the

02:55:11.400 --> 02:55:12.530
long run.

02:55:12.530 --> 02:55:18.110
So remember: If ever you’re out in the woods
and see a crudely constructed treehouse, perhaps

02:55:18.110 --> 02:55:21.271
think twice about how innocent it is.

02:55:21.271 --> 02:55:26.501
There could be something hungry lurking inside…

02:55:26.501 --> 02:55:27.501
The

02:55:27.501 --> 02:55:31.251
first thing that tipped the Foundation
off to SCP-087’s presence were the reports

02:55:31.251 --> 02:55:34.150
of numerous unexplained disappearances on
campus.

02:55:34.150 --> 02:55:38.370
There were plenty of rumors about what might
be behind them, but Field Agents suspected

02:55:38.370 --> 02:55:43.431
that the true source of the vanishing would
be something beyond civilian imagination.

02:55:43.431 --> 02:55:48.280
All anyone knew for sure was that everyone
who had gone missing was last seen in a certain

02:55:48.280 --> 02:55:52.940
administrative building on the university
grounds, and that the disappearances only

02:55:52.940 --> 02:55:55.391
seemed to happen when the elevator was out.

02:55:55.391 --> 02:56:00.271
The campus was soon flooded with Foundation
agents, creating a barrier around the administrative

02:56:00.271 --> 02:56:03.021
building, and the presumed habitat of SCP
- 087.

02:56:03.021 --> 02:56:09.141
Nobody else could get in, and hopefully, whatever
was inside couldn’t get out.

02:56:09.141 --> 02:56:14.000
One of the Foundation’s lead scientists
was flown in to consult on the investigation.

02:56:14.000 --> 02:56:16.360
What could have been behind all those students
disappearing?

02:56:16.360 --> 02:56:20.300
The doctor’s preliminary interviews with
university staff who worked in the building

02:56:20.300 --> 02:56:25.931
yielded some interesting details: Strange
noises, like banging and even a faint, shrill

02:56:25.931 --> 02:56:30.570
crying, would be heard from a door that lead
to a no longer used stairway in Hallway 3B.

02:56:30.570 --> 02:56:35.490
Staff in the building had no reason to ever
take these stairs, especially considering

02:56:35.490 --> 02:56:40.592
how many of them reported a strange sense
of unease when just standing outside the door.

02:56:40.592 --> 02:56:44.670
The only reason someone might take those stairs
is due to…Elevator malfunctions.

02:56:44.670 --> 02:56:49.070
In that instant, the doctor had put it all
together.

02:56:49.070 --> 02:56:53.021
The staff they interviewed had their memory
wiped with Amnetics – special chemicals

02:56:53.021 --> 02:56:56.340
used by the Foundation with the power to delete
human memories.

02:56:56.340 --> 02:57:01.181
The Foundation only used them for staff or
civilians who had confirmed contact with an

02:57:01.181 --> 02:57:05.250
SCP, and the doctor knew that they had a live
one on their hands.

02:57:05.250 --> 02:57:06.250
The staircase.

02:57:06.250 --> 02:57:11.210
There was something terribly wrong with that
staircase, and it was the SCP Foundation’s

02:57:11.210 --> 02:57:15.860
job to find out what – before it made anybody
else disappear.

02:57:15.860 --> 02:57:22.220
This is the story of SCP – 087, otherwise
known as The Endless Staircase, and the three

02:57:22.220 --> 02:57:25.511
doomed journeys down into its murky depths.

02:57:25.511 --> 02:57:30.551
The doctor was more than eager to begin research
into the staircase, and its frightening, anomalous

02:57:30.551 --> 02:57:31.650
properties.

02:57:31.650 --> 02:57:35.630
After all, you don’t claw your way up to
being one of the Foundation’s key researchers

02:57:35.630 --> 02:57:40.221
without being brave, and perhaps just a little
bit deranged.

02:57:40.221 --> 02:57:44.830
As was standard, once a perimeter was secured
around the staircase, the good doctor requested

02:57:44.830 --> 02:57:47.181
a selection of D-Class personnel for testing.

02:57:47.181 --> 02:57:52.181
For those not in the know, D-Class is the
Foundation’s polite way of saying “cannon

02:57:52.181 --> 02:57:53.181
fodder.”

02:57:53.181 --> 02:57:59.170
The doctor was sent three D-Class prisoners
for use in his investigation of SCP – 087.

02:57:59.170 --> 02:58:05.290
The first, D-8432, was – according to official
documentation on the incident – a “43-year

02:58:05.290 --> 02:58:09.900
old male of average build and appearance and
unremarkable psychological background.”

02:58:09.900 --> 02:58:14.631
This man once worked for the Foundation in
a more official capacity, but he was given

02:58:14.631 --> 02:58:20.601
the often-deadly demotion to D-Class due to
a dangerous mistake handling SCP – 682 that

02:58:20.601 --> 02:58:23.110
lead to the deaths of several other agents.

02:58:23.110 --> 02:58:25.960
Now, it looked like it would be his turn.

02:58:25.960 --> 02:58:30.740
The doctor explained his mission to him: Explore
the staircase, gather data, help us find out

02:58:30.740 --> 02:58:32.830
exactly what we’re dealing with here.

02:58:32.830 --> 02:58:36.410
If you come back alive, there may even be
a promotion in it for you.

02:58:36.410 --> 02:58:41.971
And with that promise, D-8432 was given his
load-out: a 75-watt flood lamp with battery

02:58:41.971 --> 02:58:47.130
power capable of lasting 24 hours, an audio
headset, and a handheld camcorder fitted with

02:58:47.130 --> 02:58:48.931
a transmission stream.

02:58:48.931 --> 02:58:54.751
D-8432 was then pushed through the door in
Hallway 3B, and out onto the staircase.

02:58:54.751 --> 02:59:00.341
According to declassified Foundation files
describing the staircase, “SCP-087 is an

02:59:00.341 --> 02:59:02.370
unlit platform staircase.

02:59:02.370 --> 02:59:07.690
Stairs descend on a 38-degree angle for 13
steps before reaching a semi-circular platform

02:59:07.690 --> 02:59:10.521
of approximately 3 meters in diameter.

02:59:10.521 --> 02:59:14.351
Descent direction rotates 180 degrees at each
platform.

02:59:14.351 --> 02:59:20.580
The design of SCP-087 limits subjects to a
visual range of approximately 1.5 flights.”

02:59:20.580 --> 02:59:25.510
But in D-8432’s mind, “unlit” really
didn’t seem like the right word.

02:59:25.510 --> 02:59:28.790
He would have chosen “all-consuming darkness.”

02:59:28.790 --> 02:59:34.811
Despite carrying a powerful 75-watt lamp,
D-8432 was only capable of partially lighting

02:59:34.811 --> 02:59:39.470
the platform he was standing on – and the
illumination only stretched down nine of the

02:59:39.470 --> 02:59:42.200
thirteen steps to the next platform.

02:59:42.200 --> 02:59:46.940
When D-8432 observed how little help his lamp
was giving him, he was instructed to shine

02:59:46.940 --> 02:59:49.910
it out of the doorway into Hallway 3B.

02:59:49.910 --> 02:59:55.910
When he did so, the light seemed to shine
far further than it ever could in SCP – 087.

02:59:55.910 --> 03:00:01.240
Already, the beginning of anomalous activity
was obvious: Everywhere else, darkness is

03:00:01.240 --> 03:00:03.141
just the absence of light.

03:00:03.141 --> 03:00:06.150
In SCP – 087, darkness eats light.

03:00:06.150 --> 03:00:11.021
It was like a tangible, black mass that only
a certain amount of light could survive, while

03:00:11.021 --> 03:00:13.250
the rest just wouldn’t show.

03:00:13.250 --> 03:00:16.101
D-8432 swallowed hard over a lump in his throat.

03:00:16.101 --> 03:00:20.931
The door to Hallway 3B was closed behind him,
and he was ordered to descend.

03:00:20.931 --> 03:00:25.230
Surviving to see that promotion was feeling
unlikely, but it’s not like he had a choice.

03:00:25.230 --> 03:00:31.380
If he tried to escape SCP – 087 before he
was permitted, he’d be shot by SCP Foundation

03:00:31.380 --> 03:00:32.540
Field Agents on the spot.

03:00:32.540 --> 03:00:36.681
So he followed the high-ranking doctor’s
orders and began to descend the steps to the

03:00:36.681 --> 03:00:38.070
next platform.

03:00:38.070 --> 03:00:42.950
Nothing about the physical makeup of the staircase
itself seemed abnormal – the base and walls

03:00:42.950 --> 03:00:46.700
were a very plain, dull concrete, with a metal
handrail.

03:00:46.700 --> 03:00:51.230
The only thing that seemed unique about it
so far was the strange light-bending properties.

03:00:51.230 --> 03:00:58.460
That was, until he reached the second platform
down and he heard it, a soft, echoing cry.

03:00:58.460 --> 03:00:59.820
A child’s cry.

03:00:59.820 --> 03:01:04.131
It was shrieks of panic, or maybe even pain,
echoing up from below.

03:01:04.131 --> 03:01:08.320
He was asked why he had stopped, and he explained
the crying sound he’d been hearing.

03:01:08.320 --> 03:01:12.580
It sounded like it was coming from far down
the stairs, maybe 200 meters below him.

03:01:12.580 --> 03:01:17.700
He could just make out the words “please”,
help”, and “down here” coming from the

03:01:17.700 --> 03:01:18.700
darkness.

03:01:18.700 --> 03:01:22.790
But the team outside the stairwell couldn’t
hear anything, so they asked him to descend

03:01:22.790 --> 03:01:23.790
further.

03:01:23.790 --> 03:01:28.931
Another platform down, and they could hear
it too, the unmistakable cries of a terrified

03:01:28.931 --> 03:01:29.931
child.

03:01:29.931 --> 03:01:32.341
“Please”, “help”, and “down here.”

03:01:32.341 --> 03:01:37.760
D-8432 was ordered to keep going and only
stop if he noticed changes to the visual environment

03:01:37.760 --> 03:01:40.120
or in the sounds he was hearing.

03:01:40.120 --> 03:01:45.010
D-8432, knowing his life was on the line,
had to keep going, and descended another twenty

03:01:45.010 --> 03:01:49.181
flights of stairs before stopping to remark
that the sounds of the child hadn’t gotten

03:01:49.181 --> 03:01:50.181
any closer.

03:01:50.181 --> 03:01:53.460
They still sounded just as far away as when
he’d first heard them.

03:01:53.460 --> 03:01:57.330
He was told his observations were noted, and
pressured to continue.

03:01:57.330 --> 03:02:03.811
Within half an hour, D-8432 had descended
a full fifty floors, with no sign of a bottom

03:02:03.811 --> 03:02:04.811
in sight.

03:02:04.811 --> 03:02:08.410
Somehow the volume of the child’s crying
had remained consistent throughout, as if

03:02:08.410 --> 03:02:13.030
it was moving away from D-8432 at the same
rate he was descending.

03:02:13.030 --> 03:02:16.620
At this point, D-8432 reported that he was
feeling uneasy.

03:02:16.620 --> 03:02:20.681
The doctor said that this was understandable,
given the circumstances.

03:02:20.681 --> 03:02:25.170
He’d been watching what little there was
to see over a live video feed the entire time,

03:02:25.170 --> 03:02:30.280
and something about the truly bottomless nature
of the staircase, and the ever-elusive crying,

03:02:30.280 --> 03:02:31.610
was undeniably eerie.

03:02:31.610 --> 03:02:35.630
But things were about to really take a turn
for the worst.

03:02:35.630 --> 03:02:39.690
As D-8432 stepped forward towards the next
set of stairs, he froze.

03:02:39.690 --> 03:02:44.601
There was something on the platform below
him, barely illuminated by the light of his

03:02:44.601 --> 03:02:45.601
75-watt bulb.

03:02:45.601 --> 03:02:46.601
It was a face.

03:02:46.601 --> 03:02:52.030
Vaguely human in size and shape, but with
a few terrifying differences: it had greyish

03:02:52.030 --> 03:02:55.530
skin, and no mouth, nostrils, or pupils.

03:02:55.530 --> 03:02:59.420
And yet, D-8432 could feel that this thing
was making eye contact with him.

03:02:59.420 --> 03:03:03.601
He couldn’t move, trapped in this thing’s
piercing gaze.

03:03:03.601 --> 03:03:10.189
In an instant, the face jerked forwards, suddenly
only about a foot away from D-8432’s face

03:03:10.189 --> 03:03:12.091
– eyes staring into his own.

03:03:12.091 --> 03:03:17.811
D-8432 screamed and ran, scaling all fifty
flights in an astonishing eighteen minutes,

03:03:17.811 --> 03:03:20.431
before charging out into Hallway 3B.

03:03:20.431 --> 03:03:25.271
There, he collapsed from the exhaustion and
the fear of what he’d just seen.

03:03:25.271 --> 03:03:30.021
Upon reviewing the footage, the strange face
was designated “SCP-087-1.”

03:03:30.021 --> 03:03:32.091
Fascinating.

03:03:32.091 --> 03:03:34.360
It was time for a second experiment.

03:03:34.360 --> 03:03:36.761
The doctor just had to know more.

03:03:36.761 --> 03:03:42.771
The second test subject was D-9035, a 28-year-old
male with a history of aggravated assaults

03:03:42.771 --> 03:03:43.771
against women.

03:03:43.771 --> 03:03:48.621
He was given the same loadout as his predecessor,
except this time with an even more powerful

03:03:48.621 --> 03:03:49.851
100-watt bulb.

03:03:49.851 --> 03:03:56.250
He was also given 100 small LED lights that
had adhesive backs and a battery life of approximately

03:03:56.250 --> 03:04:01.210
3 weeks, with which they intended to permanently
illuminate SCP – 087.

03:04:01.210 --> 03:04:05.601
However, despite the extra wattage of his
bulb, he still couldn’t illuminate beyond

03:04:05.601 --> 03:04:06.870
the ninth step.

03:04:06.870 --> 03:04:09.931
SCP – 087 wouldn’t allow it.

03:04:09.931 --> 03:04:13.851
Having no idea of the horrors that lurked
below him, he descended on the doctor’s

03:04:13.851 --> 03:04:18.341
orders, and began fixing the LEDs to walls
of each platform he passed.

03:04:18.341 --> 03:04:22.561
The LED always illuminated the landing, but
the light couldn’t pass the first step on

03:04:22.561 --> 03:04:23.561
either side.

03:04:23.561 --> 03:04:28.260
The flights of stairs themselves would remain
in perpetual darkness.

03:04:28.260 --> 03:04:35.641
After the second flight, D-9035 noticed the
same crying D-8432 had heard and became uneasy.

03:04:35.641 --> 03:04:41.561
Just like before, as D-9035 descended, the
volume of the crying didn’t seem to increase,

03:04:41.561 --> 03:04:46.480
as if for every step he descended, the source
of the crying descended one, too, keeping

03:04:46.480 --> 03:04:49.820
them at a constant 200 metres apart.

03:04:49.820 --> 03:04:55.010
Still, he was ordered to continue his descent
and the placing of LED’s even as his paranoia

03:04:55.010 --> 03:04:56.110
grew.

03:04:56.110 --> 03:05:00.761
When he reached the 51s floor, he observed
damage to the wall and steps – sections

03:05:00.761 --> 03:05:04.480
appeared to have been smashed to rubble by
an extreme force.

03:05:04.480 --> 03:05:09.570
As he descended past the broken step, he only
felt his fear, anxiety, and paranoia grow.

03:05:09.570 --> 03:05:15.791
The doctor made a note of the fact that SCP
– 087 seemed to cause instances of anxiety

03:05:15.791 --> 03:05:21.591
and terror in its occupants, even before they
encountered SCP – 087 – 1.

03:05:21.591 --> 03:05:28.980
As D-9035 reached platform 89 – a full 350
meters under the initial platform – he stopped

03:05:28.980 --> 03:05:34.171
dead in his tracks, and saw something staring
up at him from the platform below.

03:05:34.171 --> 03:05:38.720
That same terrible, grey face, with those
dead, white eyes.

03:05:38.720 --> 03:05:44.170
He was encouraged to stay calm and try to
get better footage of the face, but it charged

03:05:44.170 --> 03:05:47.431
for him and D-9035 ran for his life.

03:05:47.431 --> 03:05:51.521
He ascended the staircase at a staggering
pace, even passing out from exhaustion and

03:05:51.521 --> 03:05:54.710
remaining motionless for 14 minutes half way.

03:05:54.710 --> 03:06:00.261
When D-9035 finally gathered the strength
to get up, he scrambled back to Hallway 3B

03:06:00.261 --> 03:06:02.621
and fell into a state of catatonia.

03:06:02.621 --> 03:06:08.300
He remains unresponsive to all external stimuli
to this day, just staring off into the distance

03:06:08.300 --> 03:06:10.400
with a haunted expression.

03:06:10.400 --> 03:06:12.950
Almost like he’s still there in the hallway.

03:06:12.950 --> 03:06:18.000
The doctor wanted to conduct one more test
before he ordered SCP – 087 shut off from

03:06:18.000 --> 03:06:21.720
the world forever, and it was the most terrifying
of all.

03:06:21.720 --> 03:06:27.602
The final subject was D-9884, a 23-year-old
woman with a history of depression and the

03:06:27.602 --> 03:06:29.081
use of excessive force.

03:06:29.081 --> 03:06:34.710
The doctor had hoped that D-9884 would travel
the deepest yet, and so, he gave her the additional

03:06:34.710 --> 03:06:41.001
supplies of a backpack containing 3.75 litres
of water, 15 nutrient bars, and 1 thermal

03:06:41.001 --> 03:06:42.001
blanket.

03:06:42.001 --> 03:06:46.040
As far as the Foundation was concerned, she
was in this for the long haul.

03:06:46.040 --> 03:06:50.240
But none of them had any idea quite how right
they were.

03:06:50.240 --> 03:06:56.561
When D-9884 entered SCP – 087, all the lights
from the previous expedition had disappeared.

03:06:56.561 --> 03:06:59.601
Still, she was ordered to go deeper.

03:06:59.601 --> 03:07:03.990
She heard the crying of the mysterious child
– if it was even a child at all – and

03:07:03.990 --> 03:07:06.101
again she was ordered to go deeper.

03:07:06.101 --> 03:07:12.740
At the 496th landing, even as D-9884 seemed
to slip into a state of mortal terror, once

03:07:12.740 --> 03:07:16.081
again she was ordered to go even deeper.

03:07:16.081 --> 03:07:21.511
Every moment, he was hoping to get a better
look at the face of SCP – 087 – 1.

03:07:21.511 --> 03:07:26.730
And when D-9884 finally broke, and fled back
upstairs, he did.

03:07:26.730 --> 03:07:32.650
The face appeared but this time it was mere
inches behind her, staring directly into the

03:07:32.650 --> 03:07:37.261
camera with its blank eyes – startling even
this veteran of the supernatural.

03:07:37.261 --> 03:07:41.790
The face appearing caused D-9884 to panic
and flee, but instead of going back up the

03:07:41.790 --> 03:07:47.760
stairs to safety, she went deeper down the
staircase in an attempt to escape it.

03:07:47.760 --> 03:07:51.551
Deeper, and deeper, and deeper, until her
video feed cut out.

03:07:51.551 --> 03:07:54.251
D-9884 was never seen again.

03:07:54.251 --> 03:07:59.891
In the aftermath of the tests, the SCP was
classified as Euclid – it may have been

03:07:59.891 --> 03:08:02.780
dangerous, but at least it was easy to contain.

03:08:02.780 --> 03:08:07.351
The door to Hallway 3B was replaced with one
made out of reinforced steel, with an electro-release

03:08:07.351 --> 03:08:08.351
lock mechanism.

03:08:08.351 --> 03:08:12.521
It has been disguised to resemble a janitorial
closet consistent with the rest of the building.

03:08:12.521 --> 03:08:16.700
The lock won’t release unless a classified
number of electrical volts are applied, while

03:08:16.700 --> 03:08:18.971
the key is turned counter clockwise.

03:08:18.971 --> 03:08:22.830
And after a few inches of foam insulation
were applied to the inner side of the door,

03:08:22.830 --> 03:08:25.851
staff at the building never again reported
hearing strange noises.

03:08:25.851 --> 03:08:31.170
As for the fates of those lost within the
endless turning flights and platforms of SCP

03:08:31.170 --> 03:08:33.261
– 087, we may never know.

03:08:33.261 --> 03:08:40.170
But one can only assume it isn’t pleasant.

03:08:40.170 --> 03:08:42.370
Every neighborhood has a house like it.

03:08:42.370 --> 03:08:47.590
You can probably picture it: That old, decrepit
building on the very end of the street; it

03:08:47.590 --> 03:08:52.311
was there when you moved in, and it’ll still
be there when you move out.

03:08:52.311 --> 03:08:57.101
All sorts of salacious rumors spread about
houses like this - “it’s a drug lab”,

03:08:57.101 --> 03:09:02.450
“it’s a hideout for fugitives”, “it’s
haunted” - but these are all just stories...right?

03:09:02.450 --> 03:09:05.132
Some of these houses contain real nightmares,
though.

03:09:05.132 --> 03:09:08.570
Nightmares like SCP-136.

03:09:08.570 --> 03:09:14.330
There’s a grain of truth in every story,
and even lies can reveal certain facts about

03:09:14.330 --> 03:09:15.370
their tellers.

03:09:15.370 --> 03:09:20.860
That’s why the SCP Foundation takes reports
of so-called neighborhood “haunted houses”

03:09:20.860 --> 03:09:25.440
seriously, and performs regular checks on
such buildings to see if any of them are actually

03:09:25.440 --> 03:09:26.680
the real deal.

03:09:26.680 --> 03:09:32.650
Children can have wild imaginations - but
when children living on the same street, years

03:09:32.650 --> 03:09:37.030
apart, with no reason to have been in contact
with one another, all start reporting an eerily

03:09:37.030 --> 03:09:39.670
similar apparition in that creepy, old house.

03:09:39.670 --> 03:09:44.950
And when the stories go beyond just getting
freaked out, and delve into truly life-altering,

03:09:44.950 --> 03:09:51.450
traumatic, paralytic terror… then the Foundation
really can’t afford not to look into it.

03:09:51.450 --> 03:09:56.931
One otherwise-quiet morning in a sleepy American
town, a convoy of fumigation and asbestos

03:09:56.931 --> 03:10:02.511
removal trucks pulled in, surrounding that
creepy old house at the end of the street.

03:10:02.511 --> 03:10:06.360
Residents were probably thinking, “It’s
about time someone tore that old death-trap

03:10:06.360 --> 03:10:10.250
down”, as people in protective suits spilled
into the building.

03:10:10.250 --> 03:10:15.400
These were, of course, Foundation Field agents,
who would perform a routine sweep around every

03:10:15.400 --> 03:10:18.101
room, and fully catalogue the place.

03:10:18.101 --> 03:10:20.930
It looked like a pretty typical abandoned
house.

03:10:20.930 --> 03:10:26.250
Peeling wallpaper, dusty, rotten furniture,
all the trash and rubble that seems to appear

03:10:26.250 --> 03:10:28.780
in the absence of human life.

03:10:28.780 --> 03:10:33.920
The full sweep took little more than an hour,
but towards the end of the observation period,

03:10:33.920 --> 03:10:39.771
Agent Sims - a field agent posted in the former
children’s bedroom - began acting strangely.

03:10:39.771 --> 03:10:43.021
He posed a question over the team’s shared
radio frequency.

03:10:43.021 --> 03:10:45.660
“Hey, can anyone else hear that laughter?”

03:10:45.660 --> 03:10:50.430
Confused, the other people on the team responded
that no, they could not hear any laughter.

03:10:50.430 --> 03:10:54.230
A few other agents came to check on the room,
but they didn’t hear any laughter in there

03:10:54.230 --> 03:10:55.230
either.

03:10:55.230 --> 03:11:00.830
Even though Agent Sims appeared visibly uncomfortable,
there was no identifiable source for this

03:11:00.830 --> 03:11:01.830
discomfort.

03:11:01.830 --> 03:11:05.800
The other agents left him so they could continue
investigating the rest of the house.

03:11:05.800 --> 03:11:11.430
Other than one agent’s fraying nerves, there
didn’t appear to actually be anything anomalous

03:11:11.430 --> 03:11:12.841
about the house.

03:11:12.841 --> 03:11:18.181
Then Agent Sims screamed, and jumped out of
the second story window of the house, sailing

03:11:18.181 --> 03:11:22.391
down towards the ground and fracturing his
spine on impact.

03:11:22.391 --> 03:11:24.040
What could have made him do that?

03:11:24.040 --> 03:11:29.160
We’re talking about an SCP Foundation field
agent here - a highly-trained individual,

03:11:29.160 --> 03:11:33.581
hand-picked by the Foundation, to observe
and track terrifying and potentially deadly

03:11:33.581 --> 03:11:35.530
anomalies out in the field.

03:11:35.530 --> 03:11:39.870
What could he possibly have seen in that decrepit
old house that would lead him to believe leaping

03:11:39.870 --> 03:11:43.740
to his death was a preferable alternative
to facing it?

03:11:43.740 --> 03:11:48.181
This was a question that the Foundation absolutely
had to get an answer to.

03:11:48.181 --> 03:11:52.851
They intensified their search on the child’s
bedroom as the body of Agent Sims was carted

03:11:52.851 --> 03:11:53.851
away.

03:11:53.851 --> 03:11:59.631
That’s when they found the object that they
would later deem as SCP-136-1, a little rag

03:11:59.631 --> 03:12:01.900
doll made of old cloth.

03:12:01.900 --> 03:12:06.120
The kind of thing you could easily imagine
getting carted around by some ragamuffin child

03:12:06.120 --> 03:12:08.601
at the turn of the last century.

03:12:08.601 --> 03:12:13.830
This was the only object of interest in the
entire room, so it was tagged, bagged, and

03:12:13.830 --> 03:12:18.250
taken back to the nearest Foundation containment
facility for further testing.

03:12:18.250 --> 03:12:22.000
They had no idea what they were about to unleash.

03:12:22.000 --> 03:12:26.562
When the doll was first brought into its containment
chamber, one particular scientist on the research

03:12:26.562 --> 03:12:32.140
team - Dr. Meyers, a headstrong young researcher
freshly farmed from a prestigious university

03:12:32.140 --> 03:12:35.240
- took a morbid interest in the doll.

03:12:35.240 --> 03:12:39.740
Something about it, even in the absence of
readily apparent anomalous effects, made her

03:12:39.740 --> 03:12:42.141
feel oddly uncomfortable.

03:12:42.141 --> 03:12:45.400
The doll seemed to carry a vague aura of doom.

03:12:45.400 --> 03:12:48.650
Was this what made Agent Sims act the way
he had?

03:12:48.650 --> 03:12:50.570
Or was this only the beginning?

03:12:50.570 --> 03:12:54.230
A D-Class was brought in for the first wave
of testing.

03:12:54.230 --> 03:12:58.470
The unfortunate former-arsonist was forced
to simply stand around in the room with the

03:12:58.470 --> 03:13:03.710
doll and wait until something interesting
happened, and for twenty minutes, no anomalous

03:13:03.710 --> 03:13:05.410
activity was reported.

03:13:05.410 --> 03:13:09.990
Then, the D-Class began frantically looking
around the room, like a frightened animal.

03:13:09.990 --> 03:13:13.820
Dr. Meyers, who had been observing the test,
radioed in and asked what was happening.

03:13:13.820 --> 03:13:15.271
“It’s this laughter.

03:13:15.271 --> 03:13:18.610
This weird, freaky laughter, like some crazy
lady is in here.

03:13:18.610 --> 03:13:19.980
I can’t see her, though.

03:13:19.980 --> 03:13:21.010
Can any of you see her?

03:13:21.010 --> 03:13:22.150
Can any of you hear that?”

03:13:22.150 --> 03:13:24.440
They couldn’t see or hear anything.

03:13:24.440 --> 03:13:28.910
According to all their monitors, it was just
a lonely D-Class, standing around in an otherwise

03:13:28.910 --> 03:13:31.920
empty room with nothing but the ragdoll.

03:13:31.920 --> 03:13:36.601
Five minutes after the D-Class reported hearing
the eerie laughter, he collapsed to the ground,

03:13:36.601 --> 03:13:41.000
shrieking like a maniac and crawling away
from something he couldn’t see.

03:13:41.000 --> 03:13:45.101
He was emitting the desperate screams of a
man who truly believed something was about

03:13:45.101 --> 03:13:48.510
to take his life, but nothing was there.

03:13:48.510 --> 03:13:53.561
He backed into the corner of the room, gibbering
incoherently and scratching desperately at

03:13:53.561 --> 03:13:59.090
the walls until his fingernails were ripping
off, leaving bloody traces behind.

03:13:59.090 --> 03:14:02.830
In the end, a pair of guards entered the chamber
and had to drag him out.

03:14:02.830 --> 03:14:07.840
The D-Class had urinated in fear, and seemed
to have temporarily lost the use of his legs

03:14:07.840 --> 03:14:09.041
from sheer panic.

03:14:09.041 --> 03:14:14.260
He was out of commission for several hours
afterwards, breaking into on-and-off screaming

03:14:14.260 --> 03:14:16.940
fits whenever someone approached him.

03:14:16.940 --> 03:14:21.631
Upon reviewing the footage of the experiment,
Dr. Meyers noticed something strange: The

03:14:21.631 --> 03:14:26.110
moment that the D-Class had begun screaming,
the doll had disappeared from the room.

03:14:26.110 --> 03:14:31.260
It only rematerialized in its previous position
when the D-Class was finally dragged from

03:14:31.260 --> 03:14:32.260
the room.

03:14:32.260 --> 03:14:36.880
Eventually, the D-Class became lucid enough
to be properly interviewed about his experience.

03:14:36.880 --> 03:14:42.021
He said that after first hearing the laughter,
a sense of overpowering dread had begun building

03:14:42.021 --> 03:14:43.101
within him.

03:14:43.101 --> 03:14:50.210
Five minutes later, that was when the entity
- later dubbed SCP-136-2 - first appeared.

03:14:50.210 --> 03:14:55.150
The vision that appeared to him could generously
be described as human, but it was a little

03:14:55.150 --> 03:14:57.271
too tall to really qualify.

03:14:57.271 --> 03:15:02.200
The monster appeared to be female, but like
a freakish, carnival-house-of-mirrors exaggeration

03:15:02.200 --> 03:15:08.421
of what one thinks of being female - long,
flowing hair, large breasts, and a Barbie-Doll-Thin

03:15:08.421 --> 03:15:09.540
waist.

03:15:09.540 --> 03:15:14.460
She looked like the nightmarish doodle of
a hormonal teen boy come to life, with a face

03:15:14.460 --> 03:15:21.720
twisted into a rictus grin somewhere between
arousal and agony, showing way too many teeth.

03:15:21.720 --> 03:15:25.910
The creature was nude, and posed provocatively,
but it was anything but appealing.

03:15:25.910 --> 03:15:31.471
The D-Class reported that just seeing it was
the most frightening experience of his life…

03:15:31.471 --> 03:15:33.801
and then it started moving.

03:15:33.801 --> 03:15:38.370
It was slowly floating through the air towards
him like a vengeful ghost, that painful smile

03:15:38.370 --> 03:15:41.150
getting wider as it drew closer to him.

03:15:41.150 --> 03:15:45.130
The D-Class could only describe the whole
experience as feeling like death itself was

03:15:45.130 --> 03:15:46.681
coming towards him.

03:15:46.681 --> 03:15:50.470
When the creature was finally looming over
him as he cowered in the corner, it opened

03:15:50.470 --> 03:15:55.881
its tooth-lined jaws and let out a long, piercing
shriek, before disappearing.

03:15:55.881 --> 03:15:59.290
In the following weeks, the D-Class was kept
for testing.

03:15:59.290 --> 03:16:04.220
He experienced severe night terrors every
single night afterwards - all of them related

03:16:04.220 --> 03:16:06.730
to SCP-136.

03:16:06.730 --> 03:16:10.680
Further tests looked into the doll itself,
but there didn’t seem to be anything anomalous

03:16:10.680 --> 03:16:12.370
about its construction.

03:16:12.370 --> 03:16:16.360
It appeared to be made from the kind of plain,
non-anomalous materials you’d expect from

03:16:16.360 --> 03:16:18.220
any doll of this variety.

03:16:18.220 --> 03:16:23.681
Though occasionally, the exact materials would
change, even between observers.

03:16:23.681 --> 03:16:27.341
In addition to the most common “cloth”
variety, witnesses have reported the doll

03:16:27.341 --> 03:16:33.040
being made of clay, wood, and metal, with
10% viewing the doll as male, with the rest

03:16:33.040 --> 03:16:35.830
all agreeing that the doll is female.

03:16:35.830 --> 03:16:39.920
The Foundation conducted a battery of tests
on the doll, just to make sure that the results

03:16:39.920 --> 03:16:42.840
were largely consistent across all subjects.

03:16:42.840 --> 03:16:49.641
Over 25 different subjects were tested on
SCP-136, all reporting roughly the same results:

03:16:49.641 --> 03:16:54.521
Laughter after twenty minutes of observation,
a few minutes of silence, and then - according

03:16:54.521 --> 03:16:59.980
to subject testimonials - the appearance of
the same grinning, naked apparition, inducing

03:16:59.980 --> 03:17:03.091
a state of truly primal terror in its victims.

03:17:03.091 --> 03:17:08.610
Interestingly, not all of the subjects were
D-Classes: Some were volunteering scientists

03:17:08.610 --> 03:17:12.800
who were aware of the potential effects, but
let their morbid curiosity get the better

03:17:12.800 --> 03:17:17.950
of them, thinking they would be prepared to
face whatever terrifying vision would manifest

03:17:17.950 --> 03:17:19.080
from the doll.

03:17:19.080 --> 03:17:24.021
But in every case, they were reduced to the
same screaming, traumatized wrecks.

03:17:24.021 --> 03:17:30.980
But when a Foundation researcher named Dr.
Simon, the 25th subject of the SCP-136 experiments,

03:17:30.980 --> 03:17:35.440
volunteered for testing, things took an even
more horrifying turn.

03:17:35.440 --> 03:17:40.521
During the testing period, Dr. Simon had the
unusual experience of not actually seeing

03:17:40.521 --> 03:17:43.550
the SCP-136-2 entity.

03:17:43.550 --> 03:17:47.530
After being told how terrifying it was by
coworkers, he was a little disappointed that

03:17:47.530 --> 03:17:49.830
he didn’t get to share their fears.

03:17:49.830 --> 03:17:53.970
Later that day he went to get himself a warm
cup of coffee from the site’s employee break

03:17:53.970 --> 03:17:54.970
room.

03:17:54.970 --> 03:17:59.740
His coworkers became concerned when his coffee
mug dropped to the ground and shattered, as

03:17:59.740 --> 03:18:04.141
Dr. Simon pointed into a nearby empty hallway
and began screaming.

03:18:04.141 --> 03:18:09.830
He claimed that he could see her floating
down the hallway towards him, her face twisted

03:18:09.830 --> 03:18:12.120
into that menacing grin.

03:18:12.120 --> 03:18:15.950
As none of the other scientists could see
what Simon was seeing, they surrounded him

03:18:15.950 --> 03:18:20.400
and attempted to calm him, assuming that he
was perhaps the victim of some kind of sudden,

03:18:20.400 --> 03:18:21.550
psychotic break.

03:18:21.550 --> 03:18:27.101
But minutes later, every scientist in the
break room collapsed and fell unconscious.

03:18:27.101 --> 03:18:31.860
Not long after, they all began to wake back
up...Except Dr. Simon.

03:18:31.860 --> 03:18:36.740
He had fallen into a coma, and died while
still on life support three days later.

03:18:36.740 --> 03:18:42.761
It was the first report of SCP-136 causing
a death since Agent Sims’ unfortunate fall.

03:18:42.761 --> 03:18:48.570
Dr. Meyers immediately requested that SCP-136
be reclassified from Euclid to Keter Class

03:18:48.570 --> 03:18:52.391
so more resources could be allocated for its
containment.

03:18:52.391 --> 03:18:58.681
Administration denied any changes to the containment
procedures of SCP-136, frustrating Dr. Meyers,

03:18:58.681 --> 03:19:03.830
but little did she know that it was because
site administration had ulterior motives for

03:19:03.830 --> 03:19:05.790
SCP-136.

03:19:05.790 --> 03:19:10.181
No matter who they were, whether they were
the hardened killers of D-Class, the trained

03:19:10.181 --> 03:19:15.141
soldiers of the Foundation field agent corps,
or jaded scientists who see any number of

03:19:15.141 --> 03:19:21.130
horrors each week as part of their normal
jobs, SCP-136 had the unique ability to reduce

03:19:21.130 --> 03:19:23.740
its victims to terrified wrecks.

03:19:23.740 --> 03:19:28.921
In a move that feels decidedly more in line
with the Chaos Insurgency, site administration

03:19:28.921 --> 03:19:35.940
had started using SCP-136 to assist in enhanced
interrogation with detained people of interest.

03:19:35.940 --> 03:19:42.680
Even the toughest nuts to crack soon became
very talkative after the appearance of SCP-136-2

03:19:42.680 --> 03:19:44.220
traumatized them for life.

03:19:44.220 --> 03:19:49.940
Essentially, the administrators were making
a kind of deal with the devil: Allowing SCP-136

03:19:49.940 --> 03:19:55.050
more free reign, in exchange for them gathering
valuable intel from these victims.

03:19:55.050 --> 03:19:59.641
But as always, the problem with making deals
with the devil is that the devil is always

03:19:59.641 --> 03:20:02.141
going to collect his due in the end.

03:20:02.141 --> 03:20:07.280
Dr. Meyers’ warnings would continue to fall
upon deaf ears though, even as the creature’s

03:20:07.280 --> 03:20:09.360
power seemed to grow.

03:20:09.360 --> 03:20:13.431
Tests on D-Classes continued, with the entity
traumatizing a whole group at once during

03:20:13.431 --> 03:20:14.800
one of these experiments.

03:20:14.800 --> 03:20:19.721
However, when Dr. Meyers herself, along with
a few agents, entered the testing chamber

03:20:19.721 --> 03:20:23.101
to drag out their twitching bodies, they all
fell unconscious.

03:20:23.101 --> 03:20:29.630
When Dr. Meyers woke back up, three of the
D-Classes had fallen into comas like Dr. Simon,

03:20:29.630 --> 03:20:31.190
and died shortly after.

03:20:31.190 --> 03:20:36.511
Dr. Meyers pleaded with the administration
to terminate the doll, but her requests were

03:20:36.511 --> 03:20:37.511
denied.

03:20:37.511 --> 03:20:41.261
It was proving to be too valuable in its various
interrogations.

03:20:41.261 --> 03:20:45.500
And besides, nobody was sure if the doll even
could be terminated.

03:20:45.500 --> 03:20:51.521
Whenever it was damaged, it simply disappeared
and reappeared within a one meter radius.

03:20:51.521 --> 03:20:56.440
The only thing that hadn’t been tried was
full vaporization, which Dr. Meyers’ superiors

03:20:56.440 --> 03:20:58.970
refused to sign off on.

03:20:58.970 --> 03:21:01.910
SCP-136 was here to stay.

03:21:01.910 --> 03:21:06.700
Unfortunately, the same could not be said
for Dr. Meyers herself.

03:21:06.700 --> 03:21:11.150
After one more unfortunate testing incident
where a D-Class disappeared entirely in what

03:21:11.150 --> 03:21:17.320
seemed to be clear evidence of SCP-136’s
growing power, Dr. Meyers implored site administration

03:21:17.320 --> 03:21:21.080
to reclassify the anomaly and slate it for
termination.

03:21:21.080 --> 03:21:25.480
It was getting more powerful, more unstable,
and more dangerous.

03:21:25.480 --> 03:21:30.950
But rather than terminate the anomalous ragdoll,
in the end all they did was remove Dr. Meyers

03:21:30.950 --> 03:21:33.641
from the SCP-136 case.

03:21:33.641 --> 03:21:37.700
With her gone, there was one less thing for
them to worry about as they gave more and

03:21:37.700 --> 03:21:44.400
more victims to SCP-136, using its dark powers
to torture detained people of interest into

03:21:44.400 --> 03:21:47.110
telling them everything they wanted to know.

03:21:47.110 --> 03:21:52.950
But with the entity seeming to grow more powerful
with every victim, it seems very likely that

03:21:52.950 --> 03:21:58.130
Dr. Meyers’ worst fears will come true,
and one day those controlling the terrifying

03:21:58.130 --> 03:22:03.620
anomaly will find that they’re the ones
hearing a strange, evil laughter coming from

03:22:03.620 --> 03:22:06.580
nowhere at all.

03:22:06.580 --> 03:22:12.101
It was a beautiful September day, but Shaun
Taylor was trapped in his car in one of the

03:22:12.101 --> 03:22:14.841
worst cases of gridlock he had ever seen.

03:22:14.841 --> 03:22:19.230
He tried to look on the bright side though,
and while he was stuck in an unmoving car,

03:22:19.230 --> 03:22:24.061
at least he had a pleasant view of the wide,
shimmering lake just off the road next to

03:22:24.061 --> 03:22:25.061
him.

03:22:25.061 --> 03:22:29.141
He was admiring the scene when tiny drops
of rain started landing on his windshield.

03:22:29.141 --> 03:22:32.730
That’s funny, there wasn’t a cloud in
the sky a moment ago.

03:22:32.730 --> 03:22:34.650
There was something off about the rain though.

03:22:34.650 --> 03:22:37.891
It looked dirty, a rusty red color.

03:22:37.891 --> 03:22:39.290
Was that… blood?

03:22:39.290 --> 03:22:44.971
He didn’t have time to think about it, because
just then a thick, dense mist began to roll

03:22:44.971 --> 03:22:46.280
over the lake.

03:22:46.280 --> 03:22:48.761
A fog of blood.

03:22:48.761 --> 03:22:53.061
Just off the side of the road, he could see
a huge silhouette rising out of the water.

03:22:53.061 --> 03:22:55.040
Is that an old submarine?

03:22:55.040 --> 03:23:01.260
What Shaun didn’t know was that he was about
to have an encounter with SCP - 1861, also

03:23:01.260 --> 03:23:08.210
known as The HMS Wintersheimer - a ghostly
submarine with strange and terrifying effects.

03:23:08.210 --> 03:23:12.950
Shaun and the other drivers stuck in traffic
that day were far from the first people to

03:23:12.950 --> 03:23:18.450
have a dangerous brush with this legendary
vessel - according to SCP Foundation records,

03:23:18.450 --> 03:23:23.830
the HMS Wintersheimer has been appearing since
as early as 1916.

03:23:23.830 --> 03:23:28.680
The first recorded incident occurred in the
British seaside town of Innsmouth-On-Sea.

03:23:28.680 --> 03:23:33.360
You won’t find this town on any maps, or
in the history books, and you’re about to

03:23:33.360 --> 03:23:34.760
find out why.

03:23:34.760 --> 03:23:39.360
The 500-person population of the town, which
had already reduced by the wartime draft into

03:23:39.360 --> 03:23:46.130
the currently-raging Great World War, awoke
to red skies on February 6th, 1916.

03:23:46.130 --> 03:23:51.610
Citizens left their homes to investigate,
only to find their entire town had been enveloped

03:23:51.610 --> 03:23:54.061
in a thick, red mist.

03:23:54.061 --> 03:23:59.851
The swelling, crimson clouds up ahead began
to rain, showering the town in a hail of viscous,

03:23:59.851 --> 03:24:01.001
red goop.

03:24:01.001 --> 03:24:05.290
Anyone unlucky enough to taste it would say
that this strange rain was a dreadful mix

03:24:05.290 --> 03:24:07.200
of salt and copper.

03:24:07.200 --> 03:24:12.790
This was because, as the Foundation would
later determine, the rain and fog was a disgusting

03:24:12.790 --> 03:24:17.961
combination of saltwater, human blood, and
human cerebrospinal fluid.

03:24:17.961 --> 03:24:22.670
But the real threat was rising, just beyond
the beach.

03:24:22.670 --> 03:24:29.760
Technically speaking, the HMS Wintersheimer
vessel is designated as SCP - 1861 - A. It

03:24:29.760 --> 03:24:34.430
appears to be a World War One-era British
B-Class Submarine, designed by Vickers for

03:24:34.430 --> 03:24:36.750
the Royal Navy in 1904.

03:24:36.750 --> 03:24:42.391
By 1916, this particular type of boat was
already on its way to being obsolete, and

03:24:42.391 --> 03:24:46.450
were largely deployed in Malta, far from the
active fronts.

03:24:46.450 --> 03:24:51.180
So one of these vessels appearing on an otherwise
unremarkable stretch of English coastline

03:24:51.180 --> 03:24:55.860
should have been a clue that something was
terribly wrong - but the poor residents of

03:24:55.860 --> 03:24:59.150
Innsmouth-On-Sea didn’t know the half of
it.

03:24:59.150 --> 03:25:04.440
Soon, figures in what appeared to be archaic
diving gear began emerging from the Wintersheimer,

03:25:04.440 --> 03:25:06.220
and made their way into the township.

03:25:06.220 --> 03:25:11.351
They seemed terrified, running up to and frantically
screaming at any local they could find.

03:25:11.351 --> 03:25:14.620
“Please listen to me, something terrible
is about to happen here.

03:25:14.620 --> 03:25:17.200
We need you to come with us or you’re all
going to die.

03:25:17.200 --> 03:25:18.660
You must believe us!”

03:25:18.660 --> 03:25:20.780
The locals were frightened by what they heard.

03:25:20.780 --> 03:25:24.990
They’d been listening to news reports of
the Great War unfolding across the globe for

03:25:24.990 --> 03:25:26.250
two years now.

03:25:26.250 --> 03:25:27.891
Had it finally come to them?

03:25:27.891 --> 03:25:32.370
They pictured shells raining down from the
sky, decimating their defenseless little town

03:25:32.370 --> 03:25:33.960
in a rain of fire.

03:25:33.960 --> 03:25:38.110
The Navy must have been brought in to save
them before the German bombardment began.

03:25:38.110 --> 03:25:44.950
While some took more convincing than others,
the men in diving suits - known as SCP - 1861

03:25:44.950 --> 03:25:50.521
- B - eventually managed to persuade the entire
town to join them, and lead the townspeople

03:25:50.521 --> 03:25:52.080
down to the water.

03:25:52.080 --> 03:25:55.590
One by one, they were all boarded onto the
submarine.

03:25:55.590 --> 03:25:56.590
Hundreds of them.

03:25:56.590 --> 03:26:00.061
Many couldn’t believe their eyes as they
watched scores of people disappear in front

03:26:00.061 --> 03:26:03.200
of them into the dark bowels of the Wintersheimer.

03:26:03.200 --> 03:26:04.561
Where were they all going?

03:26:04.561 --> 03:26:05.930
How would they all fit in there?

03:26:05.930 --> 03:26:09.410
But it was too late for any of them to back
out now.

03:26:09.410 --> 03:26:13.910
The vessel submerged once more, and everyone
was gone.

03:26:13.910 --> 03:26:19.311
The entire population of Innsmouth-On-Sea
had disappeared in a rain and fog of blood,

03:26:19.311 --> 03:26:21.220
never to be seen again.

03:26:21.220 --> 03:26:25.851
The Foundation wiped all records of the town
from existence and delivered appropriate amnestic

03:26:25.851 --> 03:26:30.480
treatment to anyone who still mentioned or
remembered Innsmouth-On-Sea.

03:26:30.480 --> 03:26:36.330
The fate of those who board the HMS Wintersheimer
is always the same - vanished from the face

03:26:36.330 --> 03:26:41.580
of the earth, explained away by the Foundation
as “accidental death by extreme weather

03:26:41.580 --> 03:26:42.580
event.”

03:26:42.580 --> 03:26:47.812
There have been hundreds of documented sightings
of SCP - 1861, and the anomalous weather event

03:26:47.812 --> 03:26:53.990
can occur near any body of water wide enough
to accommodate SCP-1861-A’s comms tower

03:26:53.990 --> 03:26:56.050
and topmost platform.

03:26:56.050 --> 03:27:00.650
Depth does not seem to be any hindrance to
the submarine appearing and it can even manifest

03:27:00.650 --> 03:27:04.080
in water that’s just a few inches deep.

03:27:04.080 --> 03:27:08.030
As Shaun and the other unfortunate victims
of the rush hour traffic were being showered

03:27:08.030 --> 03:27:13.340
in thick, red droplets from above, a crimson
mist rolled in between the cars.

03:27:13.340 --> 03:27:17.870
Shaun had heard of so-called freak weather
events before - like raining frogs and fish

03:27:17.870 --> 03:27:21.461
- but this was something different, and it
frightened him.

03:27:21.461 --> 03:27:25.811
He could see now that the silhouette rising
from the lake really was an old submarine,

03:27:25.811 --> 03:27:30.480
and he watched as a legion of mysterious figures
disembarked from the vessel and began spilling

03:27:30.480 --> 03:27:31.650
onto the road.

03:27:31.650 --> 03:27:36.070
The men in ancient-looking diving suits walked
among the cars and one of them approached

03:27:36.070 --> 03:27:37.070
Shaun’s car.

03:27:37.070 --> 03:27:41.360
He began tapping frantically on the window
and Shaun could tell he was yelling something.

03:27:41.360 --> 03:27:46.811
Shaun was scared and more, but more than anything
else, he was confused.

03:27:46.811 --> 03:27:50.760
Against his better judgement, he rolled down
the window, just a crack, to hear what the

03:27:50.760 --> 03:27:51.760
man was saying.

03:27:51.760 --> 03:27:56.910
His British accented voice muted by the diving
suit, the man frantically told him “Sir!

03:27:56.910 --> 03:27:57.910
Please listen to me!

03:27:57.910 --> 03:27:59.730
I’m Lieutenant Samuel Ramsey of the HMS
Wintersheimer.

03:27:59.730 --> 03:28:00.730
We're evacuating the area.

03:28:00.730 --> 03:28:02.721
Please, you've got to come with me.

03:28:02.721 --> 03:28:05.150
You're in danger out here.”

03:28:05.150 --> 03:28:06.150
“HMS?”

03:28:06.150 --> 03:28:08.980
Shaun thought, “isn’t that what they call
British ships?

03:28:08.980 --> 03:28:12.840
What was a British submarine doing in the
middle of a lake in the United States?”

03:28:12.840 --> 03:28:17.311
Through his windshield, Shaun could already
see other men in diving suits leading people

03:28:17.311 --> 03:28:20.391
from the cars out towards the submarine.

03:28:20.391 --> 03:28:22.561
Something had to be going on here.

03:28:22.561 --> 03:28:23.561
Something big.

03:28:23.561 --> 03:28:28.061
Lieutenant Ramsey was still banging away at
the glass of Shaun’s window, becoming increasingly

03:28:28.061 --> 03:28:29.061
agitated.

03:28:29.061 --> 03:28:32.280
“Sir, if you won’t comply with my orders,
I’m within my rights to take you by force

03:28:32.280 --> 03:28:33.750
- for your own safety.”

03:28:33.750 --> 03:28:37.580
Shaun could feel the fear setting in but he
didn’t know what else to do.

03:28:37.580 --> 03:28:39.690
He turned off the car and took off his seatbelt.

03:28:39.690 --> 03:28:44.761
He was just about to open the door when there
was a tap on the passenger side window of

03:28:44.761 --> 03:28:45.761
his car.

03:28:45.761 --> 03:28:48.990
It was a soldier in what looked to be advanced
tactical gear.

03:28:48.990 --> 03:28:52.860
There were several soldiers directing cars
to drive on the shoulder to get around the

03:28:52.860 --> 03:28:54.480
mess of stopped automobiles.

03:28:54.480 --> 03:28:58.650
Shaun looked to his left and the man in the
diving suit was gone.

03:28:58.650 --> 03:29:02.681
The soldier tapped again and Shaun didn’t
need to be told twice.

03:29:02.681 --> 03:29:07.101
He followed his directions and drove around
the traffic jam and out of the mist.

03:29:07.101 --> 03:29:11.811
A half mile down the road, Shaun was stopped
by another group of soldiers and given an

03:29:11.811 --> 03:29:12.811
amnestic.

03:29:12.811 --> 03:29:20.200
He drove away never knowing how close he had
come to vanishing in the bowels of SCP-1861-A.

03:29:20.200 --> 03:29:25.730
Shaun was lucky that one of the SCP Foundation’s
Mobile Task Forces had taken over the situation,

03:29:25.730 --> 03:29:31.601
but they were too late to help those who had
already complied with SCP - 1861 - B’s orders

03:29:31.601 --> 03:29:33.450
and boarded the Wintersheimer.

03:29:33.450 --> 03:29:37.650
The Task Force made it their business to save
whoever they could, but that wasn’t their

03:29:37.650 --> 03:29:44.120
only directive: The Foundation had recorded
a huge number of SCP - 1861 instances since

03:29:44.120 --> 03:29:50.300
1916, and now, they were finally going to
figure out what was going on inside.

03:29:50.300 --> 03:29:54.000
The Foundation had already discovered that
those taken onto the Wintersheimer don’t

03:29:54.000 --> 03:29:58.630
simply disappear - once on board the submarine
they are forced into a diving suit of their

03:29:58.630 --> 03:30:07.421
own, which transforms them into new instances
of SCP - 1861 - B. Upon realizing this, Foundation

03:30:07.421 --> 03:30:09.730
scientists devised an ingenious plot.

03:30:09.730 --> 03:30:14.860
Six months before this latest instance of
1861, the Foundation dispatched two members

03:30:14.860 --> 03:30:19.561
of D-Class personnel who were familiar with
one another into the red mist.

03:30:19.561 --> 03:30:26.220
One was instructed not to interact with SCP
- 1861 - B, while the other, named Sal, was

03:30:26.220 --> 03:30:28.320
ordered to enter the submarine.

03:30:28.320 --> 03:30:32.790
His mission was to report back all findings
to Foundation researcher Dr. Klutch during

03:30:32.790 --> 03:30:35.260
the next 1861 event.

03:30:35.260 --> 03:30:39.200
The D-Class who remained on shore was brought
in once more by the Mobile Task Force during

03:30:39.200 --> 03:30:41.430
the September event that Shaun witnessed.

03:30:41.430 --> 03:30:46.080
They checked each diving suit-wearing anomaly
until they heard a familiar voice, muffled

03:30:46.080 --> 03:30:54.200
by the mask: It was Sal, and he’d been transformed
into an instance of SCP - 1861 - B. The human

03:30:54.200 --> 03:30:59.461
D-Class, receiving questions from Dr. Klutch
via a remote broadcast, commenced the interview

03:30:59.461 --> 03:31:00.970
of his former friend.

03:31:00.970 --> 03:31:05.170
It is from this vital interview that much
of the Foundation’s knowledge of the mysterious

03:31:05.170 --> 03:31:07.721
HMS Wintersheimer is drawn.

03:31:07.721 --> 03:31:12.721
According to Sal, the interior of the Wintersheimer
- which is a long, narrow, passageway - is

03:31:12.721 --> 03:31:16.330
a spatial anomaly that seems to stretch on
forever.

03:31:16.330 --> 03:31:20.860
This explains how vast numbers of people,
like the entire population of Innsmouth-On-Sea,

03:31:20.860 --> 03:31:24.190
can disappear into the submarine at once.

03:31:24.190 --> 03:31:29.130
Sal reported that, about an hour after entering
the vessel, the hatch closed and the interior

03:31:29.130 --> 03:31:35.080
began rapidly filling with water as the submarine
descended.Prisoners of the Wintersheimer were

03:31:35.080 --> 03:31:39.121
faced with two choices: Suit up… or drown.

03:31:39.121 --> 03:31:45.210
Few chose the latter option, and as soon as
the suit was on, the transformation had begun.

03:31:45.210 --> 03:31:49.811
As soon as everyone was suited up and the
submarine had fully descended, causing the

03:31:49.811 --> 03:31:54.290
1861 weather event to dissipate on earth,
the Wintersheimer had effectively entered

03:31:54.290 --> 03:31:55.950
an alternate dimension.

03:31:55.950 --> 03:32:00.671
The airlock opened, and the new recruits were
instructed to step outside and take a look

03:32:00.671 --> 03:32:01.671
around.

03:32:01.671 --> 03:32:06.230
The Wintersheimer veterans informed the new
sailors that everyone on land was likely already

03:32:06.230 --> 03:32:07.870
dead by this point.

03:32:07.870 --> 03:32:12.910
When Sal first exited the submarine, he commented
on everything around him looking eerily similar

03:32:12.910 --> 03:32:15.700
to how it’d looked on land before the mist
descended.

03:32:15.700 --> 03:32:20.620
But with one key difference: It seemed as
though everything was underwater.

03:32:20.620 --> 03:32:25.670
Well, not quite that: It was almost as though
everything was water.

03:32:25.670 --> 03:32:29.521
Like the world had taken on a kind of flowing,
liquid state.

03:32:29.521 --> 03:32:34.521
Sal and the others existed in this otherworldly
land of living water for six months, and as

03:32:34.521 --> 03:32:37.740
the months passed, things only got stranger.

03:32:37.740 --> 03:32:41.070
They found that they neither needed to eat
nor sleep.

03:32:41.070 --> 03:32:45.851
According to Sal, all they did was breathe
- and passed the time by exploring and talking

03:32:45.851 --> 03:32:47.271
to one another.

03:32:47.271 --> 03:32:51.800
Anyone who attempted to take off their suit
would dissolve and diffuse into the same liquid

03:32:51.800 --> 03:32:53.070
that surrounded them.

03:32:53.070 --> 03:32:58.061
Dr. Klutch asked Sal about the other inhabitants
of this alien realm and this was when things

03:32:58.061 --> 03:32:59.920
got truly disturbing.

03:32:59.920 --> 03:33:04.510
There were dead humans and animals floating
all over the place - missing their eyes, as

03:33:04.510 --> 03:33:08.891
though they’d been scooped out, and missing
their mouths, as though they’d been bitten

03:33:08.891 --> 03:33:12.120
out of their face by some kind of huge predator.

03:33:12.120 --> 03:33:16.710
Their empty eye sockets bled constantly, and
Sal theorized that this may have something

03:33:16.710 --> 03:33:21.710
to do with the anomalous blood mists of SCP
- 1861.

03:33:21.710 --> 03:33:25.721
When asked to provide more information on
why all the corpses were mutilated in this

03:33:25.721 --> 03:33:30.050
way, Sal said that one of his superiors on
the Wintersheimer told him “the watcher

03:33:30.050 --> 03:33:34.210
of eyes and biter of teeth deemed them worthy.”

03:33:34.210 --> 03:33:39.990
Whatever this mysterious being was, it seemed
to be a powerful figure within 1861’s water

03:33:39.990 --> 03:33:44.521
world, and Sal felt lucky that he had never
had a direct run-in with the creature himself.

03:33:44.521 --> 03:33:50.011
For his final request, Dr. Klutch asked Sal
to attempt to remove his suit.

03:33:50.011 --> 03:33:55.760
The Foundation had learned in previous instances
of 1861 that the diving suits have anomalous

03:33:55.760 --> 03:34:00.480
durability, and it was impossible for anyone
other than the wearer to remove them - hence

03:34:00.480 --> 03:34:06.370
why the Foundation could never deal with 1861-B
by using brute force.

03:34:06.370 --> 03:34:10.771
Naturally, Klutch was interested in finding
out what was going on underneath.

03:34:10.771 --> 03:34:15.610
Sal expressed fear and anxiety at first, wondering
if after all he’d been through whether he

03:34:15.610 --> 03:34:18.010
could even be considered human anymore.

03:34:18.010 --> 03:34:23.311
Eventually, he was convinced to remove the
suit, and his worst fears were confirmed.

03:34:23.311 --> 03:34:28.620
The second Sal removed his helmet, gallons
of seawater poured out and the now empty suit

03:34:28.620 --> 03:34:30.260
collapsed to the ground.

03:34:30.260 --> 03:34:35.381
Sal’s body was ever found - only some teeth
and a pair of eyes were recovered.

03:34:35.381 --> 03:34:39.960
The eyes were later confirmed as belonging
to a young girl, and the teeth were identified

03:34:39.960 --> 03:34:42.960
as having come from European red deer.

03:34:42.960 --> 03:34:47.601
And so the dark mystery of the HMS Wintersheimer
continues.

03:34:47.601 --> 03:34:51.521
Because of the unpredictable nature of its
appearances, and the resulting difficulty

03:34:51.521 --> 03:34:55.110
of containing it, the Wintersheimer has earned
a Keter Classification.

03:34:55.110 --> 03:35:01.250
The only containment procedure currently employed
by the SCP Foundation is for Mobile Task Forces

03:35:01.250 --> 03:35:06.250
to try and intercept the submarine when appearances
are reported, and hopefully prevent or at

03:35:06.250 --> 03:35:09.761
least reduce the kidnapping of civilians.

03:35:09.761 --> 03:35:12.410
With so many questions left unanswered.

03:35:12.410 --> 03:35:17.490
All we can say for certain is that if a red
mist ever descends on you and a stranger in

03:35:17.490 --> 03:35:22.351
a diving suit tells you that you’re in grave
danger - he’s absolutely right.

03:35:22.351 --> 03:35:30.021
If you have ever taken a trip to Suntop Mountain
in the Mount Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest,

03:35:30.021 --> 03:35:35.461
Washington State, then you may have come across
an old wooden structure - The Suntop Fire

03:35:35.461 --> 03:35:36.461
Lookout.

03:35:36.461 --> 03:35:41.311
Built in the early 1930s, the building was
used by the US Forest Service to keep watch

03:35:41.311 --> 03:35:43.561
for any fires in the nearby woodland.

03:35:43.561 --> 03:35:50.070
At one point, Suntop Fire Lookout would have
been manned 365 days a year, complete with

03:35:50.070 --> 03:35:53.430
a bed for staff who were stationed there on
rotation.

03:35:53.430 --> 03:35:58.311
The single story lookout house overlooks the
scenic valleys of the White River and Huckleberry

03:35:58.311 --> 03:36:02.511
Creek, but you’re not here for an informative
tourist guide.

03:36:02.511 --> 03:36:06.961
You probably don’t care about the frankly
fascinating history of the lookout and how

03:36:06.961 --> 03:36:12.260
it was used as part of the Aircraft Warning
Service during World War 2, watching for enemy

03:36:12.260 --> 03:36:13.260
planes.

03:36:13.260 --> 03:36:20.341
No, you’re here because something much darker
lurks inside the Suntop Fire Lookout.

03:36:20.341 --> 03:36:25.601
And even though it appears to be a simple,
one-story-tall wooden structure, it certainly

03:36:25.601 --> 03:36:28.671
is not short on space.

03:36:28.671 --> 03:36:34.601
SCP-3333 refers to an anomaly that the Foundation
discovered inside the Suntop Fire Lookout

03:36:34.601 --> 03:36:35.601
house.

03:36:35.601 --> 03:36:40.690
The building’s interior is a single, square
room, measuring fourteen feet by fourteen

03:36:40.690 --> 03:36:44.811
feet, with large windows on all four sides.

03:36:44.811 --> 03:36:49.610
When standing inside Suntop Fire Lookout,
looking up at the wooden ceiling, one will

03:36:49.610 --> 03:36:51.320
immediately notice a trapdoor.

03:36:51.320 --> 03:36:52.950
No big deal, right?

03:36:52.950 --> 03:36:57.720
A lot of places have a ceiling entrance to
a small crawl space, there is probably nothing

03:36:57.720 --> 03:37:01.311
behind the trapdoor, apart from a dusty, old
attic.

03:37:01.311 --> 03:37:05.840
There’s a latch that maybe once had a padlock
there, but not anymore.

03:37:05.840 --> 03:37:09.641
Opening the trapdoor will reveal a collapsible
ladder.

03:37:09.641 --> 03:37:14.340
Should anyone be brave, or indeed foolish
enough, to begin to climb, then they’ll

03:37:14.340 --> 03:37:20.130
soon find themselves right back where they
started, inside Suntop Fire Lookout.

03:37:20.130 --> 03:37:22.351
Or so it will seem.

03:37:22.351 --> 03:37:26.511
The thing about being in a place like the
Mount Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest that

03:37:26.511 --> 03:37:31.780
surrounds Suntop Fire Lookout is that woodland
areas are teeming with life.

03:37:31.780 --> 03:37:36.021
Not just plants and trees, but birds and other
animals of the forest.

03:37:36.021 --> 03:37:41.450
You can never truly be alone in a setting
like that, there is always life everywhere

03:37:41.450 --> 03:37:42.501
around you.

03:37:42.501 --> 03:37:47.820
So, when you ascend the ladder, and climb
out right back into the Suntop Fire Lookout,

03:37:47.820 --> 03:37:51.511
that is the first, most noticeable difference
you will find.

03:37:51.511 --> 03:37:57.120
It may take a while at first, but the nagging
absence of something usually so abundant in

03:37:57.120 --> 03:37:59.760
a forest will eventually become obvious.

03:37:59.760 --> 03:38:03.230
It’s quiet, far too quiet.

03:38:03.230 --> 03:38:07.641
No birdsong, or the sound of distant calls
from woodland critters.

03:38:07.641 --> 03:38:11.000
Just silence, all around.

03:38:11.000 --> 03:38:16.240
Anyone ascending the ladder will find themselves
in a copy of Suntop Fire Lookout’s interior,

03:38:16.240 --> 03:38:20.420
one story higher than the ground level of
the small wooden building, with the stairs

03:38:20.420 --> 03:38:25.580
leading up to the front door getting taller
each time to reach up to the higher and higher

03:38:25.580 --> 03:38:26.580
building.

03:38:26.580 --> 03:38:32.141
Now, you know the SCP Foundation and the types
of bizarre, inter dimensional anomalies they’re

03:38:32.141 --> 03:38:33.660
used to dealing with.

03:38:33.660 --> 03:38:39.400
Perhaps SCP-3333 is a mirror dimension, or
a plane of existence where sound doesn’t

03:38:39.400 --> 03:38:40.400
travel.

03:38:40.400 --> 03:38:44.601
It certainly seems to be identical to the
Suntop Fire Lookout, save for the lack of

03:38:44.601 --> 03:38:46.780
any organic life outside.

03:38:46.780 --> 03:38:54.130
Of course, it’s what you’ll find living
inside SCP-3333 that you may want to worry

03:38:54.130 --> 03:38:55.130
about.

03:38:55.130 --> 03:38:59.561
Climbing higher, up the next ladder and through
the next trapdoor, every time with the same

03:38:59.561 --> 03:39:00.561
result.

03:39:00.561 --> 03:39:05.470
You appear at another copy of Suntop Fire
Lookout, each one higher up than the last.

03:39:05.470 --> 03:39:10.640
What first seemed to be an innocuous, unassuming
wooden building is now an endless ascension

03:39:10.640 --> 03:39:16.950
up into the heavens, towards the unknown in
silence, without a shred of plant or animal

03:39:16.950 --> 03:39:18.610
life outside.

03:39:18.610 --> 03:39:22.710
As you climb, perhaps you start to think how
much higher these copies go.

03:39:22.710 --> 03:39:26.690
This might even be the biblical Jacob’s
Ladder, connecting Heaven and Earth.

03:39:26.690 --> 03:39:28.500
That would be nice, wouldn’t it?

03:39:28.500 --> 03:39:33.280
If you were gradually climbing your way up
to paradise, it might make it worth the trip.

03:39:33.280 --> 03:39:36.620
But SCP-3333 is nothing that pleasant.

03:39:36.620 --> 03:39:40.070
You wouldn’t be the first to attempt this
long climb.

03:39:40.070 --> 03:39:46.900
When the SCP Foundation first discovered SCP-3333,
a research detail set up an onsite base camp

03:39:46.900 --> 03:39:49.061
to examine this spatial anomaly.

03:39:49.061 --> 03:39:55.771
Their first exploration involved sending a
member of D-class personnel, designated D-4f68a,

03:39:55.771 --> 03:39:56.771
up the ladder.

03:39:56.771 --> 03:40:02.210
His D-number is a hexadecimal code that, when
translated to text, reads ‘Oh’, so we’ll

03:40:02.210 --> 03:40:04.650
call him that for brevity’s sake.

03:40:04.650 --> 03:40:12.360
During the first day’s exploration, Oh was
able to climb 184 iterations of SCP-3333,

03:40:12.360 --> 03:40:15.410
communicating with head researcher Doctor
Williams below.

03:40:15.410 --> 03:40:21.030
On the second day, Oh could see a pair of
figures standing motionless on a nearby ridge,

03:40:21.030 --> 03:40:26.260
but the pair could not be seen by Doctor Williams
and the other researchers at the base camp.

03:40:26.260 --> 03:40:30.990
Both figures disappeared shortly after Oh
spotted them with the camera he had been issued,

03:40:30.990 --> 03:40:35.700
and he felt uneasy, almost certain that he
saw them point at him.

03:40:35.700 --> 03:40:42.351
The next day, at the 345th copy of Suntop
Fire Lookout, Oh’s behavior started to noticeably

03:40:42.351 --> 03:40:43.351
change.

03:40:43.351 --> 03:40:47.891
Previously, he had been anxious about the
long climb, and hadn’t questioned directions

03:40:47.891 --> 03:40:49.730
given to him by Doctor Williams.

03:40:49.730 --> 03:40:55.681
Now, he seemed to speak more casually, resisting
instructions, asking Williams to climb back

03:40:55.681 --> 03:40:59.211
down and even calling her ‘Doc’ instead
of ‘Doctor’.

03:40:59.211 --> 03:41:04.670
Oh also reported seeing writing on the walls,
but there was no evidence of this on his camera.

03:41:04.670 --> 03:41:08.360
It appeared that something had started to
affect him.

03:41:08.360 --> 03:41:14.410
It was when Oh reached level 527 that things
seemed to change more dramatically.

03:41:14.410 --> 03:41:20.940
Rather than SCP-3333 continuing upwards, the
copies of Suntop Fire Lookout no longer had

03:41:20.940 --> 03:41:23.150
a trapdoor or ladder.

03:41:23.150 --> 03:41:27.740
They seemed to be arranged side by side, in
a grid-like pattern.

03:41:27.740 --> 03:41:32.420
Stepping out of the main doorway, Oh remarked
on the lack of sunlight, and a walkway that

03:41:32.420 --> 03:41:37.980
connected directly to the front door of the
next iteration of SCP-3333.

03:41:37.980 --> 03:41:44.500
Oh complained about the lack of natural light,
and again requested to be allowed back down.

03:41:44.500 --> 03:41:49.450
Doctor Williams instructed Oh to use the flashlights
he was provided, but they wouldn’t activate

03:41:49.450 --> 03:41:51.500
and their spare batteries had vanished.

03:41:51.500 --> 03:41:57.521
Oh then noticed a sudden movement, and just
then his microphone and camera feed went dead,

03:41:57.521 --> 03:42:00.351
almost as if someone had turned them off.

03:42:00.351 --> 03:42:05.521
It appeared that SCP-3333 had something else
lurking up there.

03:42:05.521 --> 03:42:10.391
Doctor Williams oversaw the second expedition
into SCP-3333.

03:42:10.391 --> 03:42:15.700
This time members of Mobile Task Force Mod-0,
also known by the codename “Characteristic

03:42:15.700 --> 03:42:18.180
Eigenspaces”, were sent up the ladder.

03:42:18.180 --> 03:42:22.490
Their ascent through the various copies of
Suntop Fire Lookout were not as eventful as

03:42:22.490 --> 03:42:27.890
Oh’s, with no signs of mysterious figures,
or anxious feelings that Oh seemed to feel

03:42:27.890 --> 03:42:29.140
as he climbed.

03:42:29.140 --> 03:42:34.210
When they reached level 527, where the copies
of the lookout stop progressing upwards and

03:42:34.210 --> 03:42:38.990
spread out in a pattern instead, their lights
and equipment all seemed to be in working

03:42:38.990 --> 03:42:39.990
order.

03:42:39.990 --> 03:42:45.670
However, as the MTF team split up, one by
one they encountered some sort of anomaly,

03:42:45.670 --> 03:42:51.750
or an effect of SCP-3333 that caused each
of them to vanish into the dark.

03:42:51.750 --> 03:42:55.370
Either that, or something took them.

03:42:55.370 --> 03:43:01.041
These MTF units reappeared confused, and Mod-5,
the team’s leader, Graham Purcell, issued

03:43:01.041 --> 03:43:06.460
an order to retreat and the entire squad went
back down the ladders for several days until

03:43:06.460 --> 03:43:09.261
they finally reached the base camp again.

03:43:09.261 --> 03:43:15.061
The members of Mod-0 were adamant they did
not wish to climb SCP-3333 again, but Doctor

03:43:15.061 --> 03:43:19.050
Williams was beginning to understand more
of the anomaly’s effects.

03:43:19.050 --> 03:43:24.380
It appeared to cause abrupt changes to people’s
personalities, along with some sort of phenomenon

03:43:24.380 --> 03:43:28.851
that caused things to appear and disappear
the higher one climbed.

03:43:28.851 --> 03:43:33.391
Assuming these were the results of a memetic
effect, Doctor Williams dispatched a ‘counter

03:43:33.391 --> 03:43:35.820
memetics specialist’ for the next expedition.

03:43:35.820 --> 03:43:41.200
This specialist was a blind, deaf, and mute
woman known as Annette or the ‘Nullwalker’,

03:43:41.200 --> 03:43:46.620
who communicated via a signaling system embedded
in her hand, but was otherwise immune to any

03:43:46.620 --> 03:43:49.070
memetic influences.

03:43:49.070 --> 03:43:53.080
Observed by Doctor Williams and Graham Purcell
at base camp, Annette made her way to the

03:43:53.080 --> 03:43:59.360
top of SCP-3333, reporting that she was aware
of someone watching her from outside the copies

03:43:59.360 --> 03:44:01.090
of Suntop Fire Lookout.

03:44:01.090 --> 03:44:06.711
On her body camera, a flicker of motion occurred,
something looking through the windows that

03:44:06.711 --> 03:44:10.540
ducked out of frame when the camera passed
in its direction.

03:44:10.540 --> 03:44:16.180
At the apex of SCP-3333, Annette kept her
flashlight off, but reported that she could

03:44:16.180 --> 03:44:20.630
detect blood, following it to what she assumed
was a body.

03:44:20.630 --> 03:44:25.101
Sounds of movement surrounded her, and as
Annette switched on her flashlight, Williams

03:44:25.101 --> 03:44:28.210
and Purcell saw that it wasn’t a body in
front of her.

03:44:28.210 --> 03:44:34.450
Instead, it was a pile of rotting organs,
decomposing muscles and discarded bones.

03:44:34.450 --> 03:44:42.181
And among the pile was a metal dog tag, that
read ‘MTF Mod-5: Graham Purcell’; the

03:44:42.181 --> 03:44:46.070
same man who was sitting next to Doctor Williams
at base camp.

03:44:46.070 --> 03:44:49.960
Well, the same man on the outside at least.

03:44:49.960 --> 03:44:57.351
The explanation for everything going on inside
SCP-3333, all these strange occurrences and

03:44:57.351 --> 03:45:02.391
disappearances, finally came in a video sent
from Doctor Williams’ cell phone.

03:45:02.391 --> 03:45:07.540
In it, a panicked Williams, covered in blood,
was fleeing from something at the top of the

03:45:07.540 --> 03:45:11.250
recursive stack of SCP-3333.

03:45:11.250 --> 03:45:16.681
There was no memetic effect at the apex of
the Suntop Fire Lookout copies.

03:45:16.681 --> 03:45:21.811
Nothing was causing the people that the Foundation
sent up to act unlike themselves.

03:45:21.811 --> 03:45:24.900
They simply weren’t themselves anymore.

03:45:24.900 --> 03:45:29.590
According to her frantic video, Doctor Williams
had discovered the truth about what else was

03:45:29.590 --> 03:45:32.650
hiding within SCP-3333.

03:45:32.650 --> 03:45:36.771
With just the right amount of vagueness and
intrigue, the research team had been drawn

03:45:36.771 --> 03:45:37.771
in.

03:45:37.771 --> 03:45:42.480
It was as if they’d been lured in by the
lights of an anglerfish, realizing their grim

03:45:42.480 --> 03:45:44.460
fate only too late.

03:45:44.460 --> 03:45:49.900
The D-class ‘Oh’, the MTF team, even Annette
had been replaced.

03:45:49.900 --> 03:45:56.930
An unknown group of entities on the top level
of SCP-3333 had been carefully observing them,

03:45:56.930 --> 03:46:02.040
waiting until they would not be seen to slip
in and switch places.

03:46:02.040 --> 03:46:07.141
These entities had been creating imagined
anomalous effects, like Oh seeing figures

03:46:07.141 --> 03:46:12.340
that weren’t really there, as a way of luring
more bodies further up the stack.

03:46:12.340 --> 03:46:19.000
They wanted the Foundation to keep sending
expeditions into SCP-3333, to keep them coming

03:46:19.000 --> 03:46:20.120
back.

03:46:20.120 --> 03:46:25.341
The mass of organs, musculature, and bones
that Annette had stumbled across, revealing

03:46:25.341 --> 03:46:31.601
the ruse, had once belonged to Graham Purcell,
before he was replaced.

03:46:31.601 --> 03:46:36.340
You see, the entities residing in SCP-3333
weren’t just copying people.

03:46:36.340 --> 03:46:42.131
They weren’t possessing them or mind-controlling
them, or even shape shifting to steal a person’s

03:46:42.131 --> 03:46:43.131
likeness.

03:46:43.131 --> 03:46:45.300
They were taking skin.

03:46:45.300 --> 03:46:51.200
These creatures hollowed out Graham, Oh, Annette
and the MTF team, pulling out their innards

03:46:51.200 --> 03:46:56.771
and crawling their way inside, filling these
fleshy puppets and leaving their internal

03:46:56.771 --> 03:46:58.650
organs to rot.

03:46:58.650 --> 03:47:04.421
These hollowed out people become vessels for
the entities of SCP-3333 to hide in.

03:47:04.421 --> 03:47:12.381
The whole thing had been a trap, intentionally
exploiting human weaknesses, intrigue, unanswered

03:47:12.381 --> 03:47:13.740
questions.

03:47:13.740 --> 03:47:18.690
You know what they say about curiosity, and
these entities used it to bring more potential

03:47:18.690 --> 03:47:22.320
vessels to the top of SCP-3333.

03:47:22.320 --> 03:47:27.410
They pretended to be the people who they had
replaced, imitating them so the Foundation

03:47:27.410 --> 03:47:32.700
would send more personnel to explore the tower,
increasing their supply of skins.

03:47:32.700 --> 03:47:40.160
Graham’s dog tag had revealed the deception,
and Doctor Williams had escaped up SCP-3333.

03:47:40.160 --> 03:47:44.620
The members of the research team that had
already been replaced were hot on her tail,

03:47:44.620 --> 03:47:50.601
determined to catch and hollow her out too,
and by the end of her video, they had succeeded.

03:47:50.601 --> 03:47:56.110
A month later though, a team delivering supplies
realized what had happened and the trapdoor

03:47:56.110 --> 03:47:57.370
was sealed.

03:47:57.370 --> 03:48:02.210
Suntop Fire Lookout was put under permanent
guard, but at least fifty personnel were killed

03:48:02.210 --> 03:48:04.530
or replaced by one of the entities.

03:48:04.530 --> 03:48:10.300
A new Mobile Task Force, Lamda-1 “Maxwell’s
Demons” was created to hunt down and neutralize

03:48:10.300 --> 03:48:16.271
any of the entities that escaped SCP-3333,
but it’s still unknown how many left the

03:48:16.271 --> 03:48:22.620
tower and are still out there somewhere, waiting
to use someone’s curiosity about the strange

03:48:22.620 --> 03:48:24.990
and unknown against them.

03:48:24.990 --> 03:48:32.180
Jay and Michael were a pair of urban exploration
YouTubers looking for their big break.

03:48:32.180 --> 03:48:36.400
You might remember their video exploring the
dead mall on the outskirts of your town, or

03:48:36.400 --> 03:48:41.971
the supposedly “haunted” 1950s insane
asylum out in the styx, but you certainly

03:48:41.971 --> 03:48:44.340
won’t find these videos anywhere online.

03:48:44.340 --> 03:48:50.820
After The Incident at SCP - 823, all of their
content was scrubbed away from even the most

03:48:50.820 --> 03:48:52.640
comprehensive internet archives.

03:48:52.640 --> 03:48:54.771
“Why?” you ask.

03:48:54.771 --> 03:48:59.460
Because these unfortunate urban explorers
decided that their big break would be exploring

03:48:59.460 --> 03:49:01.311
a certain abandoned theme park.

03:49:01.311 --> 03:49:05.660
And it would be one of the last decisions
they ever made.

03:49:05.660 --> 03:49:08.530
Michael and Jay had heard rumors about the
theme park.

03:49:08.530 --> 03:49:13.522
Its name was lost to time, as was the date
of its opening and closing, and the reason

03:49:13.522 --> 03:49:16.540
it was even abandoned in the first place.

03:49:16.540 --> 03:49:20.790
Even some of the most hardcore urban explorers
didn’t dare to tread there.

03:49:20.790 --> 03:49:25.540
Something about it, a good friend had once
told Jay, just didn’t feel right.

03:49:25.540 --> 03:49:31.311
Sometimes, if you dare to venture into the
forest near the theme park at night, you can

03:49:31.311 --> 03:49:32.870
still hear music.

03:49:32.870 --> 03:49:37.330
The jolly, piping tunes of rides and carnival
stands still beckoning.

03:49:37.330 --> 03:49:39.771
As if to say, “We’re still here.

03:49:39.771 --> 03:49:41.540
Come and play.”

03:49:41.540 --> 03:49:44.160
Of course, none of this frightened Jay and
Michael.

03:49:44.160 --> 03:49:48.601
They could already smell the sponsorships
from headlamp and compact camera companies.

03:49:48.601 --> 03:49:53.061
No amount of anxiety would stop them from
making their doomed trip to the so-called

03:49:53.061 --> 03:49:54.790
“Carnival of Horrors.”

03:49:54.790 --> 03:50:00.021
It’s a terrible shame - if they’d listened
to the stories of this place about how unnatural

03:50:00.021 --> 03:50:04.570
and evil it could be...They might still be
alive today.

03:50:04.570 --> 03:50:09.690
Like all the best urban explorers, they arrived
at the woods near the abandoned theme park

03:50:09.690 --> 03:50:10.840
in the dead of night.

03:50:10.840 --> 03:50:16.021
They ignored the signs warning them about
everything from structural instability, to

03:50:16.021 --> 03:50:18.721
dangerous wild animals, to asbestos.

03:50:18.721 --> 03:50:20.480
Nothing would keep them out.

03:50:20.480 --> 03:50:21.480
Nothing.

03:50:21.480 --> 03:50:25.720
They reached the abandoned theme park not
long after, though it was a mere shell of

03:50:25.720 --> 03:50:27.351
its former self.

03:50:27.351 --> 03:50:31.040
During the several decades of abandonment,
nature had reclaimed it.

03:50:31.040 --> 03:50:35.730
The ferris wheel was covered in overgrown
ivy and the carnival stands were blanketed

03:50:35.730 --> 03:50:37.101
with mold.

03:50:37.101 --> 03:50:40.990
As the duo swept through the grounds with
their flashlights and cameras, they saw a

03:50:40.990 --> 03:50:44.150
faded sign that bore the words “Thriller
Chiller” - next to the rusty skeleton of

03:50:44.150 --> 03:50:47.110
what had once been the park’s most popular
roller coaster.

03:50:47.110 --> 03:50:51.851
They also took their time to marvel at the
exceptionally creepy-looking Tunnel of Love,

03:50:51.851 --> 03:50:57.550
the broken down House of Mirrors, and a huge,
grinning statue of the park’s former mascot,

03:50:57.550 --> 03:50:58.710
Happy Hippo.

03:50:58.710 --> 03:51:02.750
This theme park was like something out of
a nightmare, which, naturally, made it potential

03:51:02.750 --> 03:51:04.070
video gold.

03:51:04.070 --> 03:51:08.440
But as the excited duo wandered further into
the park, they couldn’t help but notice

03:51:08.440 --> 03:51:11.141
the quiet, tinny carnival music.

03:51:11.141 --> 03:51:13.990
Music that seemed to be drawing them closer.

03:51:13.990 --> 03:51:19.230
Michael asked Jay if he could hear the strange,
impossible music, and felt a chill creep in

03:51:19.230 --> 03:51:20.670
when he answered that he did.

03:51:20.670 --> 03:51:22.530
Could all of the stories be true?

03:51:22.530 --> 03:51:25.720
They were lost in thought, but their legs
kept moving.

03:51:25.720 --> 03:51:27.940
They were getting closer to something now.

03:51:27.940 --> 03:51:29.541
They could feel a presence.

03:51:29.541 --> 03:51:31.590
And was that music getting louder?

03:51:31.590 --> 03:51:35.550
An instant later, though, another sound cut
through the silence - BANG!

03:51:35.550 --> 03:51:36.550
BANG!

03:51:36.550 --> 03:51:39.070
It echoed out through the still night air.

03:51:39.070 --> 03:51:41.851
Birds flew from their perches in the trees.

03:51:41.851 --> 03:51:46.641
Jay and Michael both fell to the ground, dead,
their heads taken off by the fifty caliber

03:51:46.641 --> 03:51:52.021
rounds of a highly-trained Mobile Task Force
Sniper on the payroll of the SCP Foundation.

03:51:52.021 --> 03:51:56.470
Their recording equipment, along with their
bodies, were taken and destroyed.

03:51:56.470 --> 03:51:58.790
Any trace of them was scrubbed from the internet.

03:51:58.790 --> 03:52:03.311
It may seem a little harsh, but a bullet to
the head is a much kinder fate than what would

03:52:03.311 --> 03:52:06.030
have awaited these two if they’d kept walking.

03:52:06.030 --> 03:52:09.280
That’s because the Carnival of Horrors is
no dark fairytale.

03:52:09.280 --> 03:52:13.641
The rumors are all true, and something really
is waiting in the dark.

03:52:13.641 --> 03:52:19.620
That’s why this abandoned theme park is
known to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 823,

03:52:19.620 --> 03:52:22.820
a Euclid class anomaly with a violent history.

03:52:22.820 --> 03:52:28.200
What’s even more unnerving is that the researchers
studying 823 have repeatedly implored the

03:52:28.200 --> 03:52:34.521
O5 Council to increase the park’s classification
to Keter and allocate more resources for containment,

03:52:34.521 --> 03:52:35.971
only to be denied.

03:52:35.971 --> 03:52:40.471
But after you’ve heard about the horrors
that unfolded there, and the danger it poses,

03:52:40.471 --> 03:52:43.021
you’ll probably take the researchers’
side.

03:52:43.021 --> 03:52:48.261
The park is divided into two different zones:
The Yellow Zone and the Red Zone.

03:52:48.261 --> 03:52:52.340
There are to be at least six members of Foundation
personnel present in the Yellow Zone at all

03:52:52.340 --> 03:52:55.680
times to ensure that no civilians wander in.

03:52:55.680 --> 03:53:00.000
Our two urban explorers earned themselves
a death sentence not just by wandering into

03:53:00.000 --> 03:53:04.461
the Yellow Zone, but passing dangerously close
to the Red Zone.

03:53:04.461 --> 03:53:08.360
This is the true epicenter of the park’s
dangerous, anomalous activity.

03:53:08.360 --> 03:53:13.351
It’s a place so hazardous that anyone entering,
whether they’re a civilian or a member of

03:53:13.351 --> 03:53:19.811
Foundation staff, is to be executed at a distance
by sniper fire without hesitation.

03:53:19.811 --> 03:53:24.721
Once upon a time, though nobody knows exactly
when, there was a theme park that seemed no

03:53:24.721 --> 03:53:26.521
different to any other.

03:53:26.521 --> 03:53:31.301
Eager children and thrill-seeking teens arrived
by the busload, ready to stuff their faces

03:53:31.301 --> 03:53:37.601
with cotton candy and corn dogs, and then
reverse the process on a vast array of rollercoasters.

03:53:37.601 --> 03:53:43.230
But even then during these good times, there
was something dark lurking behind the cheerful

03:53:43.230 --> 03:53:44.400
facade.

03:53:44.400 --> 03:53:50.320
Little by little everyone, visitors and employees
alike, started falling victim to strange and

03:53:50.320 --> 03:53:52.730
horrific accidents around the park.

03:53:52.730 --> 03:53:58.141
Of course, when it comes to theme parks, accidents
come with the territory, but none like this.

03:53:58.141 --> 03:54:02.771
Here are just a handful of the horrific and
mysterious deaths that occurred while the

03:54:02.771 --> 03:54:03.930
park was open.

03:54:03.930 --> 03:54:09.601
So strap in, because just like a roller coaster,
this isn’t for the faint of heart.

03:54:09.601 --> 03:54:14.530
A pair of young lovebirds decided they wanted
to enjoy the romance of the Tunnel of Love.

03:54:14.530 --> 03:54:19.841
The two sat in a swan-shaped boat as they
were ferried through darkened passageways.

03:54:19.841 --> 03:54:24.170
Anyone would assume that they were having
a great time, but at some point, terrible

03:54:24.170 --> 03:54:28.740
shrieks of pain and fear began to echo through
the ride.

03:54:28.740 --> 03:54:33.450
Attendants, confused and terrified, stopped
the ride and found that the screaming persisted.

03:54:33.450 --> 03:54:37.710
Just some stupid teens playing a prank, they
figured, and started the ride again.

03:54:37.710 --> 03:54:42.681
But when the swan-shaped boat finally exited
the Tunnel of Love, the park employees were

03:54:42.681 --> 03:54:48.930
greeted to a horrifying sight: The two teens,
dead, their bodies somehow fused together

03:54:48.930 --> 03:54:51.010
at multiple points.

03:54:51.010 --> 03:54:55.101
Another unlucky customer met a gruesome fate
inside the House of Mirrors.

03:54:55.101 --> 03:55:00.420
They entered, but while inside, they were
stalked by a mysterious, carnivorous, humanoid

03:55:00.420 --> 03:55:03.001
entity known as Subject 79.

03:55:03.001 --> 03:55:08.931
The customer was pursued and eventually caught
by Subject 79, and brutally dismembered.

03:55:08.931 --> 03:55:13.311
Some parts of the body were fused to the House
of Mirrors’ interior while others - like

03:55:13.311 --> 03:55:15.351
the right arm - were never found.

03:55:15.351 --> 03:55:20.490
This customer actually survived their ordeal
- and whether that’s a happy ending is up

03:55:20.490 --> 03:55:21.500
to you.

03:55:21.500 --> 03:55:24.730
But it wasn’t just the customers at the
park who were in danger.

03:55:24.730 --> 03:55:29.540
A 23-year-old park employee working a summer
job collapsed while entertaining children

03:55:29.540 --> 03:55:32.610
dressed as the park’s cheerful mascot, Happy
Hippo.

03:55:32.610 --> 03:55:37.641
It wasn’t uncommon for people to get overheated
and collapse in the heavy suits on hot days,

03:55:37.641 --> 03:55:44.330
but one thing was different here: He was screaming,
crying, and trying desperately to remove his

03:55:44.330 --> 03:55:45.330
mask.

03:55:45.330 --> 03:55:49.800
People rushed to help, but nobody could get
the suit off, and he was declared dead soon

03:55:49.800 --> 03:55:50.800
after.

03:55:50.800 --> 03:55:54.970
When he was eventually cut out of the suit,
coroners found that the employee had choked

03:55:54.970 --> 03:55:55.970
to death.

03:55:55.970 --> 03:56:00.050
His mouth, trachea, and lungs were filled
with a fibrous substance later determined

03:56:00.050 --> 03:56:02.860
to be identical to the stuffing of his costume.

03:56:02.860 --> 03:56:08.141
An intense roller coaster known as the Thriller
Chiller was a magnet for horrific accidents,

03:56:08.141 --> 03:56:11.271
which became more violent and intense over
time.

03:56:11.271 --> 03:56:16.120
The first accident seemed like a typical theme
park tragedy - A safety harness failed dropping

03:56:16.120 --> 03:56:19.221
a rider fifteen feet during an inverted loop.

03:56:19.221 --> 03:56:24.010
They landed on the track below, breaking their
neck and skull, causing instant death.

03:56:24.010 --> 03:56:27.980
While this was a tragedy, it wasn’t exactly
anomalous.

03:56:27.980 --> 03:56:32.410
But the next major accident on the ride was
an entirely different story.

03:56:32.410 --> 03:56:38.091
This time, fifteen people met with disaster
while riding the Thriller Chiller roller coaster.

03:56:38.091 --> 03:56:42.870
Starting from the front and moving back one
car at a time, each group of riders was decapitated

03:56:42.870 --> 03:56:44.660
by blunt force trauma.

03:56:44.660 --> 03:56:49.540
A new pair of decapitations appeared to happen
at every turn and loop on the ride.

03:56:49.540 --> 03:56:54.360
Forensic scientists still have no idea how
this could have possibly occurred.

03:56:54.360 --> 03:56:59.110
Despite all of these disasters, the park was
only finally abandoned after a day known as

03:56:59.110 --> 03:57:05.000
“Bloody Sunday”, when the anomalous powers
of the location reached a twenty year peak.

03:57:05.000 --> 03:57:10.540
It’s believed that 231 people were killed
during the carnage of that day, and another

03:57:10.540 --> 03:57:12.471
seven were horribly maimed.

03:57:12.471 --> 03:57:17.340
The SCP Foundation contained the Carnival
of Horrors not long after, but the mysterious

03:57:17.340 --> 03:57:19.341
deaths didn’t even end there.

03:57:19.341 --> 03:57:24.530
Foundation Mobile Task Force Rho-71, also
known as the Origami Toads, were sent in to

03:57:24.530 --> 03:57:29.271
assess containment procedures and discover
the source of all the anomalous deaths.

03:57:29.271 --> 03:57:34.780
They were unsuccessful though, and instead
they merely added to the list, in exceptionally

03:57:34.780 --> 03:57:36.910
horrifying ways.

03:57:36.910 --> 03:57:41.190
One agent was found dead, surrounded by empty
grenades and bullet casings.

03:57:41.190 --> 03:57:45.820
It appeared he’d removed the explosive propellant
from all of his ballistics and consumed it,

03:57:45.820 --> 03:57:47.490
dying in the process.

03:57:47.490 --> 03:57:51.620
Another was found with his jaw broken, having
apparently pulled out and inhaled his own

03:57:51.620 --> 03:57:55.341
teeth, and dying of the resulting internal
damage.

03:57:55.341 --> 03:58:00.061
The commander got the worst fate of all - so
horrifying, in fact, that we can’t tell

03:58:00.061 --> 03:58:01.880
you the full details.

03:58:01.880 --> 03:58:06.190
All you need to know is that something was
shoved into his brain that really didn’t

03:58:06.190 --> 03:58:07.320
belong there.

03:58:07.320 --> 03:58:11.860
The Foundation considered having the entire
park destroyed with a massive airstrike, courtesy

03:58:11.860 --> 03:58:15.021
of the Mobile Task Force Nu-7, aka Hammer
Down.

03:58:15.021 --> 03:58:20.021
However, the O5 Council denied this request,
on the basis that the park was too close to

03:58:20.021 --> 03:58:24.460
populated land, they’d have no plausible
cover story for the bombing, and they don’t

03:58:24.460 --> 03:58:28.921
even really know if blowing up the park would
prevent anomalous activity from occurring.

03:58:28.921 --> 03:58:34.340
The Carnival of Horrors is here to stay, folks,
the Foundation just hopes to keep it from

03:58:34.340 --> 03:58:36.240
getting new visitors.

03:58:36.240 --> 03:58:40.450
So then back to why the researchers want this
place upgraded to Keter.

03:58:40.450 --> 03:58:45.330
After all, these classifications aren’t
about how dangerous an anomaly is - they’re

03:58:45.330 --> 03:58:49.040
about how difficult and complicated they are
to contain.

03:58:49.040 --> 03:58:53.760
But here’s the problem - according to researchers,
the Red Zone - where the dangerous, anomalous

03:58:53.760 --> 03:58:57.950
activity is at its peak - isn’t bound to
one fixed position.

03:58:57.950 --> 03:59:02.900
It’s changed position at least three times
already, and even worse, it appears to be

03:59:02.900 --> 03:59:03.950
growing.

03:59:03.950 --> 03:59:06.860
Not seeming so Euclid class now, is it?

03:59:06.860 --> 03:59:12.450
After all, you might not even need to visit
the Carnival of Horrors to be in grave danger.

03:59:12.450 --> 03:59:20.760
If it keeps growing then someday soon, the
Carnival of Horrors may be visiting you…

03:59:20.760 --> 03:59:24.830
It’s a perfect day for a wedding.

03:59:24.830 --> 03:59:29.910
On a warm spring afternoon, a beautiful bride
and a handsome groom are exchanging the special

03:59:29.910 --> 03:59:33.480
rings they had custom designed and made for
each other.

03:59:33.480 --> 03:59:38.400
As they take turns placing the rings on each
other's fingers, a man standing at the end

03:59:38.400 --> 03:59:40.550
of the wedding party steps out of position.

03:59:40.550 --> 03:59:44.791
He approaches the groomsman next to him and
reaches into his jacket, taking out a pair

03:59:44.791 --> 03:59:47.351
of pliers that he hands to the groomsman.

03:59:47.351 --> 03:59:52.470
The groomsman happily takes the tool and then,
without any hesitation, shoves the pliers

03:59:52.470 --> 03:59:56.250
into his mouth and begins removing his teeth
one by one.

03:59:56.250 --> 04:00:00.881
When he is finished, he hands the bloody teeth
to the man along with the pliers.

04:00:00.881 --> 04:00:05.311
The man then goes to the next groomsman who
repeats the same process.

04:00:05.311 --> 04:00:09.860
He continues going down the line until all
of the groomsmen and bridesmaids have removed

04:00:09.860 --> 04:00:14.391
their teeth, seemingly without pain or resistance.

04:00:14.391 --> 04:00:16.960
The man then approaches the bride and groom.

04:00:16.960 --> 04:00:21.570
He hands each of them half of the pile of
teeth, which they gladly accept.

04:00:21.570 --> 04:00:26.820
They then begin to eat the teeth without delay,
seemingly not bothered by the intense damage

04:00:26.820 --> 04:00:30.450
they’re causing to their own teeth and jaws
by doing so.

04:00:30.450 --> 04:00:35.240
The man watches as the groom moves the priest
who was officiating the wedding aside.

04:00:35.240 --> 04:00:40.480
As the entire church looks on in joy, the
groom opens his mouth and the deafening sound

04:00:40.480 --> 04:00:42.590
of cicadas are heard.

04:00:42.590 --> 04:00:49.430
This is only the beginning of what the SCP
Foundation has labeled an SCP-2852 event,

04:00:49.430 --> 04:00:54.380
a terrifying and little understood phenomenon
that is better known by the nickname of the

04:00:54.380 --> 04:00:56.710
anomalous creature responsible for them…

04:00:56.710 --> 04:00:58.140
Cousin Johnny.

04:00:58.140 --> 04:01:02.301
The Foundation had been trying to contain
Cousin Johnny for decades - not that it’d

04:01:02.301 --> 04:01:04.101
ever done them any good.

04:01:04.101 --> 04:01:08.561
Johnny is a Keter-Class anomaly that’s thus
far proven impossible to contain.

04:01:08.561 --> 04:01:12.980
This is an entity so dangerous and volatile
that three different Mobile Task Forces are

04:01:12.980 --> 04:01:20.190
devoted to detecting and disrupting its activities
- MTF Upsilon-36, aka The Party Crashers.

04:01:20.190 --> 04:01:23.311
MTF Upsilon-52, aka Cater Duty.

04:01:23.311 --> 04:01:26.940
And MTF Upsilon-99, aka The Altar Boys.

04:01:26.940 --> 04:01:31.921
But so far all the Foundation has been able
to really do is swoop in afterwards and do

04:01:31.921 --> 04:01:35.750
their best to pick up the pieces of people’s
shattered lives.

04:01:35.750 --> 04:01:40.971
Cousin Johnny has so far been observed to
only operate in the North American subcontinent,

04:01:40.971 --> 04:01:46.220
and only seems to appear at Anglican or Catholic
baptisms, weddings, and funerals.

04:01:46.220 --> 04:01:50.431
However, Foundation operatives charged with
keeping a lid on Cousin Johnny harbor the

04:01:50.431 --> 04:01:55.990
hidden fear that he may one day expand his
hunting grounds, and wreak terror worldwide.

04:01:55.990 --> 04:02:02.851
If Johnny became multinational or multi denominational,
his violence, insanity, and pure evil may

04:02:02.851 --> 04:02:09.230
truly become impossible to minimize, so compatible
communities are constantly monitored for increased

04:02:09.230 --> 04:02:14.771
levels of juvenile delinquency, sterility,
domestic violence, and divorce.

04:02:14.771 --> 04:02:19.311
After all this, you’re probably wondering:
Who or what actually is Cousin Johnny, and

04:02:19.311 --> 04:02:21.910
how does he cause so much horrific tragedy?

04:02:21.910 --> 04:02:25.860
At face value, nothing about the appearance
of Cousin Johnny would suggest an anomalous

04:02:25.860 --> 04:02:28.521
nature, or even any sort of danger.

04:02:28.521 --> 04:02:33.101
He appears to be a middle-aged white male,
often with scruffy hair and a beard.

04:02:33.101 --> 04:02:38.351
On a cellular level too, Cousin Johnny appears
all too human, but when you look at his physiology

04:02:38.351 --> 04:02:40.641
it’s a whole different story.

04:02:40.641 --> 04:02:46.180
Cousin Johnny has no identifiable organs whatsoever
- his body is made out of a fibrous muscular

04:02:46.180 --> 04:02:47.180
tissue.

04:02:47.180 --> 04:02:51.450
The only exceptions are his teeth and hair,
which are made of a kind of chitin - a key

04:02:51.450 --> 04:02:56.370
component of insect exoskeletons, such as
those possessed by cicadas.

04:02:56.370 --> 04:03:00.011
Johnny’s eyes are the first clue that something
is off about him.

04:03:00.011 --> 04:03:05.210
From a distance they appear perfectly normal,
but up close, they’re glassy and dead.

04:03:05.210 --> 04:03:09.341
This is because his eyes aren’t actually
attached to any nerves inside his head.

04:03:09.341 --> 04:03:15.380
With no nervous system or vocal chords, Johnny’s
ability to see, move, and talk defy any kind

04:03:15.380 --> 04:03:17.181
of logical explanation.

04:03:17.181 --> 04:03:21.200
His speech will seem completely normal to
the people under his spell, but to anyone

04:03:21.200 --> 04:03:26.261
else, it comes out as complete nonsense, often
described as word salad.

04:03:26.261 --> 04:03:30.910
If people in attendance are briefed in advance
about this phenomenon, whatever hypnotic ability

04:03:30.910 --> 04:03:35.601
causes them to hear his sounds as intelligible
words won’t work, and they’ll be aware

04:03:35.601 --> 04:03:37.660
of how nonsensical it all sounds.

04:03:37.660 --> 04:03:41.360
But of course, that doesn’t mean they’re
safe.

04:03:41.360 --> 04:03:45.620
Cousin Johnny appears at family gatherings
and religious rituals, and immediately, he’ll

04:03:45.620 --> 04:03:48.140
be treated as though he’s always been there.

04:03:48.140 --> 04:03:49.761
You know your Cousin Johnny, right?

04:03:49.761 --> 04:03:51.631
You go way back.

04:03:51.631 --> 04:03:54.170
Or at least, you’re pretty sure you do.

04:03:54.170 --> 04:03:56.771
Nothing will appear unnatural about his sudden
presence.

04:03:56.771 --> 04:04:01.580
In fact, if you’re one of the victims of
one of his incidents, chances are, you’ll

04:04:01.580 --> 04:04:04.400
actually find yourself taking a shine to Cousin
Johnny.

04:04:04.400 --> 04:04:09.260
Sure his sense of humor is a little crude
and raunchy, but you can’t help but enjoy

04:04:09.260 --> 04:04:10.271
his company.

04:04:10.271 --> 04:04:14.440
He’s a fun guy to be around, and after all,
he’s family!

04:04:14.440 --> 04:04:19.360
As previously mentioned, he’ll only appear
at three different kinds of events: Baptisms,

04:04:19.360 --> 04:04:23.640
Weddings, and Funerals, and only at those
that are affiliated with either the Catholic

04:04:23.640 --> 04:04:25.440
or Anglican religions.

04:04:25.440 --> 04:04:30.960
The SCP Foundation has classified baptisms
that Cousin Johnny attends as Blue Level Events,

04:04:30.960 --> 04:04:35.521
Weddings are known as White Level Events,
and Funerals are Black Level Events - with

04:04:35.521 --> 04:04:40.190
each one escalating in severity, violence,
and horror.

04:04:40.190 --> 04:04:43.030
First, Baptisms - the Blue Level Events.

04:04:43.030 --> 04:04:48.061
In these events, Cousin Johnny will appear
and begin to act as a third godparent, despite

04:04:48.061 --> 04:04:50.370
there traditionally only being two.

04:04:50.370 --> 04:04:54.670
As the infant is lowered into the holy water,
the entirety of their top layer of skin will

04:04:54.670 --> 04:04:57.110
come off, like a molting snake.

04:04:57.110 --> 04:05:01.220
Despite looking horrific, this apparently
causes no harm to the child.

04:05:01.220 --> 04:05:05.430
The godparents will then eat this discarded
skin, as though it’s the most normal thing

04:05:05.430 --> 04:05:06.620
in the world.

04:05:06.620 --> 04:05:10.670
After this, the family will leave the church
together, and Cousin Johnny will leave with

04:05:10.670 --> 04:05:11.670
them.

04:05:11.670 --> 04:05:13.980
He won’t appear at any subsequent celebrations
of the child’s baptism.

04:05:13.980 --> 04:05:15.271
If this is where it ended, it’d be extremely
gross - but not exactly a living nightmare.

04:05:15.271 --> 04:05:18.910
Of course this is just the beginning of the
terror.

04:05:18.910 --> 04:05:22.340
Following Cousin Johnny’s appearance at
the baptism, the child’s risk of dying in

04:05:22.340 --> 04:05:27.521
the next six months skyrockets, and if they
survive, they’re at an increased risk of

04:05:27.521 --> 04:05:30.840
becoming unstable and violent later on in
life.

04:05:30.840 --> 04:05:35.341
Their parents and godparents will both become
unable to conceive any further children, and

04:05:35.341 --> 04:05:39.860
are likely to be found dead from drowning
within five years of the event.

04:05:39.860 --> 04:05:44.360
Those who were only tangentially involved
in the baptism ritual have a massively increased

04:05:44.360 --> 04:05:49.311
chance of failed pregnancies, or - if they
do conceive - they may become a danger to

04:05:49.311 --> 04:05:51.120
their offspring.

04:05:51.120 --> 04:05:55.131
Children who live through Blue Level Events
and survive past adolescence, will experience

04:05:55.131 --> 04:05:59.760
adverse side effects when encountering the
songs of cicadas well into adulthood - from

04:05:59.760 --> 04:06:04.180
experiencing physical sickness to going through
dangerous psychotic episodes.

04:06:04.180 --> 04:06:08.420
Weddings, or White Level Events, are more
complex and severe.

04:06:08.420 --> 04:06:12.950
In this case, Cousin Johnny will insert himself
into the wedding as a groomsman, and the most

04:06:12.950 --> 04:06:17.590
horrifying events will begin to take place
after the vows have been exchanged.

04:06:17.590 --> 04:06:21.780
Johnny will provide various implements that
allow the bridesmaids and groomsmen to remove

04:06:21.780 --> 04:06:26.820
their teeth, which are then given to the bride
and groom to eat - which they do, causing

04:06:26.820 --> 04:06:30.050
severe damage to their own teeth in the process.

04:06:30.050 --> 04:06:36.080
The groom will then vocalize an unknown cicada
call at an incredible volume, as loud as 140

04:06:36.080 --> 04:06:41.220
decibels in some instances, rendering the
bride and everyone else near the altar completely

04:06:41.220 --> 04:06:42.220
deaf.

04:06:42.220 --> 04:06:45.880
At the wedding reception, where everyone is
continuing to behave as if northing out of

04:06:45.880 --> 04:06:50.930
the ordinary is happening, Cousin Johnny will
ruin things further by giving the best man’s

04:06:50.930 --> 04:06:51.930
speech.

04:06:51.930 --> 04:06:55.330
The speech is more of his typical complete
nonsense, though if you’re there you’ll

04:06:55.330 --> 04:06:59.920
never realize this, and think that this is
the best speech you’ve ever heard, with

04:06:59.920 --> 04:07:04.370
some in the audience laughing hysterically
while others cry uncontrollably.

04:07:04.370 --> 04:07:08.080
Once his speech is done, he’ll present a
gift to the newly married couple…

04:07:08.080 --> 04:07:13.480
3.5 kilograms of human hair in various colors,
13 deceased specimens of a certain cicada

04:07:13.480 --> 04:07:18.440
known as Linne's cicada, and 23 human teeth
in a cardboard box.

04:07:18.440 --> 04:07:22.480
DNA tests on all gifts have been inconclusive
as to their origin.

04:07:22.480 --> 04:07:27.551
Much like many celebrity marriages, unions
that occurred during White Level events never

04:07:27.551 --> 04:07:32.851
last, and all end up divorced within two years
- often as a result of domestic violence,

04:07:32.851 --> 04:07:36.851
and any children born during their brief marriage
will be violent and unstable.

04:07:36.851 --> 04:07:41.200
But it’s not just the wedding party that
gets to experience the fun of a visit from

04:07:41.200 --> 04:07:42.480
Cousin Johnny.

04:07:42.480 --> 04:07:46.850
All married individuals who attended the wedding
will find that they are unable to conceive

04:07:46.850 --> 04:07:50.390
children, despite no biological indicators
of infertility.

04:07:50.390 --> 04:07:54.230
Any children present at the White Level Event
will show no interest in romance throughout

04:07:54.230 --> 04:07:59.061
their life, and often die tragically before
reaching the age of eighteen.

04:07:59.061 --> 04:08:04.540
Finally, and most horrifying of all, are funerals
- or Black Level Events.

04:08:04.540 --> 04:08:08.760
While Blue and White Level Events can potentially
be disrupted before they are completed, lessening

04:08:08.760 --> 04:08:14.130
or preventing the horrific results, there
is as yet no way to stop or prevent a Black

04:08:14.130 --> 04:08:16.600
Level Event at any stage.

04:08:16.600 --> 04:08:20.690
Any attempts to prevent Cousin Johnny from
entering the church or funeral home will lead

04:08:20.690 --> 04:08:23.280
to him simply manifesting inside.

04:08:23.280 --> 04:08:27.450
Once in the room where the funeral is taking
place, Cousin Johnny will first take up the

04:08:27.450 --> 04:08:32.271
role of eulogizer and begin speaking his standard
nonsense to the attendants.

04:08:32.271 --> 04:08:36.680
The person who was emotionally closest to
the departed will then open the casket, if

04:08:36.680 --> 04:08:41.320
this was not already an open casket funeral,
and will then produce a large knife.

04:08:41.320 --> 04:08:45.360
It’s unknown where the knives come from
as they’re not present before the event

04:08:45.360 --> 04:08:47.131
and they disappear after.

04:08:47.131 --> 04:08:51.851
The funeral attendees will then use the knife
on their wrists and sometimes throats, draining

04:08:51.851 --> 04:08:53.930
their blood into the coffin.

04:08:53.930 --> 04:08:59.220
Many lose more than enough blood to result
in death, but none ever die from this, nor

04:08:59.220 --> 04:09:02.690
do they seem to feel any pain from their wounds.

04:09:02.690 --> 04:09:07.061
As the attendees take turns bleeding into
the coffin, Cousin Johnny continues his eulogy

04:09:07.061 --> 04:09:12.811
which eventually evolves into a cicada song,
the kind sung by Linne’s cicada males.

04:09:12.811 --> 04:09:17.350
The attendants sing the same song back to
him in a kind of call and response.

04:09:17.350 --> 04:09:21.940
Cousin Johnny will then approach the coffin
and vomit in a mixture of blood, wood pulp,

04:09:21.940 --> 04:09:23.540
and dead cicadas.

04:09:23.540 --> 04:09:28.271
The funeral will then proceed as normal, and
the blood, vomit, and cicada filled casket

04:09:28.271 --> 04:09:31.380
is then taken to the cemetery and buried.

04:09:31.380 --> 04:09:35.771
Black Level Events will usually end with the
body being interred in the ground, but if

04:09:35.771 --> 04:09:40.091
there’s a wake after the funeral, the horrors
of the Black Level Event will continue.

04:09:40.091 --> 04:09:45.400
At the wake, Cousin Johnny will climb on top
of a table, lie down, and encourage the other

04:09:45.400 --> 04:09:51.890
attendants to devour him, which they do - all
while he continues to talk his nonsense.

04:09:51.890 --> 04:09:54.070
Until there is nothing left.

04:09:54.070 --> 04:09:59.550
Much like Blue and White Level events, being
in attendance leads to horrific after-effects.

04:09:59.550 --> 04:10:03.590
All participants who experience this event
will separate from their family through either

04:10:03.590 --> 04:10:06.601
suicide, moving, or divorce.

04:10:06.601 --> 04:10:10.740
Every individual present at the event will
also find that they are no longer able to

04:10:10.740 --> 04:10:15.431
produce offspring, and couples present may
also fall victim to incidences of domestic

04:10:15.431 --> 04:10:21.561
violence, often involving cannibalism, that
usually leave one or both participants dead,

04:10:21.561 --> 04:10:26.390
while six out of ten children involved will
attempt to murder one or both of their parents

04:10:26.390 --> 04:10:28.480
before they turn eighteen.

04:10:28.480 --> 04:10:33.551
These Black Level Events are so horrible for
all involved, that any members of the specialized

04:10:33.551 --> 04:10:38.070
Cousin Johnny Mobile Task Forces that happen
to witness such an event are treated with

04:10:38.070 --> 04:10:43.470
Class-A amnestics before they are transferred
to another task force or retire, to ensure

04:10:43.470 --> 04:10:47.300
that they don’t have to live with the memories
of what they saw.

04:10:47.300 --> 04:10:51.590
Prior to that, they are closely monitored
for any strange or anti-social behavior to

04:10:51.590 --> 04:10:53.820
make sure they weren’t affected by the event.

04:10:53.820 --> 04:10:58.641
And they aren’t the only SCP Foundation
staff at risk of having been impacted by Cousin

04:10:58.641 --> 04:10:59.641
Johnny.

04:10:59.641 --> 04:11:03.980
It is theorized that as many as a third of
Catholic and Anglican D-Class personnel were

04:11:03.980 --> 04:11:09.430
involved in a Black-Level event at some point,
and were driven to madness and violence by

04:11:09.430 --> 04:11:14.251
their fateful brushes with the strange relative
that no one knows.

04:11:14.251 --> 04:11:19.181
So next time you’re at a baptism, or a wedding,
or a funeral, stay vigilant.

04:11:19.181 --> 04:11:21.400
Keep an eye on the other guests.

04:11:21.400 --> 04:11:26.860
And always ask yourself: Do you really have
a Cousin Johnny?

04:11:26.860 --> 04:11:35.010
It was July of 2004, and Bill Murray was enjoying
the peak of an extremely successful career.

04:11:35.010 --> 04:11:40.101
Not only had the iconic actor starred in some
of the most beloved comedies of the 20th Century,

04:11:40.101 --> 04:11:44.811
including Ghostbusters and Groundhog Day,
he’d voiced the main character of the recently-released

04:11:44.811 --> 04:11:46.590
live action Garfield movie.

04:11:46.590 --> 04:11:50.580
It’d been a financial success, but it was
a critical flop.

04:11:50.580 --> 04:11:56.440
Not that this bothered Bill – he was happy
with the performance... and the paycheck.

04:11:56.440 --> 04:12:00.470
What he wouldn’t be quite as happy about
was the horrifying encounter he was about

04:12:00.470 --> 04:12:03.530
to have with SCP – 3166.

04:12:03.530 --> 04:12:10.240
On July 8th, Bill was enjoying a cold drink
on the porch of his luxurious Beverly Hills

04:12:10.240 --> 04:12:11.240
home.

04:12:11.240 --> 04:12:14.000
The sky was beginning to darken as the sun
set in the west.

04:12:14.000 --> 04:12:15.940
It was a blissful evening.

04:12:15.940 --> 04:12:19.150
His wife, Jennifer, was inside, watching TV.

04:12:19.150 --> 04:12:23.890
Nothing seemed particularly out of the ordinary,
until he noticed a quick flash of orange in

04:12:23.890 --> 04:12:24.890
the distance.

04:12:24.890 --> 04:12:30.040
It was almost too fast to register, this large,
orange shape darting past the corner of his

04:12:30.040 --> 04:12:31.040
eye.

04:12:31.040 --> 04:12:34.271
For a second, he entertained the thought that
it might have been an escaped tiger, but it

04:12:34.271 --> 04:12:36.750
was gone too fast to really tell.

04:12:36.750 --> 04:12:38.730
Bill finished his drink and headed inside.

04:12:38.730 --> 04:12:41.061
He’d had enough for one night.

04:12:41.061 --> 04:12:45.320
The next morning, he got up to read the paper,
and found the Garfield movie getting slaughtered

04:12:45.320 --> 04:12:46.551
by the critics.

04:12:46.551 --> 04:12:51.480
One review stated “no one can accuse Garfield:
The Movie of infidelity to its source: It

04:12:51.480 --> 04:12:56.630
faithfully conveys the banality of Jim Davis's
cartoon” Another called it“a film without

04:12:56.630 --> 04:12:58.130
energy and without spirit.”

04:12:58.130 --> 04:13:01.320
He put the paper down and ate his breakfast.

04:13:01.320 --> 04:13:06.910
A few blows to the ego were worth it for the
paydays that came with big budget family films.

04:13:06.910 --> 04:13:11.351
Just then his wife came to him with a strange
question: Were you walking around downstairs

04:13:11.351 --> 04:13:13.160
in the middle of the night?

04:13:13.160 --> 04:13:15.830
No, he hadn’t, he’d been sleeping like
a baby.

04:13:15.830 --> 04:13:17.101
Why did she ask?

04:13:17.101 --> 04:13:18.101
“Well…”

04:13:18.101 --> 04:13:19.101
Jennifer said.

04:13:19.101 --> 04:13:21.390
“I heard some rustling downstairs last night.

04:13:21.390 --> 04:13:23.330
It sounded like something big.”

04:13:23.330 --> 04:13:28.400
He hadn’t heard anything though and told
her it was probably just her imagination.

04:13:28.400 --> 04:13:31.400
He put it out of his mind and continued about
his day.

04:13:31.400 --> 04:13:34.851
He decided he would keep his eyes peeled for
that orange blur again though.

04:13:34.851 --> 04:13:40.030
Bill didn’t see anything peculiar the rest
of the morning and went to a local café for

04:13:40.030 --> 04:13:41.030
lunch.

04:13:41.030 --> 04:13:44.641
He ordered a coffee and a cream cheese bagel,
then made a quick trip to the bathroom while

04:13:44.641 --> 04:13:45.641
his food was prepared.

04:13:45.641 --> 04:13:50.580
When Bill returned to his table though, he
was something strange.

04:13:50.580 --> 04:13:54.670
Instead of a bagel, there was a large heaping
of lasagna on the table.

04:13:54.670 --> 04:13:55.851
What was going on?

04:13:55.851 --> 04:13:58.061
This café didn’t even serve lasagna.

04:13:58.061 --> 04:14:01.620
Bill knew something was terribly wrong.

04:14:01.620 --> 04:14:06.750
Things only got stranger when Bill came home
to find a small tuft of orange fur snagged

04:14:06.750 --> 04:14:08.700
on the frame of his front door.

04:14:08.700 --> 04:14:13.240
And it wasn’t synthetic fur like you see
on plush toys or stuffed animals.

04:14:13.240 --> 04:14:16.890
No, this was real animal fur.

04:14:16.890 --> 04:14:21.880
Maybe someone was just goofing off or trying
to play some weird prank on him, but it didn’t

04:14:21.880 --> 04:14:22.880
feel like it.

04:14:22.880 --> 04:14:27.180
Deep down, Bill Murray knew that he was in
grave danger.

04:14:27.180 --> 04:14:33.330
Whoever, or whatever, was behind this… it
wanted to hurt him.

04:14:33.330 --> 04:14:35.881
That night, his worst fears were realized.

04:14:35.881 --> 04:14:39.460
Bill’s wife had left town for the week and
he was heading to the kitchen in the middle

04:14:39.460 --> 04:14:44.320
of the night for a glass of water, when he
saw something - A huge figure moving up against

04:14:44.320 --> 04:14:46.860
the glass door leading to his backyard.

04:14:46.860 --> 04:14:52.950
The thing was huge, nearly seven feet tall,
with a bloated, fur-covered, misshapen body

04:14:52.950 --> 04:14:55.720
that was pressed up against the door.

04:14:55.720 --> 04:15:01.070
Its fur was bright, garish orange – a cartoon
orange.

04:15:01.070 --> 04:15:04.271
Strangest of all though was the sound it was
making.

04:15:04.271 --> 04:15:06.980
It sounded like it was purring.

04:15:06.980 --> 04:15:10.680
Bill backed away from the door and then ran
back to his room to hide.

04:15:10.680 --> 04:15:15.430
The whole night, he sat cowering as he heard
scratching against the walls, like something

04:15:15.430 --> 04:15:17.070
was trying to get in.

04:15:17.070 --> 04:15:20.950
He was terrified and too scared to do anything,
even move.

04:15:20.950 --> 04:15:24.760
Finally, as morning broke, the noises seemed
to stop.

04:15:24.760 --> 04:15:26.180
Bill had to do something.

04:15:26.180 --> 04:15:28.350
He couldn’t let this nightmare go on another
night.

04:15:28.350 --> 04:15:30.400
What if things got worse?

04:15:30.400 --> 04:15:33.261
What if that thing managed to get inside?

04:15:33.261 --> 04:15:38.340
He called the local police and when they arrived,
he explained the incredibly strange situation

04:15:38.340 --> 04:15:39.791
as best he could.

04:15:39.791 --> 04:15:44.160
He told them he was being stalked by some
kind of huge cat, or at least someone dressed

04:15:44.160 --> 04:15:46.040
like a huge cat.

04:15:46.040 --> 04:15:47.931
Also there was lasagna involved.

04:15:47.931 --> 04:15:51.630
The officers interviewing him could barely
contain their laughter as he told them his

04:15:51.630 --> 04:15:52.630
story.

04:15:52.630 --> 04:15:53.630
A giant orange cat?

04:15:53.630 --> 04:15:58.410
Perhaps, one of them theorized, he’d angered
some kind of obsessive Garfield fan through

04:15:58.410 --> 04:16:01.271
his involvement in the live action movie.

04:16:01.271 --> 04:16:06.400
After all, the original comic had been running
for years and had been extremely popular.

04:16:06.400 --> 04:16:11.070
Who knows what kind of nut jobs were obsessed
with seeing only a faithful adaptation of

04:16:11.070 --> 04:16:12.740
the source material?

04:16:12.740 --> 04:16:17.351
As the officers departed, Bill was confident
that they weren’t taking him seriously.

04:16:17.351 --> 04:16:19.851
He couldn’t rely on any of them for protection.

04:16:19.851 --> 04:16:24.820
Thankfully, from a multi-decade movie career,
he had plenty of disposable income, and decided

04:16:24.820 --> 04:16:29.390
to hire a private security team to protect
him while he looked into this mystery.

04:16:29.390 --> 04:16:34.120
He had two trained bodyguards positioned around
his home at all times for the next month.

04:16:34.120 --> 04:16:38.210
They were armed, and given the cryptic orders
to fire on anything orange.

04:16:38.210 --> 04:16:42.620
Meanwhile, Bill began to fall down a Garfield
rabbit hole.

04:16:42.620 --> 04:16:47.171
He felt strangely compelled to research all
the Garfield media he could find, as though

04:16:47.171 --> 04:16:52.040
the answer to his terrifying situation was
somehow hidden between the lines.

04:16:52.040 --> 04:16:55.490
Bill explored the entire backlog of thousands
of comic strips.

04:16:55.490 --> 04:16:58.521
He read the books and interviews with Jim
Davis.

04:16:58.521 --> 04:17:02.091
He watched the cartoons and straight-to-DVD
animated movies.

04:17:02.091 --> 04:17:06.880
Ironically for a guy who’d recently portrayed
the lasagna-loving orange cat, Bill had never

04:17:06.880 --> 04:17:10.540
felt quite so immersed in the character before.

04:17:10.540 --> 04:17:16.110
He found a strange pathos in the routine of
Garfield and his friends.One particular comic

04:17:16.110 --> 04:17:18.830
really piqued his interest, though.

04:17:18.830 --> 04:17:23.550
Originally published in October of 1989, the
comic began with Garfield being woken up by

04:17:23.550 --> 04:17:26.620
a strange chill, an almost eerie sensation.

04:17:26.620 --> 04:17:30.360
The character observed aloud that he didn’t
feel like he was in his own home.

04:17:30.360 --> 04:17:34.570
He explored his little home further, trying
to find his owner Jon or his housemate and

04:17:34.570 --> 04:17:38.370
sometimes nemesis, Odie, but found nothing.

04:17:38.370 --> 04:17:43.920
As Garfield remarked on feeling alone, a purple
speech box delivered the sinister message:

04:17:43.920 --> 04:17:48.961
“You have no idea how alone you are, Garfield.”

04:17:48.961 --> 04:17:53.850
He then finds that his home looks like it’s
been abandoned for years.

04:17:53.850 --> 04:17:58.100
The “For Sale” sign outside is practically
ancient.

04:17:58.100 --> 04:18:04.220
Garfield slowly comes to a horrifying revelation:
Everyone really is gone, and his adventures

04:18:04.220 --> 04:18:07.340
and friends now exist only in his imagination.

04:18:07.340 --> 04:18:12.170
He’s trapped in a prison of his own creation,
trying to stave off his endless loneliness,

04:18:12.170 --> 04:18:15.370
in denial about the reality of his situation.

04:18:15.370 --> 04:18:20.400
The comic ended with a quote directly from
Jim Davis himself, saying “An imagination

04:18:20.400 --> 04:18:21.610
is a powerful tool.

04:18:21.610 --> 04:18:28.021
It can tint memories of the past, shade perceptions
of the present, or paint a future so vivid

04:18:28.021 --> 04:18:34.561
that it can entice... or terrify, all depending
upon how we conduct ourselves today...”

04:18:34.561 --> 04:18:38.710
As he read those words, Bill Murray felt a
chill down his spine.

04:18:38.710 --> 04:18:42.391
Why had he wanted to get involved in the Garfield
movie in the first place?

04:18:42.391 --> 04:18:44.400
What had he gotten himself into?

04:18:44.400 --> 04:18:49.950
Before he could slip any deeper into his own
mind, Bill heard a faint, choked scream downstairs.

04:18:49.950 --> 04:18:52.820
He felt his breath catch in his throat.

04:18:52.820 --> 04:18:56.271
He was terrified but he needed to see what
was happening.

04:18:56.271 --> 04:19:00.190
He carefully and quietly began to creep down
the stairs.

04:19:00.190 --> 04:19:04.240
At the bottom, he poked his head around a
corner, and that’s when he saw a member

04:19:04.240 --> 04:19:07.091
of his security detail lying dead on the floor.

04:19:07.091 --> 04:19:11.721
His face was blue from asphyxiation, his mouth
was stuffed with lasagna.

04:19:11.721 --> 04:19:16.300
It looked like he had been force-fed to death.

04:19:16.300 --> 04:19:20.540
Bill wanted to scream but he couldn’t, or
maybe knew he shouldn’t.

04:19:20.540 --> 04:19:25.170
Just then he heard a soft, meaty thumping
noise coming from the nearby living room.

04:19:25.170 --> 04:19:31.120
He didn’t know why, but he felt compelled
to approach as if by forces beyond his control.

04:19:31.120 --> 04:19:36.890
He made his way to the living room, and when
he got there, he saw where the noise was coming

04:19:36.890 --> 04:19:37.890
from.

04:19:37.890 --> 04:19:39.740
Bill’s jaw dropped in pure horror.

04:19:39.740 --> 04:19:44.990
There was the other member of his security
detail, lying limp and lifeless under a giant

04:19:44.990 --> 04:19:45.990
orange figure.

04:19:45.990 --> 04:19:51.030
It was a grotesquely huge creature, wearing
what looked to be a kind of crude Garfield

04:19:51.030 --> 04:19:53.620
outfit made of sewn-together cat pelts.

04:19:53.620 --> 04:19:56.500
It stank of pasta and rotten meat.

04:19:56.500 --> 04:20:02.440
In its giant paw, it held a golden trophy,
which it was using to pound the security guard’s

04:20:02.440 --> 04:20:07.190
head into mush while making quiet, cat-like
purring noises.

04:20:07.190 --> 04:20:11.940
The creature suddenly stopped and looked up,
locking eyes with Bill.

04:20:11.940 --> 04:20:14.040
The fear of death came over him.

04:20:14.040 --> 04:20:20.130
He froze, as the giant, freakish Garfield
stepped over Donny’s corpse, and began to

04:20:20.130 --> 04:20:21.130
come towards him.

04:20:21.130 --> 04:20:24.340
Bill turned and ran, but Garfield was gaining
on him.

04:20:24.340 --> 04:20:27.561
Before he could make it to the front door,
the creature knocked him over.

04:20:27.561 --> 04:20:31.990
He was laid out on the ground, looking up
at it, as it reached into its own body cavity

04:20:31.990 --> 04:20:34.930
and began to pull out handfuls of lasagna.

04:20:34.930 --> 04:20:39.521
He was just about to shove a wad of the horrible
decaying pasta into Bill’s mouth, when suddenly,

04:20:39.521 --> 04:20:42.180
a DING was heard and the creature stopped.

04:20:42.180 --> 04:20:47.780
It looked up, as if sniffing the air, and
then suddenly turned and lumbered towards

04:20:47.780 --> 04:20:50.080
the kitchen.

04:20:50.080 --> 04:20:54.800
Bill watched as the Garfield monster entered
the kitchen where, somehow, there was a steaming

04:20:54.800 --> 04:20:58.061
hot fresh lasagna sitting in the open oven.

04:20:58.061 --> 04:21:02.640
The creature had sensed the presence of external
lasagna, and felt the compulsion to integrate

04:21:02.640 --> 04:21:08.050
it into its body, grabbing fistfulls and shoving
it into itself.

04:21:08.050 --> 04:21:12.630
Just then, a group of highly trained SCP Foundation
personnel burst into the room and subdued

04:21:12.630 --> 04:21:14.210
the creature.

04:21:14.210 --> 04:21:15.710
It had been an ambush.

04:21:15.710 --> 04:21:19.040
The Foundation had been tipped off to the
presence of the creature by monitoring the

04:21:19.040 --> 04:21:23.540
local police department dispatches, and the
report of a seven foot tall comic book cat

04:21:23.540 --> 04:21:27.650
terrorizing a Hollywood actor was definitely
worth looking into.

04:21:27.650 --> 04:21:34.150
The monster that had almost taken Bill Murray’s
life was SCP – 3166, a deadly pataphysical

04:21:34.150 --> 04:21:39.450
being that tends to manifest around people
somehow involved in the Garfield intellectual

04:21:39.450 --> 04:21:40.450
property.

04:21:40.450 --> 04:21:44.051
It appears whenever the public perception
of Garfield falls out of favor, and because

04:21:44.051 --> 04:21:48.550
Bill had starred in the critically-panned
Garfield movie, he was currently at the very

04:21:48.550 --> 04:21:52.650
top of SCP – 3166’s hit list.

04:21:52.650 --> 04:21:57.720
Thankfully, he managed to survive his terrifying
ordeal, and was administered amnestics by

04:21:57.720 --> 04:22:01.550
Foundation personnel so he could return to
his normal life.

04:22:01.550 --> 04:22:06.290
This frightening and mysterious creature has
been around since 1989, appearing after the

04:22:06.290 --> 04:22:11.650
publication of the haunting Garfield comic
that Bill had read that very night.

04:22:11.650 --> 04:22:15.511
It appeared in the office of United Media,
who were the publishers of the Garfield comic

04:22:15.511 --> 04:22:19.380
strip at the time, and began wreaking havoc.

04:22:19.380 --> 04:22:23.511
Since then, the creature’s manifestation
has been a constant threat whenever Garfield

04:22:23.511 --> 04:22:26.010
loses its popularity or audience.

04:22:26.010 --> 04:22:30.480
As a result, the Foundation has spent years
as the funding source behind all Garfield

04:22:30.480 --> 04:22:34.980
media, and even planting hypnotic memetics
into the comic strips to ensure that there

04:22:34.980 --> 04:22:37.851
is always a loyal fanbase.

04:22:37.851 --> 04:22:44.010
The fur is indeed real, organic cat fur, albeit
an unnaturally orange color, and instead of

04:22:44.010 --> 04:22:48.101
organs, the creature is filled with lasagna.

04:22:48.101 --> 04:22:52.641
Worst of all though, is that testing has revealed
that the meat in the lasagna is genetically

04:22:52.641 --> 04:22:56.440
identical to the flesh of Garfield’s creator,
Jim Davis.

04:22:56.440 --> 04:23:00.120
How did this thing come into existence?

04:23:00.120 --> 04:23:04.190
Perhaps it was Jim’s sheer force of imagination
that dragged it into being.

04:23:04.190 --> 04:23:09.101
As he himself said, “An imagination is a
powerful tool.”

04:23:09.101 --> 04:23:12.860
All in all, it’s lucky that Bill Murray
was able to survive his encounter, and return

04:23:12.860 --> 04:23:17.650
to his normal life – well, as normal as
life can be for Bill Murray.

04:23:17.650 --> 04:23:21.271
And if you see Bill Murray, don’t bother
asking him about SCP – 3166.

04:23:21.271 --> 04:23:28.990
The amnestics were quite effective, and just
as he’s fond of saying himself, no one will

04:23:28.990 --> 04:23:30.330
ever believe you.

04:23:30.330 --> 04:23:34.771
Cast your mind back to the height of the Cold
War.

04:23:34.771 --> 04:23:40.200
The ever-accelerating nuclear arms race brought
us closer than ever before to making the nightmare

04:23:40.200 --> 04:23:43.820
of nuclear armageddon a terrifying reality.

04:23:43.820 --> 04:23:48.851
The two main parties in this conflict are
the United States and Soviet Union, each amassing

04:23:48.851 --> 04:23:54.140
huge amounts of nuclear warheads and jumping
on any available advantage they can over their

04:23:54.140 --> 04:23:55.140
enemies.

04:23:55.140 --> 04:23:59.320
What you may not know is that, in order to
detect an impending attack from the United

04:23:59.320 --> 04:24:04.670
States, the Soviets developed what would become
known to the West as the “Dead Hand.”

04:24:04.670 --> 04:24:11.921
But this experimental piece of technology
also has another name: SCP-1984.

04:24:11.921 --> 04:24:17.021
It is no secret that the Soviet Union feared
the threat of US nuclear strikes and invasion

04:24:17.021 --> 04:24:23.200
just as much as the US feared an attack from
them, so SCP-1984 was created to act as a

04:24:23.200 --> 04:24:28.370
deterrence mechanism, specifically against
secure second strikes.

04:24:28.370 --> 04:24:33.480
Secure second strikes were both a deterrent
and overwhelming concern during the Cold War,

04:24:33.480 --> 04:24:38.010
referring to a country’s ability, after
suffering an initial nuclear attack, to still

04:24:38.010 --> 04:24:44.021
retaliate, firing on their enemy and causing
untold damage with their own arsenal of nuclear

04:24:44.021 --> 04:24:45.021
weapons.

04:24:45.021 --> 04:24:49.010
The Soviet Union knew that any action they
made that could be perceived as an attack

04:24:49.010 --> 04:24:53.682
on United States soil would be threatened
with nuclear retaliation, and that if they

04:24:53.682 --> 04:24:59.850
fired first, America would return fire and
potentially annihilate them with a second

04:24:59.850 --> 04:25:00.850
strike.

04:25:00.850 --> 04:25:05.190
SCP-1984 was to be an automated system that
would activate in response to the destruction

04:25:05.190 --> 04:25:08.600
of the Soviet’s main command and control
structure.

04:25:08.600 --> 04:25:12.930
Given that the Dead Hand was created during
the eighties, you might be forgiven for expecting

04:25:12.930 --> 04:25:18.311
a nuclear detection system built at this point
in history to consist of various sensors connected

04:25:18.311 --> 04:25:19.980
to a computer network.

04:25:19.980 --> 04:25:25.230
But you have also probably already realized
that, if that was the case, then the Foundation

04:25:25.230 --> 04:25:28.101
wouldn’t be so interested in it.

04:25:28.101 --> 04:25:33.521
In actuality, SCP-1984 is a fully autonomous
entity rather than a network of sensors for

04:25:33.521 --> 04:25:39.990
detecting incoming nuclear attacks or a computer
capable of initiating a second strike.

04:25:39.990 --> 04:25:45.220
Perhaps what makes the Foundation more interested
in the Dead Hand is that it is both self-aware,

04:25:45.220 --> 04:25:50.490
and linked simultaneously to every single
one of Russia’s nuclear launch sites.

04:25:50.490 --> 04:25:57.370
Not only this, but SCP-1984 also has direct
access to every single one of the atomic weapons

04:25:57.370 --> 04:26:03.210
stockpiled by the Soviet Union during the
Cold War, and is capable of launching Intercontinental

04:26:03.210 --> 04:26:06.601
Ballistic Missiles at a moment’s notice.

04:26:06.601 --> 04:26:14.930
In short, SCP-1984 could very easily and horrifyingly
quickly, trigger an all-out nuclear war, resulting

04:26:14.930 --> 04:26:18.211
in the extinction of all life on Earth.

04:26:18.211 --> 04:26:22.641
No wonder the Foundation considers the Dead
Hand such a massive threat.

04:26:22.641 --> 04:26:28.040
SCP-1984 itself actually consists of the preserved
remains of a Russian soldier by the name of

04:26:28.040 --> 04:26:34.090
Sergeant Marat Chernikov, who was killed during
the Soviet-Afghan War in 1982.

04:26:34.090 --> 04:26:38.140
Most of the official documentation of Chernikov’s
existence has been expunged by the Russian

04:26:38.140 --> 04:26:43.011
Federation, and he is only referenced in fragmented
documents recovered by the Foundation that

04:26:43.011 --> 04:26:45.551
refer to a ”Project December.”

04:26:45.551 --> 04:26:50.301
These remains serve as the location of a semi-sentient
consciousness that has been classified as

04:26:50.301 --> 04:26:52.010
SCP-1984-01.

04:26:52.010 --> 04:27:00.021
When it remains dormant and is not interfered
with, SCP-1984-01 has the ability to receive

04:27:00.021 --> 04:27:05.440
and process any signal broadcast to it, and
is able to decipher information contained

04:27:05.440 --> 04:27:07.260
in any signal it picks up.

04:27:07.260 --> 04:27:12.211
However, when global military tensions start
to climb, especially when those tensions affect

04:27:12.211 --> 04:27:16.971
the Russian Federation - or what were once
the satellite states of the former Soviet

04:27:16.971 --> 04:27:23.440
Union - the entity begins to manifest itself
in the physical world, and usually in various

04:27:23.440 --> 04:27:26.990
strange and differing ways.

04:27:26.990 --> 04:27:32.980
SCP-1984-01 has been known to appear in the
real world in forms such as a humanoid outline,

04:27:32.980 --> 04:27:38.061
or a bright-red specter, taking the shape
of a child with its legs cut off.

04:27:38.061 --> 04:27:42.280
Regardless of which shape it appears in, it
is when the Dead Hand manifests in a more

04:27:42.280 --> 04:27:46.641
physical form that the wider scope of its
abilities become clear.

04:27:46.641 --> 04:27:51.690
As mentioned previously, it can influence
and even launch nuclear weapons, overriding

04:27:51.690 --> 04:27:55.470
their command systems and bypassing launch
sequences.

04:27:55.470 --> 04:28:03.180
After appearing fully, SCP-1984-01 will travel
at speeds of up to 140 kilometers an hour,

04:28:03.180 --> 04:28:07.690
directly to the nearest military installation
capable of launching Intercontinental Ballistic

04:28:07.690 --> 04:28:08.801
Missiles.

04:28:08.801 --> 04:28:15.360
Once it reaches its destination, SCP-1984-01
will immediately attempt to override the necessary

04:28:15.360 --> 04:28:17.880
systems to initiate a launch.

04:28:17.880 --> 04:28:23.990
After firing missiles at their pre-determined
targets, SCP-1984-01 will hastily travel to

04:28:23.990 --> 04:28:29.091
another facility housing nuclear ordnance,
repeating the process until it has successfully

04:28:29.091 --> 04:28:31.720
launched all of Russia’s atomic weapons.

04:28:31.720 --> 04:28:38.261
When engaged, the physical manifestation of
SCP-1984 is highly aggressive, and will lethally

04:28:38.261 --> 04:28:42.980
defend itself against anyone that it observes
trying to interfere with it or stop it from

04:28:42.980 --> 04:28:45.271
causing a nuclear launch.

04:28:45.271 --> 04:28:50.640
The entity has displayed the ability to disrupt
the nervous system, causing excruciating pain

04:28:50.640 --> 04:28:53.631
and debilitating damage to human beings.

04:28:53.631 --> 04:28:58.780
Its only known weakness, if any, is a susceptibility
to microwave radiation.

04:28:58.780 --> 04:29:05.240
Although, exposure to this doesn’t seem
to cause any lasting damage to SCP-1984, instead

04:29:05.240 --> 04:29:09.101
only temporarily disorientating its physical
form.

04:29:09.101 --> 04:29:15.440
As for the origins of SCP-1984, the Soviet
Union’s official liaison with the SCP Foundation

04:29:15.440 --> 04:29:20.210
offered some clarity on this, ironically,
during early 1984.

04:29:20.210 --> 04:29:25.530
The liaison, a doctor named Sergei, described
information regarding the Dead Hand as being

04:29:25.530 --> 04:29:29.730
of “grave importance to the continued survival
of the human race”.

04:29:29.730 --> 04:29:33.860
Seeing as he was referring to an entity that
could single-handedly launch the Soviet Union’s

04:29:33.860 --> 04:29:37.160
entire nuclear arsenal, he certainly had a
point.

04:29:37.160 --> 04:29:41.910
A top-secret conference was held in Sarajevo
between the Foundation’s O5 Council and

04:29:41.910 --> 04:29:48.641
officials from both the USSR and United States,
using the 1984 Winter Olympics as cover, avoiding

04:29:48.641 --> 04:29:52.811
too many questions about several nations’
high-ranking state officials being in the

04:29:52.811 --> 04:29:54.220
same place at once.

04:29:54.220 --> 04:29:59.330
The O5 Council was then given full, in-depth
information about the Dead Hand, something

04:29:59.330 --> 04:30:04.271
they had previously assumed was a more conventional
form of nuclear deterrence.

04:30:04.271 --> 04:30:10.870
SCP-1984 was far more, and worse, far out
of the control of the Russian government.

04:30:10.870 --> 04:30:15.840
It was revealed that the entity had been designed
outside the original specifications given

04:30:15.840 --> 04:30:17.730
to those who developed it.

04:30:17.730 --> 04:30:23.120
Initially, the Soviets had intended for the
Dead Hand to be solely used as a secure second-strike

04:30:23.120 --> 04:30:24.210
response.

04:30:24.210 --> 04:30:30.260
If the leaders of the Soviet Union were killed,
SCP-1984 would react in-kind to Russia’s

04:30:30.260 --> 04:30:35.200
enemies, launching back all the USSR’s nuclear
missiles in retaliation.

04:30:35.200 --> 04:30:39.830
This is most likely where the “Dead Hand”
nickname comes from, hearkening to the idea

04:30:39.830 --> 04:30:42.001
of a “dead man’s switch.”

04:30:42.001 --> 04:30:45.990
Picture that you had been mortally wounded
by your worst enemy - shot in the stomach

04:30:45.990 --> 04:30:48.880
and laying on the ground, rapidly bleeding
out.

04:30:48.880 --> 04:30:52.870
You know that there is no chance you will
survive, but you cannot afford to let your

04:30:52.870 --> 04:30:54.141
enemy get away.

04:30:54.141 --> 04:30:59.791
What they don’t know is that you rigged
the entire building around you both with explosives.

04:30:59.791 --> 04:31:05.641
With your dying breath, you activate the detonator,
assuring your own and your enemy’s mutual

04:31:05.641 --> 04:31:06.641
destruction.

04:31:06.641 --> 04:31:09.390
Kaboom, then curtain for both of you.

04:31:09.390 --> 04:31:15.440
The pressing issue, and reason this secret
summit between the USSR, USA and SCP Foundation

04:31:15.440 --> 04:31:21.730
was held, was that SCP-1984 was no longer
interested in just waiting for Russia to be

04:31:21.730 --> 04:31:24.510
attacked and only reacting after the fact.

04:31:24.510 --> 04:31:29.220
Instead, the entity’s physical form was
trying to preemptively strike at the enemies

04:31:29.220 --> 04:31:33.990
of the Motherland, attempting to activate
nuclear launches and send atomic weapons to

04:31:33.990 --> 04:31:39.561
destroy the United States, France, West Germany,
and the People’s Republic of China.

04:31:39.561 --> 04:31:44.801
In other words, the Dead Hand was eager to
get a head start at causing total nuclear

04:31:44.801 --> 04:31:49.940
annihilation, not to mention potentially killing
millions and reducing target countries to

04:31:49.940 --> 04:31:55.600
little more than irradiated craters awash
with deadly nuclear fallout.

04:31:55.600 --> 04:32:00.830
Both the Soviet Union and United States begged
the SCP Foundation to intervene and contain

04:32:00.830 --> 04:32:07.200
SCP-1984, and under the direction of the O5
Council, they stepped in to take direct control

04:32:07.200 --> 04:32:13.450
of the situation, establishing new containment
procedures in the hopes of keeping SCP-1984

04:32:13.450 --> 04:32:16.370
from hitting as many launch buttons as it
could find.

04:32:16.370 --> 04:32:20.670
The embalmed remains that seemed to create
the manifestations of the Dead Hand entity

04:32:20.670 --> 04:32:25.930
were held securely in an Armed Containment
Complex, near Verkhoyansk, part of the Sakha

04:32:25.930 --> 04:32:28.410
Republic within the Russian Federation.

04:32:28.410 --> 04:32:33.990
SCP-1984 was placed within a standard humanoid
containment cell, which was itself held within

04:32:33.990 --> 04:32:39.960
a Faraday cage - a type of enclosure constructed
with or covered in conductive material, designed

04:32:39.960 --> 04:32:42.450
to block electromagnetic fields.

04:32:42.450 --> 04:32:48.720
This was done to block any external broadcast
signals from reaching SCP-1984, and thus causing

04:32:48.720 --> 04:32:53.561
it to manifest its other form if it learned
of an impending attack on Russia - even a

04:32:53.561 --> 04:32:57.510
fictional one, perhaps as part of a television
broadcast.

04:32:57.510 --> 04:33:01.370
As part of the Dead Hand’s containment,
all signals broadcast near its cage are to

04:33:01.370 --> 04:33:06.500
be monitored, and only broadcasts featuring
doctored information would reach the entity.

04:33:06.500 --> 04:33:12.689
Thanks to the work of the SCP Foundation’s
Information Control Team, SCP-1984 is drip-fed

04:33:12.689 --> 04:33:15.680
a stream of carefully-fabricated information.

04:33:15.680 --> 04:33:21.109
Using on-site equipment and facilities, a
team of military historians, economists, actors,

04:33:21.109 --> 04:33:26.389
and Soviet media specialists, the Information
Control Team have created an ongoing narrative

04:33:26.389 --> 04:33:28.760
wherein the Cold War never ended.

04:33:28.760 --> 04:33:35.039
Through falsified radio and television broadcasts
made to look like era-appropriate news organizations,

04:33:35.039 --> 04:33:40.939
they manage to keep SCP-1984 convinced that
the nuclear stalemate between the Soviet Union

04:33:40.939 --> 04:33:44.080
and United States is still ongoing.

04:33:44.080 --> 04:33:48.869
Unfortunately, sometimes information from
the real world is able to bleed through.

04:33:48.869 --> 04:33:55.340
An incident involving SCP-1984 occurred on
August 8th, 1984, and almost brought forth

04:33:55.340 --> 04:33:57.318
a full-scale nuclear war.

04:33:57.318 --> 04:34:01.859
While preparing for a campaign speech, the
fortieth President of the United States Ronald

04:34:01.859 --> 04:34:06.469
Reagan uttered the following joke: “I'm
pleased to tell you today that I've signed

04:34:06.469 --> 04:34:12.061
legislation that will outlaw Russia forever,
we begin bombing in five minutes.”

04:34:12.061 --> 04:34:17.148
Naturally, thousands of media outlets reported
on this, but signals of those broadcasts,

04:34:17.148 --> 04:34:22.680
including recordings of the President’s
remark, made their way to SCP-1984.

04:34:22.680 --> 04:34:26.309
Foundation researchers were both unsure of
how these transmissions breached the Faraday

04:34:26.309 --> 04:34:31.799
cage surrounding the Dead Hand, and were unable
to prevent what happened next.

04:34:31.799 --> 04:34:36.469
Hearing what it could only assume was a genuine
declaration of war, the manifestation of the

04:34:36.469 --> 04:34:44.170
SCP-1984-01 entity happened immediately after
Reagan’s words reached its containment cell.

04:34:44.170 --> 04:34:49.949
This time, the entity appeared as a semi-transparent
woman, withered and blue, wearing traditional

04:34:49.949 --> 04:34:51.730
Pashtun dress.

04:34:51.730 --> 04:34:57.680
Armed personnel guarding SCP-1984’s cage
engaged the entity, causing it to retaliate,

04:34:57.680 --> 04:35:00.930
lashing out and attacking any that stood in
its way.

04:35:00.930 --> 04:35:05.709
One captain and two privates that suffered
the brunt of SCP-1984’s offensive capabilities

04:35:05.709 --> 04:35:09.629
began bleeding heavily from their ears, seizing
violently.

04:35:09.629 --> 04:35:14.389
Most gruesomely of all, a liquid leaked from
their eyes and nose, believed to have been

04:35:14.389 --> 04:35:15.830
cerebrospinal fluid.

04:35:15.830 --> 04:35:20.369
While armed personnel attempted to utilize
microwave emitting weaponry to slow the entity

04:35:20.369 --> 04:35:26.078
down, the Information Control Team was frantically
trying to record a new falsified broadcast

04:35:26.078 --> 04:35:31.729
in the hopes that SCP-1984 would cease its
hostilities and the entity would dissipate

04:35:31.729 --> 04:35:36.398
before it was able to travel at high speed
to any nearby Soviet nuclear facilities and

04:35:36.398 --> 04:35:39.260
begin bombarding the United States.

04:35:39.260 --> 04:35:44.760
Their first attempt to record a new broadcast
that would result in a cessation of SCP-1984’s

04:35:44.760 --> 04:35:49.000
slaughter of its guards was interrupted when
a nearby wall collapsed.

04:35:49.000 --> 04:35:53.420
Desperate to re-contain the creature, Information
Control Team tried to film the broadcast a

04:35:53.420 --> 04:35:58.010
second time, and succeeded, although one of
the actors portraying a newsreader suffered

04:35:58.010 --> 04:36:03.729
a stroke and had to be edited out, to convince
the Dead Hand of its supposed authenticity.

04:36:03.729 --> 04:36:08.359
What followed was a short news clip, clarifying
that Russia’s Politburo was in on President

04:36:08.359 --> 04:36:12.908
Reagan’s joke, including old footage of
the USSR’s General Secretary Konstantin

04:36:12.908 --> 04:36:18.670
Chernenko confirming that the Soviet Union’s
nuclear forces were not on high alert.

04:36:18.670 --> 04:36:25.139
Miraculously, after fifteen more minutes of
sustained fighting with guards, SCP-1984’s

04:36:25.139 --> 04:36:30.109
physical manifestation began to disappear,
gradually dematerializing while it seemed

04:36:30.109 --> 04:36:32.869
to attack with far-less intensity.

04:36:32.869 --> 04:36:37.139
Eventually, containment was re-established,
at the cost of the deaths of seventeen members

04:36:37.139 --> 04:36:40.549
of Foundation staff, both guards and researchers.

04:36:40.549 --> 04:36:45.609
A further eight, however, suffered traumatic
brain injuries that left them all permanently

04:36:45.609 --> 04:36:46.609
disabled.

04:36:46.609 --> 04:36:52.270
The one upside is that this incident remains
the only time SCP-1984 has ever breached its

04:36:52.270 --> 04:36:57.170
containment and caused harm to others, and
considering that it could very well have launched

04:36:57.170 --> 04:37:01.260
Russia’s nuclear arsenal, the casualties
could easily have been much higher.

04:37:01.260 --> 04:37:07.318
So remember, folks, don’t joke about nuclear
weapons, especially if you’re the president.

04:37:07.318 --> 04:37:12.740
You never know what anomalies lurking in the
bodies of dead Russian soldiers might be listening,

04:37:12.740 --> 04:37:17.000
and if they are, you better hope they have
a sense of humor.

04:37:17.000 --> 04:37:20.199
You’ve been walking for days.

04:37:20.199 --> 04:37:25.408
Your body aches, you’re dripping with sweat
from the heat of the sun bearing down overhead.

04:37:25.408 --> 04:37:31.299
And yet, you’re wrapped up in layers upon
layers of clothing - even your face is covered,

04:37:31.299 --> 04:37:36.250
and you’re wearing thick, black goggles
so that not a single centimeter of your body

04:37:36.250 --> 04:37:37.729
is exposed.

04:37:37.729 --> 04:37:43.049
Your journey has been long and you feel like
you might die from exhaustion, or from overheating

04:37:43.049 --> 04:37:45.738
due to these multiple layers of clothes.

04:37:45.738 --> 04:37:48.740
But dying is better than being exposed.

04:37:48.740 --> 04:37:53.209
You saw it happen when your entire team...changed.

04:37:53.209 --> 04:37:55.809
The light can’t be trusted.

04:37:55.809 --> 04:37:58.869
Not even for a fraction of a second.

04:37:58.869 --> 04:38:00.629
It’s been like this for years.

04:38:00.629 --> 04:38:04.658
You’ve learned and survived through painful
experience.

04:38:04.658 --> 04:38:07.488
Many of those you used to know cannot say
the same.

04:38:07.488 --> 04:38:10.709
You’ve been alone for so long.

04:38:10.709 --> 04:38:15.529
You might have given up all hope, if it wasn’t
for the distress signal coming from a nearby

04:38:15.529 --> 04:38:20.789
SCP Foundation Containment Facility - Site-46.

04:38:20.789 --> 04:38:25.600
Any kind of survivors would be better than
nothing, no matter what kind of sorry shape

04:38:25.600 --> 04:38:26.729
they were in.

04:38:26.729 --> 04:38:29.859
As long as they were still human.

04:38:29.859 --> 04:38:35.119
You find your way to an opening in the side
of a mountain, and slide into the cave, hoping

04:38:35.119 --> 04:38:36.809
you weren’t spotted.

04:38:36.809 --> 04:38:40.080
The whole world is crawling with those things
now.

04:38:40.080 --> 04:38:42.680
You can’t let yourself be seen.

04:38:42.680 --> 04:38:48.109
As you trudge down the cave towards the entrance,
you see what looks like a huge, black snail-trail

04:38:48.109 --> 04:38:51.990
splattered on the ground, leading into the
facility.

04:38:51.990 --> 04:38:53.828
You try to avoid it and press on.

04:38:53.828 --> 04:38:59.400
You don’t even need a keycard to enter:
The door has been left ajar.

04:38:59.400 --> 04:39:03.730
The facility reeks of those things, but you
can’t see any of them.

04:39:03.730 --> 04:39:08.398
You just hope they’ve moved on and left
some human survivors in their wake.

04:39:08.398 --> 04:39:10.350
The place looks abandoned.

04:39:10.350 --> 04:39:14.459
Every step you take echoes through the empty
halls.

04:39:14.459 --> 04:39:18.719
When you find that the elevator’s out, you
take the stairs all the way down to Level

04:39:18.719 --> 04:39:19.719
B5…

04:39:19.719 --> 04:39:20.910
Keter Containment.

04:39:20.910 --> 04:39:26.779
Lucky for you, it seems all the cells are
empty now, the horrors that were kept inside

04:39:26.779 --> 04:39:29.658
of them have all long since flown the coop.

04:39:29.658 --> 04:39:35.279
You keep following that slimy, black trail
until you find an abandoned office.

04:39:35.279 --> 04:39:41.148
There are no people here anymore - just a
broken barricade, some empty medicine bottles,

04:39:41.148 --> 04:39:46.240
and a bucket that the people inside the office
had apparently been using as a toilet.

04:39:46.240 --> 04:39:51.558
You breathe a sigh of disappointment at finding
no one alive here, but you’re at least relieved

04:39:51.558 --> 04:39:53.110
to be out of the sun.

04:39:53.110 --> 04:39:56.398
You can finally remove your jacket and head-wrap.

04:39:56.398 --> 04:40:00.910
With your uncovered eyes, you notice that
a nearby computer terminal is still powered

04:40:00.910 --> 04:40:01.910
up.

04:40:01.910 --> 04:40:04.490
You sit down at the desk and turn on the monitor.

04:40:04.490 --> 04:40:10.040
Because of the Emergency Procedures put into
place in a K-Class scenario like this, safeguards

04:40:10.040 --> 04:40:11.620
no longer apply.

04:40:11.620 --> 04:40:17.660
You can access all the information you need
- up to and including finding out what actually

04:40:17.660 --> 04:40:18.660
happened.

04:40:18.660 --> 04:40:23.170
In the dull glow of a nearby emergency light,
you see a dark shape slumping through the

04:40:23.170 --> 04:40:24.840
halls in shadow.

04:40:24.840 --> 04:40:29.378
You tense up, then exhale as it slithers off
into an adjoining hall.

04:40:29.378 --> 04:40:31.590
You’re safe - for now.

04:40:31.590 --> 04:40:35.430
The terminal has finally loaded and authenticated
your access.

04:40:35.430 --> 04:40:37.850
You’re staring at the file for S.D.

04:40:37.850 --> 04:40:42.310
Locke’s Proposal for SCP-001: When Day Breaks.

04:40:42.310 --> 04:40:48.020
It’s the only name you can give the apocalypse
your world is currently experiencing.

04:40:48.020 --> 04:40:53.200
This is one of the only anomalies in the entire
history of the SCP Foundation to be given

04:40:53.200 --> 04:40:59.270
the Apollyon containment class - meaning containment
is truly impossible.

04:40:59.270 --> 04:41:06.378
SCP-001 is the most dangerous enemy that the
Foundation, and planet earth, has ever faced.

04:41:06.378 --> 04:41:11.030
It’s always been a principle of the SCP
Foundation to battle in the dark so that the

04:41:11.030 --> 04:41:17.148
civilian world can thrive in the light, but
now, the light has become the enemy.

04:41:17.148 --> 04:41:21.958
Anyone exposed to any amount of sunlight for
even the briefest period of time is subjected

04:41:21.958 --> 04:41:28.620
to the effects of SCP-001 - and those effects
are beyond horrifying.

04:41:28.620 --> 04:41:33.240
The SCP Foundation Administrator released
an urgent memo telling Foundation personnel

04:41:33.240 --> 04:41:39.260
to make their way to Site-19 at all costs,
because they need all the help they can get.

04:41:39.260 --> 04:41:45.308
Those exposed to SCP-001 in the process are
no longer considered human - their new designation

04:41:45.308 --> 04:41:52.638
is SCP-001-A. These new entities are to be
avoided at all costs.

04:41:52.638 --> 04:41:58.331
But, in case of emergencies, the Administrator
says it is permitted to cut off parts of your

04:41:58.331 --> 04:42:02.290
transformed comrades and eat them to avoid
starvation.

04:42:02.290 --> 04:42:08.090
No attempt should be made to kill them, since
you won’t succeed, you’ll just put yourself

04:42:08.090 --> 04:42:09.090
at risk.

04:42:09.090 --> 04:42:16.390
When the sun changed and became SCP-001, it
instantly affected 6.8 billion innocent people.

04:42:16.390 --> 04:42:20.500
The second the visible light touched them
- whether it was from the sun itself or even

04:42:20.500 --> 04:42:27.370
reflected off the moon - their bodies liquefied,
melting like candle wax into puddles of living,

04:42:27.370 --> 04:42:28.810
gelatinous slime.

04:42:28.810 --> 04:42:34.360
This effect isn’t isolated to humans, either:
Any biological entity exposed to sunlight

04:42:34.360 --> 04:42:40.520
immediately underwent the same irreversible
melting process into SCP-001-A.

04:42:40.520 --> 04:42:45.658
And the horror had only just begun.

04:42:45.658 --> 04:42:51.930
People transformed into SCP-001-A will retain
shades of their former intelligence and personality.

04:42:51.930 --> 04:42:57.640
They may even try to will their new gooey
mass into a shape resembling their original

04:42:57.640 --> 04:42:58.640
form.

04:42:58.640 --> 04:43:02.658
However, these individuals will lose their
sense of self if they come into contact with

04:43:02.658 --> 04:43:11.798
other instances of SCP-001-A. When they come
together, 001-A instances will bond on a molecular

04:43:11.798 --> 04:43:18.388
level, wadding up into horrific, giant blobs
with only one purpose: Integrating more matter

04:43:18.388 --> 04:43:19.530
into their bodies.

04:43:19.530 --> 04:43:23.878
That’s why they have to be avoided at all
costs.

04:43:23.878 --> 04:43:27.378
You continue to search the computer terminal
for answers.

04:43:27.378 --> 04:43:30.878
Perhaps there was some kind of contingency
plan put in place for this.

04:43:30.878 --> 04:43:36.128
Some way to reverse the effects, or at least
escape the nightmare Earth has become.

04:43:36.128 --> 04:43:42.398
Instead, you find a series of attachments
linked to the SCP-001 file, detailing what

04:43:42.398 --> 04:43:47.080
seems to be the last days of the people who’d
barricaded themselves in the facility.

04:43:47.080 --> 04:43:52.720
Most prominent among these were Researcher
Dr. Logan Igotta, her partner, Ari, a security

04:43:52.720 --> 04:43:55.700
officer named Commander Anand, and a few others.

04:43:55.700 --> 04:44:01.500
Dr. Igotta had locked herself in the office,
where she recorded her final messages to the

04:44:01.500 --> 04:44:02.500
world.

04:44:02.500 --> 04:44:07.370
In the first audio log, Dr. Igotta and her
companions seemed afraid but hopeful that

04:44:07.370 --> 04:44:09.980
there may be some way out of this situation.

04:44:09.980 --> 04:44:14.821
Dr. Igotta reported that most of the workers
at the facility were transformed during the

04:44:14.821 --> 04:44:16.020
initial event.

04:44:16.020 --> 04:44:21.110
Their melted bodies had fused outside the
facility, and now they were trying to bust

04:44:21.110 --> 04:44:22.790
their way back in.

04:44:22.790 --> 04:44:27.260
The defenses had held so far though, and they
seemed confident they would hold long enough

04:44:27.260 --> 04:44:31.208
for them to figure out a way to escape this
awful situation.

04:44:31.208 --> 04:44:36.370
You open the second attachment - an incident
report - and realize that things may not have

04:44:36.370 --> 04:44:39.170
been as hopeful as Dr. Igotta let on.

04:44:39.170 --> 04:44:44.398
She reported hearing the huge mass of melted
creatures hammering on the door outside again,

04:44:44.398 --> 04:44:47.920
begging for them to come out and experience
the sun with them.

04:44:47.920 --> 04:44:51.840
They wanted desperately to add to their ever-growing
biomass.

04:44:51.840 --> 04:44:56.840
In order to experiment with what exactly would
happen, they sent out one of their few remaining

04:44:56.840 --> 04:44:59.870
D-Classes wearing a full protective suit.

04:44:59.870 --> 04:45:01.750
He didn’t last long.

04:45:01.750 --> 04:45:05.840
The huge creature grabbed him with tentacles
made of reconstituted flesh.

04:45:05.840 --> 04:45:10.090
It began ripping off his protective suit as
he screamed for mercy.

04:45:10.090 --> 04:45:13.760
It was a monster made of dozens of people
and animals.

04:45:13.760 --> 04:45:15.978
He could never overpower it.

04:45:15.978 --> 04:45:21.780
The second the sun touched his skin, he melted
away, and was absorbed by the great mass holding

04:45:21.780 --> 04:45:23.238
him in place.

04:45:23.238 --> 04:45:28.700
Guns were ineffective against these SCP-001-A
super-entities.

04:45:28.700 --> 04:45:30.420
Fire would do no good.

04:45:30.420 --> 04:45:35.298
It seemed that extremely low temperatures
were the only way to slow the immense blobs

04:45:35.298 --> 04:45:39.200
down, and even then, not permanently.

04:45:39.200 --> 04:45:44.430
There was one ray of light in the darkness:
The Site Director had a secret tunnel underneath

04:45:44.430 --> 04:45:49.451
his office, connected to a tram that could
hopefully take them directly to Site 19 without

04:45:49.451 --> 04:45:50.818
risk of SCP-001 exposure.

04:45:50.818 --> 04:45:57.020
It was a good plan, and by far the best option
they had available to them.

04:45:57.020 --> 04:46:01.128
But the best plans often don’t work in practice.

04:46:01.128 --> 04:46:03.638
You open the next attachment on the terminal.

04:46:03.638 --> 04:46:05.930
This time, it’s a video feed.

04:46:05.930 --> 04:46:11.228
You can actually see Dr. Logan Igotta - and
she looks harrowed by what she’s experienced.

04:46:11.228 --> 04:46:15.629
As it turns out, while the others, including
her partner Ari, attempted to exit through

04:46:15.629 --> 04:46:18.200
the tunnel something had happened.

04:46:18.200 --> 04:46:21.450
Dr. Igotta heard Ari’s voice over her radio.

04:46:21.450 --> 04:46:23.190
But there was something wrong with it.

04:46:23.190 --> 04:46:24.378
It was too low.

04:46:24.378 --> 04:46:25.860
Too guttural.

04:46:25.860 --> 04:46:27.260
And filled with gurgles.

04:46:27.260 --> 04:46:30.578
SCP-001 had gotten to her.

04:46:30.578 --> 04:46:31.870
She was changed.

04:46:31.870 --> 04:46:34.700
The monster from above had crawled in through
the ceiling.

04:46:34.700 --> 04:46:41.410
It had taken them, all of them, and converted
them into something less than human.

04:46:41.410 --> 04:46:44.670
Any hope of escape now seemed gone.

04:46:44.670 --> 04:46:47.138
Ari told Dr. Igotta that it would be fine.

04:46:47.138 --> 04:46:51.988
That it was such a bright, beautiful, sunny
day outside, and she was wasting it locked

04:46:51.988 --> 04:46:53.888
up inside that office.

04:46:53.888 --> 04:46:58.920
She tormented Dr. Igotta with their shared
memories of picnics in the park on sunny days

04:46:58.920 --> 04:47:00.120
in the past.

04:47:00.120 --> 04:47:04.468
The monster with Ari’s voice did everything
it could to try to convince Dr. Igotta to

04:47:04.468 --> 04:47:09.040
give up and join them, but she wasn’t ready
to go just yet.

04:47:09.040 --> 04:47:12.658
You look away from the screen when you hear
a sound in the corner.

04:47:12.658 --> 04:47:18.150
You see a dark puddle of some unknown substance,
and then, some skeletal hands rising out of

04:47:18.150 --> 04:47:19.150
it.

04:47:19.150 --> 04:47:23.270
The hands are pulling themselves out of the
puddle, followed by a skeletal face covered

04:47:23.270 --> 04:47:24.680
in matted hair.

04:47:24.680 --> 04:47:28.930
You have to stop yourself from screaming,
until a flash from a nearby security light

04:47:28.930 --> 04:47:30.520
makes the figure disappear.

04:47:30.520 --> 04:47:33.478
It’s a normal puddle again.

04:47:33.478 --> 04:47:35.760
Your mind is playing tricks on you.

04:47:35.760 --> 04:47:41.510
You open the next attachment, another video,
and see that Dr. Igotta’s condition has

04:47:41.510 --> 04:47:42.510
deteriorated.

04:47:42.510 --> 04:47:45.010
She looked pale, frantic, and thin.

04:47:45.010 --> 04:47:49.738
She was using a knife to draw her own blood
onto a piece of bloodstained parchment covered

04:47:49.738 --> 04:47:51.490
in strange symbols.

04:47:51.490 --> 04:47:56.908
Igotta ranted about her theory: What if 001
took the minds and bodies of its victims,

04:47:56.908 --> 04:47:58.430
but not their souls?

04:47:58.430 --> 04:48:03.158
Through performing some kind of arcane blood
ritual, she hoped to at least rescue and keep

04:48:03.158 --> 04:48:07.238
the soul of Ari, even if her mind and body
were lost.

04:48:07.238 --> 04:48:09.120
You open the next attachment.

04:48:09.120 --> 04:48:13.218
It seems that Igotta’s ritual worked, but
not in the way she hoped.

04:48:13.218 --> 04:48:18.770
The twisted soul of Ari, driven mad by SCP-001,
had taken over the file.

04:48:18.770 --> 04:48:24.510
It begins corrupting the text of the SCP-001
file into crazy ranting about how futile it

04:48:24.510 --> 04:48:25.520
is to fight.

04:48:25.520 --> 04:48:31.890
It then cut to an even more frightening video
feed: Dr. Igotta in her sleep, tossing and

04:48:31.890 --> 04:48:35.090
turning in a makeshift bed in the corner of
her office.

04:48:35.090 --> 04:48:40.328
The camera approaches her, in first person,
and lingers over her sleeping body.

04:48:40.328 --> 04:48:46.648
An oily, skeletal hand reaches past the camera,
and runs its fingers through Dr. Igotta’s

04:48:46.648 --> 04:48:47.648
hair.

04:48:47.648 --> 04:48:51.850
It’s the exact same hand you saw reaching
out of that black puddle earlier.

04:48:51.850 --> 04:48:55.110
You must have seen Ari’s lingering spirit.

04:48:55.110 --> 04:48:59.900
With a lump in your throat, you open the next
attachment and watch the video.

04:48:59.900 --> 04:49:03.410
You see Dr. Igotta, now truly broken.

04:49:03.410 --> 04:49:08.808
She’d been haunted by Ari’s demonic spirit
for a long time now, and it has clearly taken

04:49:08.808 --> 04:49:09.850
its toll.

04:49:09.850 --> 04:49:12.648
She is waving around a handgun while she speaks.

04:49:12.648 --> 04:49:15.180
She now believes there is only one way to
escape.

04:49:15.180 --> 04:49:17.158
But not like this.

04:49:17.158 --> 04:49:20.170
She doesn’t want the gun to draw attention
to her body.

04:49:20.170 --> 04:49:24.190
She doesn’t want to become part of that
mass, even if she is dead.

04:49:24.190 --> 04:49:28.818
She opens a drawer on the desk she’s recording
at and places the gun inside.

04:49:28.818 --> 04:49:34.888
Dr. Igotta then apologizes to her loved ones
who are likely long since dead or assimilated,

04:49:34.888 --> 04:49:37.958
and turns off the recording for the last time.

04:49:37.958 --> 04:49:42.620
In that moment, you realize that there’s
a single drawer in the desk in front of you.

04:49:42.620 --> 04:49:47.520
When you reach forward and open it, you see
that the same handgun Dr. Igotta was holding

04:49:47.520 --> 04:49:49.318
is laying inside.

04:49:49.318 --> 04:49:53.030
You pick it up and study it, weighing up your
options.

04:49:53.030 --> 04:49:55.500
Perhaps there truly is no other way out...

04:49:55.500 --> 04:49:57.988
Then, you see an update on the file.

04:49:57.988 --> 04:50:01.230
One more attachment had been added while you
were studying the gun.

04:50:01.230 --> 04:50:06.480
You feel your heart pounding in your chest
as you reach forward and open the attachment.

04:50:06.480 --> 04:50:08.860
The text has been changed entirely.

04:50:08.860 --> 04:50:16.628
The file on SCP-001 is now a poem - an ode
to the sun, and to ultimate togetherness.

04:50:16.628 --> 04:50:23.558
Then a video file spontaneously opens itself
on the screen: It’s a video of you, shot

04:50:23.558 --> 04:50:24.828
from behind.

04:50:24.828 --> 04:50:30.610
You see those oily, skeletal hands reaching
for you in the dark, just like they did with

04:50:30.610 --> 04:50:31.610
Dr. Igotta.

04:50:31.610 --> 04:50:36.740
In that moment, you panic and fire the gun
behind you, hoping to scare off the spirit.

04:50:36.740 --> 04:50:40.940
Instead, the sound of the gunshots attracts
something far worse.

04:50:40.940 --> 04:50:45.270
The immense blob of screaming, melted flesh
charges towards the office.

04:50:45.270 --> 04:50:47.990
You try to barricade the door, but it’s
not enough.

04:50:47.990 --> 04:50:52.550
The flesh seeps and bursts through, and grabs
you in its meaty tentacles.

04:50:52.550 --> 04:50:57.290
You scream and try to escape, but it won’t
save you.

04:50:57.290 --> 04:50:59.048
Nothing will save you.

04:50:59.048 --> 04:51:04.138
The flesh carries you upstairs, out through
the empty halls, out into the cave.

04:51:04.138 --> 04:51:07.558
You can see the light in the distance as the
blob ferries you towards it.

04:51:07.558 --> 04:51:10.100
You won’t be alone for much longer.

04:51:10.100 --> 04:51:14.370
In fact, you won’t be alone ever again...

04:51:14.370 --> 04:51:21.058
It’s a natural instinct in many species
to protect their young - and sometimes it's

04:51:21.058 --> 04:51:25.808
not just their own babies, but any young that
look like them.

04:51:25.808 --> 04:51:31.040
Regardless of your personal feelings on human’s
earliest stage, it is a scientific fact that

04:51:31.040 --> 04:51:36.340
human babies are designed to emphasize their
own adorable helplessness to make sure that

04:51:36.340 --> 04:51:39.000
other, older humans take care of them.

04:51:39.000 --> 04:51:44.790
A baby’s cry is an inherently distressing
sound, and when we hear it, some deep, primal

04:51:44.790 --> 04:51:50.468
part of us feels the urge to comfort and care
for the child until the sound stops.

04:51:50.468 --> 04:51:55.150
But of course, we’re talking about the world
of the SCP Foundation here - where there are

04:51:55.150 --> 04:51:59.898
bunnies that can eat anything, teddy bears
that might steal your organs to make duplicates

04:51:59.898 --> 04:52:05.708
of themselves, and chocolate fountains filled
with trillions of murderous insects.

04:52:05.708 --> 04:52:10.870
Nothing is what it seems here, and even the
most innocent and cute creatures may be hiding

04:52:10.870 --> 04:52:15.660
a deadly secret - SCP-734 being no exception.

04:52:15.660 --> 04:52:18.810
Today, we’re talking about The Baby.

04:52:18.810 --> 04:52:24.090
This anomaly proves that dangerous things
can come in small packages, but where others

04:52:24.090 --> 04:52:30.640
only saw misery and death, the SCP Foundation
saw a certain potential…

04:52:30.640 --> 04:52:35.480
Our story begins in the maternity ward of
a hospital in the USA, where every medical

04:52:35.480 --> 04:52:40.950
professional’s worst nightmare was unfolding:
An unknown but incredibly fast-acting flesh-eating

04:52:40.950 --> 04:52:45.378
pathogen seemed to be running rampant across
the hospital’s population.

04:52:45.378 --> 04:52:49.398
It began when patients who weren’t even
admitted for dermatological issues started

04:52:49.398 --> 04:52:53.318
complaining of severe itches and extreme skin
pain.

04:52:53.318 --> 04:52:58.228
Some nurses and doctors in the maternity ward
began to experience similar symptoms, as well

04:52:58.228 --> 04:53:02.160
as one of the infants, leading to a massive
quarantine effort.

04:53:02.160 --> 04:53:06.628
While the initial symptoms first appeared
to be limited to severe pain and discomfort

04:53:06.628 --> 04:53:11.700
on isolated parts of the skin, the condition
of the afflicted soon escalated.

04:53:11.700 --> 04:53:17.048
Their skin began to messily flake off as the
cells comprising it lost physical cohesion

04:53:17.048 --> 04:53:18.138
and died.

04:53:18.138 --> 04:53:23.810
It was a kind of strange, anomalous rot that
seemed to work inwards, first destroying the

04:53:23.810 --> 04:53:28.890
integrity of the outer layer of skin and then
causing further disintegration to deeper parts

04:53:28.890 --> 04:53:30.128
of the body.

04:53:30.128 --> 04:53:36.128
Once the skin had shed off, the pathogen would
turn its attention to what was lying beneath.

04:53:36.128 --> 04:53:42.208
Against all odds, the disease affected organs,
muscle tissue, the vascular system, and even

04:53:42.208 --> 04:53:43.920
bones.

04:53:43.920 --> 04:53:45.520
Nothing was spared.

04:53:45.520 --> 04:53:49.920
The victims’ bodies would completely break
down, and they would be dead within a few

04:53:49.920 --> 04:53:51.190
hours.

04:53:51.190 --> 04:53:55.680
By the time the pathogen had finished ravaging
its victims, what was left didn’t even look

04:53:55.680 --> 04:53:57.308
human anymore.

04:53:57.308 --> 04:54:02.478
Not only patients but doctors and nurses that
had been walking the wards mere hours before

04:54:02.478 --> 04:54:06.878
were now little more than piles of human tissue
sitting in what had previously been their

04:54:06.878 --> 04:54:08.620
hospital beds.

04:54:08.620 --> 04:54:14.708
Whatever this was, it seemed like the fastest
progressing infection in recorded history.

04:54:14.708 --> 04:54:20.650
Hospital staff and administrators were terrified
- this appeared to be an entirely new disease,

04:54:20.650 --> 04:54:25.728
with a mysterious form of transmission and,
worst of all, no cure.

04:54:25.728 --> 04:54:30.318
They were even more confused when several
black vans pulled up outside the hospital,

04:54:30.318 --> 04:54:34.638
and mysterious men in hazmat suits spilled
out and began setting up a quarantine zone

04:54:34.638 --> 04:54:36.658
around the entire building.

04:54:36.658 --> 04:54:41.648
Whoever these strange people were, they definitely
weren’t the CDC - little did the hospital

04:54:41.648 --> 04:54:46.230
personnel know that this was the group you
never want showing up and putting your location

04:54:46.230 --> 04:54:48.700
on lockdown - it was the SCP Foundation.

04:54:48.700 --> 04:54:54.910
The infected remains of the victims were taken
away for research purposes, and the Foundation

04:54:54.910 --> 04:54:59.440
operatives immediately began conducting debriefing
interviews with witnesses.

04:54:59.440 --> 04:55:04.350
They soon determined from a mix of eyewitness
accounts and hospital surveillance footage

04:55:04.350 --> 04:55:08.920
that everyone infected with the mysterious
pathogen had all been in a particular section

04:55:08.920 --> 04:55:11.400
of the maternity ward earlier in the day.

04:55:11.400 --> 04:55:16.798
And when the operatives investigated this
area, they found another strange detail.

04:55:16.798 --> 04:55:21.180
An infant had no registered mother present
in the hospital.

04:55:21.180 --> 04:55:25.170
The Foundation would later learn that this
was likely because the baby’s mother was

04:55:25.170 --> 04:55:28.160
the first victim of the deadly disease.

04:55:28.160 --> 04:55:33.440
After eliminating all other possible options,
it seemed that the only anomalous element

04:55:33.440 --> 04:55:38.250
that could have caused all of this was the
mysterious baby, though just how the mother

04:55:38.250 --> 04:55:43.480
even survived carrying the baby to term was
a mystery in and of itself.

04:55:43.480 --> 04:55:48.590
The baby was a caucasian male human infant
between seven and eight months of age.

04:55:48.590 --> 04:55:52.930
Nothing appeared outwardly anomalous about
the child, but they could confirm that every

04:55:52.930 --> 04:55:57.478
single victim of the anomalous pathogen had
come into physical contact with the child

04:55:57.478 --> 04:55:59.370
earlier that day.

04:55:59.370 --> 04:56:03.350
Everyone who had been at the hospital was
given amnestic treatment, and the Foundation

04:56:03.350 --> 04:56:07.500
constructed plausible cover stories for the
deaths that had occurred that day.

04:56:07.500 --> 04:56:12.670
Like so many others before it, the child was
secured and spirited away to the nearest applicable

04:56:12.670 --> 04:56:14.780
Foundation containment site.

04:56:14.780 --> 04:56:20.840
There it was reclassified as SCP-734, and
finally the real testing into what precisely

04:56:20.840 --> 04:56:24.030
this infant was capable of could begin.

04:56:24.030 --> 04:56:28.628
Physiologically, SCP-734 appeared mostly non-anomalous.

04:56:28.628 --> 04:56:33.378
The infant had above-average intelligence
and physical aptitude for a child his age

04:56:33.378 --> 04:56:38.440
but otherwise showed no mutations or abnormalities
that would suggest a divergence from typical

04:56:38.440 --> 04:56:40.200
human biology.

04:56:40.200 --> 04:56:44.548
Despite a vast array of tests performed by
the Foundation into essentially every aspect

04:56:44.548 --> 04:56:49.990
of 734’s biology, they couldn’t find anything
that hinted at the origin of the mysterious

04:56:49.990 --> 04:56:51.170
pathogen.

04:56:51.170 --> 04:56:56.708
But through some trial and extremely costly
error, the Foundation was able to learn more

04:56:56.708 --> 04:56:59.478
about how exactly the pathogen worked.

04:56:59.478 --> 04:57:04.228
The only vector for transmission seemed to
be direct contact with the baby itself, up

04:57:04.228 --> 04:57:08.378
to and including the fluids and residues it
leaves behind.

04:57:08.378 --> 04:57:12.479
Those affected cannot transmit the anomalous
“flaking” effect to others, meaning that

04:57:12.479 --> 04:57:15.590
the risk of an epidemic is relievingly minimal.

04:57:15.590 --> 04:57:20.488
But of course, accidents still happen, as
was discovered when one agent misplaced her

04:57:20.488 --> 04:57:25.450
sympathy for the baby and decided to remove
her mask while interacting with him.

04:57:25.450 --> 04:57:30.500
Her logic was that her masked face might have
caused the baby some kind of distress, and

04:57:30.500 --> 04:57:35.700
as long as she was only coming into contact
with him via her own gloved hands, everything

04:57:35.700 --> 04:57:36.930
would be fine.

04:57:36.930 --> 04:57:42.870
But some dust particles were floating in the
air at the time, and SCP-734 sneezed in her

04:57:42.870 --> 04:57:43.870
face.

04:57:43.870 --> 04:57:49.000
The agent began screaming in pain and recoiling
from the baby, but it was already too late.

04:57:49.000 --> 04:57:50.978
Her fate was sealed.

04:57:50.978 --> 04:57:55.138
She was taken to the infirmary and given sedatives
so that she could hopefully die in as little

04:57:55.138 --> 04:57:56.590
pain as possible.

04:57:56.590 --> 04:58:02.328
In roughly 72% of cases, amputation of the
affected areas has prevented the entire body

04:58:02.328 --> 04:58:08.238
from succumbing to the anomalous effects of
SCP-734, but this isn’t exactly feasible

04:58:08.238 --> 04:58:11.530
when the point of contact is the victim’s
head.

04:58:11.530 --> 04:58:16.000
Within hours, the agent’s flesh had flaked
off of her face, leaving her looking like

04:58:16.000 --> 04:58:17.780
a red, bloody skull.

04:58:17.780 --> 04:58:21.750
A few hours after that, she didn’t have
a head at all.

04:58:21.750 --> 04:58:26.600
Throughout the disintegration process of this
unfortunate agent, the Foundation took grisly

04:58:26.600 --> 04:58:27.810
photographs.

04:58:27.810 --> 04:58:33.708
These photographs are shown to anyone preparing
to work on the SCP-734 research project to

04:58:33.708 --> 04:58:39.100
teach them a hard lesson on the importance
of adhering to proper safety protocols.

04:58:39.100 --> 04:58:43.590
And these protocols about how to deal with
the Baby are incredibly tight, given that

04:58:43.590 --> 04:58:47.718
even incidental contact is often a death sentence.

04:58:47.718 --> 04:58:52.350
Anyone entering the Baby’s containment chamber
needs to wear contained-atmosphere hazmat

04:58:52.350 --> 04:58:53.350
suits.

04:58:53.350 --> 04:58:57.200
Anyone who makes physical contact with the
Baby, even when suited up, is immediately

04:58:57.200 --> 04:59:02.360
removed from the area and subject to several
hours of quarantine and observation.

04:59:02.360 --> 04:59:06.718
Even inanimate objects that have been inside
the containment chamber need to be thoroughly

04:59:06.718 --> 04:59:09.638
sterilized before being removed.

04:59:09.638 --> 04:59:15.760
Given that even anomalous children like SCP-734
have very delicate needs, a handler is always

04:59:15.760 --> 04:59:19.738
standing by in full hazmat gear to take care
of the baby.

04:59:19.738 --> 04:59:24.350
These handlers are rotated every hour to maintain
alertness and safety.

04:59:24.350 --> 04:59:30.548
These handlers feed and change SCP-734 regularly
and sometimes even provide toys that have

04:59:30.548 --> 04:59:32.900
been approved by the O5 Council.

04:59:32.900 --> 04:59:38.308
The Foundation has gone to great lengths to
keep SCP-734 alive and comfortable because

04:59:38.308 --> 04:59:43.750
they believe that SCP-734 could be an important
asset for them in the future.

04:59:43.750 --> 04:59:50.648
Or, more specifically, they see great strategic
value in SCP-734’s blood.

04:59:50.648 --> 04:59:56.398
As mentioned earlier, contact with any matter
from SCP-734 triggers its deadly anomalous

04:59:56.398 --> 04:59:59.148
effects, including bodily fluids like blood.

04:59:59.148 --> 05:00:04.540
But, unlike many toxic pathogens, in this
case there is no risk of the infection getting

05:00:04.540 --> 05:00:09.430
out of control since the infected do not become
vectors for transmission.

05:00:09.430 --> 05:00:14.218
Because of this, the blood of SCP-734 can
act as a powerful weapon for both terminating

05:00:14.218 --> 05:00:20.048
anomalies deemed unviable by the O5 Council
and assassinating dangerous people who belong

05:00:20.048 --> 05:00:22.000
to rival groups.

05:00:22.000 --> 05:00:26.600
Contact with the blood would completely destroy
the target’s body, with no other anomalous

05:00:26.600 --> 05:00:31.208
effects and no evidence of who exactly conducted
the hit.

05:00:31.208 --> 05:00:36.420
SCP-734 has been fitted with an arterial catheter
so that the Foundation can collect large quantities

05:00:36.420 --> 05:00:40.950
of blood from the anomalous infant every single
week for storage and research.

05:00:40.950 --> 05:00:44.398
But it isn’t just the blood that the Foundation
sees potential in.

05:00:44.398 --> 05:00:51.228
SCP-734 himself has scored incredibly well
on the Aeslinger Loyalty Index, the test the

05:00:51.228 --> 05:00:56.780
Foundation uses to judge the loyalty of potential
applicants to the Foundation cause.

05:00:56.780 --> 05:01:02.870
As SCP-734 matures, if these scores remain
consistent, he will likely be trained to become

05:01:02.870 --> 05:01:05.298
a Foundation field agent in the future.

05:01:05.298 --> 05:01:10.290
An agent capable of killing someone with a
touch would, needless to say, be an asset

05:01:10.290 --> 05:01:15.590
to certain covert missions that the Foundation
would probably prefer to keep off the books.

05:01:15.590 --> 05:01:20.220
Of course, the SCP Foundation recruiting certain
compliant anomalies to perform missions for

05:01:20.220 --> 05:01:22.490
them is far from unprecedented.

05:01:22.490 --> 05:01:30.458
The most infamous of these is SCP-076, also
known as Able, a supernatural, eternally-resurrecting

05:01:30.458 --> 05:01:34.148
swordsman and perhaps one of the finest warriors
who ever lived.

05:01:34.148 --> 05:01:38.318
The Foundation took note of this and channeled
his eternal thirst for battle into working

05:01:38.318 --> 05:01:40.798
with his very own Mobile Task Force.

05:01:40.798 --> 05:01:45.078
He could assist in missions by taking out
his bloodlust on enemy groups of interest

05:01:45.078 --> 05:01:47.010
and dangerous anomalies.

05:01:47.010 --> 05:01:51.900
However, this ended up working a little too
well and led to disaster.

05:01:51.900 --> 05:01:56.790
Able was so good at his job that he burned
through all his allotted missions at astonishing

05:01:56.790 --> 05:01:57.790
speed.

05:01:57.790 --> 05:02:02.468
Left with nothing more to do, Able got antsy,
which led to him turning his murderous desires

05:02:02.468 --> 05:02:06.968
on his fellow team members and then the Foundation
as a whole.

05:02:06.968 --> 05:02:12.190
It was an all-out massacre before his colleagues
were finally able to kill him and return him

05:02:12.190 --> 05:02:13.190
to containment.

05:02:13.190 --> 05:02:17.658
The failure of this initiative gave the very
idea of letting anomalies work for the Foundation

05:02:17.658 --> 05:02:19.798
in the field a bad name.

05:02:19.798 --> 05:02:26.318
But since then, things have changed, especially
with the establishment of MTF Alpha-9, aka

05:02:26.318 --> 05:02:31.840
Last Hope, a new mobile task force formed
entirely of anomalous individuals and their

05:02:31.840 --> 05:02:32.840
handlers.

05:02:32.840 --> 05:02:39.328
These consist of somewhat more stable anomalies,
such as Able’s counterpart, SCP-073, also

05:02:39.328 --> 05:02:40.660
known as Cain.

05:02:40.660 --> 05:02:45.888
Cain cannot be harmed, with any harm befalling
him simply being mirrored back on his attacker,

05:02:45.888 --> 05:02:50.968
and his vast array of knowledge makes him
an incredibly useful intelligence asset.

05:02:50.968 --> 05:02:56.670
Another of the several members of Last Hope
is Iris, also known as SCP-105.

05:02:56.670 --> 05:03:01.360
Much like Cain, Iris not only has anomalous
powers that make her immensely valuable for

05:03:01.360 --> 05:03:06.791
missions in the field, she’s also compliant
and capable of listening to reason, unlike

05:03:06.791 --> 05:03:07.818
Cain.

05:03:07.818 --> 05:03:13.260
Her abilities include being able to actively
surveil and even interact with photos of any

05:03:13.260 --> 05:03:16.590
location, especially when taken with her anomalous
camera.

05:03:16.590 --> 05:03:22.930
Someday, SCP-734 could count himself among
other anomalous Foundation agents like these,

05:03:22.930 --> 05:03:27.170
providing he continues to show promise and
doesn’t develop a dislike of the Foundation

05:03:27.170 --> 05:03:31.468
as he ages, since after all, he won’t be
a baby forever.

05:03:31.468 --> 05:03:37.138
So if ever you find yourself on the Foundation’s
bad side, you have a good reason to be paranoid.

05:03:37.138 --> 05:03:42.070
You’ll have no idea that one day, the man
who’s going to kill you will approach and

05:03:42.070 --> 05:03:44.298
shake your hand with a smile.

05:03:44.298 --> 05:03:49.040
It won’t be until later when you feel that
strange tingle on your palm and feel the skin

05:03:49.040 --> 05:03:54.370
starting to flake away that you’ll realize
you’ve been a dead man walking for hours.

